": "**77.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "330", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "332", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "333", "mode": "normal", "text": "**78.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "334", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "336", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "337", "mode": "normal", "text": "**79.** Every municipality governed by this Code is represented by its council; its powers are exercised and its duties discharged by such council and its officers.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "338", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "340", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "341", "mode": "normal", "text": "**80.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "342", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "344", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "345", "mode": "normal", "text": "**81.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "346", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "348", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "349", "mode": "normal", "text": "**82.** The council must directly exercise the powers conferred upon it by this Code; it cannot delegate them. Nevertheless, it may appoint committees composed of as many of its members at it deems advisable, with power to examine and study any question whatever. In such case the committees must render account of their labours by reports signed by their chairman or by a majority of their members; and no report of a committee has any effect whatever until it has been adopted by the council at a regular sitting. Where a committee is appointed by the council of a regional county municipality whose territory includes that of a core city within the meaning of paragraph 9.1 of section 1 of the Act respecting land use planning and development ( chapter A‐19.1", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "350", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "352", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "353", "mode": "normal", "text": "**83.** By-laws, resolutions and other municipal enactments must be passed by the council in session.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "354", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "356", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "357", "mode": "normal", "text": "**84.** Any council which, under this Code, no longer possesses the powers which were conferred upon it under the authority of Acts antecedent to 1 November 1916, may repeal any enactment which it may have passed under such powers.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "358", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "360", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "361", "mode": "normal", "text": "**85.** Every one who is entitled to be heard before the council or any of its committees, may be heard in person or by any other person acting of his behalf, whether authorized by power of attorney or not. He may also call and examine witnesses.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "362", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "364", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "365", "mode": "normal", "text": "**86.** The council or any committee, on every question or matter pending before them, may:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "366", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "368", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "369", "mode": "normal", "text": "**87.** If any one so summoned before the council or any committee fails, without just cause, to appear at the time and place mentioned in the summons, when compensation has been paid or offered to him for his reasonable travelling expenses for going and returning, and $1 a day for his time, he incurs a fine of not less than $4 nor more than $10.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "370", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "372", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "373", "mode": "normal", "text": "**88.** Any document, order or proceeding of a council, the publication of which is required by this Code, or by the council itself, must be published in the same manner as public notices.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "374", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "376", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "377", "mode": "normal", "text": "**89.** Any person depositing or filing any document relating to municipal matters in the office of the municipality or before the council in session, is entitled to a receipt or acknowledgment certifying to the deposit or filing of such document. Such receipt is given by the clerk-treasurer, if the deposit is made at his office, or by the person presiding at the council, if filed before the council in session. Any clerk-treasurer or person presiding, who neglects or refuses to receive any such document, or to deposit the same in the archives of the municipality, or to give the required receipt, incurs a fine of not more than $100 in each case, in addition to the damages occasioned by such refusal or neglect.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "378", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "380", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "381", "mode": "normal", "text": "**90.** Every document produced as an exhibit, and filed in the office of the municipality or with its officers, must be returned, on being tendered a receipt therefor, to the person who produced the same, whenever he requires it, after it has served the purpose for which it was filed.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "382", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "384", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "385", "mode": "normal", "text": "**91.** The office of the municipality is that which is occupied by the clerk-treasurer in his official capacity, in accordance with article 183, and must be in the territory of the municipality, except in the case mentioned in article 92.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "386", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "388", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "389", "mode": "normal", "text": "**92.** The office of a municipality or of any officer or employee of such municipality may be established in a local municipal territory situated in proximity to that of the municipality.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "390", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "392", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "393", "mode": "normal", "text": "**94.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "394", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "396", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "397", "mode": "normal", "text": "**95.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "398", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "400", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "401", "mode": "normal", "text": "**96.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "402", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "404", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "405", "mode": "normal", "text": "**97.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "406", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "408", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "409", "mode": "normal", "text": "**98.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "410", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "412", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "413", "mode": "normal", "text": "**99.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "414", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "416", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "417", "mode": "normal", "text": "**100.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "418", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "420", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "421", "mode": "normal", "text": "**101.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "422", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "424", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "425", "mode": "normal", "text": "**102.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "426", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "428", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "429", "mode": "normal", "text": "**103.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "430", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "432", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "433", "mode": "normal", "text": "**104.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "434", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "436", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "437", "mode": "normal", "text": "**105.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "438", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "440", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "441", "mode": "normal", "text": "**106.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "442", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "444", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "445", "mode": "normal", "text": "**107.** No vote given by a person illegally holding office as member of a council, and no act in which, in such capacity, he has participated, can be set aside, with respect to persons who have acted in good faith, solely by reason of the illegal exercise of such office.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "446", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "448", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "449", "mode": "normal", "text": "**108.** Any member of a council who, to his own knowledge, is not at the time duly qualified, votes at any sitting of the council, or of any committee thereof, is liable to a fine of not more than $100 for each such vote.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "450", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "452", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "453", "mode": "normal", "text": "**109.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "454", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "456", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "457", "mode": "normal", "text": "**110.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "458", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "460", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "461", "mode": "normal", "text": "**111.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "462", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "464", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "465", "mode": "normal", "text": "**112.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "466", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "468", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "469", "mode": "normal", "text": "**113.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "470", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "472", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "473", "mode": "normal", "text": "**114.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "474", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "476", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "477", "mode": "normal", "text": "**115.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "478", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "480", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "481", "mode": "normal", "text": "**116.** The council may, at any time, appoint one of the councillors as acting-mayor who, in the absence of the mayor or when the office is vacant, discharges the duties of the mayoralty, with all the privileges and rights, and subject to all the obligations thereunto attached.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "482", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "484", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "485", "mode": "normal", "text": "**117.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "486", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "488", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "489", "mode": "normal", "text": "**118.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "490", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "492", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "493", "mode": "normal", "text": "**119.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "494", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "496", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "497", "mode": "normal", "text": "**120.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "498", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "500", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "501", "mode": "normal", "text": "**121.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "502", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "504", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "505", "mode": "normal", "text": "**122.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "506", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "508", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "509", "mode": "normal", "text": "**123.** The council of the regional county municipality may, by by-law, constitute an executive committee composed of the warden, the deputy warden and the number of other council members specified in the by-law. Subject to the third paragraph, the council shall, by resolution, appoint the members of the executive committee in accordance with the number indicated in the by-law. In the case of a regional county municipality whose territory includes that of a core city within the meaning of paragraph 9.1 of section 1 of the Act respecting land use planning and development ( chapter A-19.1 A majority of the members of the committee constitutes a quorum.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "510", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "512", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "513", "mode": "normal", "text": "**124.** The council may, by by-law, delegate to the executive committee any of the powers it may exercise by resolution. However, the council cannot delegate to the executive committee the appointment and fixing of the salary of an employee assigned to a post the holder of which is not an employee within the meaning of the Labour Code ( chapter C-27 The resolutions made by the executive committee have the same force and effect as if they were made by the council.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "514", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "516", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "517", "mode": "normal", "text": "**125.** The council, when it considers it advisable, may replace any member of the executive committee it has itself designated. It may also, by by-law, withdraw from the committee all or part of the powers it has delegated to it under article 124.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "518", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "520", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "521", "mode": "normal", "text": "**126.** The warden or, when he is absent, the deputy warden is ex officio The clerk-treasurer of the regional county municipality is ex officio", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "522", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "524", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "525", "mode": "normal", "text": "**127.** In exercising any power devolved on it by delegation of the council, the executive committee is subject to the rules of this Code respecting the holding of its sittings and the general conduct of its affairs, inasmuch as such rules apply to such council and are consistent with the application of this Section.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "526", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "528", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "529", "mode": "normal", "text": "**128.** The delegates of every regional county municipality are three in number. Such delegates exercise the powers and discharge the duties which devolve upon them under this Code, in conjunction with the delegates of the other regional county municipalities concerned.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "530", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "532", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "533", "mode": "normal", "text": "**129.** The warden is, ex officio Subject to the third paragraph, the other two delegates are appointed by the council, from among its members, at the sitting held in the month of November. They remain in office until their successors are duly installed even if they have ceased to form part of the council, unless, in the latter case, they have been replaced under article 130. In the case of a regional county municipality whose territory includes that of a core city within the meaning of paragraph 9.1 of section 1 of the Act respecting land use planning and development ( chapter A‐19.1", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "534", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "536", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "537", "mode": "normal", "text": "**130.** Whenever any one of the delegates dies, or is unable to attend to his duties during two consecutive months, or refuses to discharge such duties during a like period, the council appoints another delegate in his stead, at the first sitting held after such death or the expiry of two months. If one of the delegates ceases to form part of the council, his successor must be appointed by the council without delay.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "538", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "540", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "541", "mode": "normal", "text": "**131.** The council may appoint, from its members, a substitute for each of the three delegates. Such substitute shall act whenever his principal is unable to perform his duties.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "542", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "544", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "545", "mode": "normal", "text": "**132.** The board of delegates is composed of the delegates from the regional county municipalities in which the inhabitants of the territory thereof, or some of them, are interested in any work or matter which comes under the jurisdiction of such municipalities.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "546", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "548", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "549", "mode": "normal", "text": "**133.** The board of delegates sits for the purpose of taking into consideration and deciding matters within its jurisdiction, whenever required so to do, or whenever it deems necessary, by following the formalities prescribed for the summoning of the meeting.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "550", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "552", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "553", "mode": "normal", "text": "**134.** The delegates meet at the time and place indicated in the notice of meeting given to them.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "554", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "556", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "557", "mode": "normal", "text": "**135.** The meeting of the board of delegates is convened, upon a requisition in writing, by two members of the board, or by the clerk-treasurer of one of the regional county municipalities. Such meeting is convened and held in the same manner as a special sitting of the council of a regional county municipality. The place where such meeting is held is selected by those who convene the same.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "558", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "560", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "561", "mode": "normal", "text": "**136.** Any person interested in a question submitted, or about to be submitted, to the board of delegates, may call upon the clerk-treasurer of one of such regional county municipalities to convene a meeting of the board of delegates, if a meeting of such board has not already been convened, to be held within the 15 days next following.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "562", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "564", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "565", "mode": "normal", "text": "**137.** The clerk-treasurer of the regional county municipality who called the meeting is, ex officio If the meeting has been convened by two members of the board, the clerk-treasurer of the municipality whereof such two members are the delegates, is the secretary of the board. If the two members belong to different councils, the secretary of the board is appointed by the delegates, and must be the clerk-treasurer of one of the regional county municipalities. The secretary keeps minutes of the proceedings of the delegates, and deposits the same with all other documents of the board, in the archives of the municipality whose officer he is; and he forwards a copy to the office of each of the other regional county municipalities interested. The clerk-treasurer of each regional county municipality must forward to each local municipality interested, among the municipalities whose territory is included in that of the regional county municipality, a copy of every decision of the board of delegates.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "566", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "568", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "569", "mode": "normal", "text": "**138.** Four of the delegates summoned to the meeting form a quorum of the board.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "570", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "572", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "573", "mode": "normal", "text": "**139.** The meeting is presided over by any one of the delegates present, chosen from among themselves. In the case of an equal division of votes in their choice of a chairman, the chairman is chosen by lot.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "574", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "576", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "577", "mode": "normal", "text": "**140.** Every disputed question is decided by the vote of the majority of the delegates present, the chairman having the same right to vote as the other delegates; in the event of an equal division of votes, the application shall be submitted to the Minister of Municipal Affairs, Regions and Land Occupancy and the latter shall appoint a person to act as an arbitrator whose decision shall have the same effect as a decision rendered by the board of delegates. The costs of the arbitration shall be paid in equal shares by the municipalities concerned. The fees of the arbitrator shall, if they have not been determined by the Minister of Municipal Affairs, Regions and Land Occupancy when appointing him, be fixed by a judge of the Court of Québec, on an application, after notice to the parties interested. The costs on such application shall form part of the costs of arbitration.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "578", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "580", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "581", "mode": "normal", "text": "**141.** Articles 88 and 689 to 692 apply likewise to all documents, orders or proceedings of the board of delegates. Articles 85, 89 and 90 apply likewise to the board of delegates.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "582", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "584", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "585", "mode": "normal", "text": "**143.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "586", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "588", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "589", "mode": "normal", "text": "**144.** The council of the regional county municipality sits at the place established for its first sitting in accordance with the Act respecting municipal territorial organization ( chapter O-9", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "590", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "592", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "593", "mode": "normal", "text": "**145.** The local council sits at the place selected for the first sitting in accordance with the Act respecting municipal territorial organization ( chapter O-9 The council may, by by-law, determine that the place at which it sits is in a local municipal territory situated in proximity to the territory of the municipality.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "594", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "596", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "597", "mode": "normal", "text": "**146.** The Québec flag must be flown on or in front of the municipal building where the meetings of the council are held, to the right if two flags are flown or in the middle in other cases.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "598", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "600", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "601", "mode": "normal", "text": "**147.** The quorum of the council of a local municipality is a majority of its members.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "602", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "604", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "605", "mode": "normal", "text": "**148.** The council of a regional county municipality shall hold regular sittings at least once every two months, including one on the fourth Wednesday in November. The council of a local municipality shall hold regular sittings at least once a month. The council shall determine the schedule of its regular sittings, setting the date and time of each sitting, before the beginning of the calendar year. Any documents useful in making decisions must, barring exceptional situations, be available to the members of the council not later than 72 hours before the time set for the beginning of the sitting. However, the council may decide that a regular sitting is to begin on a date and at a time other than that specified in the schedule.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "606", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "608", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "609", "mode": "normal", "text": "**149.** The sittings are public, and the proceedings must be audible and intelligible.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "610", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "612", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "613", "mode": "normal", "text": "**150.** The sitting of the council includes a period during which the persons attending may put oral questions to the council members. The council may, by by-law, prescribe the length of the period, the time at which it is held and the procedure to be followed in putting a question. It may also, by by-law, prescribe measures to give precedence to questions put by persons who reside in the territory of the municipality, or who are the owners of an immovable or the occupants of a business establishment situated in that territory.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "614", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "616", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "617", "mode": "normal", "text": "**151.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "618", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "620", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "621", "mode": "normal", "text": "**152.** A special sitting of any council may be convened at any time by the head, by the clerk-treasurer or by two members of such council, by giving special notice in writing of such sitting to all the members of the council, other than those convening the same. Any documents useful in making decisions must be available to the council members at the time the notice is given. The notice of meeting may be notified to the members by a technological means in accordance with articles 133 and 134 of the Code of Civil Procedure ( chapter C-25.01", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "622", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "624", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "625", "mode": "normal", "text": "**153.** At a special sitting, only the subjects or matters mentioned in the notice calling the council together, may be taken into consideration except with the unanimous consent of the members of the council if they all are present. The council, before preceding to business at such sitting, must set forth and declare in the minutes of the sitting that notice of meeting has been notified in conformity with this Code, to all the members of the council who are not present at the opening of the sitting. If it appears that the notice of meeting has not been notified to all the absent members, the sitting must be immediately closed, under penalty of the nullity of all its proceedings.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "626", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "628", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "629", "mode": "normal", "text": "**154.** Any sitting can be adjourned by the council to any other hour of the same day or to a subsequent day, without its being necessary to give notice of such adjournment to the members who were not present, save in the case mentioned in article 155.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "630", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "632", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "633", "mode": "normal", "text": "**155.** Two members of the council, when there is no quorum present, may adjourn the sitting at the expiration of one hour from the time it is established that there is no quorum. The hour of the adjournment and the names of the members present must be entered in the minutes of the sitting. In such case a special notice in writing of the adjournment is given by the clerk-treasurer to the members of the council who were not present at the time of adjournment. The service of such notice must be established at the resumption of the adjourned sitting, in the same manner as that of the notice convening a special sitting, and the absence of service of such notice renders null every proceeding adopted at such part of the adjourned sitting.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "634", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "636", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "637", "mode": "normal", "text": "**156.** The notice of convocation of a special sitting of the council, as well as the notice of adjournment in the case mentioned in article 155, must be given to each member of the council at least three days before the date fixed for the sitting, or the resumption of the adjourned sitting, if it relates to the council of the regional county municipality, and at least two days before the day fixed, if it relates to the local council. That notice shall be notified by the person who gives the notice, an officer or employee of the municipality, a peace officer, a bailiff or an employee of a public or private mail delivery or courier enterprise.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "638", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "640", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "641", "mode": "normal", "text": "**157.** Notwithstanding the preceding articles, the failure to comply with the formalities prescribed for convening a sitting of the council cannot be invoked when all the members of the council present in the territory of the municipality have attended such sitting.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "642", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "644", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "645", "mode": "normal", "text": "**158.** The sittings of the council are presided over by its head or by the acting mayor, or, in their absence, by one of its members chosen from among the councillors present.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "646", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "648", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "649", "mode": "normal", "text": "**159.** The officer presiding over the sitting of the council maintains order and decorum and decides questions of order, saving appeal to the council. He may order that any person disturbing a sitting of the council be removed from the place where the sitting is held.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "650", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "652", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "653", "mode": "normal", "text": "**160.** Every disputed question is decided by a majority of the votes of the members present, excepting in cases where a provision of law requires a greater number of concordant votes. However, a local municipality may, by by-law, specify the cases in which a disputed question must be decided by a majority greater than the majority required under the first paragraph.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "654", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "656", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "657", "mode": "normal", "text": "**161.** The head of the council or any person presiding at a sitting of the council shall be entitled to vote but not obliged to do so; when a vote results in a tie, the decision shall be deemed to be in the negative. However, the warden who has been replaced as representative of the municipality, in accordance with section 210.27 of the Act respecting municipal territorial organization ( chapter O-9", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "658", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "660", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "661", "mode": "normal", "text": "**162.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "662", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "664", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "665", "mode": "normal", "text": "**163.** If the majority of the members of a local council have a personal interest in any question submitted to their decision, such question must be referred to the council of the regional county municipality, which, in respect of the consideration and decision of such question, possesses all the rights and privileges, and is subject to all the obligations of the local council.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "666", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "668", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "669", "mode": "normal", "text": "**164.** Every member present at a meeting of the council is bound to vote, unless he is exempted or debarred therefrom by reason of his interest in the matter concerned, under the Act respecting elections and referendums in municipalities ( chapter E-2.2 Every vote must be given by word of mouth, and, upon demand, the votes are entered in the minute book of the council.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "670", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "672", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "673", "mode": "normal", "text": "**165.** In addition to the officers whom it is bound to appoint, the municipality may, to secure the execution of its ordinances and of the requirements of law, appoint all other officers, and dismiss and replace them. The municipality may fix the salary of all its public servants and employees.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "674", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "676", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "677", "mode": "normal", "text": "**166.** If any municipal office becomes vacant, such vacancy must be filled by the council within the 30 days next following.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "678", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "680", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "681", "mode": "normal", "text": "**167.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "682", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "684", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "685", "mode": "normal", "text": "**168.** No act, duty, writing or proceeding executed in his official capacity by a municipal officer who holds office illegally, can be set aside solely on the ground of his so holding such office illegally.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "686", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "688", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "689", "mode": "normal", "text": "**170.** Every officer appointed to replace another, holds office only for the remainder of the term for which his predecessor was appointed.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "690", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "692", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "693", "mode": "normal", "text": "**171.** Every officer who has ceased to discharge the duties of his office, is bound to deliver at the office of the municipality, within eight days next following, all the moneys, keys, books, papers, articles, insignia, documents and archives belonging to such office. In the event of the death or absence from Québec of such officer, his representatives must make such delivery, within one month from such death or such absence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "694", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "696", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "697", "mode": "normal", "text": "**172.** The municipality is entitled, in addition to any other legal recourse whatsoever, to recover by seizure before judgment, from such officer or his representatives, all such moneys, keys, books, papers, articles, insignia, documents or archives, with damages, interest and costs. The municipality may exercise the same rights and recourse against every person detaining the said effects and refusing to deliver them up.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "698", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "700", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "701", "mode": "normal", "text": "**173.** Every person who refuses or neglects to obey any lawful order of any municipal officer, given under this Code or any municipal by-law incurs, for each offence, a fine of not less than $1 nor more than $5, saving cases otherwise provided for. Every person who hinders or prevents or attempts to hinder or prevent such officer in the execution of his duties, incurs for each offence a fine of not less than $2 nor more than $10, and is liable in damages towards those who have suffered damage.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "702", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "704", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "705", "mode": "normal", "text": "**174.** Every municipal officer in whose hands any document whatsoever is deposited or filed, is bound, on demand, to give a receipt therefor, under penalty of the fine enacted by article 89. Should the document deposited or filed form part of the archives of the municipality, it is the duty of the officer who received the same, to file it among the archives without delay, under the same penalty.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "706", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "708", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "709", "mode": "normal", "text": "**175.** The municipality is responsible for the acts of its officers in the performance of the duties for which they are employed, as well as for the damages occasioned by their refusal to discharge or their negligence in discharging their duties, saving its recourse against such officers; the whole without prejudice to a recourse in damages against the officers by those who have suffered damage.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "710", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "712", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "713", "mode": "normal", "text": "**176.** At the end of the fiscal year, the clerk-treasurer shall draw up the financial report for that fiscal year and certify that it is accurate. The report must include the municipality’s financial statements and any other document or information required by the Minister. The clerk-treasurer shall also, at the Minister’s request, produce a statement fixing the effective aggregate taxation rate of the municipality, in accordance with Division III of Chapter XVIII.1 of the Act respecting municipal taxation ( chapter F-2.1 The Minister may prescribe any rule relating to the documents and information referred to in the first two paragraphs.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "714", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "716", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "717", "mode": "normal", "text": "**177.** The municipality may bring an action to account against any employee responsible for moneys belonging to it, and he may, if sufficient cause exists, be condemned to render an account thereof, and to pay the sum which he is declared to owe, with interest, expenses and legal costs, and, in addition, to pay any damages, if any be due.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "718", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "720", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "721", "mode": "normal", "text": "**178.** The municipality may by by-law establish a tariff of fees payable to municipal officers for their services, whether by the persons who have applied for them or by those on whose account they are rendered, or by the municipality, in cases in which such fees have not been fixed by law.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "722", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "724", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "725", "mode": "normal", "text": "**179.** Every municipality must have an officer entrusted with the care of its office and archives, and such officer is designated by the name of “clerk-treasurer”. However, the council may choose to appoint a clerk and a treasurer, in which case it must apportion between those persons the duties and powers inherent in the office of clerk-treasurer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "726", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "728", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "729", "mode": "normal", "text": "**180.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "730", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "732", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "733", "mode": "normal", "text": "**181.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "734", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "736", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "737", "mode": "normal", "text": "**182.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "738", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "740", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "741", "mode": "normal", "text": "**183.** The office of the clerk-treasurer is established in the place where the sittings of the council are held, or in any other place fixed, from time to time, by resolution of the council; provided the same be not in a hotel, inn, or place of public entertainment, in which alcoholic beverages are sold.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "742", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "744", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "745", "mode": "normal", "text": "**184.** The assistant clerk-treasurer, if one is appointed by the council, may perform all the duties of the office of the clerk-treasurer, with the same rights, powers and privileges and subject to the same obligations and penalties. In case of a vacancy in the office of clerk-treasurer, the assistant clerk-treasurer or, if there is no assistant clerk-treasurer, the director general must perform the duties of the office until the vacancy is filled.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "746", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "748", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "749", "mode": "normal", "text": "**185.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "750", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "752", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "753", "mode": "normal", "text": "**186.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "754", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "756", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "757", "mode": "normal", "text": "**187.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "758", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "760", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "761", "mode": "normal", "text": "**188.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "762", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "764", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "765", "mode": "normal", "text": "**189.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "766", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "768", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "769", "mode": "normal", "text": "**190.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "770", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "772", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "773", "mode": "normal", "text": "**191.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "774", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "776", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "777", "mode": "normal", "text": "**192.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "778", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "780", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "781", "mode": "normal", "text": "**193.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "782", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "784", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "785", "mode": "normal", "text": "**194.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "786", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "788", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "789", "mode": "normal", "text": "**195.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "790", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "792", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "793", "mode": "normal", "text": "**196.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "794", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "796", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "797", "mode": "normal", "text": "**197.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "798", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "800", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "801", "mode": "normal", "text": "**198.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "802", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "804", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "805", "mode": "normal", "text": "**199.** The clerk-treasurer is the custodian of all the books, registers, plans, maps, archives and other documents and papers, which are either the property of the municipality or are deposited, filed and preserved in the office of the municipality. He cannot divest himself of the custody of such archives, except with the permission of the council, or under the authority of a court.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "806", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "808", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "809", "mode": "normal", "text": "**200.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "810", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "812", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "813", "mode": "normal", "text": "**201.** The clerk-treasurer must attend every sitting of the council and draw up minutes of all the acts and proceedings thereof, in a register kept for that purpose, called: “The minute book of the council”. All minutes of a sitting of the council must be signed by the person presiding over the council and countersigned by the clerk-treasurer, and be approved by the council at the same or at the following meeting, but the lack of such approval does not prevent the minute from making proof. Whenever a by-law or a resolution is amended or repealed, mention must be made thereof in the margin of the minute book, opposite such by-law or resolution, together with the date of its amendment or repeal.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "814", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "816", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "817", "mode": "normal", "text": "**202.** Copies and extracts, certified by the clerk-treasurer, from all books, registers, archives, documents and papers preserved in the office of the municipality, are evidence of their contents.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "818", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "820", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "821", "mode": "normal", "text": "**203.** The clerk-treasurer shall collect all moneys payable to the municipality and, subject to all other legal provisions shall deposit the same in any bank or any deposit institution authorized under the Deposit Institutions and Deposit Protection Act ( chapter I-13.2.2 The council may invest the moneys mentioned in the first paragraph in the purchase of securities in a mutual fund which is managed by a financial institution, and all the securities of which are held by municipalities, by bodies referred to in section 18 of the Act respecting the Pension Plan of Elected Municipal Officers, by school service centres or by school boards or by two or more such entities. The investments made by such a fund must be limited to those set out in the first paragraph. The Minister may, by regulation, determine other securities in which the council may invest, through the agency of the mutual fund referred to in the second paragraph, the moneys mentioned in the first paragraph, or determine the forms of investment in which the council may invest the moneys through the agency of such a fund. All cheques issued and promissory notes or other securities executed by the municipality must be signed jointly by the mayor and the clerk-treasurer or, in case of the absence or inability to act of the mayor or of a vacancy in the office of mayor, by any member of the council previously authorized and by the clerk-treasurer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "822", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "824", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "825", "mode": "normal", "text": "**204.** Unless otherwise provided for in a by-law under article 960.1, the clerk-treasurer pays out of the funds of the municipality all sums of money due by it whenever, by resolution, he is authorized to do so by the council or, where such is the case, by a decision of the executive committee of a regional county municipality. If the sum to be paid does not exceed $25, the authorization of the head of the council is sufficient. Even in the absence of authorization from the council or from its head, it is his duty to pay, out of the funds of the municipality, any draft or order drawn upon him, or any sum demanded, by any one empowered so to do by this Code, or by any municipal by-law. No draft or order may, however, be legally paid unless the same shows sufficiently the use made or to be made of the sum therein mentioned.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "826", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "828", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "829", "mode": "normal", "text": "**205.** No clerk-treasurer may, under penalty of a fine of $20 for each infraction:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "830", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "832", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "833", "mode": "normal", "text": "**206.** The clerk-treasurer is bound to keep the books of account of the municipality in such a way as to:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "834", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "836", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "837", "mode": "normal", "text": "**207.** The clerk-treasurer is bound to keep a repertory in which he mentions, in a summary manner and in the order of their dates, all reports, procès-verbaux", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "838", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "840", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "841", "mode": "normal", "text": "**208.** The clerk-treasurer’s books of account and the vouchers for his expenditures together with all the registers or documents forming part of archives of the municipality may be inspected during regular working hours, by any person applying to do so.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "842", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "844", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "845", "mode": "normal", "text": "**209.** The person in charge of access to documents of the municipality shall issue to any person applying therefor, copies of or extracts from any book, roll, register or other document which forms part of the archives. However, the person in charge of access to documents may, notwithstanding section 171 of the Act respecting Access to documents held by public bodies and the Protection of personal information ( chapter A-2.1 The clerk-treasurer shall send without delay by mail, to the principal establishment of any person whose place of work and domicile are outside the territory of the municipality, who shall have filed in the office of the municipality a general application to that effect, and shall have made such principal establishment known, a certified copy of every public notice, by-law, resolution or procès-verbal Notwithstanding the second and third paragraphs of section 11 of the Act respecting Access to documents held by public bodies and the Protection of personal information ( chapter A-2.1", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "846", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "848", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "849", "mode": "normal", "text": "**210.** Every municipality must have a director general, who is the chief officer of the municipality, and a clerk-treasurer. If the council considers it expedient, it may appoint a single person to hold the offices of director general and clerk-treasurer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "850", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "852", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "853", "mode": "normal", "text": "**211.** Under the authority of the council or of the executive committee, the director general is responsible for the administration of the municipality and for that purpose he shall plan, organize, direct and supervise the activities of the municipality.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "854", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "856", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "857", "mode": "normal", "text": "**212.** In application of articles 210 and 211, the director general shall, in particular, perform the following duties:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "858", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "860", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "861", "mode": "normal", "text": "**213.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "862", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "864", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "865", "mode": "normal", "text": "**214.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "866", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "868", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "869", "mode": "normal", "text": "**215.** The clerk-treasurer must perform every duty required of him under the provisions of the law respecting the jury lists and the list of parliamentary electors; he must also perform every duty required of him by this Code respecting valuation rolls, collection rolls and other matters.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "870", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "872", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "873", "mode": "normal", "text": "**216.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "874", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "876", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "877", "mode": "normal", "text": "**217.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "878", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "880", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "881", "mode": "normal", "text": "**218.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "882", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "884", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "885", "mode": "normal", "text": "**219.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "886", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "888", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "889", "mode": "normal", "text": "**220.** Subject to the Act respecting liquor permits ( chapter P-9.1", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "890", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "892", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "893", "mode": "normal", "text": "**221.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "894", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "896", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "897", "mode": "normal", "text": "**222.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "898", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "900", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "901", "mode": "normal", "text": "**223.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "902", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "904", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "905", "mode": "normal", "text": "**224.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "906", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "908", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "909", "mode": "normal", "text": "**225.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "styl