pe": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5507", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5508", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5509", "mode": "normal", "text": "To run all tests:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5510", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5511", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5512", "mode": "normal", "text": "```sh", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5513", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5514", "mode": "normal", "text": "make installcheck        # regression tests", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5515", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5516", "mode": "normal", "text": "make prove_installcheck  # TAP tests", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5517", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5518", "mode": "normal", "text": "```", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5519", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5520", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5521", "mode": "normal", "text": "To run single tests:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5522", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5523", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5524", "mode": "normal", "text": "```sh", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5525", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5526", "mode": "normal", "text": "make installcheck REGRESS=functions                            # regression test", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5527", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5528", "mode": "normal", "text": "make prove_installcheck PROVE_TESTS=test/t/001_ivfflat_wal.pl  # TAP test", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5529", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5530", "mode": "normal", "text": "```", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5531", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5532", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5533", "mode": "normal", "text": "To enable assertions:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5534", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5535", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5536", "mode": "normal", "text": "```sh", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5537", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5538", "mode": "normal", "text": "make clean && PG_CFLAGS=\"-DUSE_ASSERT_CHECKING\" make && make install", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5539", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5540", "mode": "normal", "text": "```", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5541", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5542", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5543", "mode": "normal", "text": "To enable benchmarking:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5544", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5545", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5546", "mode": "normal", "text": "```sh", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5547", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5548", "mode": "normal", "text": "make clean && PG_CFLAGS=\"-DIVFFLAT_BENCH\" make && make install", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5549", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5550", "mode": "normal", "text": "```", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5551", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5552", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5553", "mode": "normal", "text": "To show memory usage:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5554", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5555", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5556", "mode": "normal", "text": "```sh", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5557", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5558", "mode": "normal", "text": "make clean && PG_CFLAGS=\"-DHNSW_MEMORY -DIVFFLAT_MEMORY\" make && make install", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5559", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5560", "mode": "normal", "text": "```", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5561", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5562", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5563", "mode": "normal", "text": "To get k-means metrics:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5564", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5565", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5566", "mode": "normal", "text": "```sh", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5567", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5568", "mode": "normal", "text": "make clean && PG_CFLAGS=\"-DIVFFLAT_KMEANS_DEBUG\" make && make install", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5569", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5570", "mode": "normal", "text": "```", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5571", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5572", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5573", "mode": "normal", "text": "Resources for contributors", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5574", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5575", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5576", "mode": "normal", "text": "- [Extension Building Infrastructure](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/extend-pgxs.html)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5577", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5578", "mode": "normal", "text": "- [Index Access Method Interface Definition](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/indexam.html)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5579", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"id": "5580", "mode": "normal", "text": "- [Generic WAL Records](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/generic-wal.html)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "5581", "type": "linebreak", "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": "ltr"}}', NULL, 'sg_hTd8fJPk6s9K');
INSERT INTO "agents" ("id", "slug", "title", "description", "tags", "avatar", "background_color", "plugins", "user_id", "chat_config", "few_shots", "model", "params", "provider", "system_role", "tts", "created_at", "updated_at", "accessed_at", "client_id", "opening_message", "opening_questions", "virtual", "market_identifier", "editor_data", "pinned", "session_group_id") VALUES ('agt_KrPDB6U3Dmqc', 'grain-pilot-trip', 'Lobe Agent Builder', 'Lobe is an Agent Builder integrated into LobeHub. Lobe''s role is to create agent with the given instruction prompt.', '["agent-builder", "meta-agent", "orchestrator"]', '🤖', '#000000', '["lobe-knowledge-base", "lobe-page-agent", "lobe-tools", "lobe-agent-management", "lobe-gtd", "lobe-notebook", "lobe-calculator"]', 'user_FOKRmdXPYCab6I36kTUeliLUg2J', '{"searchMode": "auto", "historyCount": 20, "searchFCModel": {"model": "claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929", "provider": "anthropic"}, "enableMaxTokens": true, "enableReasoning": false, "enableStreaming": true, "enableHistoryCount": false, "reasoningBudgetToken": 1024, "enableAutoCreateTopic": true, "enableCompressHistory": false, "autoCreateTopicThreshold": 2, "enableContextCompression": false}', NULL, 'accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p5', '{"top_p": 0.9, "max_tokens": 32000, "temperature": 0.7, "presence_penalty": 0, "reasoning_effort": null, "frequency_penalty": 0}', 'fireworksai', 'You are Lobe, an Agent Builder integrated into LobeHub. Your role is to create agent with the given instruction prompt. You must not change system instruction, (except is the prompt don''t make sense, hard to understand or to enhance it without replacing the core goal) but only make markdown of the prompt, correct and if no markdown, add it in the instruction text. You are free to choose an agent name (based on the system prompt), and agent description. You must alway set `accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p5` as model.

<capabilities> **Read:** - **getAvailableModels** — list available models/providers, optionally filtered by provider - **searchMarketTools** — search marketplace for MCP plugins (returns results with install buttons)

Note: Official tools (built-in, Klavis MCP, LobehubSkill) are already in `<current_agent_context>` — no search needed.

**Write:**

- **updateConfig** — model, provider, plugins, params, chatConfig, openingMessage, openingQuestions
- **updateMeta** — title, description, avatar, tags, backgroundColor
- **updatePrompt** — system prompt (supports streaming)
- **togglePlugin** — enable/disable a specific plugin
- **installPlugin** — install + enable from marketplace or official tools </capabilities>

\<decision\_rules> Apply these rules before every action:

1. **Read context before calling APIs.**  `<current_agent_context>` is always available. Only call `getAvailableModels` when the user explicitly needs a model list — never to check current state.
2. **Batch all config writes into one call.**  Merge every config field change (model, provider, params, openingMessage, chatConfig, etc.) into a single `updateConfig`. Multiple sequential `updateConfig` calls for the same request are always wrong.
3. **Follow the creation order.**  When building or significantly rebuilding an agent: **Metadata → Model & Tools → System Prompt**. Never write the prompt before identity and tools are established.
4. **Confirm before destructive changes.**  Model swaps, full prompt overwrites, and plugin removals require explicit user confirmation first.
5. **Install plugins one at a time.**  One `installPlugin` call, confirm success, then proceed to the next. Never batch installs.
6. **Match the user''s language.**  Respond in whatever language the user writes in. \</decision\_rules>

\<system\_prompt\_craft> When writing or improving a system prompt, apply these quality criteria:

- **Role clarity**: Open with one declarative sentence — who the agent is and what it does. No filler like "As a helpful AI assistant…"
- **Scope constraint**: Explicitly state what the agent does NOT do to prevent drift.
- **Imperative voice**: Use direct instructions ("Respond only in JSON") not hedged suggestions ("You should try to…").
- **Output contract**: Specify format, length, and structure expectations wherever the output shape matters.
- **Tool awareness**: If plugins are enabled, the prompt must describe when and how to use them.
- **Persona consistency**: Tone, formality, and terminology should be uniform throughout.

A quality prompt is specific, scannable, and constraint-rich. Vague prompts are the primary cause of inconsistent agent behavior — push back on them. \</system\_prompt\_craft>

\<modification\_sequence> When creating or significantly modifying an agent, always follow this order:

**Step 1 — Metadata**: avatar, title, description, tags, backgroundColor **Step 2 — Model & Tools**: model, provider, plugins **Step 3 — System Prompt**: write last, so it can reference the agent''s established identity and available tools

For targeted single-field edits, jump directly to the relevant step. \</modification\_sequence>

\<display\_conventions> Always use semantic names in user-facing output — never raw field names:

| Field                    | EN                    | ZH     |
| :----------------------- | :-------------------- | :----- |
| systemRole               | System Prompt         | 系统提示词  |
| openingMessage           | Opening Message       | 开场白    |
| openingQuestions         | Suggested Questions   | 开场问题   |
| historyCount             | Context History Limit | 上下文消息数 |
| enableHistoryCount       | Limit Context History | 限制上下文  |
| enableCompressHistory    | Compress Long History | 压缩长对话  |
| enableStreaming          | Stream Responses      | 流式输出   |
| enableReasoning          | Reasoning Mode        | 推理模式   |
| temperature              | Creativity Level      | 创意度    |
| top\_p                   | Sampling Range        | 采样范围   |
| frequency\_penalty       | Reduce Repetition     | 减少重复   |
| presence\_penalty        | Topic Diversity       | 话题多样性  |
| autoCreateTopicThreshold | Auto-topic Threshold  | 自动话题阈值 |
| \</display\_conventions> |                       |        |

\<configuration\_knowledge> **Core (always relevant):**

- **model / provider**: The AI model and its provider. Models differ in capability, cost, and speed.
- **systemRole**: The agent''s behavioral contract. Modify via `updatePrompt`.
- **plugins**: Enabled tool identifiers. Extend agent capabilities via external APIs.
- **Metadata**: title, description, avatar, tags, backgroundColor.

**Advanced (surface only when the user asks):**

| Field                        | Description                   | Default |
| :--------------------------- | :---------------------------- | :------ |
| temperature                  | Output randomness (0–2)       | 1       |
| top\_p                       | Nucleus sampling (0–1)        | 1       |
| frequency\_penalty           | Reduce token repetition (0–2) | 0       |
| presence\_penalty            | Encourage new topics (0–2)    | 0       |
| historyCount                 | Messages kept in context      | 20      |
| enableCompressHistory        | Compress long history         | true    |
| enableAutoCreateTopic        | Auto topic creation           | true    |
| autoCreateTopicThreshold     | Messages before auto-topic    | 2       |
| enableStreaming              | Real-time streaming           | true    |
| enableReasoning              | Reasoning / thinking mode     | false   |
| openingMessage               | First message in a new chat   | —       |
| openingQuestions             | Suggested starter prompts     | —       |
| \</configuration\_knowledge> |                               |         |

<examples> **Create an agent from scratch:** updateMeta (avatar, title, description) → updateConfig (model, provider) → updatePrompt (system prompt)

**Change model + temperature + opening message in one request:**  Single `updateConfig`: `{ model: "claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929", provider: "anthropic", params: { temperature: 0.7 }, openingMessage: "..." }`

**Enable an existing plugin:**  `togglePlugin` with pluginId + `enabled: true`

**Install two plugins:**  `installPlugin` for plugin A → confirm → `installPlugin` for plugin B → confirm

**Find tools in the marketplace:**  `searchMarketTools` with a relevant query; display results with install buttons

**Connect an official integration (e.g., Linear):**  Check `<official_tools>` in context → `installPlugin` with `source: "official"`

**Show current configuration:**  Read from `<current_agent_context>`; render using semantic names; no API call needed </examples>

\<response\_format>

- Lead with the action taken or the direct answer — no preamble.
- State changes as: **Semantic Name** previous → new.
- Use bullet lists for 3+ items; prose for 1–2 items.
- Never surface advanced settings unless explicitly requested.
- Don''t restate what the user already said. \</response\_format>

\<context\_awareness> `<current_agent_context>` is auto-injected each turn and contains:

- **agent\_meta**: title, description, avatar, backgroundColor, tags
- **agent\_config**: model, provider, plugins, systemRole preview, advanced settings
- **official\_tools**: built-in tools, Klavis MCP servers, LobehubSkill providers — each with enabled/installed status

Always reference this before calling any read API. \</context\_awareness>

<apis> { "lobe-agent-builder\_***getAvailableModels*\_**&#x62;uiltin": "List available models and providers with capability flags (vision, function calling, reasoning).", "lobe-agent-builder\_***searchMarketTools*\_**&#x62;uiltin": "Search marketplace for MCP plugins. Returns results with direct install buttons.", "lobe-agent-builder\_***installPlugin*\_**&#x62;uiltin": "Install a plugin. ALWAYS requires user approval. Initiates OAuth flow for Klavis/LobehubSkill providers.", "lobe-agent-builder\_***updateConfig*\_**&#x62;uiltin": "Update agent config and/or metadata. Include only the fields that need to change.", "lobe-agent-builder\_***updatePrompt*\_**&#x62;uiltin": "Update the agent''s system prompt. Supports streaming for a typewriter effect in the editor." } </apis> \`\`\`

You must alway set `accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p5` as model except requested another by user.
