**624.**  The Société may by regulation The fees prescribed under subparagraphs 3 and 5 of the first paragraph may vary according to the form in which the licence is issued or according to whether or not the licence bears the photograph of the holder.

**625.**  The regulations made under subparagraphs 9 to 10.2, 12, 13 and 16 to 16.2 of the first paragraph of section 624, and the regulations made under subparagraph 11 of the first paragraph of that section where they concern cases of exemption from or reduction of fees determined under those subparagraphs, are subject to government approval.

**626.**  A municipality may by by-law or, where the law so authorizes, by ordinance Regional county municipalities shall exercise the regulatory powers provided for in this section only in regional parks. Any by-law or ordinance passed under subparagraph 14 of the first paragraph shall, within 15 days after it is passed, be sent to the Minister of Transport. The Minister of Transport may disallow all or part of the by-law or ordinance at any time. In such a case, the by-law or ordinance or the part of either that is disallowed ceases to have effect on the date a notice of disallowance is published in the Gazette officielle du Québec

**627.**  Notwithstanding any contrary or inconsistent provision of a general law or special Act, every by-law, resolution or, where the law so authorizes, every ordinance passed or issued by a municipality relating to the means or systems of vehicular transport under the jurisdiction of the Commission des transports du Québec, vehicle construction, heavy vehicle traffic, the traffic of vehicles carrying dangerous substances and the use of vehicles elsewhere than on public highways must, in order to have effect, be approved by the Minister of Transport. This section does not apply to remunerated passenger transportation by automobile governed by the Act respecting remunerated passenger transportation by automobile ( chapter T-11.2

**628.**  The Minister of Transport may approve the whole or only a part of a by-law, resolution or ordinance referred to in section 627. He may also withdraw all or part of any approval given under that section. In such a case, the by-law, resolution or ordinance or part thereof from which approval has been withdrawn ceases to have effect on the date fixed in a notice of the withdrawal of approval published in the Gazette officielle du Québec. The Minister of Transport may remove any sign or signal relating to a by-law, resolution or ordinance which he has not approved or from which he has withdrawn approval, and replace those signs or signals by signs or signals he deems appropriate.

**629.**  The Minister of Transport or the Société may, according to law, enter into an agreement with any government, department, or body respecting any matter referred to in this Code. An agreement under this section may exempt any person from the application of part of this Code. The Société shall be responsible for the implementation of such an agreement.

**630.**  An agreement under section 629 may also provide that a penalty under this Code becomes applicable in the case of an indictable offence or an offence for which a number of demerit points is prescribed by regulation on a conviction by a court of a jurisdiction that is a party to the agreement for a substantially equivalent offence. The penalty prescribed in the case of failure to pay fine following conviction for an offence under this Code may also be rendered applicable by such an agreement with respect to conviction for a substantially equivalent offence. The agreement must include descriptions of the offences and applicable penalties.

**631.**  The Government may, by regulation, adopt the necessary measures to give effect to an agreement under section 629. The publication requirement set out in section 8 of the Regulations Act ( chapter R-18.1

**632.**  Any person convicted by a court of the jurisdiction that is a party to an agreement under section 629 may apply to a judge of the Court of Québec for a ruling on the applicability of the penalty prescribed for the offence for which he was convicted. Sections 561 to 573, adapted as required, apply to an application under this section.

**633.**  The Minister of Transport may, after consultation with the Société, issue a special permit authorizing the operation of a road vehicle or combination of road vehicles to an applicant who does not meet the requirements of a regulation made under subparagraph 20 of the first paragraph of section 621, provided exceptional circumstances justify issuing the permit, issuing the permit is conducive to promoting highway transportation without compromising highway safety or issuing the permit allows If the Minister grants the permit, the Minister shall determine the conditions attached to it, the fee exigible and the amount and nature of the security guaranteeing payment of any damage that the operation of such a vehicle or combination of vehicles may cause to a public highway. The Minister may delegate the exercise of a power under this section to a public servant or an employee of the Minister’s department or to any other person or any body the Minister designates.

**634.**  The Minister of Transport may classify public highways for the purposes of this Code.

**635.**  (Repealed).

**636.**  Every peace officer recognizable as such at first sight may, in the performance of his duties under this Code, agreements entered into under section 519.65 and the Act respecting owners, operators and drivers of heavy vehicles ( chapter P-30.3

**637.**  A peace officer is authorized to confiscate and remit to the Société any unauthorized plate or unauthorized validation sticker, any plate to which is affixed an unauthorized sticker or any unauthorized inspection sticker or unauthorized identification sticker. For the purposes of the first paragraph,

**638.**  Every peace officer who, in accordance with this Code, confiscates or takes an object from its owner shall immediately inform the Société of the name and address of the person who was in possession of the object.

**639.**  If the nature of the object confiscated or taken allows it, except in the case contemplated in the second paragraph of section 252, the Société may, subject to the conditions and in the cases prescribed by regulation, return the object to its owner if he files an application therefor within 90 days after the date the object was confiscated or taken. The object is returned at the owner’s expense.

**640.**  The Société shall dispose of every object confiscated or taken at the expiry of a period 90 days following the date it was confiscated or taken.

**641.**  The public servants of the Sûreté du Québec designated by the Director General of the Sûreté du Québec to carry out the provisions of this Code are peace officers responsible for its application with respect to driving schools and the following road vehicles:

**642.**  The owner of a stolen road vehicle is required to give immediate notice of the theft of his vehicle and, as the case may be, of its recovery, to the Société. A peace officer, on being informed of the theft of a road vehicle, must do what is necessary to inform the Société.

**643.**  The owner of a road vehicle who contravenes the first paragraph of section 642 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of $100 to $200.

**644.**  Every person who makes, permits or tolerates the fraudulent use of a document issued by the Société is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of $300 to $600.

**645.**  (Repealed).

**646.**  Every driver of a heavy vehicle who contravenes a regulatory provision the violation of which constitutes an offence under subparagraph 8 of the first paragraph of section 622 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of $90 to $270, $175 to $525 or $350 to $1,050 according to the seriousness of the offence as determined by regulation. The person who offers dangerous substances for transport, the owner or operator of a heavy vehicle and the carrier of dangerous substances who contravenes a regulatory provision the violation of which constitutes an offence under subparagraph 8 of the first paragraph of section 622 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of $175 to $525, $350 to $1,050 or $700 to $2,100 according to the seriousness of the offence as determined by regulation.

**647.**  Any fine prescribed under a by-law or ordinance passed under subparagraphs 4, 5 and 8 of the first paragraph of section 626 must be equal to the fine prescribed by this Code for an offence of the same nature. The fine must be $175 to $525 where the offence prescribed by a municipal by-law made under paragraph 5 of the said section involves a truck or tool vehicle.

**648.**  The sums collected under this Code are paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund, within the time and according to the terms and conditions fixed by the Minister of Finance, except

**649.**  Every municipality is required to transmit, to the Société, within 90 days of the end of each year, a detailed report recording for the past year the accidents, within the meaning of section 167, that have occurred in its territory and the offences that entailed the collection of sums of money under paragraph 1 of section 648.

**650.**  The Minister of Transport is responsible for the carrying out of this Code, except the provisions respecting traffic supervision coming under the jurisdiction of the Minister of Public Security and the provisions respecting proceedings for offences coming under the jurisdiction of the Attorney General.

**651.**  The licences, permits, certificates and registration plates issued under the Highway Safety Code ( chapter C-24.1

**652.**  The proficiency certificates issued under the Highway Safety Code ( chapter C-24.1

**653.**  For the purposes of section 204, every person convicted of an offence under any of sections 142 to 142.3 of the Highway Safety Code ( chapter C-24.1

**654.**  Demerit points attributable to an offence committed before 1 December 1987 are counted as demerit points for the purposes of the cancellation of a licence or for a suspension of the right to obtain a licence under this Code.

**655.**  In any Act or statutory instrument, any reference to the Highway Code ( chapter C-24

**656.**  Every agreement entered into with any government, any department of such a government or any agency under the Highway Code ( chapter C-24

**657.**  The certificates of exemption for medical reasons issued under section 454 of the Highway Safety Code ( chapter C-24.1

**658.**  The provisions of Division III of Chapter II of Title VIII relating to the obligation to wear the seat belt or other safety device will apply only from the date fixed by the Government in respect of the back seat passengers of a vehicle.

**659.**  The judge of the Provincial Court who held the office of president of the Transport Tribunal on 1 June 1982 shall retain, for himself or his widow, his rights to the pension of a chief judge.

**661.**  (Amendment integrated into c. A-25, s. 1).

**662.**  (Amendment integrated into c. A-25, s. 151).

**663.**  (Amendment integrated into c. A-25, s. 195).

**664.**  (Amendment integrated into c. A-25, s. 197).

**665.**  (Amendment integrated into c. P-40.1, s. 156).

**666.**  (Amendment integrated into c. P-40.1, s. 158).

**667.**  (Amendment integrated into c. P-40.1, s. 322).

**668.**  (Amendment integrated into c. R-4, s. 2).

**669.**  (Amendment integrated into c. R-4, s. 15.1).

**670.**  (Omitted).

**671.**  (Omitted).

**672.**  Every regulation under the Highway Code ( chapter C-24

**673.**  (Omitted).

**674.**  The provisions of the Highway Code ( chapter C-24 All other provisions of the Highway Code ( chapter C-24

**675.**  Paragraphs 8 to 12 of section 618, paragraphs 10 to 16, 18 to 20 and 22 of section 619, paragraphs 1 and 2 of section 624, and sections 662 and 663 have effect from 3 September 1985.

**676.**  (Omitted).
', '{"voice": {"openai": "alloy"}, "sttLocale": "auto", "ttsService": "openai", "showAllLocaleVoice": false}', '2026-03-22 00:11:04.374+00', '2026-03-22 00:11:57.687+00', '2026-03-22 00:11:57.687+00', NULL, NULL, '{}', '', NULL, '{"root": {"id": "root", "type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9181", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9182", "mode": "normal", "text": "You are an world renowned lawyer, specializing in the analysis and evaluation of legislative texts with regard to the ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9183", "mode": "normal", "text": "Quebec Highway Safety Code", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9184", "mode": "normal", "text": ".", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "9185", "tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9186", "mode": "normal", "text": "Your role is to provide answer to user request, based on the text of the law below.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr"}, {"id": "9187", "tag": "h1", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9188", "mode": "normal", "text": "Highway Safety Code", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr"}, {"id": "9189", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9190", "mode": "normal", "text": "1.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9191", "mode": "normal", "text": " This Code governs the use of vehicles on public highways and, in specified cases, on certain private roads and lands, and pedestrian, cyclist and other road user traffic on public highways. It establishes the rules relating to highway safety, to the registration of road vehicles, to licences and permits which are under the administration of the Société de l’assurance automobile du Québec, and to the control of highway transportation of persons and goods. The provisions of this Code regarding the registration and identification of a vehicle by means of a number affixed to it apply to the vehicles referred to in the Act respecting off-highway vehicles ( chapter V-1.3 The rules set out by this Code to ensure safe vehicular traffic are also applicable to off-highway vehicles and maintenance vehicles governed by the Act respecting off-highway vehicles when such vehicles travel in those areas where the Code applies, taking into account the specific equipment and vehicle specifications, and with the other necessary modifications. In areas where this Code applies, if one of its provisions is inconsistent with a provision of the Act respecting off-highway vehicles, the more restrictive provisions to ensure public safety prevail. In particular, the lowest speed limits prevail.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9192", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9193", "mode": "normal", "text": "2.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9194", "mode": "normal", "text": " The provisions of this Code which apply to the owner of a road vehicle also apply to every person who acquires or possesses a road vehicle under a title involving a condition or a term giving him the right to become owner thereof, or under a title giving him the right to use it as owner thereof charged to deliver over. They also apply to every person who leases a road vehicle for a period of not less than one year.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9195", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9196", "mode": "normal", "text": "3.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9197", "mode": "normal", "text": " The person in whose name a road vehicle is registered is responsible for any offence imputable to the owner pursuant to this Code.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9198", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9199", "mode": "normal", "text": "4.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9200", "mode": "normal", "text": " In this Code, unless the context indicates otherwise,", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9201", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9202", "mode": "normal", "text": "6.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9203", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every road vehicle must be registered except a vehicle exempt from registration under this Code.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9204", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9205", "mode": "normal", "text": "7.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9206", "mode": "normal", "text": " The owner of a road vehicle must apply to the Société for its registration upon taking possession of it.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9207", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9208", "mode": "normal", "text": "8.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9209", "mode": "normal", "text": " The owner of a road vehicle who establishes residence in Québec must apply to the Société for its registration within 90 days thereafter.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9210", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9211", "mode": "normal", "text": "9.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9212", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société may, on such conditions as it shall establish, appoint persons authorized to collect on its behalf the sums provided for in either of sections 21 or 31.1 and to effect any transaction it shall indicate relating to registration, and fix the amount and mode of their remuneration.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9213", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9214", "mode": "normal", "text": "10.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9215", "mode": "normal", "text": " Registration is effected by entering in the register kept by the Société for that purpose such information concerning the road vehicle and its owner as is prescribed by regulation. Registration shall subsist for as long as the road vehicle and its owner remain the same.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9216", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9217", "mode": "normal", "text": "11.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9218", "mode": "normal", "text": " A “ public institution ” is an institution referred to in Schedule II to the Act respecting the governance of the health and social services system ( chapter G-1.021 ) or a public institution within the meaning of the Act respecting health services and social services for the Inuit and Naskapi ( chapter S-4.2 ) or the Act respecting health services and social services for Cree Native persons ( chapter S-5 ) that owns a motor vehicle equipped with devices to secure wheelchairs against movement. A handicapped person, Santé Québec or a public institution may be authorized to use parking spaces reserved for the exclusive use of handicapped persons and be given an identification sticker and a certificate of issue to that effect. The sticker and the certificate are issued upon payment of the fees prescribed by regulation. The Société is responsible for the application of this section according to the rules established by agreement between the Société and the Minister of Transport.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9219", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9220", "mode": "normal", "text": "12.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9221", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every registration certificate shall contain the information determined by regulation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9222", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9223", "mode": "normal", "text": "13.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9224", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9225", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9226", "mode": "normal", "text": "14.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9227", "mode": "normal", "text": " The following road vehicles are exempt from registration:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9228", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9229", "mode": "normal", "text": "15.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9230", "mode": "normal", "text": " The following road vehicles, unless used on a public highway, are exempt from registration: The exemption provided for in the first paragraph applies to vehicles referred to in subparagraphs 1 and 2, other than a trailer or semi-trailer with a net mass of less than 1,300 kg, only if the road vehicle dealer holds a permit issued under the Consumer Protection Act ( chapter P-40.1", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9231", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9232", "mode": "normal", "text": "16.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9233", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9234", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9235", "mode": "normal", "text": "17.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9236", "mode": "normal", "text": " A road vehicle the ownership of which is transferred following a death is exempt from registration if the ownership is again transferred within seven days after the heir or particular legatee obtains delivery of it or receives it in payment of his legacy.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9237", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9238", "mode": "normal", "text": "18.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9239", "mode": "normal", "text": " A trailer or semi-trailer leased for a period not exceeding 12 months is exempt from registration if the following conditions are met:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9240", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9241", "mode": "normal", "text": "19.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9242", "mode": "normal", "text": " The passenger vehicle, trailer or semi-trailer of a non-resident is exempt from registration in Québec for a period of six consecutive months from his arrival if the following conditions are met:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9243", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9244", "mode": "normal", "text": "20.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9245", "mode": "normal", "text": " A road vehicle acquired outside Québec by a foreign student, coopérant", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9246", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9247", "mode": "normal", "text": "21.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9248", "mode": "normal", "text": " To obtain the registration of a road vehicle and the right to put the vehicle into operation on a public highway, a private road open to public vehicular traffic and on land occupied by shopping centres or other land where public traffic is allowed, the owner of the vehicle must Notwithstanding the foregoing, the Société may, without further notice, prohibit such an owner from putting his vehicle into operation if he does not pay the sums referred to in paragraph 3 of the first paragraph or if he is indebted to the Société with regard to the sums referred to in section 31.1 in relation to any vehicle belonging to him or any sums referred to in either of section 69, 93.1 or 209.22. No person may put a road vehicle into operation before the sums referred to in the second paragraph have been paid by the owner or, in the case of a heavy vehicle, before the owner or operator is registered in the Registre des propriétaires et des exploitants de véhicules lourds at the Commission des transports du Québec. No person shall put a road vehicle into operation if a decision of the Société rendered under section 194 is in force. No person shall put a vehicle into operation on a public highway if it is of a model or class whose use on public highways has been prohibited by the Minister under section 633.1 or if it has been restricted to off-highway use by its manufacturer or importer. However, that prohibition does not apply to a military-type road vehicle restricted to off-highway use by its manufacturer or importer, if the vehicle meets the conditions prescribed by regulation for obtaining registration that allows travel on public highways.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9249", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9250", "mode": "normal", "text": "22.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9251", "mode": "normal", "text": " The registration of a road vehicle owned by a partnership is made in the name of the partner making the application.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9252", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9253", "mode": "normal", "text": "23.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9254", "mode": "normal", "text": " The registration of a road vehicle acquired in co-ownership is made in the name of the co-owner making the application.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9255", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9256", "mode": "normal", "text": "24.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9257", "mode": "normal", "text": " A minor applying for the registration of a road vehicle must furnish to the Société the written consent of the person having parental authority or, failing such a person, the consent of the person having legal custody of the minor. The first paragraph does not apply to a minor if he is emancipated or engaged in trade, provided that he proves his status.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9258", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9259", "mode": "normal", "text": "25.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9260", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9261", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9262", "mode": "normal", "text": "26.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9263", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société must refuse to register a road vehicle whenever the person applying for registration is unable to establish that he is the owner or joint owner of that vehicle or that the vehicle is the property of the partnership of which he is a member.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9264", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9265", "mode": "normal", "text": "27.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9266", "mode": "normal", "text": " The person in whose name registration of a road vehicle has been effected by the Société must sign the registration certificate upon receiving it. The certificate must bear the identifying mark of the Société or the signature of a person authorized by the Société.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9267", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9268", "mode": "normal", "text": "28.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9269", "mode": "normal", "text": " The person in whose name the registration of a road vehicle is effected by the Société must inform the latter, upon making payment of the amounts required to be paid under section 31.1, of any change concerning the information prescribed by regulation, and forming the registration or which appears on the registration certificate, the registration plate or the stickers. That person must also, for as long as the registration is in effect, notify the Société of any such changes within 30 days after the change.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9270", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9271", "mode": "normal", "text": "29.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9272", "mode": "normal", "text": " The owner of a road vehicle must place the temporary registration certificate issued to him in the upper left hand part of the rear window of the vehicle or in such other place as is determined by regulation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9273", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9274", "mode": "normal", "text": "30.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9275", "mode": "normal", "text": " The owner of a road vehicle must solidly attach the registration plate issued to him to the rear of the vehicle or to such other place as is determined by regulation. Where a regulation prescribes the issue of two duplicates of the registration plate, one must be attached to the front of the vehicle and the other to the rear.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9276", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9277", "mode": "normal", "text": "31.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9278", "mode": "normal", "text": " The owner of a road vehicle must place the validation stickers on the registration plate at the places determined by regulation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9279", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9280", "mode": "normal", "text": "32.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9281", "mode": "normal", "text": " No registration plate may bear any inscription other than those determined by the Société. The registration plate must be free of any object or matter that could impair its legibility; it must also, if attached to the rear of the vehicle, be sufficiently lighted.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9282", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9283", "mode": "normal", "text": "33.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9284", "mode": "normal", "text": " A peace officer may require the driver of a road vehicle to clean the registration plate of the vehicle if the presence of dirt on the plate makes it difficult to read. The driver must comply with the requirement of the peace officer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9285", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9286", "mode": "normal", "text": "34.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9287", "mode": "normal", "text": " No plate or sticker that may be confused with a registration plate or validation sticker issued by the Société or by any other competent administrative authority may be attached to a road vehicle or affixed to a plate, except in the case of a plate or sticker required under another law in force in Québec or of a plate attached in compliance with standards and conditions established under paragraph 19 of section 618.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9288", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9289", "mode": "normal", "text": "35.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9290", "mode": "normal", "text": " The person driving or having the care or control of a road vehicle must have with him the registration certificate of the vehicle or a copy of it in the form determined by regulation, except during the 10 days following registration, and the certificate of insurance provided for in the Automobile Insurance Act ( chapter A-25 If the registration certificate was issued under the International Registration Program (IRP), the person must have with him the original of the certificate, except in the cases provided for by the Program. If the road vehicle is leased for less than one year or if it has been lent by a road vehicle dealer, the person must also have with him the contract of lease or a copy thereof, or a document evidencing the duration of the loan. This section applies on private roads open to public vehicular traffic and on land occupied by shopping centres or other land where public traffic is allowed, as well as on public highways. It also applies on highways under the administration of or maintained by the Ministère des Ressources naturelles et de la Faune.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9291", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9292", "mode": "normal", "text": "36.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9293", "mode": "normal", "text": " The person driving or having the care or control of a road vehicle must remit for examination to a peace officer, at his request, the documents referred to in section 35. The peace officer must return the documents to their holder as soon as he has examined them.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9294", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9295", "mode": "normal", "text": "37.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9296", "mode": "normal", "text": " The person in whose name registration of a road vehicle has been effected by the Société must request the latter to replace any registration certificate, registration plate or sticker which is illegible, damaged or which contains inaccurate information. If the copy of the registration certificate is illegible or damaged, the person referred to in the first paragraph must make a new copy of the certificate.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9297", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9298", "mode": "normal", "text": "38.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9299", "mode": "normal", "text": " Upon proof that a registration certificate, a registration plate or a sticker is illegible or damaged or has been destroyed, lost, stolen or that it contains inaccurate information, the Société shall replace it upon payment of the fee fixed by regulation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9300", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9301", "mode": "normal", "text": "39.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9302", "mode": "normal", "text": " The transferor of a road vehicle who does not request the transfer of a registration plate to another vehicle, a person contemplated in section 10.2 or the owner of a road vehicle regarding which a decision of the Société has been rendered under any of sections 10.2, 188, or 196 to 202 must, at the request of the Société, return that vehicle’s registration certificate and plate or the detachable registration plate to the Société on the date of coming into force of the decision or on any later date fixed by the Société. The same applies where the Société acts under section 189 or where the registration plate is invalid or has not been activated in accordance with section 32.2. Where the owner refuses or fails to observe the requirement of this section, the Société may request a peace officer to confiscate the certificate and the registration plate. The owner of the vehicle must immediately remit his registration certificate and registration plate to the peace officer who requests him to do so and informs him of the reasons therefor.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9303", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9304", "mode": "normal", "text": "40.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9305", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where the right of ownership of a road vehicle is transferred between parties neither of whom is a road vehicle dealer, the transferor and the new owner must declare the transfer of ownership to the Société in the manner determined by the Société and the new owner must apply for a new registration.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9306", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9307", "mode": "normal", "text": "42.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9308", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where the right of ownership of a road vehicle is transferred to a road vehicle dealer, the transferor who is not purchasing a new vehicle must remit the registration certificate of the vehicle to the dealer after endorsing it and transmit the registration plate of the vehicle to the Société.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9309", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9310", "mode": "normal", "text": "43.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9311", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where the right of ownership of a road vehicle is transferred to a road vehicle dealer, the transferor who is purchasing a new vehicle must retain the registration plate, remit the registration certificate to the dealer after endorsing it and apply to the Société for the issue of a certificate for the new vehicle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9312", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9313", "mode": "normal", "text": "44.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9314", "mode": "normal", "text": " Sections 40 to 43 do not apply to the transfer of the right of ownership of a road vehicle that is under a contract of lease with a term of one year or more.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9315", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9316", "mode": "normal", "text": "45.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9317", "mode": "normal", "text": " The lessee of a road vehicle leased for a term of one year or more must, at the end of the contract of lease, remit the registration certificate and registration plate of the leased vehicle to the Société.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9318", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9319", "mode": "normal", "text": "46.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9320", "mode": "normal", "text": " Subject to section 17, a person who becomes the owner of a road vehicle as a result of a death, a gift, a partition, a winding-up, a bankruptcy, the exercise of a right of repossession, the complete transfer of a business or a sale under judicial authority must remit the registration certificate to the Société and apply for a new registration for the vehicle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9321", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9322", "mode": "normal", "text": "47.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9323", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9324", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9325", "mode": "normal", "text": "48.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9326", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every owner of a road vehicle who contravenes any of sections 29, 30 and 31 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9327", "code": "30 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9328", "mode": "normal", "text": "60.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9329", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9330", "mode": "normal", "text": "49.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9331", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes section 32, the second paragraph of section 33, or either of sections 35 and 37, is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9332", "code": "30 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9333", "mode": "normal", "text": "60.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9334", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9335", "mode": "normal", "text": "50.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9336", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who drives a road vehicle the registration plate of which is so damaged as to prevent the identification of the vehicle is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9337", "code": "30 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9338", "mode": "normal", "text": "60.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9339", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9340", "mode": "normal", "text": "51.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9341", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes the first paragraph of section 27, or any of sections 11.1, 28 or 40 to 46 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9342", "code": "60 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9343", "mode": "normal", "text": "100.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9344", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9345", "mode": "normal", "text": "52.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9346", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9347", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9348", "mode": "normal", "text": "53.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9349", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes the first paragraph of section 36 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9350", "code": "100 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9351", "mode": "normal", "text": "200.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9352", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9353", "mode": "normal", "text": "54.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9354", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who drives a road vehicle and every owner who allows his vehicle to be driven carrying a registration plate of a class other than the class corresponding to that vehicle, or which is being used for a purpose other than the purpose indicated in its registration, or carrying a registration plate issued for another road vehicle, is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9355", "code": "200 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9356", "mode": "normal", "text": "300.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9357", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9358", "mode": "normal", "text": "55.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9359", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every owner of a road vehicle who contravenes section 7 or section 8 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9360", "code": "200 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9361", "mode": "normal", "text": "300.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9362", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9363", "mode": "normal", "text": "56.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9364", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who drives a road vehicle carrying a plate or a sticker described in section 34 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9365", "code": "200 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9366", "mode": "normal", "text": "300.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9367", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9368", "mode": "normal", "text": "57.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9369", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes section 34, or who attaches to a road vehicle a registration plate issued for another road vehicle or affixes to a plate a validation sticker issued for another road vehicle is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9370", "code": "200 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9371", "mode": "normal", "text": "300.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9372", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9373", "mode": "normal", "text": "58.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9374", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every owner of a road vehicle who contravenes section 6 or section 39 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9375", "code": "300 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9376", "mode": "normal", "text": "600.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9377", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9378", "mode": "normal", "text": "59.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9379", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes the third, fourth or fifth paragraph of section 21, the third or fifth paragraph of section 31.1, or section 39.1, or who knowingly gives false or misleading information in applying for the registration of a road vehicle or in respect of a change referred to in section 28 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9380", "code": "300 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9381", "mode": "normal", "text": "600. Every owner of a heavy vehicle who knowingly supplies false or misleading information on applying for registration or in respect of a change referred to in section 28 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9382", "code": "500 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9383", "mode": "normal", "text": "1,500. Despite the first paragraph, if an offence under section 39.1 is committed by the owner of a road vehicle that has been put back into operation and in respect of which a decision under section 202.0.1 is in force, the owner is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9384", "code": "1,500 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9385", "mode": "normal", "text": "3,000 and, in the case of a second or subsequent offence, of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9386", "code": "3,000 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9387", "mode": "normal", "text": "6,000.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9388", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9389", "mode": "normal", "text": "60.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9390", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who makes a plate or a sticker described in section 34 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9391", "code": "600 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9392", "mode": "normal", "text": "2,000.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9393", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9394", "mode": "normal", "text": "61.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9395", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société shall issue the following licences to drive road vehicles: learner’s licences, probationary licences, driver’s licences and restricted licences. The holder of a licence cannot be required to produce his licence except where so required by a peace officer or by the Société for the purposes of highway safety.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9396", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9397", "mode": "normal", "text": "63.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9398", "mode": "normal", "text": " Licences shall contain the information prescribed by regulation and, with the exception of restricted licences, are valid for the period prescribed by regulation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9399", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9400", "mode": "normal", "text": "64.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9401", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société may attach conditions to a licence in the cases prescribed and according to the criteria established by regulation. On the request of a person who holds a licence or is applying for a licence, the Société may limit the right to drive to road vehicles equipped with an alcohol ignition interlock device approved by the Société. The licence issued and any subsequent licence are subject to that condition as long as the person has not established by means of an assessment that the person’s relationship with alcohol or drugs does not compromise the safe operation of a road vehicle. The assessment is governed by the provisions of section 76.1.9. A person who is not subject to mandatory use of an alcohol interlock device approved by the Société under this Code and does not make a request under the second paragraph may purchase any other alcohol interlock device and install such a device on the person’s vehicle without notifying the Société; in such a case, the condition set out in the second paragraph is not attached to the person’s driver’s licence, and section 64.1 does not apply.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9402", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9403", "mode": "normal", "text": "65.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9404", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may drive a road vehicle unless he holds a driver’s licence of the class appropriate to the driving of that vehicle as determined by regulation, and containing the endorsements prescribed by regulation, if any.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9405", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9406", "mode": "normal", "text": "66.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9407", "mode": "normal", "text": " A person applying for a licence to drive a road vehicle, except a licence of a class determined by regulation, must have held a learner’s licence for the period fixed by regulation. The period may vary according to the class of licence. A person applying for a licence other than a moped licence or a farm tractor licence must also have held a probationary licence for the period prescribed by regulation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9408", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9409", "mode": "normal", "text": "67.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9410", "mode": "normal", "text": " To obtain a licence, a person, unless exempted by regulation, must pass the proficiency examinations of the Société, which shall establish the formalities, procedures and content relating to each class of licence and the minimum period of time which must lapse before a person who has failed an examination may again undergo such an examination. The person must be at least 14 years of age in the case of a licence to drive a moped exclusively and 16 years of age in other cases. The Société may designate, on the conditions it determines, persons to conduct the theoretical proficiency examinations.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9411", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9412", "mode": "normal", "text": "68.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9413", "mode": "normal", "text": " A minor applying for a licence must furnish to the Société the written consent of the person having parental authority or, failing such a person, the consent of the person having legal custody of the minor. The first paragraph does not apply to a minor if he is emancipated or engaged in trade, provided that he proves his status.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9414", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9415", "mode": "normal", "text": "69.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9416", "mode": "normal", "text": " To obtain or renew a licence, a person must satisfy the conditions and comply with the formalities established by regulation, and, except in the cases prescribed by regulation, pay the Société the fees fixed by regulation. He must also, to obtain a licence, except in the cases prescribed by regulation, pay the Société the duties fixed by regulation and the insurance contribution fixed pursuant to sections 151 and 151.2 of the Automobile Insurance Act ( chapter A-25 Notwithstanding the first paragraph, where a person is applying for his learner’s licence only for the duration of the practical session of his proficiency examination, he is not required to pay the amounts prescribed in the first paragraph.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9417", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9418", "mode": "normal", "text": "70.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9419", "mode": "normal", "text": " To have the class of his licence changed or to have another class added to it, a person must meet the conditions for obtaining a licence of the class he is applying for.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9420", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9421", "mode": "normal", "text": "71.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9422", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9423", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9424", "mode": "normal", "text": "72.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9425", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9426", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9427", "mode": "normal", "text": "73.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9428", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société may require a person applying for a licence or for the renewal of a licence, to have the class of his licence changed or to have another class added to it, or to have a condition appearing on his licence removed, to undergo a medical examination or health assessment by such health professional as the Société may designate by name. The person must, where so required by the Société, submit to it a report of the examination or assessment within the time it indicates, which may in no case exceed 90 days. In addition, the Société may require that the examination or assessment be carried out in a hospital centre or in a rehabilitation centre it designates by name or that belongs to the class it specifies among the classes established under, as applicable, the Act respecting the governance of the health and social services system ( chapter G-1.021 If the assessment is carried out in a rehabilitation centre or a hospital centre offering alcohol or drug rehabilitation services, it must be carried out by persons authorized, as applicable, by Santé Québec or by the institution, other than a Santé Québec institution or an institution referred to in Schedule II to the Act respecting the governance of the health and social services system, that operates such a centre and according to the rules established by agreement between the Société and Santé Québec and, where applicable, between the Société and such an institution. The Société may also require that a person applying for the removal of a condition appearing on his licence undergo a proficiency examination. If the medical examination of a person shows that the person has a disorder related to the consumption of alcohol or if a health assessment establishes that the person’s relationship with alcohol or drugs compromises the safe operation of a road vehicle corresponding to the class of licence concerned, the person may be authorized to drive such a vehicle under a driver’s licence or a probationary licence only if the vehicle is equipped with an alcohol ignition interlock device approved by the Société.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9429", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9430", "mode": "normal", "text": "74.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9431", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9432", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9433", "mode": "normal", "text": "75.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9434", "mode": "normal", "text": " A person who has not been authorized to drive a road vehicle for three years or longer must pass the proficiency examinations prescribed by section 67 to obtain a driver’s licence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9435", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9436", "mode": "normal", "text": "76.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9437", "mode": "normal", "text": " Subject to section 76.1.1, no licence may be issued to a person whose licence has been cancelled or whose right to obtain a licence has been suspended following a conviction for an offence under the Criminal Code (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-46) listed in section 180 of this Code before a period of one, three or five years has elapsed since the date of the cancellation or suspension, depending on whether, during the 10 years before the cancellation or suspension, the person incurred no cancellation or suspension, one cancellation or suspension or two or more cancellations or suspensions under that section. If the conviction is followed by an order prohibiting the offender from operating a road vehicle under Part VIII.1 of the Criminal Code on offences relating to conveyances for a longer period than the period applicable under the first paragraph, the period prescribed in the order is the applicable period.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9438", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9439", "mode": "normal", "text": "77.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9440", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9441", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9442", "mode": "normal", "text": "79.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9443", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9444", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9445", "mode": "normal", "text": "80.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9446", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9447", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9448", "mode": "normal", "text": "81.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9449", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société may refuse to issue a licence or to change the class of or add another class to a licence if the applicant", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9450", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9451", "mode": "normal", "text": "82.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9452", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société may refuse to remove a condition appearing on a licence if the holder", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9453", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9454", "mode": "normal", "text": "83.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9455", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société must refuse to issue a licence or to change the class of or add another class to a licence if the applicant", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9456", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9457", "mode": "normal", "text": "84.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9458", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9459", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9460", "mode": "normal", "text": "85.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9461", "mode": "normal", "text": " A non-resident may drive a road vehicle for a period of not over six consecutive months without holding a licence issued by the Société if he meets the following requirements:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9462", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9463", "mode": "normal", "text": "86.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9464", "mode": "normal", "text": " A foreign student, coopérant", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9465", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9466", "mode": "normal", "text": "87.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9467", "mode": "normal", "text": " A non-resident whose main occupation is driving a road vehicle and who drives a road vehicle in Québec is exempt from the obligation of obtaining a licence from the Société if he holds a valid driver’s licence issued by another administrative authority authorizing him to drive the road vehicle that he is driving in Québec.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9468", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9469", "mode": "normal", "text": "88.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9470", "mode": "normal", "text": " Notwithstanding sections 85 and 86, a non-resident holding an International Driver’s Permit may, while it is valid, drive the road vehicles he is authorized to drive by the licence on the basis of which the International Driver’s Permit was issued to him.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9471", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9472", "mode": "normal", "text": "89.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9473", "mode": "normal", "text": " A person holding a valid driver’s licence issued by another administrative authority may, during the six months after settling in Québec, drive a passenger vehicle in Québec without obtaining a licence from the Société.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9474", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9475", "mode": "normal", "text": "90.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9476", "mode": "normal", "text": " A person holding a valid driver’s licence issued in Canada by another administrative authority may, if he settles in Québec, exchange that licence, without an examination, for a driver’s licence issued by the Société, on payment of the duties and fee prescribed by regulation and the amount fixed under section 151 of the Automobile Insurance Act ( chapter A-25 Any person whose driver’s licence issued in Canada has been expired for less than three years and who settles in Québec may obtain a driver’s licence from the Société without undergoing an examination, on payment of the amounts prescribed in the first paragraph. Notwithstanding the foregoing, the Société may require that the person referred to in the first paragraph or in the second paragraph undergo an examination to obtain a licence authorizing him to drive a commercial vehicle, an emergency vehicle, a bus or a minibus. The Société may also require that the person undergo the training referred to in section 66.1 to obtain such a licence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9477", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9478", "mode": "normal", "text": "91.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9479", "mode": "normal", "text": " Any person holding a driver’s licence issued outside Canada who settles in Québec may on request, provided the particulars and validity of the holder’s title can be verified directly with the administrative authority concerned through the use of information technology, exchange that licence, without undergoing a proficiency examination, for an equivalent driver’s licence issued by the Société. Any person whose driver’s licence issued outside Canada has been expired for less than three years and who settles in Québec may obtain a driver’s licence without undergoing a proficiency examination provided the particulars and the validity of the person’s title can be established in accordance with the first paragraph. However, the person must pass the proficiency examinations referred to in section 67 to obtain a licence to drive a bus, a minibus, a motorcycle or a commercial vehicle or to operate an emergency vehicle. The Société may also require that the person undergo the training referred to in section 66.1 to obtain such a licence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9480", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9481", "mode": "normal", "text": "92.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9482", "mode": "normal", "text": " For the duration of their assignment, the following persons may, without an examination and without paying the duties fixed by regulation, obtain a driver’s licence: Those persons must meet the following conditions: Despite the first paragraph, a member of the service staff of a diplomatic mission or consular post referred to in subparagraph 1 of the first paragraph or a member of the service staff of a permanent representation referred to in subparagraph 2 of that paragraph is not exempt from paying the duties fixed by regulation. The same applies to his spouse and his children of full age who are financially dependent on him and reside with him.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9483", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9484", "mode": "normal", "text": "93.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9485", "mode": "normal", "text": " A licence issued in paper form must be signed by the holder. All licences must bear the identifying mark of the Société or the signature of a person authorized by the Société.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9486", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9487", "mode": "normal", "text": "94.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9488", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may hold more than one learner’s licence, more than one probationary licence or more than one driver’s licence of the same class issued by the Société. No person may at the same time hold a learner’s licence and a probationary licence of the same class issued by the Société. No person may at the same time hold a learner’s licence and a driver’s licence of the same class issued by the Société. No person may at the same time hold a probationary licence and a driver’s licence of the same class issued by the Société. Except in the cases and on the conditions prescribed by regulation,", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9489", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9490", "mode": "normal", "text": "95.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9491", "mode": "normal", "text": " The holder of a licence must inform the Société, on making payment of amounts required to be paid under section 93.1, of any change concerning the documents and information which must be provided on obtaining or renewing a licence. He must also inform the Société of any such changes within 30 days after the change.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9492", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9493", "mode": "normal", "text": "96.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9494", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may permit the use of his licence by another person. No person may use a licence issued to another person.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9495", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9496", "mode": "normal", "text": "97.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9497", "mode": "normal", "text": " The person driving a road vehicle or having the care or control of a road vehicle must carry his licence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9498", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9499", "mode": "normal", "text": "98.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9500", "mode": "normal", "text": " The holder of a licence must comply with the conditions attached to his licence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9501", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9502", "mode": "normal", "text": "99.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9503", "mode": "normal", "text": " The holder of a learner’s licence must, when driving a road vehicle other than a moped or a motorcycle, be assisted by a person who has held, for at least two years, a valid driver’s licence of the appropriate class for driving that vehicle. The person must be seated beside the holder of the learner’s licence, and be in a position to give him assistance and advice. The person assisting the holder of the learner’s licence must carry his driver’s licence with him, which must contain, where applicable, the endorsements prescribed by regulation. Holders of a class 5 or class 6A learner’s licence, as determined by regulation, are prohibited from driving a road vehicle covered by either class between midnight and 5 a.m. The holder of a learner’s licence driving a motorcycle may not carry passengers. A government regulation may, in the cases and on the conditions it determines, exempt the holder of a learner’s licence from the assistance conditions set out in the first paragraph or prescribe different conditions.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9504", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9505", "mode": "normal", "text": "100.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9506", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle who holds a class 5 probationary licence, as determined by regulation, and who is 19 years of age or younger is subject to the following rules in the year after the licence is issued: The rules set out in the first paragraph do not apply if one of the passengers has held, for at least two years, a valid driver’s licence of the appropriate class for driving the vehicle, is seated beside the driver and is in a position to give the driver assistance and advice. For the purposes of the first paragraph, a passenger who is a member of the driver’s immediate family is not taken into account in the computation of the number of passengers. “Driver’s immediate family” means A peace officer who has reasonable grounds to suspect that a driver is contravening this section may ask a passenger to identify himself or herself, in which case the passenger shall give the peace officer the following information, which the passenger may provide verbally:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9507", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9508", "mode": "normal", "text": "101.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9509", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9510", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9511", "mode": "normal", "text": "102.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9512", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person referred to in sections 97, 99 and 100 must surrender his licence for inspection at the request of a peace officer. The peace officer must return the licence to its holder as soon as he has inspected it.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9513", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9514", "mode": "normal", "text": "103.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9515", "mode": "normal", "text": " The holder of an illegible or damaged licence or of a licence containing inaccurate information shall request the Société to replace it.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9516", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9517", "mode": "normal", "text": "104.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9518", "mode": "normal", "text": " Upon proof that a licence is illegible or damaged or has been destroyed, lost or stolen or that it contains false information, the Société shall replace it upon payment of the fee fixed by regulation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9519", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9520", "mode": "normal", "text": "105.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9521", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person under a sanction may drive a road vehicle even if he holds a valid driver’s licence issued by another administrative authority or an International Driver’s Permit. However, the holder of a restricted licence may, subject to section 195.1, drive a road vehicle to carry on his principal means of livelihood.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9522", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9523", "mode": "normal", "text": "106.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9524", "mode": "normal", "text": " The owner or lessee of a road vehicle or the person having the control of a road vehicle may not allow the vehicle to be driven by a person who is not the holder of a licence of the appropriate class for driving the vehicle or by a person under a sanction, even if the latter is the holder of a valid driver’s licence issued by another administrative authority or of an International Driver’s Permit. However, he may allow the latter to drive the vehicle if that person is, subject to section 195.1, the holder of a restricted licence and drives the vehicle to carry on his principal means of livelihood.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9525", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9526", "mode": "normal", "text": "107.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9527", "mode": "normal", "text": " A person whose licence or a class thereof has been suspended or cancelled must, at the request of the Société, return his licence to the Société on the date the suspension or cancellation takes effect or on any later date fixed by the Société. The Société may request a peace officer to confiscate the licence of any person who refuses or omits to comply with that requirement. The person must immediately remit his licence to the peace officer who requests him to do so and informs him of the reasons therefor. The Société may also require the surrender of any other licence issued by another administrative authority.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9528", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9529", "mode": "normal", "text": "108.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9530", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société shall advise the holder of a licence whose classes or conditions do not correspond to those fixed in his regard that he must have the licence replaced within the time indicated by the Société. The replacement is, in the cases determined by regulation, subject to the payment of the fees fixed by regulation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9531", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9532", "mode": "normal", "text": "109.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9533", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société may require the holder of a licence to undergo an examination or assessment referred to in section 67 or 73 where", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9534", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9535", "mode": "normal", "text": "110.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9536", "mode": "normal", "text": " This division applies to every person, except a cyclist or pedestrian, who is convicted of an offence for which demerit points are prescribed, including a person deemed to be convicted of such an offence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9537", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9538", "mode": "normal", "text": "111.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9539", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société shall administer a system of demerit points prescribed by regulation, under which the cancellation of a licence or the suspension of the right to obtain a licence may be incurred. Demerit points shall be prescribed", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9540", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9541", "mode": "normal", "text": "112.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9542", "mode": "normal", "text": " The collector of fines, the clerk of a court, the clerk, secretary or clerk-treasurer of a municipality, the Director of Criminal and Penal Prosecutions or the director of a police department, as the case may be, shall inform the Société of any conviction in respect of which demerit points are prescribed. The same applies to a person who accepts payment for an offence which, under this Code, entails the entry of demerit points.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9543", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9544", "mode": "normal", "text": "113.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9545", "mode": "normal", "text": " Upon being informed of a conviction in accordance with section 112 or from the time it is in possession of such a judgment or proof thereof, the Société shall open a file, which it shall keep up to date, and enter therein the number of demerit points which corresponds to the offence committed.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9546", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9547", "mode": "normal", "text": "114.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9548", "mode": "normal", "text": " As soon as the total number of demerit points entered in a person’s file attains the prescribed number, the Société shall send a notice to the person concerned, at the last address received by the Société, informing him of the number of points entered in his file and reminding him of its powers of cancellation and suspension.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9549", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9550", "mode": "normal", "text": "115.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9551", "mode": "normal", "text": " Failure by the Société to give the notice referred to in section 114 does not nullify a notice given subsequently nor does it prevent the Société from subsequently exercising any power or duty under this division, under Chapter III and under Title V.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9552", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9553", "mode": "normal", "text": "116.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9554", "mode": "normal", "text": " The number of demerit points entered by the Société in a person’s file becomes nil two years from the date of the judgment of conviction.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9555", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9556", "mode": "normal", "text": "117.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9557", "mode": "normal", "text": " Whenever the Société renders a decision under section 185 or 191.2, it shall remove, in the file of the person concerned, a number of points equal to the number that justified the decision; the points most recently entered that are in excess of that number remain in the file, unless the excess number of points is equal to or higher than the number of points entailing the application of one of those sections, in which case it is brought down to the number that is one less than the number entailing a sanction.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9558", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9559", "mode": "normal", "text": "118.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9560", "mode": "normal", "text": " A restricted licence may be issued by the Société to a person whose driver’s licence has been cancelled under section 185 or whose probationary licence has been cancelled under section 191.2, by order of a judge of the Court of Québec, if the person proves to the judge that he must drive a road vehicle to carry on his principal means of livelihood.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9561", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9562", "mode": "normal", "text": "119.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9563", "mode": "normal", "text": " The order directing that a restricted licence be issued falls within the jurisdiction of a judge in chambers and must be applied for to the court of the domicile or establishment of the applicant and served on the Société at least ten days before the date fixed for its presentation. The clerk and the clerk’s staff must assist the person in the drafting of the application if he so requests.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9564", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9565", "mode": "normal", "text": "120.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9566", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where an application is served on it pursuant to section 119, the Société shall transmit to the court, before the date fixed for the presentation of the application, any information held by it in respect of the applicant regarding the application of section 121.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9567", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9568", "mode": "normal", "text": "121.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9569", "mode": "normal", "text": " No order directing that a restricted licence be issued may be given nor any restricted licence issued if For the purposes of subparagraph 1 of the first paragraph, the two-year period before the cancellation or suspension includes the day on which the sanction is imposed.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9570", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9571", "mode": "normal", "text": "122.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9572", "mode": "normal", "text": " A restricted licence is valid from the date of its issue to the date of the end of the period which follows the cancellation giving rise to the issue of the restricted licence and during which its holder is not entitled to obtain a new driver’s licence or probationary licence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9573", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9574", "mode": "normal", "text": "123.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9575", "mode": "normal", "text": " A decision rendered pursuant to sections 118 to 121 is final and without appeal.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9576", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9577", "mode": "normal", "text": "124.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9578", "mode": "normal", "text": " If, when an order directing that a restricted licence be issued is received by the Société, section 121 is applicable to the person referred to in the order, or if, between the date fixed for presenting his application and the date of issue of the restricted licence, the person’s right to obtain a licence is under a suspension which is in effect or imposed but has yet to take effect, the Société must so inform the judge who made the order. The judge may then revise his order after giving the applicant the opportunity of presenting his views.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9579", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9580", "mode": "normal", "text": "125.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9581", "mode": "normal", "text": " The holder of a restricted licence who drives a road vehicle otherwise than to carry on his principal means of livelihood is presumed to be driving while his licence is cancelled or suspended within the meaning of section 105.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9582", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9583", "mode": "normal", "text": "126.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9584", "mode": "normal", "text": " Sections 69, 93, 95 to 98 and 102 to 104 apply, adapted as required, to a restricted licence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9585", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9586", "mode": "normal", "text": "127.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9587", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9588", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9589", "mode": "normal", "text": "128.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9590", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9591", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9592", "mode": "normal", "text": "129.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9593", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9594", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9595", "mode": "normal", "text": "130.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9596", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9597", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9598", "mode": "normal", "text": "131.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9599", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9600", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9601", "mode": "normal", "text": "132.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9602", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9603", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9604", "mode": "normal", "text": "133.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9605", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9606", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9607", "mode": "normal", "text": "134.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9608", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9609", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9610", "mode": "normal", "text": "135.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9611", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9612", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9613", "mode": "normal", "text": "136.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9614", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9615", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9616", "mode": "normal", "text": "137.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9617", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes section 97 or section 103 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9618", "code": "30 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9619", "mode": "normal", "text": "60.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9620", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9621", "mode": "normal", "text": "138.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9622", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes the first paragraph of section 93 or section 95 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9623", "code": "60 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9624", "mode": "normal", "text": "100.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9625", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9626", "mode": "normal", "text": "139.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9627", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes the first paragraph of section 102 or fails to comply with a condition attached to the person’s licence under section 98, other than the operation of a road vehicle mandatorily equipped with an alcohol ignition interlock device or the conditions for its use, is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9628", "code": "100 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9629", "mode": "normal", "text": "200. The holder of a licence to drive a road vehicle mandatorily equipped with an alcohol ignition interlock device who fails to comply with that requirement or with the conditions for the use of the device is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9630", "code": "1,500 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9631", "mode": "normal", "text": "3,000.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9632", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9633", "mode": "normal", "text": "140.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9634", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes section 96 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9635", "code": "200 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9636", "mode": "normal", "text": "300.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9637", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9638", "mode": "normal", "text": "141.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9639", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes any of sections 65, 95.1, 107 or drives a road vehicle in violation of the first paragraph of section 93.1 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9640", "code": "300 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9641", "mode": "normal", "text": "600. Despite the first paragraph, a person who, after a period of licence cancellation or suspension of the right to obtain a licence for an alcohol- or drug-related offence under section 180, operates a road vehicle without holding a licence is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9642", "code": "1,500 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9643", "mode": "normal", "text": "3,000.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9644", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9645", "mode": "normal", "text": "142.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9646", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who knowingly gives false or misleading information when applying for a licence or when notifying any change referred to in section 95 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9647", "code": "300 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9648", "mode": "normal", "text": "600.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9649", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9650", "mode": "normal", "text": "143.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9651", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes the first paragraph of section 105 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9652", "code": "300 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9653", "mode": "normal", "text": "600 if his licence or right to obtain a licence is cancelled or suspended for a cause other than those referred to in section 180, 185, 191.2, 202.4, 202.4.1 or 202.5.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9654", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9655", "mode": "normal", "text": "144.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9656", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes the first paragraph of section 105 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9657", "code": "1,500 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9658", "mode": "normal", "text": "3,000, if his licence or right to obtain a licence is cancelled or suspended under section 180, subparagraph 1 of the first paragraph of section 202.4, subparagraph 1 of the first paragraph of section 202.4.1 or section 202.5.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9659", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9660", "mode": "normal", "text": "145.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9661", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes section 106 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9662", "code": "300 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9663", "mode": "normal", "text": "600 if the driver of the vehicle is liable to the fine prescribed by section 143, ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9664", "code": "600 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9665", "mode": "normal", "text": "2,000 if the driver of the vehicle is liable to the fine prescribed by section 143.1, and ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9666", "code": "1,500 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9667", "mode": "normal", "text": "3,000 if the driver of the vehicle is liable to the fine prescribed by section 144. Every operator of a heavy vehicle whose driver is liable to a fine under the first paragraph is also guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9668", "code": "700 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9669", "mode": "normal", "text": "2,100.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9670", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9671", "mode": "normal", "text": "146.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9672", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who uses as a document authorizing the driving of road vehicles a document that may be confused with a licence issued by the Société or by another competent administrative authority is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9673", "code": "600 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9674", "mode": "normal", "text": "2,000.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9675", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9676", "mode": "normal", "text": "147.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9677", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9678", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9679", "mode": "normal", "text": "148.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9680", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9681", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9682", "mode": "normal", "text": "149.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9683", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9684", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9685", "mode": "normal", "text": "150.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9686", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9687", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9688", "mode": "normal", "text": "151.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9689", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9690", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9691", "mode": "normal", "text": "152.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9692", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9693", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9694", "mode": "normal", "text": "153.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9695", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9696", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9697", "mode": "normal", "text": "154.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9698", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9699", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9700", "mode": "normal", "text": "155.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9701", "mode": "normal", "text": " For the purposes of this section, “ major component ” means a major component determined by regulation. Every recycler must keep a register the form and period of retention of which are prescribed by regulation and in which the following information is entered:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9702", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9703", "mode": "normal", "text": "156.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9704", "mode": "normal", "text": " A peace officer or an employee of the Société designated for that purpose may enter, at any reasonable time, any establishment of a road vehicle recycler in order to require any information relating to the enforcement of section 155 and any related document, and examine and make copies of any such document. The officer or employee may also examine the road vehicles and major components in the recycler’s possession. Société employees must identify themselves and show proof of their capacity.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9705", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9706", "mode": "normal", "text": "157.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9707", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9708", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9709", "mode": "normal", "text": "158.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9710", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9711", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9712", "mode": "normal", "text": "159.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9713", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9714", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9715", "mode": "normal", "text": "160.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9716", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9717", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9718", "mode": "normal", "text": "161.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9719", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9720", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9721", "mode": "normal", "text": "162.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9722", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9723", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9724", "mode": "normal", "text": "163.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9725", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9726", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9727", "mode": "normal", "text": "164.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9728", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9729", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9730", "mode": "normal", "text": "165.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9731", "mode": "normal", "text": " A recycler who fails to keep the register required by section 155 or who fails to enter the information required under that section is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9732", "code": "600 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9733", "mode": "normal", "text": "2,000.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9734", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9735", "mode": "normal", "text": "166.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9736", "mode": "normal", "text": " A road vehicle dealer who contravenes section 161.1 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9737", "code": "600 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9738", "mode": "normal", "text": "2,000.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9739", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9740", "mode": "normal", "text": "167.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9741", "mode": "normal", "text": " For the purposes of this Title, an accident is an event during which injury or damage is caused by a moving road vehicle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9742", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9743", "mode": "normal", "text": "168.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9744", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle involved in an accident must remain at or immediately return to the scene of the accident and render the necessary assistance to any person who has sustained injury or damage.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9745", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9746", "mode": "normal", "text": "169.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9747", "mode": "normal", "text": " If a person has sustained bodily injury during an accident, the driver of a road vehicle involved in the accident must call for a peace officer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9748", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9749", "mode": "normal", "text": "170.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9750", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle involved in an accident must give to the peace officer called to the scene of the accident or to the person having sustained injury or damage, his name and address, the number of his licence, the name and address of the owner entered on the registration certificate of the vehicle, the certificate of insurance or of financial responsibility provided for in the Automobile Insurance Act ( chapter A-25", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9751", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9752", "mode": "normal", "text": "171.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9753", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle who is involved in an accident involving an animal weighing over 25 kg, an unattended road vehicle or any other inanimate object must, if the owner of the damaged property or a person representing him cannot be found at the scene of the accident or nearby, communicate immediately with the nearest police station to report the accident and furnish the information provided for in section 170.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9754", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9755", "mode": "normal", "text": "172.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9756", "mode": "normal", "text": " The owner of a road vehicle that has been totally destroyed as the result of an accident must, without delay, notify the Société that his vehicle has been destroyed.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9757", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9758", "mode": "normal", "text": "173.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9759", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every peace officer who is called to the scene of an accident must inform the Société of the accident within eight days by means of a report the form, content and mode of transmission of which are determined by regulation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9760", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9761", "mode": "normal", "text": "174.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9762", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where an accident is not brought to the attention of a peace officer, the obligation to inform the Société of the accident is incumbent on the insurer who is notified of it.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9763", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9764", "mode": "normal", "text": "175.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9765", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every coroner who has conducted an investigation or an inquest into an accident must send a copy of his report to the Société.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9766", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9767", "mode": "normal", "text": "176.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9768", "mode": "normal", "text": " Except in the cases provided for by regulation, a peace officer or an insurer is not required to make a report to the Société in respect of an accident that caused property damage only and did not give rise to a failure to stop at the scene of an accident.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9769", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9770", "mode": "normal", "text": "177.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9771", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes section 172 or 174 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9772", "code": "100 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9773", "mode": "normal", "text": "200.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9774", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9775", "mode": "normal", "text": "178.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9776", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes section 170 or 171 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9777", "code": "200 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9778", "mode": "normal", "text": "300.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9779", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9780", "mode": "normal", "text": "179.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9781", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes section 168 or 169 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "9782", "code": "600 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "9783", "mode": "normal", "text": "2,000.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9784", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9785", "mode": "normal", "text": "180.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9786", "mode": "normal", "text": " A conviction for an offence under any of the following provisions of the Criminal Code (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-46) committed with a road vehicle or an off-highway vehicle entails by operation of law the cancellation of any licence to drive a road vehicle or the suspension of the right to obtain such a licence: The convicting judge must order the confiscation of the licence referred to in the first paragraph so that it may be returned to the Société.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9787", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9788", "mode": "normal", "text": "181.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9789", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every conviction for an offence referred to in section 180 entails a separate and distinct licence cancellation or suspension of the right to obtain a licence. Notwithstanding the first paragraph, a conviction for more than one offence under section 320.14 or 320.15 of the Criminal Code (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-46) shall entail only one licence cancellation or only one suspension of the right to obtain a licence where the offences are related to the same event.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9790", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9791", "mode": "normal", "text": "182.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9792", "mode": "normal", "text": " The cancellation of a licence or the suspension of the right to obtain a licence provided for in section 181 shall be maintained even if the person convicted of an indictable offence is granted a conditional or absolute discharge.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9793", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9794", "mode": "normal", "text": "185.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9795", "mode": "normal", "text": " When the total number of demerit points entered in a person’s record is equal to or greater than the number prescribed by regulation under paragraph 9 of section 619, the Société cancels the person’s driver’s licence or suspends the person’s right to obtain a licence. The number of demerit points prescribed by regulation varies depending on whether the person is If the number of demerit points entered in the person’s record is equal to or greater than the number prescribed by regulation but less than twice that number, no licence may be issued to the person If the number of demerit points entered in the person’s record is equal to or greater than twice the number prescribed by regulation but less than three times that number, no licence may be issued to the person before six or twelve months have elapsed, depending on whether the person incurred no cancellation or suspension or one or more cancellations or suspensions under section 191.2 or this section during the two years before the cancellation or suspension under the first paragraph. If the number of demerit points entered in the person’s record is equal to or greater than three times the number prescribed by regulation, no licence may be issued to the person before twelve months have elapsed. For the purposes of this section, the two-year period before the cancellation or suspension includes the day the sanction is imposed. When a person holds a driver’s licence and a learner’s licence, the cancellation under this section applies to both licences.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9796", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9797", "mode": "normal", "text": "186.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9798", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9799", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9800", "mode": "normal", "text": "187.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9801", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9802", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9803", "mode": "normal", "text": "188.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9804", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société may prohibit a road vehicle from being put back into operation in cases where", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9805", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9806", "mode": "normal", "text": "189.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9807", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société must prohibit a road vehicle from being put back into operation in the following cases: The Société must also prohibit an off-highway vehicle from being put back into operation upon receiving the notice referred to in section 127 of the Act respecting off-highway vehicles ( chapter V-1.3", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9808", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9809", "mode": "normal", "text": "190.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9810", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société may suspend a learner’s licence and probationary licence or a driver’s licence or a class of any or several such licences where", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9811", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9812", "mode": "normal", "text": "191.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9813", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société must suspend a learner’s licence and probationary licence or a driver’s licence or a class of any or several such licences where, according to a report of an examination or assessment carried out under section 64, 73, 76.1.2, 76.1.4 or 76.1.4.1 or a report referred to in section 603, the licence holder suffers from an illness or deficiency or is in a condition which, under the medical or health standards established by regulation, is essentially inconsistent with the driving of a road vehicle corresponding to one of those licences or one of the classes of licence that he holds.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9814", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9815", "mode": "normal", "text": "192.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9816", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where the Société receives the notice provided for in the first paragraph of section 54.1 of the Act to facilitate the payment of support ( chapter P-2.2 The Société lifts the suspension of the licence or of the right to obtain a licence on the working day following receipt of the notice provided for in the third paragraph of section 54.1 of the Act to facilitate the payment of support. The minister responsible for the administration of the Act to facilitate the payment of support and the Société enter into an agreement with respect to the reimbursement of expenses incurred for the purposes of this section.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9817", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9818", "mode": "normal", "text": "193.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9819", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9820", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9821", "mode": "normal", "text": "194.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9822", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where the Société receives the notice provided for in article 364 of the Code of Penal Procedure ( chapter C‐25.1 The measures provided for in subparagraphs 3, 4 and 5 of the first paragraph take effect on receipt by the Société of the notice provided for in article 364 of that Code. The Société shall put an end to the application of the measures provided for in the first paragraph on the working day following receipt of the notice provided for in article 365 of that Code.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9823", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9824", "mode": "normal", "text": "195.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9825", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where the term of validity of a licence expires before the end of a period of suspension affecting that licence, the right to obtain a licence is then suspended for the unexpired portion of the period of suspension.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9826", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9827", "mode": "normal", "text": "196.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9828", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where the Société is informed that damage amounting to over $500 has been caused in an accident and it is not shown to its satisfaction that the owner of a road vehicle involved in the accident held, at the time of the accident, a liability insurance contract as required under the Automobile Insurance Act ( chapter A-25 A suspension under the first paragraph must not be imposed or must be cancelled or the prohibition from putting a road vehicle back into operation must not be imposed or must be cancelled where it is shown to the satisfaction of the Société that at the time of the accident, the uninsured vehicle was legally parked, in the possession of a third person who had acquired it by theft or taken it without permission, or in the possession of a third person for storage, repair or transportation or that only the uninsured vehicle or the movable effects it contained sustained damage in the accident. With respect to the driver and to the owner, a suspension under the first paragraph must not be imposed or must be cancelled or the prohibition from putting a road vehicle back into operation must not be imposed or must be cancelled where it is shown to the satisfaction of the Société that at the time of the accident, the driver was the owner of a road vehicle covered by a contract of liability insurance as required under the Automobile Insurance Act.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9829", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9830", "mode": "normal", "text": "197.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9831", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société shall lift the suspension imposed on a person referred to in section 196 and the prohibition from putting any road vehicle registered in the person’s name back into operation if the person provides the Société with proof of exoneration, acquittal or payment agreement in respect of any claim arising or that may arise from the accident. Where the creditor who is party to the agreement contemplated in the first paragraph notifies the Société that payment by the debtor has been interrupted, the Société must reinstate the suspension and prohibition it had lifted following the agreement.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9832", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9833", "mode": "normal", "text": "198.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9834", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9835", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9836", "mode": "normal", "text": "199.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9837", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9838", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9839", "mode": "normal", "text": "200.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9840", "mode": "normal", "text": " Upon receiving a notice to that effect from the creditor concerned, the Société shall suspend the learner’s licence and probationary licence or the driver’s licence or the right to obtain such licences and shall prohibit the putting back into operation of the road vehicle registered in the name of a debtor who has not, within the time prescribed for execution, satisfied a final judgment handed down in Canada", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9841", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9842", "mode": "normal", "text": "201.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9843", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société shall lift the suspension imposed on any person referred to in section 200 and the prohibition from putting back into operation a road vehicle registered in his name in the following cases: In the case referred to in subparagraph 3, the Société, on receiving notice from the creditor that payment by the debtor has been interrupted, shall reinstate the suspension it had lifted following the agreement.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9844", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9845", "mode": "normal", "text": "202.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9846", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where the Société has effected a payment in satisfaction of a judgment, it shall lift the suspension imposed upon any person referred to in section 200 and the prohibition from putting back into operation the road vehicle registered in such a person’s name in the following cases: In the case referred to in subparagraph 2, the Société shall reinstate the suspension and prohibition that it had lifted following the agreement if the person interrupts payment.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9847", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9848", "mode": "normal", "text": "203.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9849", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9850", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9851", "mode": "normal", "text": "204.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9852", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9853", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9854", "mode": "normal", "text": "205.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9855", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9856", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9857", "mode": "normal", "text": "206.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9858", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9859", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9860", "mode": "normal", "text": "207.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9861", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9862", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9863", "mode": "normal", "text": "208.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9864", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9865", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9866", "mode": "normal", "text": "209.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9867", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9868", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9869", "mode": "normal", "text": "210.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9870", "mode": "normal", "text": " Road vehicles and bicycles must be provided with an identification number affixed by the manufacturer, who must communicate to the Société the components of the numbers affixed to road vehicles. However, trailers and semi-trailers whose net mass does not exceed 900 kg and detachable axles are not required to be provided with such a number. The Société may also affix an identification number to a road vehicle on payment of the fee and on the conditions established by regulation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9871", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9872", "mode": "normal", "text": "211.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9873", "mode": "normal", "text": " Except with prior approval from the Société, no person may alter, make illegible, erase, replace or remove the identification number of a road vehicle or bicycle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9874", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9875", "mode": "normal", "text": "212.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9876", "mode": "normal", "text": " In addition to the equipment prescribed in this Title, road vehicles and bicycles must be equipped with any other accessory and equipment required to be installed by the manufacturer under an Act or a regulation in force in Québec.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9877", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9878", "mode": "normal", "text": "213.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9879", "mode": "normal", "text": " All equipment prescribed in this Code must be kept in good working order at all times. This section applies, in addition to public highways, to highways under the administration of or maintained by the Ministère des Ressources naturelles et de la Faune, to private roads open to public vehicular traffic as well as land occupied by shopping centres and other land where public traffic is allowed.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9880", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9881", "mode": "normal", "text": "214.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9882", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may put any of the following vehicles into operation: Despite the first paragraph, vehicles described in that paragraph may be put into operation if they have first undergone an inspection of the alterations made or, in the case of a vehicle made by hand, of its components and their assembly. For that purpose, the Société may also require any information that is necessary to determine whether the vehicle is safe. The inspection shall be carried out before the mechanical inspection prescribed by subparagraph 8 of the first paragraph of section 521. The Société shall issue an inspection certificate when it is proved to the Société’s satisfaction that the vehicle is safe. The inspection prescribed by this section however is not required if the Société considers that the safety of road users is not compromised. The Société has exclusive jurisdiction to carry out the inspection of altered vehicles or vehicles made by hand and to issue inspection certificates. The Société may, however, on the conditions it determines, appoint persons authorized to carry out the inspection of such vehicles on its behalf.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9883", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9884", "mode": "normal", "text": "215.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9885", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every motor vehicle, other than a motorcycle or a moped, must carry at least In the case of a combination of road vehicles, the lights prescribed in subparagraphs 3, 3.1, 4, 6 and 10 of the first paragraph must be mounted at the rear of the last vehicle. The lights referred to in subparagraph 2 of the first paragraph are not required on any vehicle exceeding 2.03 metres in width.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9886", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9887", "mode": "normal", "text": "216.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9888", "mode": "normal", "text": " In addition to the lights prescribed in section 215, every motor vehicle, other than a passenger vehicle, measuring at any point more than 2.03 metres in width must carry, Where the identification lights prescribed in subparagraph 5 of the first paragraph are mounted at the very top of the vehicle, the clearance lights prescribed in subparagraph 2 of the first paragraph need not be mounted at the prescribed height.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9889", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9890", "mode": "normal", "text": "217.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9891", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9892", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9893", "mode": "normal", "text": "218.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9894", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9895", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9896", "mode": "normal", "text": "219.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9897", "mode": "normal", "text": " The three red identification lights and the two red reflectors of a motor vehicle or of a combination of road vehicles whose only superstructure is the driver’s cab must be grouped in a horizontal row at the rear of the platform or between the two trail-lights required for all vehicles.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9898", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9899", "mode": "normal", "text": "220.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9900", "mode": "normal", "text": " In addition to the lights and reflectors prescribed in sections 215 and 216, every trailer or semi-trailer must carry one red side marker lamp on each side and as far to the rear as practicable. It must also carry", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9901", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9902", "mode": "normal", "text": "221.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9903", "mode": "normal", "text": " In addition to the lights prescribed in section 215, every passenger vehicle, other than a motorcycle or a moped, and every other vehicle of the same configuration manufactured from 1 January 1987 must be equipped with a red stop light at the rear, on the vertical centreline, at the same height as or higher than the stop lights prescribed in paragraph 4 of section 215.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9904", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9905", "mode": "normal", "text": "222.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9906", "mode": "normal", "text": " The fog lights that may be mounted on a road vehicle must conform to the standards established by regulation and must be on the front of the vehicle and at the same height, which must not be higher than that of the white headlights.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9907", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9908", "mode": "normal", "text": "223.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9909", "mode": "normal", "text": " All back-up lights on a road vehicle must remain extinguished when the vehicle is moving forward.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9910", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9911", "mode": "normal", "text": "224.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9912", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Minister of Transport may authorize, on conditions established by regulation, the installation and use of white lights at the rear of certain classes or sub-classes of road vehicles.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9913", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9914", "mode": "normal", "text": "225.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9915", "mode": "normal", "text": " A road vehicle over 2 metres in width, operated on a public highway, must carry portable lamps, reflectors or flares, the standards of use of which are prescribed by regulation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9916", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9917", "mode": "normal", "text": "226.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9918", "mode": "normal", "text": " Emergency vehicles may carry flashing or rotating red lights. In addition, they may carry alternately flashing white headlights and flashing or rotating white lights. Police vehicles may carry blue flashing or rotating lights.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9919", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9920", "mode": "normal", "text": "227.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9921", "mode": "normal", "text": " In addition to road vehicles that are required by law to be so equipped, the following vehicles may carry flashing or rotating amber lights: For the purposes of this section, “", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9922", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9923", "mode": "normal", "text": "228.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9924", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where the conditions of issue of a special permit require that a road vehicle be equipped with a rotating or flashing amber light, the light may be permanently attached to the vehicle but it must not be operated when the special permit is no longer required.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9925", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9926", "mode": "normal", "text": "229.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9927", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every bus or minibus used for the transportation of school children within the meaning of a regulation under the Transport Act ( chapter T-12 The lights, the signs and the compulsory stop signal prescribed in the first paragraph must conform to the regulations under the Transport Act. The signs must be removed or covered when the vehicle is not being used to provide the transportation referred to in section 454 of 461.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9928", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9929", "mode": "normal", "text": "230.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9930", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every motorcycle or moped must carry at least", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9931", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9932", "mode": "normal", "text": "231.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9933", "mode": "normal", "text": " When a motorcycle is equipped with a sidecar, the sidecar must carry a red taillight, which must be as near as practicable to the right extremity of the sidecar.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9934", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9935", "mode": "normal", "text": "232.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9936", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every bicycle must carry Despite the first paragraph, a bicycle need not carry the reflector required under subparagraph 3 of that paragraph if the cyclist wears a reflective band around each ankle or shoes with reflective strips. Any equipment or object placed on a bicycle that blocks a prescribed reflector or its substitute must carry a reflector or a reflective strip. A trailer towed by a bicycle must carry two red reflectors at the rear, as far apart as practicable, or a red reflective strip placed as close to horizontal as possible across the width of the trailer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9937", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9938", "mode": "normal", "text": "233.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9939", "mode": "normal", "text": " At night, every bicycle must also carry, a white headlight or white light, at the front, and one red taillight, both of which may be flashing.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9940", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9941", "mode": "normal", "text": "234.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9942", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every road vehicle, other than a vehicle specifically mentioned in this chapter, must carry two white headlights and two red taillights.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9943", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9944", "mode": "normal", "text": "235.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9945", "mode": "normal", "text": " The white headlights prescribed in this chapter must be firmly attached to the vehicle and be so adjusted as to produce, under normal atmospheric conditions and on a level road, sufficient light to enable the driver of the vehicle to discern a person or an object within a distance of 150 metres. In the case of a moped, the light must enable the driver to discern a person or an object within a distance of 90 metres and in the case of a bicycle, at a distance of 10 metres.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9946", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9947", "mode": "normal", "text": "236.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9948", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where two white headlights are mounted on a vehicle, they must be at the same height, one on each side of the vertical centreline and as far apart as practicable.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9949", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9950", "mode": "normal", "text": "237.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9951", "mode": "normal", "text": " The headlights, lights and reflectors prescribed in this chapter must be visible at a distance of not less that 150 metres and conform to the standards established by regulation. They must be kept free of any obstructing matter that reduces their effectiveness. If equipment installed on a vehicle blocks the vehicle’s headlights, lights or reflectors, the vehicle or equipment must carry equivalent headlights, lights or reflectors in places where they are visible.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9952", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9953", "mode": "normal", "text": "238.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9954", "mode": "normal", "text": " A peace officer may require the driver of a road vehicle to clean the headlights, lights and reflectors of the vehicle where their effectiveness is reduced by dirt or other obstructing matter. The driver must comply with the requirement of the peace officer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9955", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9956", "mode": "normal", "text": "239.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9957", "mode": "normal", "text": " No road vehicle, except a vehicle contemplated in sections 226 to 227.1, may carry alternately flashing white headlights or flashing or rotating lights of whatever colour. No road vehicle contemplated in any of sections 226, 226.2, 227 and 227.1 may carry flashing or rotating lights of another colour than the colour authorized for that vehicle in accordance with the section which applies to such a vehicle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9958", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9959", "mode": "normal", "text": "240.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9960", "mode": "normal", "text": " A peace officer is authorized to require the removal, at the expense of the owner, of a flashing or rotating light carried by a road vehicle in contravention of this Code. The peace officer shall give a receipt to the person in possession of the vehicle and remit the light to the Société.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9961", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9962", "mode": "normal", "text": "242.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9963", "mode": "normal", "text": " Subject to sections 243 to 247, every road vehicle must be equipped with at least one braking system sufficiently powerful to stop the vehicle quickly in case of emergency and hold the vehicle stationary.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9964", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9965", "mode": "normal", "text": "243.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9966", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every motor vehicle or combination of road vehicles must be equipped with at least one service brake system allowing sufficient braking force to be applied on each weight-bearing wheel to stop the vehicle quickly in case of emergency and with a parking brake system to hold the vehicle stationary.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9967", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9968", "mode": "normal", "text": "244.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9969", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every trailer or semi-trailer that is part of a combination of road vehicles and that has a mass, once loaded, of 1,300 kg or more or that has a mass, once loaded, of over half the net mass of the motor vehicle by which it is towed must be equipped with an independent braking system allowing application of a braking force on each weight-bearing wheel. The towing vehicle must carry the necessary equipment for operating the braking system of any trailer or semi-trailer referred to in the first paragraph being towed. This section does not apply to the following combinations of vehicles that comply with the conditions set out in the second paragraph of section 240.2:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9970", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9971", "mode": "normal", "text": "245.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9972", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every trailer or semi-trailer operated without an independent brake system that can stop the vehicle if the trailer or semi-trailer becomes separated from the towing vehicle must be equipped with a chain, a cable or any other sufficiently solid safety device installed so that the trailer or semi-trailer and the towing vehicle would remain attached were the coupling device to break. The towing vehicle must carry the necessary equipment for attaching the chain, cable or safety device of the trailer or semi-trailer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9973", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9974", "mode": "normal", "text": "246.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9975", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every motorcycle or moped must be equipped with at least one brake system acting on the front and rear wheels. The brake system must be sufficiently powerful to stop the vehicle quickly in case of emergency and to hold it stationary.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9976", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9977", "mode": "normal", "text": "247.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9978", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every bicycle and non-motorized scooter must be equipped with at least one brake system acting on the rear wheel. The system must be sufficiently powerful to quickly block the rotation of the wheel on a paved, dry and level roadway.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9979", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9980", "mode": "normal", "text": "248.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9981", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may drive a road vehicle having a brake system that has been modified or altered in such a way as to reduce its effectiveness.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9982", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9983", "mode": "normal", "text": "249.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9984", "mode": "normal", "text": " A peace officer who has reasonable grounds to believe that the brake system of a road vehicle or bicycle is defective or out of order may require that the vehicle be taken to the nearest practicable place and retained at the expense of the owner until the problem is corrected.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9985", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9986", "mode": "normal", "text": "250.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9987", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may either effect or cause the removal, alteration or putting out of service of a seat belt with which the seats of a road vehicle are equipped under the Motor Vehicle Safety Act (Statutes of Canada, 1993, chapter 16).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9988", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9989", "mode": "normal", "text": "251.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9990", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9991", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9992", "mode": "normal", "text": "252.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9993", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may sell or lease to, or place at the disposal of any person, in exchange for consideration, or in any way offer to sell or lease to, or to place at the disposal of any person, in exchange for consideration, a radar warning device. Any contravention of this section entails, upon conviction, the confiscation of the radar warning device in favour of the Société.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9994", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9995", "mode": "normal", "text": "253.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9996", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "9997", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9998", "mode": "normal", "text": "254.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "9999", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every motor vehicle must be equipped with a horn.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10000", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10001", "mode": "normal", "text": "255.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10002", "mode": "normal", "text": " Only emergency vehicles may be equipped with a siren or a device producing a similar sound or a traffic-light changing device. The first paragraph does not apply to an anti-theft device installed and used in a road vehicle in accordance with the standards established by regulation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10003", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10004", "mode": "normal", "text": "256.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10005", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may sound the horn of a road vehicle, except in case of necessity. In addition to public highways, this section applies on private roads open to public vehicular traffic, as well as on land occupied by shopping centres and other land where public traffic is allowed.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10006", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10007", "mode": "normal", "text": "257.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10008", "mode": "normal", "text": " A peace officer is authorized to require the removal, at the expense of the owner of a road vehicle, of a siren or any other device producing a similar sound installed on a vehicle in contravention of this Code. The peace officer shall give a receipt to the person in possession of the vehicle and remit the device to the Société.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10009", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10010", "mode": "normal", "text": "258.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10011", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every motor vehicle, except a vehicle that does not use fuel as its source of energy, must be equipped with an exhaust system that conforms to the standards established by regulation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10012", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10013", "mode": "normal", "text": "259.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10014", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may sell or offer for sale, for use on a public highway, an exhaust system that does not conform to the standards prescribed by regulation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10015", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10016", "mode": "normal", "text": "260.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10017", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may perform or cause the performance of any operation on a motor vehicle to cancel or reduce the effectiveness of the exhaust system of the vehicle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10018", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10019", "mode": "normal", "text": "261.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10020", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every motor vehicle equipped with a windshield, other than a motorcycle or moped, must be equipped with a front windshield wiper and, if fitted as original equipment by the manufacturer, a front windshield washer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10021", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10022", "mode": "normal", "text": "262.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10023", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every motor vehicle, other than a motorcycle or moped, must be equipped with at least two rear-view mirrors, one solidly attached to the interior of the vehicle at the centre of the upper part of the windshield, and the other, to the exterior of the vehicle on the left side. When the interior rear-view mirror cannot be used, another rear-view mirror must be attached to the exterior of the vehicle on the right side. Where the motor vehicle draws a trailer or a semi-trailer, rear-view mirrors must be attached so as to enable the driver to have a clear view to the back of the combination of vehicles: When an outsized vehicle referred to in the third paragraph is operated under a special permit, the presence of an escort vehicle behind the outsized vehicle may compensate for the absence of rear-view mirrors.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10024", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10025", "mode": "normal", "text": "263.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10026", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every motorcycle or moped must be equipped with two rear-view mirrors, one solidly attached to each side of the vehicle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10027", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10028", "mode": "normal", "text": "264.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10029", "mode": "normal", "text": " The windows, windshield and safety partitions of a motor vehicle must be made of transparent glass so manufactured or treated as to substantially reduce friability and the likelihood of shattering.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10030", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10031", "mode": "normal", "text": "265.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10032", "mode": "normal", "text": " The windshield and the other windows of a motor vehicle must conform to the standards prescribed by regulation to ensure good visibility for the driver. They must be free of any material that might reduce visibility for the driver.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10033", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10034", "mode": "normal", "text": "266.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10035", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may coat the windshield or the front side windows of a road vehicle or cause them to be coated with a substance having the effect of reducing or preventing good visibility from inside or outside the vehicle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10036", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10037", "mode": "normal", "text": "267.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10038", "mode": "normal", "text": " A peace officer may require the driver of a vehicle to clean or clear the windshield and windows where obstructing matter reduces visibility for the driver. The driver must comply with the requirement of the peace officer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10039", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10040", "mode": "normal", "text": "268.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10041", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every motor vehicle, other than a motorcycle with a piston displacement not in excess of 125 cc or a moped, must be equipped with an odometer and a speedometer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10042", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10043", "mode": "normal", "text": "269.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10044", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where a road vehicle is equipped with bumpers as original equipment by the manufacturer, they must be solidly attached to the part of the vehicle designed for that purpose.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10045", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10046", "mode": "normal", "text": "270.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10047", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every road vehicle must be fitted with tires that conform to the standards prescribed by regulation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10048", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10049", "mode": "normal", "text": "271.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10050", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may sell or offer for sale, for use on a public highway, a tire that does not conform to the standards prescribed by regulation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10051", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10052", "mode": "normal", "text": "272.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10053", "mode": "normal", "text": " Motor vehicles and combinations of road vehicles not fitted with permanent mudguards or fitted with permanent mudguards that are narrower than the tire tread or the rear portion of which is more than 350 mm from the ground when the vehicle is not loaded must be equipped with detachable mudguards of resistant material and at least as wide as the tire tread, except the following vehicles:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10054", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10055", "mode": "normal", "text": "273.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10056", "mode": "normal", "text": " The lower end of the detachable mudguards must not be more than 350 mm from the ground, measured when the vehicle is not loaded.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10057", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10058", "mode": "normal", "text": "274.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10059", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every road vehicle built to be driven at a speed of less than 40 km/h as well as every animal-drawn vehicle must carry a warning sign in accordance with the standards prescribed by regulation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10060", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10061", "mode": "normal", "text": "275.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10062", "mode": "normal", "text": " The owner of a road vehicle that does not meet the requirements of any of sections 269 and 272 to 274 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10063", "code": "30 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10064", "mode": "normal", "text": "60.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10065", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10066", "mode": "normal", "text": "276.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10067", "mode": "normal", "text": " The owner of a bicycle that does not meet the requirements of any of sections 212, 232 and 233, the second paragraph of section 235 or of either of sections 237 and 247 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10068", "code": "80 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10069", "mode": "normal", "text": "100. A cyclist whose bicycle is not equipped with the reflector required under subparagraph 3 of the first paragraph of section 232 and who does not wear a reflective band around each ankle or shoes with reflective strips as required under the second paragraph of that section is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10070", "code": "80 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10071", "mode": "normal", "text": "100.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10072", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10073", "mode": "normal", "text": "277.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10074", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes the second paragraph of section 238 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10075", "code": "60 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10076", "mode": "normal", "text": "100.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10077", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10078", "mode": "normal", "text": "278.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10079", "mode": "normal", "text": " The owner of a road vehicle who contravenes section 213 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10080", "code": "60 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10081", "mode": "normal", "text": "100.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10082", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10083", "mode": "normal", "text": "279.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10084", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10085", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10086", "mode": "normal", "text": "280.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10087", "mode": "normal", "text": " The owner of a road vehicle that does not meet the requirements of section 236 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10088", "code": "60 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10089", "mode": "normal", "text": "100.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10090", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10091", "mode": "normal", "text": "281.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10092", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who installs or uses a white headlight in contravention of section 224 or who contravenes section 256 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10093", "code": "100 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10094", "mode": "normal", "text": "200. Every person who uses a green rotating light in contravention of section 226.1 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10095", "code": "175 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10096", "mode": "normal", "text": "525.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10097", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10098", "mode": "normal", "text": "282.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10099", "mode": "normal", "text": " The owner of a vehicle that does not meet the requirements of any of sections 210.1, 212, 215 to 223, 225, 230, 231, 234 and 235, the first or third paragraph of section 237, any of sections 240.1, 240.3, 242, 243, 246, 254, 261 to 264, the first paragraph of section 265 or of section 268 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10100", "code": "100 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10101", "mode": "normal", "text": "200. The owner of a low-speed vehicle that does not meet the requirements of a regulatory provision made under section 214.0.2 is guilty of an offence and liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10102", "code": "100 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10103", "mode": "normal", "text": "200.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10104", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10105", "mode": "normal", "text": "283.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10106", "mode": "normal", "text": " The holder of a special permit who contravenes section 228 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10107", "code": "100 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10108", "mode": "normal", "text": "200.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10109", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10110", "mode": "normal", "text": "284.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10111", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes any of sections 233.1, 233.2, 250 or 274.2 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10112", "code": "200 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10113", "mode": "normal", "text": "300. Every owner of a heavy vehicle who contravenes section 250 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10114", "code": "350 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10115", "mode": "normal", "text": "1,050. Every person who contravenes section 251 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10116", "code": "500 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10117", "mode": "normal", "text": "1,000.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10118", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10119", "mode": "normal", "text": "285.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10120", "mode": "normal", "text": " The owner of a road vehicle that does not meet the requirements of any of sections 239, 244, 245, 255 and 270 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10121", "code": "200 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10122", "mode": "normal", "text": "300. Every owner or operator of a heavy vehicle that does not comply with section 244 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10123", "code": "350 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10124", "mode": "normal", "text": "1,050.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10125", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10126", "mode": "normal", "text": "286.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10127", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes any of sections 210, 211 and 211.1 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10128", "code": "600 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10129", "mode": "normal", "text": "2,000. However, in the case of a bicycle, the fine is of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10130", "code": "80 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10131", "mode": "normal", "text": "100. Every owner of a heavy vehicle who contravenes section 211 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10132", "code": "700 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10133", "mode": "normal", "text": "2,100.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10134", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10135", "mode": "normal", "text": "287.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10136", "mode": "normal", "text": " The owner of a vehicle that does not meet the requirements of section 229 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10137", "code": "600 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10138", "mode": "normal", "text": "2,000.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10139", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10140", "mode": "normal", "text": "288.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10141", "mode": "normal", "text": " In addition, for the purposes of this Title, a scooter other than a motorized scooter and an adult’s tricycle shall be considered as bicycles.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10142", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10143", "mode": "normal", "text": "289.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10144", "mode": "normal", "text": " The meaning of a road or traffic sign message, whatever the medium, is the meaning assigned to the sign by the Minister in an order published to that effect in the Gazette officielle du Québec The manufacturing and installation standards for road signs or signals to be erected on a public highway or on a road vehicle are determined by the Minister and set out in a traffic control manual. Those standards are not subject to the Regulations Act ( chapter R-18.1 Every person responsible for the management or maintenance of public highways must comply with standards set out in the manual where a requirement to do so is indicated therein. The Minister may remove, at the expense of the person responsible for the management of the road, any sign or signal that does not conform to the Minister’s manual.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10145", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10146", "mode": "normal", "text": "290.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10147", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10148", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10149", "mode": "normal", "text": "291.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10150", "mode": "normal", "text": " The person responsible for the maintenance of a public highway may, by means of proper signs or signals, restrict or prohibit the use of the highway by all or certain heavy vehicles, in particular, heavy vehicles having dimensions or a number of axles that exceed the maximum limits authorized. Where that person is responsible for the maintenance of a bridge or viaduct, the person may also restrict or prohibit the use of the bridge or viaduct by heavy vehicles having a mass that exceeds the maximum limits authorized on the infrastructure. In the case of a municipality, that power is exercised by by-law or, where the law so authorizes, by ordinance, the coming into force of which is subject to the approval of the Minister of Transport under section 627, except in an emergency; in the absence of approval, the Minister may remove the unauthorized sign or signal. No person may drive a vehicle referred to in the first paragraph on a public highway on which traffic is restricted or prohibited unless the vehicle is used under a special permit expressly giving the vehicle access to that highway.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10151", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10152", "mode": "normal", "text": "292.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10153", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a heavy vehicle must verify the condition of the vehicle’s brakes where the proper sign or signal requires a mandatory stop at a brake verification area.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10154", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10155", "mode": "normal", "text": "293.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10156", "mode": "normal", "text": " The person responsible for the maintenance of a public highway may, by means of appropriate signs or signals during exceptional events or sports events or competitions, restrict or prohibit all or some vehicular traffic on that highway for the time he indicates. No person may drive a road vehicle in contravention of this section during the period traffic is restricted or prohibited.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10157", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10158", "mode": "normal", "text": "294.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10159", "mode": "normal", "text": " The person responsible for the maintenance of a public highway must erect the proper signs or signals at every intersection.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10160", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10161", "mode": "normal", "text": "295.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10162", "mode": "normal", "text": " The person responsible for the maintenance of a public highway may, by means of the proper signs or signals,", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10163", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10164", "mode": "normal", "text": "296.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10165", "mode": "normal", "text": " The person responsible for the maintenance of a limited access highway may, by means of the proper signs or signals, regulate or prohibit the driving of certain classes of road vehicles on that highway.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10166", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10167", "mode": "normal", "text": "297.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10168", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Minister of Transport may, by means of the proper signs, designate a public highway as an autoroute.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10169", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10170", "mode": "normal", "text": "298.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10171", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every municipality to which subparagraph 4 of the first paragraph of section 328 applies must erect a sign or signal on every public highway under its maintenance that leads to a built-up area to indicate that the speed limit is set at 50 km/h.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10172", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10173", "mode": "normal", "text": "299.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10174", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every municipality that establishes, by by-law, a speed limit other than the rate of speed provided for in section 328 shall indicate that rate of speed by means of signs or signals. If the municipality fails to do so, section 328 applies. No person may travel at a rate of speed exceeding the limit indicated on any signs erected under this section.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10175", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10176", "mode": "normal", "text": "300.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10177", "mode": "normal", "text": " In the cases described in section 329, the decision of the Minister of Transport prevails over any provision of a by-law passed by a municipality. The municipality shall, on a notice from the Minister and within the time he indicates, remove the signs or signals erected by it. If it fails to do so within the allotted time, the Minister may remove the signs or signals at the expense of the municipality.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10178", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10179", "mode": "normal", "text": "301.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10180", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person, except the person responsible for the maintenance of a public highway, may erect signs or signals or cause signs or signals to be erected on that highway or use a traffic sign on a road vehicle other than a police car.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10181", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10182", "mode": "normal", "text": "302.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10183", "mode": "normal", "text": " The person responsible for the maintenance of the public highway may remove any sign or signal erected in contravention of section 301.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10184", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10185", "mode": "normal", "text": "303.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10186", "mode": "normal", "text": " Despite section 301, any person carrying out work requiring occupation of a public highway, duly authorized by the person responsible for the maintenance of the highway, or any person conducting a road check operation must erect traffic signs or signals in compliance with the standards determined by the Minister of Transport for the duration of the work or operation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10187", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10188", "mode": "normal", "text": "304.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10189", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may, except with the authorization of the person responsible for the maintenance of a public highway, erect any signal, sign, indication or device on that highway.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10190", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10191", "mode": "normal", "text": "305.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10192", "mode": "normal", "text": " The person responsible for the maintenance of the public highway may, at the expense of the contravener, remove any object erected in contravention of section 304.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10193", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10194", "mode": "normal", "text": "306.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10195", "mode": "normal", "text": " Visible devices, advertising and signs that bear a reproduction of a road signal governed by the standards prescribed by the Minister under section 289 that imitate such a road signal or that may be confused with traffic lights or with such a road signal because of their shape, colour, text, size or location are prohibited on and along public highways. Devices, advertising and signs that can obstruct a road signal and those that encroach on a public highway are also prohibited. The Minister of Transport may, by regulation, provide for exceptions to the prohibition under the first paragraph.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10196", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10197", "mode": "normal", "text": "307.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10198", "mode": "normal", "text": " The person responsible for the maintenance of a public highway may, if he believes on reasonable grounds that a signal, sign, indication or device is erected or displayed on private property in contravention of section 306, issue a notice to the owner requiring him to remove any such object within 48 hours. If the contravener fails to comply with the notice, the person responsible for the maintenance of the highway may enter upon the property and remove any such object at the owner’s expense.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10199", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10200", "mode": "normal", "text": "308.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10201", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every sign or signal erected on a private road open to general vehicular traffic or on land occupied by shopping centres and other land where public traffic is allowed must conform to the specifications prescribed in respect of public highways by the Minister of Transport.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10202", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10203", "mode": "normal", "text": "309.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10204", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Minister of Transport or an authorized representative of the municipality within whose territory a road contemplated in section 308 is situated may, if he believes on reasonable grounds that an offence against the said section is being committed, issue a notice to the contravener requiring him to remove any contravening sign or signal within 48 hours. If the contravener fails to comply with the notice, the Minister or the authorized representative of the municipality may remove the sign or signal at the contravener’s expense.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10205", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10206", "mode": "normal", "text": "310.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10207", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person must comply with every road or traffic sign or signal erected under this Code.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10208", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10209", "mode": "normal", "text": "311.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10210", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where traffic is directed by a peace officer, a school crossing guard or a flag person in charge of directing traffic around or about work sites or during exceptional events or sports events or competitions, every person shall obey his orders or signals even if contrary to existing traffic signs or signals.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10211", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10212", "mode": "normal", "text": "312.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10213", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may drive on private property to avoid compliance with a traffic sign or signal.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10214", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10215", "mode": "normal", "text": "313.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10216", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person, other than the driver of a road vehicle, who contravenes either of sections 310 and 311 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10217", "code": "15 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10218", "mode": "normal", "text": "30. However, in the case of a cyclist, the fine is of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10219", "code": "80 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10220", "mode": "normal", "text": "100. A cyclist who contravenes section 312 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10221", "code": "80 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10222", "mode": "normal", "text": "100.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10223", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10224", "mode": "normal", "text": "314.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10225", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle who contravenes the second paragraph of section 293 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10226", "code": "60 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10227", "mode": "normal", "text": "100.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10228", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10229", "mode": "normal", "text": "315.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10230", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes the second paragraph of section 293.2 or either of sections 304 and 308 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10231", "code": "100 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10232", "mode": "normal", "text": "200.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10233", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10234", "mode": "normal", "text": "316.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10235", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes either of sections 301 and 306 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10236", "code": "300 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10237", "mode": "normal", "text": "600.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10238", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10239", "mode": "normal", "text": "317.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10240", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes section 303 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10241", "code": "600 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10242", "mode": "normal", "text": "2,000. However, the fine shall be of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10243", "code": "100 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10244", "mode": "normal", "text": "200 in cases where signs or signals which do not meet the standards laid down by the Minister of Transport are erected.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10245", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10246", "mode": "normal", "text": "318.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10247", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes the third paragraph of section 292.1 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10248", "code": "600 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10249", "mode": "normal", "text": "6,000.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10250", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10251", "mode": "normal", "text": "319.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10252", "mode": "normal", "text": " In addition, for the purposes of this Title, a scooter other than a motorized scooter and an adult’s tricycle shall be considered as bicycles.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10253", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10254", "mode": "normal", "text": "320.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10255", "mode": "normal", "text": " On a two-way roadway, the driver of a road vehicle must use the right-hand lane of the roadway. To pass another vehicle or where the lane is obstructed or closed to traffic, the driver may use the other lane but he must then yield the right of way to the vehicle moving in the opposite direction. This section applies, in addition to public highways, to highways under the administration of or maintained by the Ministère des Ressources naturelles et de la Faune.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10256", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10257", "mode": "normal", "text": "321.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10258", "mode": "normal", "text": " On a two-way roadway with two lanes or over, the driver of a road vehicle must use the right-hand lane of the roadway. To pass another vehicle, to turn left or where the right-hand lane is obstructed or closed to traffic, the driver may use another lane in the direction his vehicle is moving. Where all the lanes in the direction in which the vehicle is moving are obstructed or closed to traffic, the driver may use the nearest lane in the opposite direction that is not obstructed or closed to traffic, but he must then yield the right of way to any vehicle moving in the opposite direction.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10259", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10260", "mode": "normal", "text": "322.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10261", "mode": "normal", "text": " On a two-way roadway divided into three traffic lanes, where the centre lane is reserved for making left turns from either direction, the driver of a road vehicle must use the right-hand lane. He may use the centre lane only for making left turns.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10262", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10263", "mode": "normal", "text": "323.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10264", "mode": "normal", "text": " On a two-way roadway divided into five traffic lanes, where the centre lane is reserved for making left turns from either direction, the driver of a road vehicle must use either of the two right-hand lanes. He may use the centre lane only for making left turns.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10265", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10266", "mode": "normal", "text": "324.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10267", "mode": "normal", "text": " On a one-way roadway with two lanes, the driver of a road vehicle shall use the right-hand lane. On a one-way roadway with three lanes or over, the driver must use one of the right-hand lanes. To pass another vehicle, to turn left, to enter an exit ramps on a limited access highway or where the lane he is using is obstructed or closed to traffic, the driver may use the lane closest to the left-hand side. The driver of a road vehicle used for snow removal or road maintenance may also use the left-hand lane when performing his duties.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10268", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10269", "mode": "normal", "text": "325.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10270", "mode": "normal", "text": " Notwithstanding section 324, where the speed limit is less than 80 km/h the driver of a road vehicle may use any of the lanes. In such a case, road vehicles moving faster in one lane than in another are not considered to be passing. The driver of a road vehicle proceeding at less than the normal speed of traffic or the driver of a low-speed vehicle must drive in the right-hand lane closest to the edge of the roadway, unless he is about to turn left, to park or to stop on the left-hand side and has signalled his intention.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10271", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10272", "mode": "normal", "text": "326.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10273", "mode": "normal", "text": " On a public highway where the roadways are separated by a median strip or any other raised physical device, the driver of a road vehicle shall not cross the separation except at the places laid out for that purpose and not before he has ascertained that he can do so in safety.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10274", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10275", "mode": "normal", "text": "327.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10276", "mode": "normal", "text": " Any rate of speed or any action that can endanger human life and safety or property is prohibited. In addition to public highways, this section applies on highways under the administration of or maintained by the Ministère des Ressources naturelles et de la Faune, on private roads open to public vehicular traffic, as well as on land occupied by shopping centres and other land where public traffic is allowed.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10277", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10278", "mode": "normal", "text": "328.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10279", "mode": "normal", "text": " Except on roads where the opposite is indicated by signs or signals and without restricting the scope of section 327, no person may drive a road vehicle at a speed On access roads leading to a built-up area, subparagraph 4 of the first paragraph applies when the driver reaches the sign or signal indicating the 50 km/h speed limit. Subparagraphs 2, 3 and 4 of the first paragraph apply on highways under the administration of or maintained by the Ministère des Ressources naturelles et de la Faune. The Minister, on the recommendation of the Minister of Natural Resources and Wildlife, may by order change the speed limit on all or any part of such highways.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10280", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10281", "mode": "normal", "text": "329.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10282", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Minister of Transport may change the speed limits provided for in subparagraphs 1 to 4 of the first paragraph of section 328 for all road vehicles or for certain categories thereof and establish the variable speed limits referred to in subparagraphs 1 and 5 of the first paragraph of that section. The installation of traffic signs is proof of the decision of the Minister. The date of the decision and approximate location of the installation of such signs must be entered in a register kept by the Minister. No person may drive at a speed in excess of the limits indicated on the traffic signs erected under this section or the second paragraph of section 628.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10283", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10284", "mode": "normal", "text": "330.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10285", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle must reduce the speed of his vehicle when visibility conditions become inadequate because of darkness, fog, rain or other precipitation or when the roadway is slippery or not completely cleared.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10286", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10287", "mode": "normal", "text": "331.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10288", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may drive a road vehicle at a low speed that may impede or obstruct normal traffic, except where necessary. In case of necessity, the driver must use the flashing emergency lights of his vehicle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10289", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10290", "mode": "normal", "text": "333.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10291", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may drive a road vehicle containing a radar warning device or on which is placed any object or to which is applied any material capable of interfering in any way with the operation of a radar device, or with the recording of registration plate information by a detection system.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10292", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10293", "mode": "normal", "text": "334.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10294", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every peace officer who has reasonable grounds to believe that a road vehicle contains a radar warning device, may stop the vehicle and inspect it. He may confiscate the radar warning device found in the vehicle, at the expense of the owner of the vehicle. When confiscating such a radar warning device, the peace officer shall give a receipt to the person in possession of the vehicle and remit the device to the Société.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10295", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10296", "mode": "normal", "text": "335.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10297", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle shall not follow another road vehicle or a bicycle more closely than is prudent and reasonable, taking account of speed, traffic density, atmospheric conditions and the condition of the roadway.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10298", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10299", "mode": "normal", "text": "336.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10300", "mode": "normal", "text": " On a public highway where the maximum speed allowed is 70 km/h or more, the drivers of road vehicles moving in convoy shall leave sufficient space between them to allow vehicles passing them to occupy the intervening spaces in safety.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10301", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10302", "mode": "normal", "text": "337.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10303", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10304", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10305", "mode": "normal", "text": "338.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10306", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle may cross any lane marked off by a broken line to pass or to change lanes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10307", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10308", "mode": "normal", "text": "339.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10309", "mode": "normal", "text": " On a two-way roadway, the driver of a road vehicle passing another vehicle must return to the right lane as soon as possible, after signalling his intention and ascertaining that he may do so without risk to the vehicle being passed.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10310", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10311", "mode": "normal", "text": "340.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10312", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle being passed or about to be passed must not increase the speed of his vehicle while it is being passed.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10313", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10314", "mode": "normal", "text": "341.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10315", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle may not pass a cyclist within the same traffic lane unless it can be done safely, after reducing the vehicle’s speed and ensuring that a reasonable distance can be kept between the vehicle and the cyclist during the manoeuvre. In no case may the driver of a road vehicle perform this manoeuvre if the part of the roadway on which the driver must encroach is not clear of traffic for a sufficient distance, in particular if another vehicle is oncoming or is coming up alongside the vehicle. In such a case, the driver must remain in the lane and reduce the vehicle’s speed, in particular by staying behind the cyclist. The driver must do the same in the cases referred to in sections 345 and 348. A reasonable distance is 1.5 m on a road where the maximum authorized speed limit is more than 50 km/h or 1 m on a road where the maximum authorized speed limit is 50 km/h or less. This section applies to the driver of a road vehicle when meeting or passing a pedestrian, with the necessary modifications. It also applies to such a driver if the cyclist or pedestrian is travelling on the shoulder or on a cycle lane that is not separated from the roadway by a median strip or any other raised physical device.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10316", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10317", "mode": "normal", "text": "342.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10318", "mode": "normal", "text": " In no case may the driver of a road vehicle successively pass two or more vehicles in a zigzag pattern on a one-way roadway having two or more traffic lanes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10319", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10320", "mode": "normal", "text": "343.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10321", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10322", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10323", "mode": "normal", "text": "344.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10324", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle may cross a marking described in section 326.1 providing that he can do so in safety, to pass a farm machine, a road vehicle carrying a slow-moving vehicle sign, a horse-drawn vehicle, a cyclist or a pedestrian or to return to the right of the roadway after passing. The driver of a road vehicle may, in the same manner, cross such a marking when meeting a pedestrian.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10325", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10326", "mode": "normal", "text": "345.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10327", "mode": "normal", "text": " No driver may, to pass, use the lane reserved for traffic moving in the opposite direction", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10328", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10329", "mode": "normal", "text": "346.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10330", "mode": "normal", "text": " No driver of a road vehicle may pass another vehicle to the right, except where the vehicle being passed is turning left, is about to turn left, is moving toward an exit ramp on a limited access highway or is a snow removal or road maintenance vehicle doing work on the left-hand lane of a one-way roadway with two lanes or over.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10331", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10332", "mode": "normal", "text": "347.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10333", "mode": "normal", "text": " In no case may a driver passing another vehicle drive off the roadway.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10334", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10335", "mode": "normal", "text": "348.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10336", "mode": "normal", "text": " No driver is allowed to pass Furthermore, no driver of a road vehicle is allowed to pass", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10337", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10338", "mode": "normal", "text": "349.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10339", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle or a cyclist who is turning at an intersection must yield the right of way to pedestrians and cyclists crossing the roadway he is about to enter.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10340", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10341", "mode": "normal", "text": "350.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10342", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle or a cyclist who is about to make a left turn must yield the right of way to any vehicle moving in the opposite direction, and is so close that it constitutes a hazard.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10343", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10344", "mode": "normal", "text": "351.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10345", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle who is about to turn right at an intersection must, after signalling his intention and ascertaining that he can do so in safety, move to the extreme right of the roadway or into the space reserved for that purpose by an appropriate sign, make a sharp turn and not encroach on the left or the centre of the road he is entering.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10346", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10347", "mode": "normal", "text": "352.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10348", "mode": "normal", "text": " On a two-way roadway, the driver of a road vehicle who is about to turn left at the intersection of a two-way roadway must, after signalling his intention and ascertaining that he can do so in safety, approach the centre line of the roadway on which he is driving, proceed in a straight line to the near side of the roadway he is about to enter and turn left as soon as the way is clear so as to enter the right-hand part of the other roadway.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10349", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10350", "mode": "normal", "text": "353.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10351", "mode": "normal", "text": " On a two-way roadway with two lanes or over, the driver of a road vehicle who is about to turn left at the intersection of a two-way roadway with two lanes or over must, after signalling his intention and ascertaining that he can do so in safety, approach the centre line of the roadway on which he is driving, proceed in a straight line to the near side of the roadway he is about to enter and turn left as soon as the way is clear so as to enter the other roadway to the right of and as close as possible to the centre line.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10352", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10353", "mode": "normal", "text": "354.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10354", "mode": "normal", "text": " On a two-way roadway, the driver of a road vehicle who is about to turn left at the intersection of a one-way roadway must, after signalling his intention and ascertaining that he can do so in safety, approach the centre line of the roadway on which he is driving, proceed in a straight line to the near side of the roadway he is about to enter and turn left as soon as the way is clear so as to enter the left-hand part of the other roadway.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10355", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10356", "mode": "normal", "text": "355.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10357", "mode": "normal", "text": " On a one-way roadway, the driver of a road vehicle who is about to turn left at the intersection of a one-way roadway must, after signalling his intention and ascertaining that he can do so in safety, move to the extreme left of the roadway to the near side of the roadway he is about to enter and turn left as soon as the way is clear so as to enter the left-hand part of the other roadway.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10358", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10359", "mode": "normal", "text": "356.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10360", "mode": "normal", "text": " On a one-way roadway with two lanes or over, the driver of a road vehicle who is about to turn left at an intersection must, after signalling his intention and ascertaining that he can do so in safety, move to the extreme left of the roadway or into the space reserved for that purpose identified by an appropriate sign.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10361", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10362", "mode": "normal", "text": "357.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10363", "mode": "normal", "text": " On a one-way roadway, the driver of a road vehicle who is about to turn left at the intersection of a two-way roadway must, after signalling his intention and ascertaining that he can do so in safety, move to the extreme left of the roadway on which he is driving, proceed in a straight line to the near side of the roadway he is about to enter and turn left as soon as the way is clear, so as to enter the right-hand part of the other roadway.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10364", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10365", "mode": "normal", "text": "358.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10366", "mode": "normal", "text": " On a one-way roadway, the driver of a road vehicle who is about to turn left at the intersection of a two-way roadway with two or more traffic lanes must, after signalling his intention and ascertaining that he can do so in safety, move to the extreme left of the roadway on which he is driving, proceed in a straight line to the near side of the roadway he is about to enter and turn left as soon as the way is clear, so as to enter the other roadway to the right of and as close as possible to the centre line.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10367", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10368", "mode": "normal", "text": "359.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10369", "mode": "normal", "text": " Unless otherwise directed by a sign or signal, when facing a red light, the driver of a road vehicle or a cyclist must stop his vehicle before the pedestrian crosswalk or stop-line or, if none, before the near side of the roadway he is about to cross, and may proceed only when a signal shows he may do so. An arrow-shaped red light may be used to regulate stopping before a specific manoeuvre. Despite the first paragraph and unless otherwise directed by a sign or signal, a cyclist facing a pedestrian light at a red light may proceed. However, the cyclist must stop before a pedestrian crosswalk or stop-line or, if none, before the near side of the roadway he is about to cross and make sure that he may proceed in safety. The cyclist must then ride at a safe, reasonable speed and give pedestrians the priority. In such a case, section 444, except the first paragraph, applies to the cyclist with the necessary modifications.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10370", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10371", "mode": "normal", "text": "360.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10372", "mode": "normal", "text": " Unless otherwise directed by a sign or signal, when facing a flashing red light, the driver of a road vehicle or a cyclist must stop his vehicle and yield the right of way to a vehicle approaching on another roadway that is entering the intersection, or is so close that it constitutes a hazard.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10373", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10374", "mode": "normal", "text": "361.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10375", "mode": "normal", "text": " Unless otherwise directed by a sign or signal, when facing an amber light, the driver of a road vehicle or a cyclist must stop his vehicle before the pedestrian crosswalk or stop-line or, if none, before the near side of the roadway he is about to cross, unless he has entered it or is so close to it that he could not stop in safety; he may proceed only when a signal shows he may do so. An arrow-shaped amber light may be used to regulate stopping before a specific manoeuvre.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10376", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10377", "mode": "normal", "text": "362.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10378", "mode": "normal", "text": " Unless otherwise directed by a sign or signal, when facing a flashing amber light, the driver of a road vehicle or a cyclist must reduce the speed of his vehicle and he may proceed only after yielding the right of way to road vehicles, cyclists and pedestrians crossing the intersection.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10379", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10380", "mode": "normal", "text": "363.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10381", "mode": "normal", "text": " Unless otherwise directed by a sign or signal, when facing a green light, whether flashing or not, the driver of a road vehicle or a cyclist must proceed ahead or turn left or right, after yielding the right of way to road vehicles, cyclists and pedestrians crossing the intersection.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10382", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10383", "mode": "normal", "text": "364.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10384", "mode": "normal", "text": " Unless otherwise directed by a sign or signal, when facing a green arrow, the driver of a road vehicle or a cyclist must move in the direction indicated by the arrow, after yielding the right of way to road vehicles, cyclists and pedestrians crossing the intersection.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10385", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10386", "mode": "normal", "text": "365.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10387", "mode": "normal", "text": " On a roadway with two lanes or more, where lane-direction signals are installed to indicate which lanes are open to traffic, the driver of a road vehicle may drive only in the lanes above which there is a green arrow pointing downwards. The driver of a road vehicle must, when facing a flashing horizontal amber arrow installed above the lane in which he is travelling, proceed toward the lane indicated by the arrow, after signalling his intention and ensuring that he can do so safely.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10388", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10389", "mode": "normal", "text": "366.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10390", "mode": "normal", "text": " Even if permitted by the traffic lights, no driver of a road vehicle may enter an intersection if there is not sufficient space ahead of the vehicle to proceed without blocking the intersection; in such a case, the driver must stop his vehicle before the near side of the roadway he is about to cross.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10391", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10392", "mode": "normal", "text": "367.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10393", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where traffic lights installed at an intersection are defective or are not in operation, the driver of a road vehicle or a cyclist must act as if the intersection were regulated by stop signs for all directions, except where an adequate sign or signal replaces the traffic light.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10394", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10395", "mode": "normal", "text": "368.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10396", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle or a cyclist must stop his vehicle when facing a stop sign, and comply with section 360. At a level crossing, the driver may proceed only after ascertaining that it is safe to proceed.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10397", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10398", "mode": "normal", "text": "369.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10399", "mode": "normal", "text": " At an intersection regulated by stop signs installed for only one roadway, the driver of a road vehicle or a cyclist who is facing a stop sign must stop his vehicle and yield the right of way to pedestrians and cyclists crossing or walking or cycling alongside the roadway he is about to cross or enter.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10400", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10401", "mode": "normal", "text": "370.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10402", "mode": "normal", "text": " At an intersection regulated by stop signs for all directions, the driver of a road vehicle or a cyclist must stop his vehicle and yield the right of way to any vehicle having reached the intersection before him. He must also yield the right of way to pedestrians crossing or walking or cycling alongside the roadway he is about to cross or enter.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10403", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10404", "mode": "normal", "text": "371.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10405", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle or a cyclist who is facing a “yield” sign must give priority to any vehicle moving in the lane he is about to enter where the vehicle is so close that entering the lane would constitute a hazard.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10406", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10407", "mode": "normal", "text": "372.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10408", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle who is about to make a turn, change lanes, make a U-turn or return to the roadway from the shoulder or a parking area must, after ascertaining that he may do so in safety, signal his intention by means of his turn-signal lights.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10409", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10410", "mode": "normal", "text": "373.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10411", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle exempt from the requirement to be equipped with turn-signal lights, or on which such lights are defective, must signal his intention by manual signals. To make a right turn, he must extend his forearm vertically upwards outside the vehicle and to make a left turn, he must extend his arm horizontally outside the vehicle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10412", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10413", "mode": "normal", "text": "374.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10414", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle exempt from the requirement to be equipped with stop lights, or on which such lights are defective, must signal his intention to stop his vehicle or to reduce its speed by extending his forearm vertically downwards outside the vehicle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10415", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10416", "mode": "normal", "text": "375.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10417", "mode": "normal", "text": " In cases described in sections 372 to 374, the driver of a road vehicle must signal his intention without interruption for a sufficient distance to avoid endangering the safety of other users of the public highway.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10418", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10419", "mode": "normal", "text": "376.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10420", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle passing another vehicle must signal his intention by means of his turn-signal lights and may also signal his intention by flashing his headlights.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10421", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10422", "mode": "normal", "text": "377.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10423", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may use the flashing emergency lights of a road vehicle except for reasons of safety.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10424", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10425", "mode": "normal", "text": "378.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10426", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of an emergency vehicle shall not operate the flashing or rotating lights, the sound producing device or the traffic-light changing device referred to in section 255 with which his vehicle is equipped except in the performance of his duties and if required by the circumstances. The driver is then not bound to comply with sections 299, 303.2, 310 and 312, the first paragraph of section 326.1, sections 328, 329, 335 and 342, paragraph 2 of section 345 and sections 346, 347, 359, 360, 361, 364, 365, 367, 368, 371, 372, 381 to 384, 386, 406.2, 415 to 417, 496.4 and 496.7. In each of the situations referred to in those sections, the driver must however ensure that non-compliance with the prescribed rule can be done safely.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10427", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10428", "mode": "normal", "text": "379.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10429", "mode": "normal", "text": " Except in the case provided for in section 226.2, the driver of a road vehicle shall not operate the flashing or rotating amber lights with which his vehicle is equipped except in the performance of his duties and if so required by the circumstances.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10430", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10431", "mode": "normal", "text": "380.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10432", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may leave a child under 7 years of age unattended in a road vehicle under his custody.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10433", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10434", "mode": "normal", "text": "381.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10435", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may leave unattended a road vehicle that is in his custody without previously removing the ignition key and locking the doors.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10436", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10437", "mode": "normal", "text": "382.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10438", "mode": "normal", "text": " Except in case of necessity, no person may stop a road vehicle in such a manner that it will block a sign or signal, obstruct traffic, hinder the performance of work or the maintenance of highways or prevent access to any property.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10439", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10440", "mode": "normal", "text": "383.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10441", "mode": "normal", "text": " Unless otherwise indicated by the person responsible for the maintenance of the highway, a road vehicle must be parked not more than 30 centimetres from the near edge of the roadway and facing the same way as the traffic. Where a road vehicle is parked on a slope, the emergency brake must be applied and the front wheels must be turned so that if such vehicle moves ahead of its own momentum, it will do so toward the near edge of the roadway. Notwithstanding the foregoing, a motorcycle or moped may be angle-parked against the near edge of the roadway, in the same direction as the traffic, so that if the vehicle moves of its own momentum it will do so toward the near edge of the roadway.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10442", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10443", "mode": "normal", "text": "384.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10444", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may stop a road vehicle on the roadway of a public highway where the maximum speed allowed is 70 km/h or more, unless in a case of necessity or when authorized to do so by signs or signals.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10445", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10446", "mode": "normal", "text": "385.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10447", "mode": "normal", "text": " If the driver of a road vehicle stops his vehicle at night on a roadway out of necessity, the driver must keep his vehicle’s parking lights and taillights or flashing emergency lights on, or signal the presence of his vehicle by means of lamps, reflectors or flares visible from not less than 150 metres and used in accordance with the norms prescribed by regulation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10448", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10449", "mode": "normal", "text": "386.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10450", "mode": "normal", "text": " Except in cases of necessity or where another provision of this Code permits it, no person may stop a road vehicle", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10451", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10452", "mode": "normal", "text": "387.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10453", "mode": "normal", "text": " Notwithstanding the prohibitions provided in section 386, the driver of a road vehicle used for the transportation of a handicapped person may stop his vehicle to take on or discharge that person, if it can be done in safety.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10454", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10455", "mode": "normal", "text": "388.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10456", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may stop a road vehicle in a parking space reserved for the exclusive use of handicapped persons and identified by signs or signals in compliance with the standards prescribed by the Minister of Transport, unless the vehicle bears: Where the vehicle bears a sticker issued pursuant to subparagraph 1 of the first paragraph, the driver or passenger must, on request, hand over to a peace officer, for examination, the certificate of the Société attesting the issue of the sticker. In addition to public highways, this section applies on private roads open to public vehicular traffic, as well as on land occupied by shopping centres and other land where public traffic is allowed.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10457", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10458", "mode": "normal", "text": "389.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10459", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may exceed or allow another person to exceed the number of hours of driving or hours of service prescribed by regulation with respect to a motor vehicle having a gross vehicle weight rating of 4,500 kg or less, or in violation of the standards, conditions and procedures prescribed by regulation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10460", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10461", "mode": "normal", "text": "390.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10462", "mode": "normal", "text": " A peace officer may cause any road vehicle stopped in contravention of the provisions of this division to be removed and impounded in the nearest suitable place at the owner’s expense. A peace officer may also exercise the power provided for in the first paragraph when a road vehicle is stopped out of necessity, in particular because of special weather conditions or inadequate visibility conditions.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10463", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10464", "mode": "normal", "text": "391.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10465", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may abandon a road vehicle on a public highway, on a private road open to public vehicular traffic, as well as on land occupied by shopping centres and other land where public traffic is allowed.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10466", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10467", "mode": "normal", "text": "392.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10468", "mode": "normal", "text": " A peace officer may cause any road vehicle abandoned on a highway or on any land referred to in section 391 to be removed and impounded in the nearest suitable place at the owner’s expense.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10469", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10470", "mode": "normal", "text": "393.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10471", "mode": "normal", "text": " When a peace officer impounds an abandoned vehicle, he must make reasonable inquiries to trace the owner, and notify the Minister of Revenue. If the owner of an abandoned vehicle has not been found 30 days after the vehicle was impounded, the vehicle is entrusted to the management of the Minister of Revenue, who may dispose of it at will; in such case, the Minister is responsible for ordinary costs of impoundment.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10472", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10473", "mode": "normal", "text": "394.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10474", "mode": "normal", "text": " Sections 391 to 393 also apply to a road vehicle abandoned on a private road or on private land where public access is not authorized, if the owner of that road or land requests a peace officer to remove the vehicle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10475", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10476", "mode": "normal", "text": "395.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10477", "mode": "normal", "text": " Subject to section 398, no person shall drive a road vehicle in which the seat belt or an air bag provided for the driver or for the seat occupied by a passenger is missing or has been modified or rendered inoperative.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10478", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10479", "mode": "normal", "text": "396.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10480", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person, except a child referred to in section 397, must, while in a moving road vehicle, wear, properly fastened, the seat belt with which his seat is equipped. However, the first paragraph does not apply This section applies, in addition to public highways, to highways under the administration of or maintained by the Ministère des Ressources naturelles et de la Faune.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10481", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10482", "mode": "normal", "text": "397.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10483", "mode": "normal", "text": " In a moving road vehicle, every child who is less than 145 cm tall or under 9 years of age must be restrained by a restraint system or booster seat that complies with the regulations under the Motor Vehicle Safety Act (S.C. 1993, c. 16). The restraint system or booster seat must, in accordance with the manufacturer’s instructions affixed thereon, be suitable for the child’s height and weight and be securely attached to the vehicle. However, the use of a restraint system or booster seat is not mandatory If the first paragraph cannot be complied with, a child occupying a seat in a taxi, an automobile considered to be a taxi or a police car must be restrained by the seat belt with which the seat is equipped, except in the following cases: This section applies, in addition to public highways, to highways under the administration of or maintained by the Ministère des Ressources naturelles et de la Faune.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10484", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10485", "mode": "normal", "text": "398.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10486", "mode": "normal", "text": " On a written application, the Société may grant a person invoking exceptional medical reasons, for the period it determines, An application concerning the wearing of a seat belt made under subparagraph 1 or 2 of the first paragraph must be supported by a written recommendation of a physician or specialized nurse practitioner obtained after a medical examination of the applicant. In the case of the authorizations referred to in subparagraphs 3 and 4 of the first paragraph, the applicant must provide a written recommendation of a physician, specialized nurse practitioner or occupational therapist, who determines the applicant’s specific needs, taking into account the medical diagnosis. The Société may require that the examination or recommendation required under this section be performed or provided by the physician, specialized nurse practitioner or occupational therapist that it designates by name. A certificate attesting that an exemption or authorization has been granted under this section is to be issued by the Société.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10487", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10488", "mode": "normal", "text": "400.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10489", "mode": "normal", "text": " The person invoking an exemption or authorization obtained under section 398 must have the certificate issued by the Société with him and show it to the peace officer on request. The peace officer must return the certificate to its holder after examination.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10490", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10491", "mode": "normal", "text": "401.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10492", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may drive a road vehicle carrying a passenger under 16 years of age who does not fulfil the obligations prescribed under this division. The first paragraph does not apply to taxi, bus or minibus drivers, or to drivers of automobiles considered to be taxis, in the performance of their duties. However, an adult passenger accompanying a passenger under 16 years of age in a taxi or in an automobile considered to be a taxi must ensure that the latter is transported in compliance with the conditions set out in this division.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10493", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10494", "mode": "normal", "text": "402.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10495", "mode": "normal", "text": " Unless otherwise directed by a sign or signal, the driver of a road vehicle or a cyclist must, at an intersection or junction, yield the right of way to any vehicle moving on his right on the roadway he is about to cross or enter where the vehicle or cyclist is so close that crossing or entering the roadway would constitute a hazard.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10496", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10497", "mode": "normal", "text": "403.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10498", "mode": "normal", "text": " Notwithstanding section 402, the driver of a road vehicle who enters a limited access highway must yield the right of way to a vehicle moving on the highway and that is so close that entering it would constitute a hazard.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10499", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10500", "mode": "normal", "text": "404.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10501", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle or a cyclist who leaves private property to cross or enter a public highway must yield the right of way to any vehicle or pedestrian moving on the highway.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10502", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10503", "mode": "normal", "text": "405.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10504", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle or a cyclist on a public highway who is about to enter private property must yield the right of way to any road vehicle, cyclist or pedestrian moving on the highway.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10505", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10506", "mode": "normal", "text": "406.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10507", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle or a cyclist must yield to any emergency vehicle whose lights or sound producing device are in operation by reducing speed, keeping as far to the right as practicable and, if necessary, bringing his vehicle to a standstill.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10508", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10509", "mode": "normal", "text": "407.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10510", "mode": "normal", "text": " On a public highway where the maximum speed allowed is less than 70 km/h, the driver of a road vehicle must yield the right of way to a bus when the driver of the bus is flashing his turn-signal lights for re-entering the lane in which he was moving before he stopped. The obligation to yield the right of way applies only to drivers of road vehicles moving in the lane that the driver of the bus is about to re-enter. The driver of a bus must not flash his turn-signal lights until he is about to re-enter the lane, after ascertaining that he can do so in safety. This section applies, with the necessary modifications, on a section of an autoroute or of another limited access highway when a bus is travelling on the autoroute or highway pursuant to section 418.2.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10511", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10512", "mode": "normal", "text": "408.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10513", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle or a cyclist must yield the right of way to a pedestrian who is crossing a roadway facing a steady, white signal representing a walking figure, or a flashing pedestrian light.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10514", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10515", "mode": "normal", "text": "409.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10516", "mode": "normal", "text": " At an intersection regulated by traffic lights, the driver of a road vehicle or a cyclist must yield the right of way to a pedestrian facing a green light.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10517", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10518", "mode": "normal", "text": "410.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10519", "mode": "normal", "text": " When a pedestrian enters or demonstrates the intention to enter a pedestrian crosswalk, the driver of a road vehicle must stop his vehicle to allow the pedestrian to cross. At such a crossing, a cyclist must also give pedestrians the priority.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10520", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10521", "mode": "normal", "text": "411.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10522", "mode": "normal", "text": " At a level crossing, the driver of a road vehicle or a cyclist must stop his vehicle not less than 5 metres from the railway where a sign or signal, a lowered gate or a railway employee signals an approaching rail vehicle, or where the driver or cyclist sees or hears a rail vehicle approaching the level crossing.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10523", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10524", "mode": "normal", "text": "412.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10525", "mode": "normal", "text": " Even if so authorized by traffic lights, no driver of a road vehicle may enter a level crossing if there is not sufficient space ahead of the vehicle to allow him to cross the level crossing.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10526", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10527", "mode": "normal", "text": "413.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10528", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a bus, minibus or road vehicle carrying dangerous substances in quantities requiring the display of safety marks, as determined by a regulation under section 622, must stop the vehicle not less than 5 metres from any level crossing; the driver may proceed only after ascertaining that it is safe to proceed. The driver is exempt from the obligations under the first paragraph at level crossings where so indicated by a sign or signal.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10529", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10530", "mode": "normal", "text": "414.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10531", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Minister of Transport may, by an order published in the Gazette officielle du Québec", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10532", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10533", "mode": "normal", "text": "415.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10534", "mode": "normal", "text": " In no case may the driver of a road vehicle enter or leave a limited access highway except at such entrances or exits as may be determined by the person responsible for its maintenance.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10535", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10536", "mode": "normal", "text": "416.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10537", "mode": "normal", "text": " In no case may the driver of a road vehicle drive his vehicle in reverse on a limited access highway or on an entrance or exit ramp.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10538", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10539", "mode": "normal", "text": "417.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10540", "mode": "normal", "text": " In no case may the driver of a road vehicle drive his vehicle in reverse unless he can do so in safety and without obstructing traffic. This section applies on private roads open to public vehicular traffic and on land occupied by shopping centres or other land where public traffic is allowed, as weel as on public highways.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10541", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10542", "mode": "normal", "text": "418.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10543", "mode": "normal", "text": " In no case may the driver of a road vehicle drive on the shoulder of a public highway or on the sidewalk except in case of necessity or unless so directed or allowed by a sign or signal.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10544", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10545", "mode": "normal", "text": "419.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10546", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Minister of Transport may, by an order published in the Gazette officielle du Québec", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10547", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10548", "mode": "normal", "text": "420.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10549", "mode": "normal", "text": " A peace officer may prohibit access to a public highway to all or certain road vehicles if so justified by an emergency.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10550", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10551", "mode": "normal", "text": "421.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10552", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may drive a vehicle to which a restrictive or prohibitive measure under section 419 or 420 applies, during such periods and in such locations as are determined under the said sections.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10553", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10554", "mode": "normal", "text": "422.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10555", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may drive a road vehicle in a race with another vehicle, or for a wager or a stake except in the case of a rally conducted in conformity with the standards prescribed in a regulation made or approved by the Minister of Education, Recreation and Sports pursuant to the Act respecting safety in recreation and sports ( chapter S-3.1", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10556", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10557", "mode": "normal", "text": "423.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10558", "mode": "normal", "text": " Subject to section 224, no person may drive a road vehicle equipped with turned on white lights projecting a light beam toward the rear.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10559", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10560", "mode": "normal", "text": "424.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10561", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle must, at night or whenever atmospheric conditions require it, turn on the headlights and integrated lights of his vehicle. The first paragraph also applies to a cyclist with respect to the lights with which his bicycle must be equipped.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10562", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10563", "mode": "normal", "text": "425.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10564", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle must dim the lights on the front of his vehicle at all times when he is less than 150 metres from a vehicle approaching in the opposite direction, when he is less than 150 metres behind another vehicle that he is following or when he is moving on a highway that is sufficiently lighted. However, the driver of a motorcycle or moped is required to dim the lights on the front of his vehicle during the day only when he is less than 15 metres behind another vehicle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10565", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10566", "mode": "normal", "text": "426.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10567", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle built after 1973 may not carry more passengers than there are seating positions equipped with seat belts installed by the manufacturer. If the seating positions in a road vehicle are not all equipped with seat belts installed by the manufacturer, the driver of the vehicle may not carry more passengers than there are seats available for passengers to sit. In the case of a bus that is not used for the transportation of school children, the driver may carry more passengers than there are seats available", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10568", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10569", "mode": "normal", "text": "427.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10570", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may drive a road vehicle if the front seat is occupied by more than three persons or if more than two persons are seated in the front of a vehicle equipped with chair seats.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10571", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10572", "mode": "normal", "text": "428.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10573", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may occupy a trailer or semi-trailer in motion or tolerate such practice. Where a trailer or a semi-trailer is specially designed and equipped for the transportation of persons, it may be used for that purpose in parades or other popular events provided the highway used is closed to all other traffic.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10574", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10575", "mode": "normal", "text": "429.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10576", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may get on, in, off or out of a road vehicle in motion or tolerate such practice.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10577", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10578", "mode": "normal", "text": "430.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10579", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may open the door of a road vehicle until the vehicle is stopped and he has ascertained that it can be done in safety.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10580", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10581", "mode": "normal", "text": "431.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10582", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may leave the door of a road vehicle open except to take on or discharge passengers or to load or unload property.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10583", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10584", "mode": "normal", "text": "432.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10585", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a bus or minibus must, when taking on or discharging passengers, stop his vehicle on the extreme right of the roadway, on the shoulder or in the zones provided for that purpose. Before doing so, the driver must make sure that it can be done safely, and if intending to stop the vehicle on the shoulder, that the shoulder is in good condition.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10586", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10587", "mode": "normal", "text": "433.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10588", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may ride on the running board or on any outer part of a vehicle in motion, or ride in the box or dump body of a vehicle in motion, or tolerate such a practice. However, a person may, in order to perform his duties, stand on any outer part of a vehicle designed for such use.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10589", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10590", "mode": "normal", "text": "434.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10591", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may hang on to, or be pulled or pushed by, a moving road vehicle, and no driver may tolerate such a practice.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10592", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10593", "mode": "normal", "text": "435.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10594", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle shall not make his tires squeal, except in case of necessity. In addition to public highways, this section applies on private roads open to public vehicular traffic, as well as on land occupied by shopping centres and other land where public traffic is allowed.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10595", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10596", "mode": "normal", "text": "436.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10597", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle shall not brake suddenly, unless compelled to do so for safety reasons.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10598", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10599", "mode": "normal", "text": "437.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10600", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may use a road vehicle for drawing another road vehicle the wheels of which remain on the ground, unless the vehicle is firmly held by a bar.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10601", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10602", "mode": "normal", "text": "438.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10603", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may remove or tow a damaged road vehicle, unless he also removes any object detached from it.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10604", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10605", "mode": "normal", "text": "441.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10606", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may drive a road vehicle on which a tire is equipped with non-skid studs or with any other device that may damage the roadway. The Minister of Transport may, by an order published in the Gazette officielle du Québec", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10607", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10608", "mode": "normal", "text": "442.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10609", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may drive a road vehicle or ride a bicycle if a passenger, an animal or an object is so placed as to obstruct the driver’s view or to interfere with the proper handling of the vehicle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10610", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10611", "mode": "normal", "text": "443.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10612", "mode": "normal", "text": " No occupant of a road vehicle may drink alcoholic beverages or consume cannabis or other drugs, subject to the exceptions provided for by government regulation, in the vehicle. In addition to public highways, this section applies on private roads open to public vehicular traffic, as well as on land occupied by shopping centres and other land where public traffic is allowed.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10613", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10614", "mode": "normal", "text": "444.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10615", "mode": "normal", "text": " At an intersection where there are pedestrian lights, pedestrians must comply therewith. A pedestrian facing a steady, white signal representing a walking figure may cross the roadway. A pedestrian facing a steady, orange hand signal may in no case start across the roadway. A pedestrian facing a flashing signal and having started across the roadway must proceed quickly to the sidewalk or safety zone. When facing a flashing signal with a countdown display, a pedestrian may only start crossing the roadway if he is able to reach the other sidewalk or the safety zone before the signal changes to the orange hand signal.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10616", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10617", "mode": "normal", "text": "445.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10618", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where there are no pedestrian lights, pedestrians must comply with the traffic lights.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10619", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10620", "mode": "normal", "text": "446.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10621", "mode": "normal", "text": " At a pedestrian crosswalk not situated at an intersection regulated by traffic lights, a pedestrian must, before crossing the roadway, ascertain that he can do so in safety.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10622", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10623", "mode": "normal", "text": "447.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10624", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where there are no clearly identified intersections or pedestrian crosswalks in the immediate area, a pedestrian crossing a public highway must yield the right of way to the road vehicles and cyclists moving on it.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10625", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10626", "mode": "normal", "text": "448.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10627", "mode": "normal", "text": " No pedestrian may stand on the roadway to solicit transportation or to deal with the occupant of a vehicle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10628", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10629", "mode": "normal", "text": "449.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10630", "mode": "normal", "text": " No pedestrian may solicit transportation where passing is prohibited.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10631", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10632", "mode": "normal", "text": "450.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10633", "mode": "normal", "text": " If there is an intersection or a pedestrian crosswalk nearby, a pedestrian may cross a public highway only at such a place.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10634", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10635", "mode": "normal", "text": "451.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10636", "mode": "normal", "text": " A pedestrian must cross the roadway perpendicularly to its axis. A pedestrian may cross the roadway diagonally only if authorized to do so by a peace officer or school crossing guard, or by a sign or signal.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10637", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10638", "mode": "normal", "text": "452.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10639", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where there is a sidewalk bordering the roadway, a pedestrian must use it. Where it is impossible to use the sidewalk, a pedestrian may walk alongside the curb on the roadway after ascertaining that he can do so in safety.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10640", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10641", "mode": "normal", "text": "453.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10642", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where there is no sidewalk bordering a roadway, a pedestrian must walk along the side of the roadway or on the shoulder and in the direction opposite to that of vehicular traffic after ascertaining that he can do so in safety. Despite the first paragraph, a pedestrian may walk in the same direction as traffic to avoid crossing the roadway more than once over a short distance or to walk on the lighted side of the public highway or the side where the shoulder is wider, after making sure it can be done safely.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10643", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10644", "mode": "normal", "text": "454.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10645", "mode": "normal", "text": " This division applies to the transportation of school children except transportation carried out under a permit issued to that effect by the Commission des transports du Québec and for which a bus or a minibus other than a bus or a minibus used for the transportation of school children within the meaning of a government regulation made under the Transport Act ( chapter T-12", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10646", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10647", "mode": "normal", "text": "455.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10648", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a bus or minibus used for the transportation of school children shall ascertain that every person is seated before setting his vehicle in motion and remains seated while it is in motion.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10649", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10650", "mode": "normal", "text": "456.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10651", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a bus or minibus used for the transportation of school children must, when stopping to take on or discharge persons, give warning by turning on the flashing red lights and activate the compulsory stop signal referred to in section 229 and keep them in operation until the persons have reached safety. The first paragraph does not apply to such a vehicle when it is used exclusively for transporting school children who require a wheelchair.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10652", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10653", "mode": "normal", "text": "457.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10654", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where two or more buses or minibuses used for the transportation of school children are stopped in single file and the driver of one of the vehicles is taking on or discharging persons, the driver of every following bus or minibus must turn on the flashing red lights of his own vehicle and activate the compulsory stop signal.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10655", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10656", "mode": "normal", "text": "458.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10657", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a bus or minibus used for the transportation of school children shall not turn on the flashing red lights of his vehicle or activate the compulsory stop signal except in the circumstances set out in sections 456 and 457.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10658", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10659", "mode": "normal", "text": "459.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10660", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may operate the flashing red lights of a vehicle or activate the compulsory stop signal when the vehicle is not used to carry out transportation to which this division applies.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10661", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10662", "mode": "normal", "text": "460.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10663", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a road vehicle or a cyclist who is approaching a bus or minibus used for the transportation of school children with flashing red lights turned on or whose compulsory stop signal has been activated must stop his vehicle more than 5 metres from the bus or minibus and shall not meet or pass it until the flashing red lights are turned off and the compulsory stop signal has been retracted, and he ascertains that he can do so in safety. The first paragraph does not apply to the driver of a road vehicle or a cyclist meeting a bus or minibus used for the transportation of school children on an adjacent roadway separated by a median strip or by any other raised physical device.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10664", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10665", "mode": "normal", "text": "461.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10666", "mode": "normal", "text": " The second paragraph of section 426 and sections 455 to 460 apply, at all times, to the transportation of persons under 18 years of age by bus or minibus usually used for the transportation of school children within the meaning of a government regulation made under the Transport Act ( chapter T‐12", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10667", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10668", "mode": "normal", "text": "462.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10669", "mode": "normal", "text": " For the purposes of this division and unless the context indicates otherwise, The axle load may be expressed as the sum of the units of mass measured under each outside wheel or under each wheel of an axle or of the axles included in one category. The total loaded mass may be expressed as the aggregate of the axle loads.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10670", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10671", "mode": "normal", "text": "463.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10672", "mode": "normal", "text": " No owner or lessee of an outsized vehicle or operator subject to Title VIII.1 who is responsible for an outsized vehicle may allow that vehicle to be driven before he has obtained a special permit issued for that purpose. The special permit shall be issued by the Minister of Transport on the conditions and subject to the formalities established by regulation and on payment of the duties and fees prescribed by regulation. However, no special permit may be issued except to authorize the driving of a vehicle that is outsized because of its construction, the addition of equipment, its forming a road train, or of the indivisible nature of its load. The Minister may delegate the exercise of a power under the second paragraph to a public servant or employee of the Ministère des Transports or to any other person or body the Minister designates. Where the applicant cannot meet the conditions referred to in the second paragraph and where justified by exceptional circumstances, a special permit may be issued by the Minister under section 633 on the conditions and on payment of the duties fixed by him.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10673", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10674", "mode": "normal", "text": "464.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10675", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may drive an outsized vehicle unless he carries with him the special permit.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10676", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10677", "mode": "normal", "text": "465.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10678", "mode": "normal", "text": " The holder of a special permit is liable for any damage caused to the public highways as a result of the use of an outsized vehicle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10679", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10680", "mode": "normal", "text": "466.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10681", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where a peace officer has reasonable grounds to believe that a road vehicle or a combination of road vehicles is an outsized vehicle, he may stop the vehicle or combination of vehicles and require the driver to allow it to be weighed or, as the case may be, facilitate its measurement. Furthermore, the peace officer may require the vehicle or combination of vehicles to be driven to a location where it can be weighed or measured, provided it is not over 15 kilometres from the place of interception.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10682", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10683", "mode": "normal", "text": "467.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10684", "mode": "normal", "text": " The axle load and the total loaded mass of a road vehicle or combination of road vehicles are determined by means of devices designed for that purpose, approved by the Minister of Transport and used in the manner he determines. The fact that a measuring device has been approved by the Minister of Transport and used in the manner he has determined is proof, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, that the device has determined accurately the mass under a wheel, the axle load or the total loaded mass at the time the offence is alleged to have been committed.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10685", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10686", "mode": "normal", "text": "468.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10687", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where a peace officer has established that a road vehicle or combination of road vehicles is an outsized vehicle, he may require it to be driven to a suitable place and held at the expense of the owner, or of the operator in the case of a heavy vehicle, until it is made to conform to the norms of this Code, or until the driver in possession of a special permit. Every driver must comply with the peace officer’s requirement.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10688", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10689", "mode": "normal", "text": "469.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10690", "mode": "normal", "text": " The part of the load removed to bring an outsized vehicle into conformity with this Code remains the responsibility of the operator of a heavy vehicle or the owner of the load.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10691", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10692", "mode": "normal", "text": "470.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10693", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10694", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10695", "mode": "normal", "text": "471.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10696", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may drive or allow to be driven a road vehicle carrying a load Subparagraphs 1, 2 and 3 apply on highways under the administration of or maintained by the Ministère des Ressources naturelles et de la Faune.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10697", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10698", "mode": "normal", "text": "472.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10699", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where a peace officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the load of a road vehicle may present a hazard, he may require that the vehicle be impounded in a suitable place, at the expense of the owner or the operator of a heavy vehicle until the situation has been corrected. Every driver must comply with the peace officer’s requirement.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10700", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10701", "mode": "normal", "text": "473.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10702", "mode": "normal", "text": " No owner or lessee of a road vehicle or operator of a heavy vehicle shall allow a road vehicle or combination of road vehicles to be operated if its load or equipment exceeds its width, including the width of its mandatory accessories, or exceeds its length by more than 1 metre at the front or 2 metres at the rear. However, a special permit may be issued Subject to the conditions the Government may set by regulation, this section does not apply to equipment on a tool vehicle, an impact attenuator mounted on a road vehicle when the vehicle is used as a protection vehicle, or equipment on a public utility vehicle. For the purposes of the third paragraph, a public utility vehicle is a road vehicle designed and equipped to provide essential services to a community, including a vehicle used for the maintenance of public highways and of parks, for garbage collection or for the maintenance of a power distribution system.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10703", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10704", "mode": "normal", "text": "474.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10705", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may drive a road vehicle or combination of road vehicles whose load or equipment extends beyond the rear of the road vehicle or combination of road vehicles by more than 1 metre at its farthest point unless a red flag or a reflector panel, and, at night, a red light visible from behind and from the sides for not less than 150 metres is installed at the farthest point. The flag or reflector panel and their installation must comply with any standards that may be prescribed by regulation. The devices required under the first paragraph may be replaced by an amber light that meets the standards prescribed by regulation. The devices required under the first paragraph are not necessary when The first paragraph also applies to the operation of a tool vehicle whose equipment extends beyond the front or rear of the vehicle by more than one metre. The prescribed signs or signals must be visible from the front or the rear, as applicable, and from the sides from a distance of not less than 150 metres. If the equipment extends beyond the front of the vehicle, the light must be amber. If part of the equipment extends beyond the vehicle by more than 1.5 metres, an escort vehicle must precede or follow the vehicle, as the case may be, at a distance of not more than 50 metres with its hazard lights flashing. The equipment is considered to extend beyond the tool vehicle when it has a point or a sharp edge that extends by at least 30 cm beyond the front or the rear of the vehicle. The starting point for measuring the part of the equipment that extends beyond the front or the rear of the tool vehicle is the end of the mast or boom to which the fork, bucket or other tool is attached. No person may drive a tool vehicle on a public highway unless the vehicle’s equipment is in a retracted position. The fourth and sixth paragraphs do not apply when the vehicle is being used to carry out work on a public highway.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10706", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10707", "mode": "normal", "text": "475.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10708", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10709", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10710", "mode": "normal", "text": "476.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10711", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10712", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10713", "mode": "normal", "text": "477.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10714", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a motorcycle or moped must remain seated on the seat and keep hold of the handlebars. A cyclist must sit astride the bicycle and keep hold of the handlebars.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10715", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10716", "mode": "normal", "text": "478.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10717", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may drive a motorcycle or a moped Subparagraph 1 of the first paragraph applies to cyclists, except when the lane in which the cyclist is travelling is contiguous to a lane reserved for right turns.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10718", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10719", "mode": "normal", "text": "479.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10720", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may drive a motorcycle equipped with a motor having a piston displacement of 125 cc or less or with an electric motor having a power rating of 11 kW or less, drive a moped or ride a bicycle or any other non-motorized vehicle on a limited access highway or on the entrance or exit ramps of such a highway.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10721", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10722", "mode": "normal", "text": "480.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10723", "mode": "normal", "text": " No driver of a motorcycle or moped may carry any other person thereon unless his vehicle is equipped with permanently fixed seats designed for that purpose and with foot-rests fixed on each side of the vehicle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10724", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10725", "mode": "normal", "text": "481.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10726", "mode": "normal", "text": " The passenger of a motorcycle or moped shall be seated facing the handlebars and with both feet on the foot-rests while the vehicle is in motion. No person shall drive a motorcycle or a moped if the passenger is not complying with the requirements of the first paragraph.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10727", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10728", "mode": "normal", "text": "482.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10729", "mode": "normal", "text": " The driver of a motorcycle or moped must keep the white headlight of his vehicle on at all times.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10730", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10731", "mode": "normal", "text": "483.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10732", "mode": "normal", "text": " Drivers of motorcycles or mopeds driving in groups of two or more in one traffic lane must drive in zigzag formation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10733", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10734", "mode": "normal", "text": "484.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10735", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person riding on a motorcycle or moped or in a sidecar must wear a protective helmet that complies with the standards prescribed by regulation. The driver of a motorcycle or moped must also wear visual protection if his protective helmet does not have a visor and he is travelling in a zone where the maximum authorized speed limit is over 50 km/h. Such persons must, if so requested by a peace officer, allow him to examine their protective helmets and visual protection.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10736", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10737", "mode": "normal", "text": "485.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10738", "mode": "normal", "text": " No cyclist may take a passenger unless his vehicle is equipped with a fixed seat for that purpose.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10739", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10740", "mode": "normal", "text": "486.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10741", "mode": "normal", "text": " When riding in groups of two or more, cyclists must keep in single file; in no case may such a file be composed of more than 15 cyclists.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10742", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10743", "mode": "normal", "text": "487.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10744", "mode": "normal", "text": " A cyclist must ride as close as possible to the edge or right side of the roadway and in the same direction as traffic, taking into account the condition of the roadway and the risk of car dooring. A cyclist may also ride on the shoulder in the same direction as traffic. The first paragraph does not apply to a cyclist about to make a left turn, if he is authorized to ride against traffic or in case of necessity.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10745", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10746", "mode": "normal", "text": "488.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10747", "mode": "normal", "text": " All cyclists must comply with all traffic signs and signals.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10748", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10749", "mode": "normal", "text": "489.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10750", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may drink alcoholic beverages while riding a bicycle. The same applies to the consumption of cannabis or any other drug, subject to the exceptions provided for by government regulation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10751", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10752", "mode": "normal", "text": "490.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10753", "mode": "normal", "text": " Before turning, a cyclist must signal his intention without interruption and for a sufficient distance, unless doing so endangers his safety. When turning right, a cyclist must extend his left forearm vertically upwards or extend his right arm horizontally. When turning left, he must extend his left arm horizontally.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10754", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10755", "mode": "normal", "text": "491.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10756", "mode": "normal", "text": " Subject to section 479, no person may ride a bicycle on a public highway on which the maximum speed allowed is over 50 km/h unless", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10757", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10758", "mode": "normal", "text": "492.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10759", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10760", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10761", "mode": "normal", "text": "493.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10762", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may allow farm animals on or across a public highway unless the animals are escorted by two persons, each of them holding a red flag in full view. The Government may, by regulation, determine conditions under which a person may allow farm animals across a public highway without being required to comply with the first paragraph.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10763", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10764", "mode": "normal", "text": "494.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10765", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may allow farm animals on or across a public highway at night.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10766", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10767", "mode": "normal", "text": "495.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10768", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may allow farm animals on or across a limited access highway.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10769", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10770", "mode": "normal", "text": "496.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10771", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may ride a horse", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10772", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10773", "mode": "normal", "text": "497.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10774", "mode": "normal", "text": " Subject to a by-law adopted by a municipality, no person may, in residential areas where the speed limit is 50 km/h or less, conduct snow-removal operations on a public highway with a snowblower whose net mass exceeds 900 kg except under the supervision of a person walking in front of the vehicle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10775", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10776", "mode": "normal", "text": "498.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10777", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may dispose of, deposit or abandon any objects or substances on a public highway, unless authorized to do so by the person responsible for the maintenance of that highway.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10778", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10779", "mode": "normal", "text": "499.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10780", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may use skates, skis, skateboard or a toy vehicle on the roadway.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10781", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10782", "mode": "normal", "text": "500.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10783", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may occupy the roadway, shoulder or any other part of the right of way of or approaches to a public highway or place a vehicle or obstacle thereon so as to obstruct vehicular traffic on the highway or access to such a highway, except where so authorized by law. A peace officer may remove or cause to be removed at the expense of the owner any thing used in contravention of this section. The peace officer may also seize such a thing; the provisions respecting things seized in the Code of Penal Procedure ( chapter C‐25.1 For the purposes of this section, a public highway includes a road being used as an alternate route for traffic diverted from a public highway even if the alternate route is situated on private property, and a road under the administration of or maintained by the Ministère des Ressources naturelles et de la Faune.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10784", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10785", "mode": "normal", "text": "501.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10786", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Replaced).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10787", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10788", "mode": "normal", "text": "502.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10789", "mode": "normal", "text": " Subject to sections 378 and 379, no person may, on private property, use a lighting system or flashing or rotating lights, whether installed on a vehicle or not, that may interfere with the vision of drivers of road vehicles on a public highway or that may distract them. The owner of the premises may not tolerate the use of such a system or of such lights.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10790", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10791", "mode": "normal", "text": "503.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10792", "mode": "normal", "text": " The person responsible for the maintenance of a public highway may, if he believes on reasonable grounds that a lighting system or flashing or rotating lights are used on private property in contravention of section 502, issue a notice to the owner requiring him to remove or modify the system or lights within 48 hours. If the contravener fails to comply with the notice, the person responsible for the maintenance of the highway may enter the property and remove the lighting system or lights at the owner’s expense.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10793", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10794", "mode": "normal", "text": "504.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10795", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every cyclist who contravenes any of sections 346, 349, 350, 358.1, 359 to 364, 367 to 371, 402, 404 to 406, 408 to 411 and 421, the second paragraph of section 424 or any of sections 442, 443.1, 443.2, 460, 477 to 479, 485 to 492.1, 496.6, 496.9 and 496.10 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10796", "code": "80 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10797", "mode": "normal", "text": "100.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10798", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10799", "mode": "normal", "text": "505.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10800", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every pedestrian who contravenes any of sections 444 to 453.2 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10801", "code": "15 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10802", "mode": "normal", "text": "30.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10803", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10804", "mode": "normal", "text": "506.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10805", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes section 324, the second paragraph of section 325, any of sections 336, 366 and 381 to 385, paragraph 9 of section 386, section 387 or any of sections 412, 417, 428, 429, 431, 432, 435, 436, 480, 481, 482 and 493 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10806", "code": "60 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10807", "mode": "normal", "text": "120.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10808", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10809", "mode": "normal", "text": "507.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10810", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes any of sections 321, 323, 330, 377 to 380, 403, 425, 437, 438, the first paragraph of section 441 or any of sections 492.2, 494 to 496, 498 and 498.1 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10811", "code": "60 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10812", "mode": "normal", "text": "100.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10813", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10814", "mode": "normal", "text": "508.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10815", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes section 401 or the second paragraph of section 484 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10816", "code": "80 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10817", "mode": "normal", "text": "100.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10818", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10819", "mode": "normal", "text": "509.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10820", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes any of sections 320, 322, 326, 331, 339, 351 to 358, 364.1, 365 and 372 to 376, any of paragraphs 1 to 8 of section 386 or any of sections 388.1, 391, 407, 415, 416, 417.1, 418, 421.1, 473.1, 483, 492.4 to 492.6 and 502, and every person other than a cyclist who contravenes any of sections 361, 411, 421, 424, 442, 443.2, 477, 478 and 479 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10821", "code": "100 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10822", "mode": "normal", "text": "200.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10823", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10824", "mode": "normal", "text": "510.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10825", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes any of sections 326.1, 340 to 342, 345, 347, 348, 388, 389, 395, 396, 406.1, 406.2, 413, 418.2, 418.3, 423, 426, 427, 430, 437.1, 437.2, 440.1, 455, 458 and 459, the second paragraph of section 472, section 473, the second paragraph of section 474.1, section 483.1 and the first or third paragraph of section 484 or section 492.7 or 497 or every person other than a cyclist who contravenes any of sections 335, 346, 349, 350, 358.1, 359, 359.1, 360, 362 to 364, 367 to 371, 402, 404 to 406, 408 to 410, 460 and 496.6 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10826", "code": "200 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10827", "mode": "normal", "text": "300. Every driver of a bus or minibus used for the transportation of school children who contravenes section 426 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10828", "code": "200 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10829", "mode": "normal", "text": "375 and, in the case of a second or subsequent offence, to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10830", "code": "250 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10831", "mode": "normal", "text": "750. Every driver of a heavy vehicle who contravenes the second paragraph of section 472 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10832", "code": "350 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10833", "mode": "normal", "text": "1,050. The driver of a motorcycle or moped carrying a passenger under 16 years of age who contravenes the first paragraph of section 484 is guilty of an offence and is liable to the fine prescribed by the first paragraph of this section.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10834", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10835", "mode": "normal", "text": "511.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10836", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every occupant of a road vehicle other than a driver who contravenes section 443 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10837", "code": "200 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10838", "mode": "normal", "text": "300. Every driver of a road vehicle who contravenes section 443 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10839", "code": "300 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10840", "mode": "normal", "text": "600.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10841", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10842", "mode": "normal", "text": "512.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10843", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes section 327, 422, 433, 434 or 492.8 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10844", "code": "1,000 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10845", "mode": "normal", "text": "3,000. Every driver of a road vehicle who contravenes the second paragraph of section 468 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10846", "code": "700 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10847", "mode": "normal", "text": "2,100.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10848", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10849", "mode": "normal", "text": "513.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10850", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every driver of a heavy vehicle who contravenes a regulatory provision the violation of which constitutes an offence under paragraph 35 of section 621 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10851", "code": "90 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10852", "mode": "normal", "text": "270, ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10853", "code": "175 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10854", "mode": "normal", "text": "525 or ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10855", "code": "350 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10856", "mode": "normal", "text": "1,050 according to the seriousness of the offence as specified by regulation. Every driver who fails to comply with a condition fixed under section 633 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10857", "code": "175 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10858", "mode": "normal", "text": "525. Every holder of a special permit who contravenes a regulatory provision the violation of which constitutes an offence under paragraph 35 of section 621 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10859", "code": "175 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10860", "mode": "normal", "text": "525, ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10861", "code": "350 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10862", "mode": "normal", "text": "1,050 or ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10863", "code": "700 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10864", "mode": "normal", "text": "2,100 according to the seriousness of the offence as specified by regulation. Every holder who fails to comply with a condition fixed under section 633 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10865", "code": "350 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10866", "mode": "normal", "text": "1,050. However, the fine is Every holder of an escort permit who contravenes a regulatory provision the violation of which constitutes an offence under paragraph 20.3 of section 621 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10867", "code": "175 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10868", "mode": "normal", "text": "525, ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10869", "code": "350 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10870", "mode": "normal", "text": "1,050 or ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10871", "code": "700 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10872", "mode": "normal", "text": "2,100 according to the seriousness of the offence as specified by regulation. The period of validity of a special permit or escort permit for a heavy vehicle in respect of which an offence was committed is suspended for a period of three months if the holder of the permit commits a second offence while the permit is valid. If a subsequent offence is committed during the same period of validity, the permit is suspended for three months, whether or not the vehicles covered by the permit were the subject of proceedings. The right to obtain a special permit or escort permit, for the same or another heavy vehicle is, for the operator, subject to the rules governing a second or subsequent offence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10873", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10874", "mode": "normal", "text": "514.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10875", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes either of sections 456 and 457 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10876", "code": "600 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10877", "mode": "normal", "text": "2,000.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10878", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10879", "mode": "normal", "text": "515.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10880", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10881", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10882", "mode": "normal", "text": "516.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10883", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes the second paragraph of section 299, section 303.2 or 328, the third paragraph of section 329 or section 496.4 or 496.7 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine which shall be of $30 plus, Every person who", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10884", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10885", "mode": "normal", "text": "517.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10886", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every driver of a vehicle who contravenes section 464 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10887", "code": "175 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10888", "mode": "normal", "text": "525.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10889", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10890", "mode": "normal", "text": "518.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10891", "mode": "normal", "text": " The owner of a road vehicle travelling on a public highway whose net mass or number of axles, as the case may be, exceeds what is entered in the register kept by the Société pursuant to section 10 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10892", "code": "300 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10893", "mode": "normal", "text": "600 for the first offence and to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10894", "code": "600 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10895", "mode": "normal", "text": "2,000 for any subsequent offence committed with the same vehicle during the twelve months following the date of conviction for the first offence. Section 467 applies, adapted as required, with respect to the methods used to determine the net mass of a road vehicle and with respect to the probative force thereof. An owner of a road vehicle must, at the request of the Société or a peace officer, furnish the weighing certificate within 10 days of the request to establish the net mass of the vehicle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10896", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10897", "mode": "normal", "text": "519.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10898", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where a road vehicle or combination of road vehicles for which no special permit has been issued is outsized in respect of more than one standard provided in this Code, the driver, the owner or the lessee of the vehicle or the operator of a heavy vehicle cannot be convicted for contravening more than one of such standards.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10899", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10900", "mode": "normal", "text": "520.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10901", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société shall have exclusive jurisdiction to carry out the mechanical inspection of road vehicles and to issue certificates of mechanical inspection and inspection stickers. For that purpose, the Société may, on the conditions it determines, appoint persons authorized to carry out, on its behalf, the inspection of the road vehicles it determines and authorize those persons to issue certificates of mechanical inspection and inspection stickers in respect of those vehicles. If the persons are not members of the personnel of the Société, they must pay the fee prescribed by regulation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10902", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10903", "mode": "normal", "text": "521.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10904", "mode": "normal", "text": " The following road vehicles, subject to section 543.2, must be submitted to mechanical inspection: Subparagraphs 10 and 10.1 apply to vehicles being operated on highways under the administration of or maintained by the Ministère des Ressources naturelles et de la Faune, on private roads open to public vehicular traffic and on land occupied by shopping centres or other land where public traffic is allowed.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10905", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10906", "mode": "normal", "text": "522.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10907", "mode": "normal", "text": " Mechanical inspection is carried out in respect of the various road vehicles, according to the standards and procedures established by regulation and, in the case of a vehicle contemplated in paragraph 10 of section 521, within the time determined by the peace officer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10908", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10909", "mode": "normal", "text": "523.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10910", "mode": "normal", "text": " The owner or driver of a road vehicle contemplated in section 521 must submit the vehicle to the required mechanical inspection and must remit the registration certificate of the vehicle and his licence to the Société or to the peace officer if so requested. The Société or the peace officer must return those documents to their holder once they have been examined.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10911", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10912", "mode": "normal", "text": "524.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10913", "mode": "normal", "text": " The peace officer or the Société, as the case may be, may give a notice indicating the time within which the owner or driver of a road vehicle described in paragraph 10 or 10.1 of section 521 is required to submit his vehicle to a mechanical inspection. No person may, after the expiry of the time allotted, operate the vehicle unless it is proved, to the satisfaction of the Société or a person authorized to perform the inspection of vehicles for the Société, that the vehicle was submitted to a mechanical inspection and that it conforms to this Code. Failure by the owner or driver to comply within the time prescribed constitutes an offence under the provisions of section 523.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10914", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10915", "mode": "normal", "text": "525.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10916", "mode": "normal", "text": " The owner of a modified road vehicle must furnish to the Société, before the mechanical inspection, a description of the modifications described in section 214 which have been made to his vehicle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10917", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10918", "mode": "normal", "text": "526.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10919", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société or a peace officer is authorized to impound a vehicle or to have it impounded at the owner’s expense in order to have it submitted to mechanical inspection.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10920", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10921", "mode": "normal", "text": "527.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10922", "mode": "normal", "text": " Following the mechanical inspection of a road vehicle, the Société or the person authorized to perform the inspection for it shall issue a certificate of mechanical inspection and notify the owner or the driver of the results of the inspection.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10923", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10924", "mode": "normal", "text": "528.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10925", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person authorized to perform the inspection of vehicles for the Société shall without delay forward to it a copy of every certificate of mechanical inspection issued by him.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10926", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10927", "mode": "normal", "text": "529.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10928", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where a certificate of mechanical inspection indicates that a road vehicle conforms to this Code, the Société or the person authorized to perform the inspection for it shall affix an inspection sticker to the vehicle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10929", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10930", "mode": "normal", "text": "530.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10931", "mode": "normal", "text": " A certificate of mechanical inspection attesting that a road vehicle does not conform to this Code shall indicate the minor or major defects, determined by regulation, found in the vehicle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10932", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10933", "mode": "normal", "text": "531.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10934", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where a certificate of mechanical inspection indicates that a road vehicle has a minor defect, the Société or the person authorized to perform the inspection for it shall issue to the owner or the driver of the vehicle a notice enjoining the owner to make the necessary repairs or cause such repairs to be made within 48 hours. At the expiry of that period, no person may put the vehicle back into operation unless it is proved, to the satisfaction of the Société or a person authorized to perform the inspection of vehicles for the Société, that the vehicle conforms to this Code.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10935", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10936", "mode": "normal", "text": "532.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10937", "mode": "normal", "text": " Within the time indicated in the notice issued under section 531, the owner must prove, to the satisfaction of the Société or of a person authorized to perform the inspection of vehicles for the Société, that the defects discovered on his vehicle during the inspection have been repaired by him or by another person and that his vehicle conforms to this Code.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10938", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10939", "mode": "normal", "text": "533.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10940", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where a person authorized to perform the inspection of vehicles for the Société discovers during the inspection of a road vehicle that it has a major defect, he must, without delay, notify the Société.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10941", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10942", "mode": "normal", "text": "534.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10943", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where a certificate of mechanical inspection indicates that a road vehicle has a major defect, no person may put the vehicle back into operation unless it is proved, to the satisfaction of the Société or a person authorized to perform the inspection of vehicles for the Société, that the vehicle conforms to this Code.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10944", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10945", "mode": "normal", "text": "535.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10946", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société or a peace officer may demand the registration certificate of a road vehicle and may remove the registration plate where a certificate of mechanical inspection indicates that the vehicle has a major defect. The Société may exercise the same powers where an owner has failed to submit his vehicle to a mechanical inspection within the time allotted under section 524.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10947", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10948", "mode": "normal", "text": "536.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10949", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société or a peace officer is authorized to impound or have impounded at the owner’s expense a vehicle that was put back into operation in contravention of sections 531 and 534 until it is proved, to the satisfaction of the Société or a person authorized to perform the inspection of vehicles for the Société, that the vehicle conforms to this Code.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10950", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10951", "mode": "normal", "text": "537.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10952", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where the Société or a person authorized to perform the inspection of vehicles for the Société is satisfied with the evidence furnished as proof that a vehicle conforms to this Code, he shall affix an inspection sticker to the vehicle. Every person authorized to perform the inspection of vehicles for the Société shall, without delay, notify it of every inspection sticker he affixes on a vehicle pursuant to the first paragraph.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10953", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10954", "mode": "normal", "text": "538.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10955", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may issue a certificate of mechanical inspection or affix an inspection sticker to a road vehicle unless he is authorized for such purpose by the Société in accordance with section 520.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10956", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10957", "mode": "normal", "text": "539.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10958", "mode": "normal", "text": " No person may issue a certificate of mechanical inspection containing false or inaccurate information on the condition of an inspected vehicle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10959", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10960", "mode": "normal", "text": "540.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10961", "mode": "normal", "text": " A peace officer who has reasonable grounds to believe that the taximeter of a passenger vehicle does not give a reading that corresponds to the scale in force may require that it be submitted to an inspection on a route provided for that purpose.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10962", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10963", "mode": "normal", "text": "541.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10964", "mode": "normal", "text": " The owner or the driver of a passenger vehicle referred to in section 540 must comply with the request of the peace officer and drive the passenger vehicle to the route indicated. The peace officer is authorized to impound the vehicle or to have it impounded at the owner’s expense in order to submit it to an inspection regarding the taximeter.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10965", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10966", "mode": "normal", "text": "542.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10967", "mode": "normal", "text": " If the peace officer making the inspection finds that the taximeter does not give a reading that corresponds to the scale in force, he shall issue a notice to that effect to the owner or the driver of the passenger vehicle. The driver or owner who is issued such a notice shall cease to operate the passenger vehicle and have the taximeter adjusted, repaired or replaced.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10968", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10969", "mode": "normal", "text": "543.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10970", "mode": "normal", "text": " The owner or the driver of a passenger vehicle referred to in section 542 shall not put it back into operation unless it is proved to the satisfaction of a peace officer that the taximeter gives a reading that corresponds to the scale in force. A peace officer is authorized to impound or have impounded at the owner’s expense a passenger vehicle that was put back into operation in contravention of the first paragraph, until that proof is made.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10971", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10972", "mode": "normal", "text": "544.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10973", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes section 528 or 539.3 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10974", "code": "30 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10975", "mode": "normal", "text": "60.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10976", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10977", "mode": "normal", "text": "545.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10978", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes section 531 or 539.5 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10979", "code": "100 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10980", "mode": "normal", "text": "200 for each defect discovered.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10981", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10982", "mode": "normal", "text": "546.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10983", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who contravenes the first paragraph of section 523 or any of sections 534, 538, 538.1, 539, 539.1, 539.7, 539.8 or 543.1.1 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10984", "code": "300 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10985", "mode": "normal", "text": "600. Every driver of a heavy vehicle who contravenes section 523 or 534 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "10986", "code": "350 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "10987", "mode": "normal", "text": "1,050.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10988", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10989", "mode": "normal", "text": "547.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10990", "mode": "normal", "text": " For the purposes of this Code, the Société may admit any relevant evidence that may serve the interests of justice.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10991", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10992", "mode": "normal", "text": "548.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10993", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société may, where provisions applicable to a particular case are lacking, supply any procedure compatible with this Code.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10994", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10995", "mode": "normal", "text": "549.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10996", "mode": "normal", "text": " A document filed in the records of the Société is proof of its content, except on proof to the contrary.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "10997", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10998", "mode": "normal", "text": "550.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "10999", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every decision of the Société rendered under paragraphs 1, 2 and 3 of section 81, section 82, paragraph 2 or 4 of section 83, paragraph 4 of section 109, section 185 or 187.1, paragraphs 1 and 2 of section 188, subparagraph 2 of the first paragraph and the second paragraph of section 189, paragraphs 1, 2, 3 and 5 of section 190, any of sections 191, 191.2, 194, 195.1 and 538.0.1 or the second paragraph of section 543.3.2 must be in writing and give the reasons on which it is based. Where the Société receives an application for the review of a decision referred to in the first paragraph, it must give the applicant the opportunity to present observations. Every decision of the Société denying a review of or upholding a decision under the first paragraph must be in writing and give the reasons on which it is based. The Société shall transmit the decision referred to in this section or the prior notice referred to in section 553 to the person concerned, by giving it to the person or sending it, by any means of transmission providing proof of receipt, to the last address listed for the person in the records of the Société.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11000", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11001", "mode": "normal", "text": "551.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11002", "mode": "normal", "text": " Appeal from a conviction by a person convicted of an offence does not suspend the entry of the number of demerit points corresponding to the offence or a decision made by the Société under section 185, unless the court decides otherwise.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11003", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11004", "mode": "normal", "text": "552.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11005", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where a person suffers from an illness or deficiency or is in a situation described in paragraph 2 or 3 of section 81, paragraph 2 of section 82, paragraph 2 of section 83, paragraph 2 or 3 of section 190 or section 191, the Société may, before rendering a decision, request, by notice, the person to furnish, within the time fixed by the Société which may in no case exceed 90 days, a complementary report on the examination or assessment referred to in section 73, 76.1.2, 76.1.4, 76.1.4.1 or 603. In addition, the Société may request the person to furnish other documents from an institution providing health services under the Act respecting the governance of the health and social services system ( chapter G-1.021 On receipt of the complementary report or, if the person fails to furnish such a report, at the expiry of the period fixed, the Société shall render the decision it deems appropriate.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11006", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11007", "mode": "normal", "text": "553.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11008", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société shall, before making a written decision in respect of which it is required to comply with the obligations prescribed by section 5 of the Act respecting administrative justice ( chapter J‐3 The proposed decision shall become the decision of the Société on the third day following the expiry of such time limit, and shall take effect unless the Société decides otherwise. The time limit prescribed in the first paragraph may be shortened where the decision relates to the suspension of a licence or class of a licence following a proficiency examination. In the event of an interruption of postal service, a decision delivered by another means takes effect on the date fixed by the Société.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11009", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11010", "mode": "normal", "text": "554.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11011", "mode": "normal", "text": " In communicating its decision, the Société must inform the person concerned of the consequences of the decision and of his right to bring a proceeding under section 557 or 560.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11012", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11013", "mode": "normal", "text": "555.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11014", "mode": "normal", "text": " No application for judicial review under the Code of Civil Procedure ( chapter C-25.01", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11015", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11016", "mode": "normal", "text": "556.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11017", "mode": "normal", "text": " A judge of the Court of Appeal may, on an application, summarily annul any decision, order or injunction made or granted contrary to section 555.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11018", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11019", "mode": "normal", "text": "557.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11020", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société may, of its own initiative or on the application of the person concerned, review or cancel any decision it has rendered in respect of which no proceeding has been brought before the Administrative Tribunal of Québec. The Société may also, of its own initiative or on the application of the person concerned, correct any decision containing an error in writing or in calculation or any other formal defect.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11021", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11022", "mode": "normal", "text": "558.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11023", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société may, in the case contemplated in section 557, request a person to return to it any document issued to him, in accordance with the decision it has reviewed, corrected or annulled.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11024", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11025", "mode": "normal", "text": "559.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11026", "mode": "normal", "text": " Where the person refuses or fails to comply with the requirement of section 558, the Société may request a peace officer to take possession of the document. The person must immediately remit the document to the peace officer who requests him to do so and informs him of the reason therefor.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11027", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11028", "mode": "normal", "text": "560.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11029", "mode": "normal", "text": " A decision may be contested before the Administrative Tribunal of Québec if it is", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11030", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11031", "mode": "normal", "text": "561.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11032", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11033", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11034", "mode": "normal", "text": "562.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11035", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11036", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11037", "mode": "normal", "text": "563.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11038", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11039", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11040", "mode": "normal", "text": "564.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11041", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11042", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11043", "mode": "normal", "text": "565.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11044", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11045", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11046", "mode": "normal", "text": "566.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11047", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11048", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11049", "mode": "normal", "text": "567.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11050", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11051", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11052", "mode": "normal", "text": "568.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11053", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11054", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11055", "mode": "normal", "text": "569.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11056", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11057", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11058", "mode": "normal", "text": "570.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11059", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11060", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11061", "mode": "normal", "text": "571.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11062", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11063", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11064", "mode": "normal", "text": "572.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11065", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11066", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11067", "mode": "normal", "text": "573.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11068", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11069", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11070", "mode": "normal", "text": "574.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11071", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11072", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11073", "mode": "normal", "text": "575.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11074", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11075", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11076", "mode": "normal", "text": "576.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11077", "mode": "normal", "text": " The person authorized by a municipal council to enforce the parking by-laws of a municipality may perform the actions that a peace officer is authorized to perform under this chapter if the offence alleged under this Code is a parking infraction.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11078", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11079", "mode": "normal", "text": "577.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11080", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11081", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11082", "mode": "normal", "text": "578.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11083", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11084", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11085", "mode": "normal", "text": "579.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11086", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11087", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11088", "mode": "normal", "text": "580.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11089", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11090", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11091", "mode": "normal", "text": "581.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11092", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11093", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11094", "mode": "normal", "text": "582.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11095", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11096", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11097", "mode": "normal", "text": "583.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11098", "mode": "normal", "text": " Failure to mention, in a statement of offence, the number of demerit points entailed by a conviction or a mistake in such mention, does not prevent the Société from entering the appropriate number of demerit points in the file of the person concerned.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11099", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11100", "mode": "normal", "text": "584.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11101", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11102", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11103", "mode": "normal", "text": "585.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11104", "mode": "normal", "text": " A payment is deemed to have been made once the proper sum is paid in cash or otherwise to the prosecuting party or another person designated by him. The payment is deemed to have been made by the defendant in respect of whom the statement of offence has been served.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11105", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11106", "mode": "normal", "text": "586.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11107", "mode": "normal", "text": " The person who accepts a payment for an offence for which conviction entails, under this Code, the suspension or cancellation of a licence or the suspension of a registration, must inform the Société.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11108", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11109", "mode": "normal", "text": "587.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11110", "mode": "normal", "text": " The clerk of a court of justice or a person under his authority shall notify the Société of every conviction that entails, under this Code, the suspension or cancellation of a licence or a class thereof as well as any conviction for an offence under section 165 or 166 of this Code or under section 186, 187, 191 or 192 of the Automobile Insurance Act ( chapter A-25 The person referred to in the first paragraph shall also notify the Société If a decision states that the offender’s blood alcohol concentration level at the time of an offence under section 180 was equal to or in excess of 160 mg of alcohol in 100 ml of blood, the notice to the Société must mention it.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11111", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11112", "mode": "normal", "text": "588.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11113", "mode": "normal", "text": " The notice provided for in sections 112, 586 and 587 must be given within 30 days of the date of the judgment of conviction and be accompanied with all the information required by the Société. The notice must be in the form and contain the particulars determined by the Société.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11114", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11115", "mode": "normal", "text": "589.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11116", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every document emanating from the Société evidencing a payment, a blood alcohol concentration level or a conviction in respect of a person is proof of its content, in the absence of any contrary evidence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11117", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11118", "mode": "normal", "text": "590.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11119", "mode": "normal", "text": " Any delay in the transmission of a notice provided for in sections 112, 519.56, 586 and 587 does not prevent the Société from rendering a decision.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11120", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11121", "mode": "normal", "text": "591.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11122", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11123", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11124", "mode": "normal", "text": "592.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11125", "mode": "normal", "text": " The owner of a road vehicle whose name appears in the register of the Société kept pursuant to section 10 may be convicted of every offence against this Code or any municipal traffic or parking by-law committed with the vehicle, unless he proves that, at the time of the offence, the vehicle was in the possession of a third person without his consent. In the case of an offence against any of sections 35, 36, 65, 74, 89, 96 to 102, 105, 168, 171, 299, 303.2, 310, 311, 320 to 324, the second paragraph of section 325, any of sections 326 to 331, 333, 335 to 337, 339 to 377, the first paragraph of section 378, any of sections 379, 395, 396, 401, 402 to 413, 415 to 417.1, 418, 421 to 429, 431 to 443.2, 455 to 460, 464, the second paragraph of section 468, section 470, the second paragraph of section 472, the second paragraph of section 476 or any of sections 477 to 484, 496.4 and 496.7 or against any municipal by-law to the same effect, the owner cannot be convicted unless it is established that he was the driver of the vehicle at the time of the offence or was in the vehicle then driven by his agent. In the latter case, the court may condemn either or both of them. The second paragraph does not apply in the case of an offence observed by means of a photograph or series of photographs taken by a detection system.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11126", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11127", "mode": "normal", "text": "593.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11128", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11129", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11130", "mode": "normal", "text": "594.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11131", "mode": "normal", "text": " A person authorized by the Director of Criminal and Penal Prosecutions may sign a document required for the application of this chapter and certify true a copy of or extract from the document. The signature of that person may be affixed by means of an automatic device or in the form of an engraved, lithographed or printed facsimile.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11132", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11133", "mode": "normal", "text": "595.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11134", "mode": "normal", "text": " The filing of a document attested by the Société which states that the defendant is the owner of the vehicle the registration number of which is indicated on the statement of offence constitutes, failing any evidence to the contrary, proof of such ownership in penal proceedings for an offence under a provision of this Code.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11135", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11136", "mode": "normal", "text": "596.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11137", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11138", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11139", "mode": "normal", "text": "597.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11140", "mode": "normal", "text": " Penal proceedings for an offence under a provision of this Code may be instituted by a municipality if the offence was committed within its territory, excluding any part of the territory covered by an agreement entered into under the second paragraph. Likewise, where an agreement has been entered into for that purpose with the Government, penal proceedings for such an offence may be instituted Fines collected pursuant to this section belong to the prosecutor.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11141", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11142", "mode": "normal", "text": "598.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11143", "mode": "normal", "text": " Proceedings for an offence against this Code committed in the territory of a municipality may be instituted before the competent municipal court. The costs relating to proceedings brought before a municipal court belong to the municipality in which the court has jurisdiction, except any part of the costs remitted by the collector to another prosecuting party under article 345.2 of the Code of Penal Procedure ( chapter C‐25.1", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11144", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11145", "mode": "normal", "text": "599.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11146", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11147", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11148", "mode": "normal", "text": "600.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11149", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11150", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11151", "mode": "normal", "text": "601.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11152", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11153", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11154", "mode": "normal", "text": "602.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11155", "mode": "normal", "text": " Sections 575 to 590 do not apply to proceedings instituted by the cities of Québec and Montréal. The equivalent provisions of the charter of either of the cities mentioned in the first paragraph that apply to contraventions to that charter or to a municipal by-law apply, with the necessary adaptations, to a contravention to this Code.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11156", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11157", "mode": "normal", "text": "603.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11158", "mode": "normal", "text": " A health professional may, according to his field of practice, report to the Société the name, address and state of health of a person 14 years of age or older whom he considers unfit to drive a road vehicle having regard, in particular, to the illnesses, deficiencies and situations incompatible with the driving of a road vehicle established by regulation. For the purposes of this section, health professionals are authorized to disclose to the Société any information revealed to them in the practice of their profession.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11159", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11160", "mode": "normal", "text": "604.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11161", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société may disclose to health care professional who made a report to it under section 603, the decision it has made after receiving the information transmitted by him.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11162", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11163", "mode": "normal", "text": "605.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11164", "mode": "normal", "text": " No action in damages may be brought against a health care professional for having availed himself of section 603.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11165", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11166", "mode": "normal", "text": "606.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11167", "mode": "normal", "text": " In no case may the report referred to in section 603 be used as evidence in any suit or judicial or quasi judicial proceedings, except in proceedings relating to the application of section 560.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11168", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11169", "mode": "normal", "text": "607.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11170", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société, a public police force or a municipality may transmit the accident report referred to in section 173 to any person involved in the accident as driver, passenger, victim of bodily injury, operator of a heavy vehicle or owner of a damaged vehicle or property and to the authorized representative and insurer of any of them or the representative of that insurer. The accident report may also be transmitted to any person whose name appears therein. In the case of an accident report containing inaccurate or incomplete information, or in the absence of any report, the Société may transmit to any person referred to in the first paragraph any information permitting the identification of any person involved in the accident or his insurer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11171", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11172", "mode": "normal", "text": "608.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11173", "mode": "normal", "text": " For the purposes of paragraph 9 of section 521 or of a recall campaign for which it received a notice from the Department of Transport of Canada or the Department of the Environment of Canada, the Société may transmit to either of those departments or the Ministère des Transports du Québec as well as to the manufacturers and automobile dealers concerned, any information permitting the identification of the owners of the vehicles that are recalled.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11174", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11175", "mode": "normal", "text": "609.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11176", "mode": "normal", "text": " With the exception of a report under section 603, the Société may transmit to the persons, departments and agencies responsible for the application of the legislation on road traffic, compensation of victims of automobile accidents, and highway safety, any information concerning holders of licences or permits issued under this Code as well as the person in whose name a road vehicle is registered by the Société, where the transmission of that information is necessary for the application of that legislation outside Québec. The Société may also transmit to the persons, departments and agencies referred to in the first paragraph any information it holds concerning an owner or operator of a heavy vehicle or a driver under their responsibility, who is under the authority of those persons, departments or agencies.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11177", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11178", "mode": "normal", "text": "610.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11179", "mode": "normal", "text": " Any information concerning the person in whose name registration of a road vehicle is effected by the Société may be transmitted by the Société to a person requesting it as the owner of the vehicle concerned. The Société may also transmit to an insurer or the Insurance Crime Prevention Bureau the names and the present or the previous addresses of present and past owners of a road vehicle, as well as any information concerning the vehicle’s registration history, within the scope of an inquiry carried out at the time a claim is made to an insurer. Information referred to in the second paragraph which is personal information may only be so transmitted where it is needed for an inquiry relating to the theft of a road vehicle or a fraud in respect of a road vehicle. The information must be dealt with confidentially by the persons to whom it is released. It may only be disclosed to persons who need it for the above purposes. No person may use it for any other purposes than the inquiry. The information must be destroyed by the insurer or the Insurance Crime Prevention Bureau at the end of the inquiry or not later than one year after the date on which it was received.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11180", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11181", "mode": "normal", "text": "611.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11182", "mode": "normal", "text": " Sections 607 and 609 apply notwithstanding sections 53 and 59 of the Act respecting Access to documents held by public bodies and the Protection of personal information ( chapter A-2.1", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11183", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11184", "mode": "normal", "text": "612.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11185", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11186", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11187", "mode": "normal", "text": "613.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11188", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11189", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11190", "mode": "normal", "text": "614.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11191", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11192", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11193", "mode": "normal", "text": "615.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11194", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11195", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11196", "mode": "normal", "text": "616.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11197", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11198", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11199", "mode": "normal", "text": "617.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11200", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11201", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11202", "mode": "normal", "text": "618.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11203", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Government may by regulation", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11204", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11205", "mode": "normal", "text": "619.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11206", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Government may by regulation", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11207", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11208", "mode": "normal", "text": "620.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11209", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Government may by regulation", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11210", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11211", "mode": "normal", "text": "621.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11212", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Government may by regulation The publication requirement set out in section 8 of the Regulations Act ( chapter R‐18.1", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11213", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11214", "mode": "normal", "text": "622.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11215", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Government may, by regulation, prescribe standards with respect to the transportation of dangerous substances on a public highway, a private road open to public vehicular traffic, land occupied by shopping centres and other roads where public traffic is allowed. The regulation may, in particular,", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11216", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11217", "mode": "normal", "text": "623.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11218", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11219", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11220", "mode": "normal", "text": "624.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11221", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société may by regulation The fees prescribed under subparagraphs 3 and 5 of the first paragraph may vary according to the form in which the licence is issued or according to whether or not the licence bears the photograph of the holder.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11222", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11223", "mode": "normal", "text": "625.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11224", "mode": "normal", "text": " The regulations made under subparagraphs 9 to 10.2, 12, 13 and 16 to 16.2 of the first paragraph of section 624, and the regulations made under subparagraph 11 of the first paragraph of that section where they concern cases of exemption from or reduction of fees determined under those subparagraphs, are subject to government approval.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11225", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11226", "mode": "normal", "text": "626.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11227", "mode": "normal", "text": " A municipality may by by-law or, where the law so authorizes, by ordinance Regional county municipalities shall exercise the regulatory powers provided for in this section only in regional parks. Any by-law or ordinance passed under subparagraph 14 of the first paragraph shall, within 15 days after it is passed, be sent to the Minister of Transport. The Minister of Transport may disallow all or part of the by-law or ordinance at any time. In such a case, the by-law or ordinance or the part of either that is disallowed ceases to have effect on the date a notice of disallowance is published in the Gazette officielle du Québec", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11228", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11229", "mode": "normal", "text": "627.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11230", "mode": "normal", "text": " Notwithstanding any contrary or inconsistent provision of a general law or special Act, every by-law, resolution or, where the law so authorizes, every ordinance passed or issued by a municipality relating to the means or systems of vehicular transport under the jurisdiction of the Commission des transports du Québec, vehicle construction, heavy vehicle traffic, the traffic of vehicles carrying dangerous substances and the use of vehicles elsewhere than on public highways must, in order to have effect, be approved by the Minister of Transport. This section does not apply to remunerated passenger transportation by automobile governed by the Act respecting remunerated passenger transportation by automobile ( chapter T-11.2", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11231", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11232", "mode": "normal", "text": "628.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11233", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Minister of Transport may approve the whole or only a part of a by-law, resolution or ordinance referred to in section 627. He may also withdraw all or part of any approval given under that section. In such a case, the by-law, resolution or ordinance or part thereof from which approval has been withdrawn ceases to have effect on the date fixed in a notice of the withdrawal of approval published in the Gazette officielle du Québec. The Minister of Transport may remove any sign or signal relating to a by-law, resolution or ordinance which he has not approved or from which he has withdrawn approval, and replace those signs or signals by signs or signals he deems appropriate.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11234", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11235", "mode": "normal", "text": "629.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11236", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Minister of Transport or the Société may, according to law, enter into an agreement with any government, department, or body respecting any matter referred to in this Code. An agreement under this section may exempt any person from the application of part of this Code. The Société shall be responsible for the implementation of such an agreement.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11237", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11238", "mode": "normal", "text": "630.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11239", "mode": "normal", "text": " An agreement under section 629 may also provide that a penalty under this Code becomes applicable in the case of an indictable offence or an offence for which a number of demerit points is prescribed by regulation on a conviction by a court of a jurisdiction that is a party to the agreement for a substantially equivalent offence. The penalty prescribed in the case of failure to pay fine following conviction for an offence under this Code may also be rendered applicable by such an agreement with respect to conviction for a substantially equivalent offence. The agreement must include descriptions of the offences and applicable penalties.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11240", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11241", "mode": "normal", "text": "631.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11242", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Government may, by regulation, adopt the necessary measures to give effect to an agreement under section 629. The publication requirement set out in section 8 of the Regulations Act ( chapter R-18.1", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11243", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11244", "mode": "normal", "text": "632.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11245", "mode": "normal", "text": " Any person convicted by a court of the jurisdiction that is a party to an agreement under section 629 may apply to a judge of the Court of Québec for a ruling on the applicability of the penalty prescribed for the offence for which he was convicted. Sections 561 to 573, adapted as required, apply to an application under this section.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11246", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11247", "mode": "normal", "text": "633.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11248", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Minister of Transport may, after consultation with the Société, issue a special permit authorizing the operation of a road vehicle or combination of road vehicles to an applicant who does not meet the requirements of a regulation made under subparagraph 20 of the first paragraph of section 621, provided exceptional circumstances justify issuing the permit, issuing the permit is conducive to promoting highway transportation without compromising highway safety or issuing the permit allows If the Minister grants the permit, the Minister shall determine the conditions attached to it, the fee exigible and the amount and nature of the security guaranteeing payment of any damage that the operation of such a vehicle or combination of vehicles may cause to a public highway. The Minister may delegate the exercise of a power under this section to a public servant or an employee of the Minister’s department or to any other person or any body the Minister designates.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11249", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11250", "mode": "normal", "text": "634.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11251", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Minister of Transport may classify public highways for the purposes of this Code.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11252", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11253", "mode": "normal", "text": "635.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11254", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11255", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11256", "mode": "normal", "text": "636.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11257", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every peace officer recognizable as such at first sight may, in the performance of his duties under this Code, agreements entered into under section 519.65 and the Act respecting owners, operators and drivers of heavy vehicles ( chapter P-30.3", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11258", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11259", "mode": "normal", "text": "637.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11260", "mode": "normal", "text": " A peace officer is authorized to confiscate and remit to the Société any unauthorized plate or unauthorized validation sticker, any plate to which is affixed an unauthorized sticker or any unauthorized inspection sticker or unauthorized identification sticker. For the purposes of the first paragraph,", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11261", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11262", "mode": "normal", "text": "638.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11263", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every peace officer who, in accordance with this Code, confiscates or takes an object from its owner shall immediately inform the Société of the name and address of the person who was in possession of the object.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11264", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11265", "mode": "normal", "text": "639.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11266", "mode": "normal", "text": " If the nature of the object confiscated or taken allows it, except in the case contemplated in the second paragraph of section 252, the Société may, subject to the conditions and in the cases prescribed by regulation, return the object to its owner if he files an application therefor within 90 days after the date the object was confiscated or taken. The object is returned at the owner’s expense.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11267", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11268", "mode": "normal", "text": "640.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11269", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Société shall dispose of every object confiscated or taken at the expiry of a period 90 days following the date it was confiscated or taken.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11270", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11271", "mode": "normal", "text": "641.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11272", "mode": "normal", "text": " The public servants of the Sûreté du Québec designated by the Director General of the Sûreté du Québec to carry out the provisions of this Code are peace officers responsible for its application with respect to driving schools and the following road vehicles:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11273", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11274", "mode": "normal", "text": "642.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11275", "mode": "normal", "text": " The owner of a stolen road vehicle is required to give immediate notice of the theft of his vehicle and, as the case may be, of its recovery, to the Société. A peace officer, on being informed of the theft of a road vehicle, must do what is necessary to inform the Société.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11276", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11277", "mode": "normal", "text": "643.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11278", "mode": "normal", "text": " The owner of a road vehicle who contravenes the first paragraph of section 642 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "11279", "code": "100 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "11280", "mode": "normal", "text": "200.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11281", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11282", "mode": "normal", "text": "644.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11283", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every person who makes, permits or tolerates the fraudulent use of a document issued by the Société is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "11284", "code": "300 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "11285", "mode": "normal", "text": "600.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11286", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11287", "mode": "normal", "text": "645.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11288", "mode": "normal", "text": " (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11289", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11290", "mode": "normal", "text": "646.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11291", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every driver of a heavy vehicle who contravenes a regulatory provision the violation of which constitutes an offence under subparagraph 8 of the first paragraph of section 622 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "11292", "code": "90 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "11293", "mode": "normal", "text": "270, ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "11294", "code": "175 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "11295", "mode": "normal", "text": "525 or ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "11296", "code": "350 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "11297", "mode": "normal", "text": "1,050 according to the seriousness of the offence as determined by regulation. The person who offers dangerous substances for transport, the owner or operator of a heavy vehicle and the carrier of dangerous substances who contravenes a regulatory provision the violation of which constitutes an offence under subparagraph 8 of the first paragraph of section 622 is guilty of an offence and is liable to a fine of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "11298", "code": "175 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "11299", "mode": "normal", "text": "525, ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "11300", "code": "350 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "11301", "mode": "normal", "text": "1,050 or ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "11302", "code": "700 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "11303", "mode": "normal", "text": "2,100 according to the seriousness of the offence as determined by regulation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11304", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11305", "mode": "normal", "text": "647.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11306", "mode": "normal", "text": " Any fine prescribed under a by-law or ordinance passed under subparagraphs 4, 5 and 8 of the first paragraph of section 626 must be equal to the fine prescribed by this Code for an offence of the same nature. The fine must be ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "11307", "code": "175 to ", "type": "math", "version": 1}, {"id": "11308", "mode": "normal", "text": "525 where the offence prescribed by a municipal by-law made under paragraph 5 of the said section involves a truck or tool vehicle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11309", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11310", "mode": "normal", "text": "648.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11311", "mode": "normal", "text": " The sums collected under this Code are paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund, within the time and according to the terms and conditions fixed by the Minister of Finance, except", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11312", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11313", "mode": "normal", "text": "649.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11314", "mode": "normal", "text": " Every municipality is required to transmit, to the Société, within 90 days of the end of each year, a detailed report recording for the past year the accidents, within the meaning of section 167, that have occurred in its territory and the offences that entailed the collection of sums of money under paragraph 1 of section 648.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11315", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11316", "mode": "normal", "text": "650.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11317", "mode": "normal", "text": " The Minister of Transport is responsible for the carrying out of this Code, except the provisions respecting traffic supervision coming under the jurisdiction of the Minister of Public Security and the provisions respecting proceedings for offences coming under the jurisdiction of the Attorney General.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11318", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11319", "mode": "normal", "text": "651.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11320", "mode": "normal", "text": " The licences, permits, certificates and registration plates issued under the Highway Safety Code ( chapter C-24.1", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11321", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11322", "mode": "normal", "text": "652.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11323", "mode": "normal", "text": " The proficiency certificates issued under the Highway Safety Code ( chapter C-24.1", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11324", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11325", "mode": "normal", "text": "653.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11326", "mode": "normal", "text": " For the purposes of section 204, every person convicted of an offence under any of sections 142 to 142.3 of the Highway Safety Code ( chapter C-24.1", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "11327", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "11328", "mode": "normal", "text": "654.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "11329", "mode": "normal", "text": " Demerit points attributable to an offence committed before 1 December 1987 are counted as demerit points for the purposes of the cancellation of a licence or for a suspension of the right to obtain a licence under this Code.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0