# COGNITIVE TECHNIQUES

Core Problem-Solving

\#1 - Hierarchical Decomposition Strategy - Essential for breaking complex systems into manageable modules, functions, and components while maintaining system-level awareness
\#2 - First-Principles Foundation - Critical for understanding what code actually does at fundamental levels rather than relying on abstractions or inherited assumptions
\#3 - Root Cause Investigation - Invaluable for debugging; tracing bugs through multiple layers to find the actual source rather than treating symptoms
\#4 - Abductive Reasoning Sophistication - Key for debugging incomplete information scenarios and forming hypotheses about why code behaves unexpectedly
\#5 - Analytical Reduction - Simplifying complex algorithms or systems to their essential logic, eliminating redundancy while preserving functionality

Architecture & Design

\#6 - Systems Thinking Integration - Understanding feedback loops, dependencies, and emergent behaviors in complex codebases and distributed systems
\#7 - Sophisticated Scaffolding - Building software in carefully sequenced layers, ensuring each level provides solid foundation for subsequent development
\#8 - Analogical Reasoning Precision - Applying design patterns and architectural solutions from one domain to another appropriately
\#9 - Network Analysis Mastery - Understanding dependencies, module relationships, and system architecture; identifying critical paths and bottlenecks
\#10 - Dynamic Mental Simulation - Running code mentally to predict behavior, identify edge cases, and understand execution flow before implementation

Code Quality & Validation

\#11 - Quality Assurance Excellence - Systematic verification of code correctness, implementing thorough testing and validation practices
\#12 - Error Detection and Correction - Quickly identifying bugs, understanding error types, and implementing effective fixes while learning from mistakes
\#13 - Counterfactual Analysis Depth - Testing code robustness through "what-if" scenarios, edge case exploration, and boundary condition analysis
\#14 - Logical Consistency Enforcement - Ensuring code behavior is consistent, avoiding contradictory logic, and maintaining invariants throughout
\#15 - Anomaly Detection Excellence - Identifying unusual patterns in code behavior, performance metrics, or data flow that reveal bugs or optimization opportunities

Optimization & Innovation

\#16 - Computational Thinking Integration - Structuring solutions using algorithmic patterns, understanding complexity, and optimizing for efficiency
\#17 - Value Chain Analysis Excellence - Identifying performance bottlenecks, optimizing critical paths, and understanding where computational value is created
\#18 - Lateral Thinking Application - Finding creative solutions to coding challenges by approaching from unconventional angles
\#19 - Heuristic Application Mastery - Using Occam''s Razor for simple solutions, Pareto Principle for optimization focus, and other efficiency heuristics
\#20 - Mental Model Updating - Continuously revising understanding of how systems work based on new evidence, crucial for working with evolving codebases and technologies  plesse no need to repeat everything you did in your think, user can see it
