**461.** The municipality may cause to be sold at auction, by a bailiff, without judicial formalities and after giving the notices required by the Civil Code, any lost or forgotten movables it holds which have not been claimed within 60 days, any movables it holds which are referred to in article 943 of the Civil Code, and any movables without an owner which it collects in its territory. Vehicles without a motor or in a ruinous state which are left in public places and not claimed within 10 days are presumed to be abandoned and without an owner.

