**860.** The legislative provisions listed in the Schedule I are repealed to the extent indicated therein.

**861.** Every provision, in force on 31 December 1987, of a general law, special Act, letters patent, proclamation, order, order in council, ordinance, regulation, by-law or resolution shall be inoperative to the extent that it is inconsistent with this Act.

**862.** Any provision of the charter of a municipality which on 31 December 1987 is inoperative pursuant to the second or fourth paragraph of section 2 of the Cities and Towns Act ( chapter C-19

**863.** Any provision of a general law or special Act providing that a by-law, resolution or order of a municipality must be submitted for approval to the qualified voters of that municipality or of another municipality is considered to refer to Title II of this Act. The qualified voters at the referendum are those determined under Title II of this Act, even if the provision contemplated in the first paragraph refers to them as “electors”, “municipal electors”, “elector-proprietors” or “proprietors” or other similar expressions.

**864.** If the provision contemplated in the first paragraph of section 863 provides that the consultation of the qualified voters may or must be preceded by an application from a certain number of them, only those entitled to have their names entered on the referendum list shall be considered and the provisions of this Act which concern the manner in which the rights of a legal person may be exercised, the manner in which qualified voters entitled to have their names entered on the referendum list and the applications demanding that a referendum poll be held are counted, apply, adapted as required, to an application contemplated in this paragraph. If the required number of such applications is reached, a referendum poll shall be held without registration procedure. For the purposes of this section, the date of reference used to determine who are the qualified voters is the date on which the person for whom they are intended receives the required number of applications.

**865.** Every reference in any general law or special Act to a provision replaced or repealed by this Act is a reference to the corresponding provision of this Act, if any.

**866.** Every member of the council of a municipality in office on 31 December 1987 shall remain in office until his term ends in accordance with this Act.

**867.** Every municipality governed by the Municipal Code of Québec ( chapter C‐27.1 The by-law shall be passed and transmitted to the Minister not later than 30 September 1987. If approved by the Minister, it must, in order to have effect, come into force not later than on 31 December 1987. The secretary-treasurer shall transmit to the Minister, as soon as practicable, a certified copy of the public notice by which the by-law is published and, where it is not included in the notice, a certified copy of the certificate of publication of the notice.

**868.** All the offices of member of the council of the municipality in which the by-law passed under section 867 is in force on 31 December 1987 shall be open for nominations at the regular election contemplated in section 869. One half of the offices held by councillors shall again be open for nominations at a regular election to be held two years later. Those offices shall be determined by means of a drawing of lots carried out by the secretary-treasurer at a sitting of the council held during the six-month period preceding the publication of the notice of election. The other half of the offices held by councillors and the office of mayor shall be open for nominations at a regular election to be held two years after the election provided for in the second paragraph. Subsequently, a regular election shall be held every second year. The alternation of offices open for nominations, introduced by the second and third paragraphs, shall continue for such regular elections until the first general election held after the repeal of the by-law passed under section 867.

**869.** The day fixed as polling day for the first regular election which must be held in accordance with this Act in a municipality is the first Sunday of November of the calendar year in which the next fixed-date election for all the offices of member of the council or, as the case may be, for the office of mayor is to be held under the Act governing the municipality in that respect on 31 December 1987. If necessary, the term of any member of the council in office on 31 December 1987 shall be extended or reduced to comply with the first paragraph, subject to a premature ending of his term under this Act and subject to section 869.1. If the periodicity of elections observed by the municipality on 31 December 1987 and that provided for by the Act governing the municipality in that respect at that date do not coincide, the calendar year referred to in the first paragraph is the year in which, according to the periodicity observed by the municipality, the next fixed-date election for all the offices of member of the council or, as the case may be, for the office of mayor is to be held.

**870.** The division of the territory of a municipality for election purposes and the composition of its council, as they stand on 31 December 1987, remain unchanged until they are changed in accordance with this Act.

**871.** Section 44 applies only from the election referred to in section 869 to a municipality whose territory, on 31 December 1987, is not divided for election purposes and whose council consists, on that date, of less than six offices of councillor.

**872.** Sections 62 and 63 and paragraph 3 of section 300 do not apply to any person who, on 31 December 1987 legally holds, at the same time, the office of member of the council of a municipality and an office referred to in the said provisions, until that plurality ceases. Plurality does not cease at the expiry of the person’s term in one office if that term is renewed.

**873.** Paragraphs 1 and 2 of section 300 do not apply during the current term of a member of the council of a municipality in office on 31 December 1987 unless, pursuant to the legislative provisions then applicable he was not eligible when he was elected or he subsequently ceased to be eligible under those provisions.

**874.** The second and third paragraphs of section 318 do not apply to a member of the council in office on 31 December 1987 whose term of office, pursuant to those paragraphs, should have ended before 1 January 1988. His term of office shall end on the day on which the judgment declaring him disqualified becomes a res judicata

**875.** No ground for disqualification which ceases to exist by reason of the coming into force of this Act may be invoked to have a person declared disqualified for office as a member of the council of the municipality, unless the judicial proceedings for that purpose are brought before 1 January 1988.

**876.** Until the list of electors of a municipality governed by the Municipal Code of Québec ( chapter C-27.1

**877.** Until the list of electors prepared under this Act comes into force, the list of electors or the schedule to the valuation roll used at the last election is deemed to be the list in force of the municipality or, as the case may be, of the electoral district or ward.

**878.** Until a tariff established under section 580 comes into force, the tariff established by the Minister of Municipal Affairs, Regions and Land Occupancy under section 303 of the Cities and Towns Act ( chapter C‐19

**879.** (Repealed).

**880.** Until a tariff established under section 584 comes into force, the tariff established by the Government under section 482 of the Election Act ( chapter E-3.2

**881.** The Government, the Minister of Municipal Affairs, Regions and Land Occupancy, the chief electoral officer, any municipality or any person may perform any act contemplated in this Act after 23 June 1987 but before 1 January 1988, including making or publishing an order, regulation, by-law, resolution or ordinance, in order to give effect to the provisions of this Act as soon as practicable after the latter date. No act referred to in the first paragraph may become binding before 1 January 1988.

**882.** Proceedings brought before 31 December 1987 in accordance with any provision amended, replaced or repealed by this Act may be continued in accordance with that provision as it stood on that date where it cannot be continued in accordance with this Act, in particular by reason of the time limits fixed by this Act or any other Act. The first paragraph does not apply to proceedings referred to in section 12 or 13 of the Interpretation Act ( chapter I-16 Any vacancy in the office of a member of the council occurring before 1 January 1988 shall be filled in accordance with the provisions in force on 31 December 1987.

**883.** All the orders, orders in council, letters patent, proclamations, regulations, by-laws, resolutions and ordinances in force on 31 December 1987 and issued or made under a provision replaced or repealed by this Act remain in force until the date fixed for the cessation of their effect, until their object is achieved or until they are replaced or repealed by this Act. Where such is the case, they are deemed to have been issued or made under the corresponding provision of this Act. Notwithstanding the foregoing, they are without effect if their object is to fix the hours of the poll, fix the term of the members of the council, order that the poll be held at several places or that the vote be taken by voice vote or, except for the purposes of section 869.1, fix the first Monday of November as the date of the poll at a regular election.

**884.** Every act performed before 1 January 1988 under any provision replaced or repealed by this Act retains its effects if it is still relevant. Where such is the case, it is deemed to have been performed under the corresponding provision of this Act.

**885.** Every person in office on 31 December 1987 and appointed under a provision replaced or repealed by this Act shall remain in office until the expiry of the period for which he was appointed or until he is replaced or otherwise ceases to hold office according to law. Where such is the case, the person is deemed to have been appointed under the corresponding provision of this Act. Nothing in the first paragraph shall prevent a person from continuing to hold office notwithstanding the expiry of the period for which he was appointed, until he is replaced or re-appointed, if the law so provides.

**886.** Not later than 30 September each calendar year, the chief electoral officer and the Commission de la représentation shall make a report on their respective activities under this Act for their preceding fiscal year to the President of the National Assembly. The report shall be tabled in the National Assembly within 30 days of its receipt if the Assembly is in session or, if it is not sitting, within 30 days of the opening of the next session or of resumption.

**887.** The Minister of Municipal Affairs, Regions and Land Occupancy is responsible for the administration of this Act.

**888.** Sections 38, 106 to 109, 139 and 166 and the first paragraph of section 564 apply notwithstanding the second paragraph of section 11 of the Act respecting Access to documents held by public bodies and the Protection of personal information ( chapter A-2.1 Sections 261, 579, 659.0.1 and 659.0.2 apply notwithstanding section 9 of the said Act. The third and fourth paragraphs of section 659 apply notwithstanding the provisions of the said Act to which those paragraphs refer and notwithstanding section 71 of the said Act.

**889.** (Omitted).
', '{"voice": {"openai": "alloy"}, "sttLocale": "auto", "ttsService": "openai", "showAllLocaleVoice": false}', '2026-03-22 22:42:06.821+00', '2026-04-03 10:21:58.391+00', '2026-04-03 10:21:58.391+00', NULL, NULL, '{}', '', NULL, '{"root": {"id": "root", "type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "5", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "6", "mode": "normal", "text": "You are an world renowned lawyer, specializing in the analysis and evaluation of legislative texts with regard to the **Quebec Act respecting elections and referendums in municipalities**.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "7", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8", "mode": "normal", "text": "      ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "9", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "10", "mode": "normal", "text": "Your role is to provide answer to user request, based on the text of the law below.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "11", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "12", "mode": "normal", "text": "---", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "13", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "15", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "16", "mode": "normal", "text": "# Act respecting elections and referendums in municipalities", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "17", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "19", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "20", "mode": "normal", "text": "**1.** This Title applies to all municipalities except regional county municipalities, northern, Cree or Naskapi villages or any municipality whose council, according to the Act establishing or governing the municipality, is not composed of persons elected by its citizens.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "21", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "23", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "24", "mode": "normal", "text": "**2.** An election shall be held every four years for all the offices on the council of a municipality.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "25", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "27", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "28", "mode": "normal", "text": "**3.** The polling date is the first Sunday in November.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "29", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "31", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "32", "mode": "normal", "text": "**4.** Every municipality having a population of 20,000 or over on 1 January of the calendar year preceding the year in which a general election is to be held must divide its territory into electoral districts. The same rule applies to any other municipality that, on 31 December 1987, was required to divide or had divided its territory into electoral districts.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "33", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "35", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "36", "mode": "normal", "text": "**5.** Any municipality that is not required to divide its territory into electoral districts may submit itself to that requirement by by-law of its council passed by a two-third majority of its members, which must, under pain of absolute nullity, come into force during the second calendar year preceding that in which a general election must be held. As soon as practicable after the coming into force of the by-law, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall transmit a certified copy thereof to the Commission de la représentation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "37", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "39", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "40", "mode": "normal", "text": "**6.** A municipality that is required, by operation of law or after voluntarily submitting itself to the requirement, to divide its territory into electoral districts for the purposes of a general election shall be under the same requirement for the purposes of all subsequent general elections.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "41", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "43", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "44", "mode": "normal", "text": "**7.** Where a municipality having a population of under 20,000 is required to divide its territory into electoral districts, it may exempt itself from that requirement by a by-law of its council passed by a two-thirds majority of its members. Subject to a requirement by operation of law or to the municipality voluntarily submitting itself again to the requirement of dividing its territory into electoral districts, the municipality is no longer required to so divide its territory for the purposes of any general election held from the second calendar year following the calendar year in which the by-law referred to in the first paragraph comes into force. As soon as practicable after the coming into force of the by-law, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall transmit a certified copy thereof to the Commission de la représentation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "45", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "47", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "48", "mode": "normal", "text": "**8.** For election purposes, a municipality shall divide its territory into electoral districts only.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "49", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "51", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "52", "mode": "normal", "text": "**9.** The number of electoral districts of a municipality shall be The population of a municipality is its population on the date of passage, as provided in section 14, of the draft by-law dividing its territory into electoral districts.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "53", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "55", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "56", "mode": "normal", "text": "**10.** The Minister of Municipal Affairs, Regions and Land Occupancy may, upon an application, authorize a municipality to divide its territory into a smaller number of electoral districts than the minimum number or into a greater number than the maximum number. The Minister shall transmit a copy of the authorization to the Commission de la représentation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "57", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "59", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "60", "mode": "normal", "text": "**11.** The electoral districts shall be delimited in such a manner as to ensure that each has the greatest possible socioeconomic homogeneity, taking into account criteria such as physical barriers, population trends, parish and borough boundaries, size and distance.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "61", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "63", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "64", "mode": "normal", "text": "**12.** Subject to section 12.0.1, each electoral district shall be delimited in such a manner that, according to the document provided for in section 12.1, the number of electors in the district is not more than 15% above or below the quotient obtained by dividing the total number of electors of the municipality by the number of districts. The percentage shall be 25% in the case of a municipality having a population of under 20,000 on the date of passage of the draft by-law dividing its territory into electoral districts. A municipality may make exceptions to the first paragraph; the by-law dividing its territory into electoral districts shall then be submitted to the Commission de la représentation for approval.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "65", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "67", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "68", "mode": "normal", "text": "**13.** For the purposes of this division, the population of a municipality is its population on the date of passage of the draft by-law dividing its territory into electoral districts, and an elector is a person whose name is entered on the permanent list of electors on the date on which the chief electoral officer receives the request referred to in the second paragraph of section 12.1, and a person whose name is entered on the list of electors of the municipality as the owner of an immovable or the occupant of a business establishment.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "69", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "71", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "72", "mode": "normal", "text": "**14.** The council of a municipality required to divide its territory into electoral districts shall, by resolution, after 1 January of the calendar year preceding that in which the general election for which the division is required must be held, pass a draft by-law effecting the division.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "73", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "75", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "76", "mode": "normal", "text": "**15.** The draft by-law shall describe the boundaries of the proposed electoral districts according to the standards established by the Commission de la représentation. It shall, wherever possible, use the names of thoroughfares and mention the number of electors included in each district. The draft by-law shall also include a map or a sketch of the proposed districts. The Commission is not governed by the Regulations Act ( chapter R-18.1 If the draft by-law does not comply with the first or second paragraphs, the municipality must start the procedure for dividing its territory into electoral districts over again, unless it is complying with another measure submitted by the Commission de la représentation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "77", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "79", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "80", "mode": "normal", "text": "**16.** Within 15 days of passage of the draft by-law, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall publish, in a newspaper having general circulation in the municipality, a notice setting forth In addition to or in lieu of the description required under subparagraph 2 of the first paragraph, the notice may include a map or a sketch of the proposed electoral districts.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "81", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "83", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "84", "mode": "normal", "text": "**17.** Within 15 days of publication of the notice, every elector may inform the clerk or the clerk-treasurer in writing of his objection to the draft by-law.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "85", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "87", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "88", "mode": "normal", "text": "**18.** The council shall hold a public meeting to hear the persons present in respect of the draft by-law if the number of objections received within the prescribed time is equal to or exceeds", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "89", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "91", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "92", "mode": "normal", "text": "**19.** Not later than ten days before the public meeting, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall publish, in a newspaper having general circulation in the municipality, a notice indicating the place, day, time and purpose of the meeting, and transmit a copy thereof, along with a certified copy of the draft by-law, to the Commission de la représentation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "93", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "95", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "96", "mode": "normal", "text": "**20.** The public meeting does not constitute a sitting of the council. A majority of the members of the council and the clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall attend the meeting. The meeting shall be presided over by the mayor or, where he is unable to act or where the office of mayor is vacant, by one of the council members present designated by them. The designated member may maintain order in the same manner as the chairman of a sitting of the council and has the same powers. The persons present may make representations verbally or table documents. The documents shall be treated as if they had been tabled at a sitting of the council. The clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall draw up the minutes of the meeting.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "97", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "99", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "100", "mode": "normal", "text": "**21.** The council of the municipality shall pass a by-law dividing its territory into electoral districts after the expiry of the time in which electors may make objections to the draft by-law or after the day of the public meeting, as the case may be, but before 1 June of the calendar year preceding that in which the general election for which the division is required is to be held. As soon as practicable after passage of the by-law, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall transmit a certified copy thereof to the Commission de la représentation. On a written recommendation of the Commission de la représentation to the municipality, and if the number of electors is not affected, the council of the municipality may amend a provision of the by-law referred to in the first paragraph in order to correct a clerical error or an error in concordance between the description and the accompanying map or sketch, or to comply with the standards referred to in section 15. The amendment forms an integral part of the by-law, as if it had been adopted with it. The clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall transmit a certified copy of the amended by-law to the Commission without delay.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "101", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "103", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "104", "mode": "normal", "text": "**22.** Where the council is obliged to hold a public meeting in respect of the draft by-law, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer, within 15 days after passage of the by-law, shall publish, in a newspaper having general circulation in the municipality, a notice setting forth In addition to or in lieu of the description required under subparagraph 2 of the first paragraph, the notice may include a map or a sketch of the proposed electoral districts. Within five days of publication of the notice, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall transmit a certified copy thereof to the Commission, with an attestation of its date of publication.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "105", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "107", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "108", "mode": "normal", "text": "**23.** Within 15 days of publication of the notice, every elector may inform the Commission in writing of his objection to the by-law.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "109", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "111", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "112", "mode": "normal", "text": "**24.** The Commission shall inform the municipality in writing of any objection received within the prescribed time.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "113", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "115", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "116", "mode": "normal", "text": "**25.** The Commission shall hold a public meeting to hear the persons present in respect of the by-law, if the number of objections received within the prescribed time is equal to or exceeds the number needed under section 18 to require the holding of a public meeting of the council in respect of the draft by-law.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "117", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "119", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "120", "mode": "normal", "text": "**26.** Not later than ten days before the public meeting, the Commission shall publish, in a newspaper having general circulation in the municipality, a notice indicating the place, day, time and purpose of the meeting and transmit a copy thereof to the municipality.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "121", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "123", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "124", "mode": "normal", "text": "**27.** The municipality is entitled to be heard at the public meeting held by the Commission. The persons present may make representations verbally or table documents.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "125", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "127", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "128", "mode": "normal", "text": "**28.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "129", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "131", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "132", "mode": "normal", "text": "**29.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "133", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "135", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "136", "mode": "normal", "text": "**30.** Subject to section 34, the by-law dividing the territory of the municipality into electoral districts comes into force on 31 October of the calendar year preceding that in which the general election for which the division is required is to be held.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "137", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "139", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "140", "mode": "normal", "text": "**31.** The Commission shall divide into electoral districts the territory of a municipality whose council has not passed a by-law to that effect within the time prescribed in section 21. However, even after the expiry of that time, the council may pass the by-law as long as the Commission has not carried out the division. The Commission shall also make the division where, after holding a public meeting in respect of the by-law passed by the council, it considers that the division required by the by-law is not to be effected. Before making a decision under this section, the Commission may hold a public meeting to hear the persons present in respect of the division into districts it proposes or the by-law of the municipality, as the case may be.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "141", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "143", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "144", "mode": "normal", "text": "**32.** The Commission shall transmit to the municipality a certified copy of the decision whereby the division into electoral districts is effected or the division provided for in the by-law of the municipality is maintained.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "145", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "147", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "148", "mode": "normal", "text": "**33.** The Commission shall publish a notice of its decision in a newspaper having general circulation in the municipality. The notice shall set forth If the Commission divides the territory into electoral districts, the notice must also contain a description of the boundaries of the electoral districts. In addition to or in lieu of the description, the notice may include a map or a sketch of the electoral districts.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "149", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "151", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "152", "mode": "normal", "text": "**34.** The division of the territory into electoral districts by the Commission comes into force on the day of the publication of the notice. The same applies if the decision of the Commission to maintain the division provided for in the by-law of the municipality is made after the date specified in section 30.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "153", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "155", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "156", "mode": "normal", "text": "**35.** The costs relating to a division into electoral districts effected by the Commission shall be borne by the municipality.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "157", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "159", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "160", "mode": "normal", "text": "**36.** The division into electoral districts applies for the purposes of the first general election following the coming into force of the by-law of the municipality or of the decision of the Commission, as the case may be. It also applies for the purposes of any subsequent by-election held before the second general election following the coming into force of the by-law or decision.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "161", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "163", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "164", "mode": "normal", "text": "**37.** Except on a question of jurisdiction, no application for judicial review under the Code of Civil Procedure ( chapter C-25.01 A judge of the Court of Appeal may, on an application, summarily annul any decision, order or injunction made or granted contrary to the first paragraph.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "165", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "167", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "168", "mode": "normal", "text": "**38.** The Commission or any of its members or employees may, in the performance of their duties, examine any document held by a municipality and obtain copy of it free of charge.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "169", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "171", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "172", "mode": "normal", "text": "**39.** The chairman of the Commission shall coordinate and distribute the work of the members of the Commission. Any member of the Commission designated by the chairman for that purpose may exercise any power or perform any duty indicated by the chairman.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "173", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "175", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "176", "mode": "normal", "text": "**40.** The Commission may, in respect of a municipality having a population of under 20,000, delegate the exercise of any power or the performance of any duty it indicates to any person it designates for that purpose. The instrument of delegation shall be published in the Gazette officielle du Québec.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "177", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "179", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "180", "mode": "normal", "text": "**41.** A municipality that is not required to divide its territory into electoral districts may maintain the division into wards existing on 31 December 1987. The council of such a municipality may, by by-law, order that the territory of the municipality cease to be divided for election purposes, on the terms and conditions it determines. The clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall transmit a certified copy of the by-law to the chief electoral officer as soon as possible after its coming into force.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "181", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "183", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "184", "mode": "normal", "text": "**42.** The council of a municipality whose territory is divided into electoral districts shall be composed of the mayor and one councillor for each electoral district.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "185", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "187", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "188", "mode": "normal", "text": "**43.** The council of a municipality whose territory is divided into wards shall be composed of the mayor and the number of councillors prescribed for each ward by the Act, letters patent, by-law or other juridical instrument governing the municipality in that respect.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "189", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "191", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "192", "mode": "normal", "text": "**44.** The council of a municipality whose territory is not divided for election purposes shall be composed of the mayor and six councillors.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "193", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "195", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "196", "mode": "normal", "text": "**45.** On the application of a municipality whose territory is not divided for election purposes, the Minister of Municipal Affairs, Regions and Land Occupancy may fix, on the terms and conditions he determines, a number of councillors under or over six. In similar manner, the Minister may order the number of councillors of the municipality again fixed at six. The Minister shall publish a notice of his decision in the Gazette officielle du Québec.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "197", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "199", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "200", "mode": "normal", "text": "**46.** The council of a municipality whose territory is not divided for election purposes shall assign a number to the seat of each councillor. The council of a municipality whose territory is divided into wards shall assign a number to the seat of each councillor in each ward for which there is more than one councillor. Until the council numbers the seats, each seat shall be numbered according to the alphabetical order of the names of the councillors in office on 31 December 1987 and of the last persons who held the seats that are vacant on that date.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "201", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "203", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "204", "mode": "normal", "text": "**47.** Every person who is of full age and a Canadian citizen, who is neither disqualified from voting under section 53 nor disqualified from voting as a result of a judgment rendered under article 288 of the Civil Code and who meets one of the following two conditions is an elector of a municipality:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "205", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "207", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "208", "mode": "normal", "text": "**48.** The domicile of a person is as provided in the Civil Code for all civil purposes. Notwithstanding the foregoing, a person who has left his principal establishment in Québec for more than one year is deemed to have changed his domicile, except where he carries on duties outside Québec on behalf of the Government of Québec or of Canada.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "209", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "211", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "212", "mode": "normal", "text": "**49.** A detained person retains his domicile notwithstanding his detention.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "213", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "215", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "216", "mode": "normal", "text": "**50.** A person who leaves his domicile temporarily to work or study in the territory of another municipality may be considered as being domiciled either in the territory where his actual domicile is situated or in the territory where he resides for the purposes of his work or studies. A person lodged in a facility maintained by an institution operating a hospital centre, a residential and long-term care centre or a rehabilitation centre within the meaning of the Act respecting the governance of the health and social services system ( chapter G-1.021 A person is deemed to choose to be considered domiciled at the place where he resides rather than at his actual domicile where he makes an application to that effect during the revision of the list of electors or referendum list. The person’s choice shall be valid until it is revoked and as long as the person resides at the same place.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "217", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "219", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "220", "mode": "normal", "text": "**51.** The rules provided in the Civil Code concerning the setting up, against third persons, of acts transferring immovable real rights apply in determining whether a person is the owner of an immovable.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "221", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "223", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "224", "mode": "normal", "text": "**52.** To exercise the right to vote, a person must, at the time of voting, be an elector of the municipality and have his name entered on the list of electors of the municipality. An elector who has obtained an authorization to vote under the first paragraph of section 219 is, after being admitted to vote under the second paragraph of that section, deemed to have his name entered on the list at the place where it should have been entered. A person who is not an elector of the municipality when the person votes in an advance poll solely because that person is not then of full age, but who will have attained full age by polling day, is deemed to be an elector of the municipality.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "225", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "227", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "228", "mode": "normal", "text": "**53.** A person is disqualified from voting in a municipal election if he is convicted of an offence that is a corrupt electoral practice within the meaning of section 645, the Act respecting school elections to elect certain members of the boards of directors of English-language school service centres ( chapter E-2.3 The disqualification shall continue for five years from the day on which the judgment convicting the person becomes a res judicata.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "229", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "231", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "232", "mode": "normal", "text": "**54.** Every person who is an elector of a municipality, or will be such an elector on polling day, may be entered on the list of electors. However, in the case of undivided co-owners of an immovable and of co-occupants of a business establishment, only the co-owner or the co-occupant designated for that purpose pursuant to section 55 is entitled to have his name entered on the list of electors as the owner of the immovable or as the occupant of the business establishment.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "233", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "235", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "236", "mode": "normal", "text": "**55.** Co-owners or co-occupants who are electors or who will be on polling day shall designate, from among themselves, if necessary, by means of a power of attorney signed by a majority of them, a person not otherwise entitled under section 58 to be entered on the list of electors in a higher ranking capacity.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "237", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "239", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "240", "mode": "normal", "text": "**56.** Not later than 22 days before polling day, the returning officer shall give a public notice stating that sole owners or occupants and designated co-owners and co-occupants are entitled to have their names entered on the list of electors and mentioning how they may obtain information on the rules governing the entry of their names on the list of electors. The notice shall invite sole owners and occupants who wish to make a first application for entry or to withdraw the existing entry to transmit to the returning officer, within the prescribed time, the application or a signed writing requesting the withdrawal. The notice shall also invite co-owners and co-occupants who wish to make a first designation or replace the existing designation to transmit to the returning officer, within the prescribed time, the power of attorney.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "241", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "243", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "244", "mode": "normal", "text": "**57.** In no case may the name of a person appear more than once on the list of electors of the municipality.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "245", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "247", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "248", "mode": "normal", "text": "**58.** A person who is an elector in several capacities shall be registered in only one capacity according to the following order of preference: Where several immovables are contemplated in subparagraph 2 or 4 of the first paragraph, the immovable with the highest property value shall be the immovable considered. Where several business establishments are contemplated in subparagraph 3 or 5 of the said paragraph, the business establishment with the highest rental value shall be the business establishment considered.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "249", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "251", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "252", "mode": "normal", "text": "**59.** Every elector whose name is entered on the list of electors of an electoral district or ward is entitled to vote for a candidate for each of the offices of mayor and of councillor of the district or ward.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "253", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "255", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "256", "mode": "normal", "text": "**60.** Every elector whose name is entered on the list of electors of a municipality whose territory is not divided for election purposes is entitled to vote for a candidate for each of the offices of mayor and of councillor of the municipality.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "257", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "259", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "260", "mode": "normal", "text": "**61.** A person is eligible for office as a member of the council of a municipality if he is entitled to have his name entered on the list of electors of the municipality and if he resides in the territory of the municipality.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "261", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "263", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "264", "mode": "normal", "text": "**62.** The following persons are ineligible:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "265", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "267", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "268", "mode": "normal", "text": "**63.** The following persons are also ineligible for office as members of the council of a municipality:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "269", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "271", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "272", "mode": "normal", "text": "**64.** For the purposes of this section, the meaning of the word “ leader ” is the meaning given to that word in section 364. Any person holding the office of leader of a party or any independent candidate at a previous election whose financial report or return of election expenses required under any of sections 408, 419, 479, 483.1, 484, 485 or 492 has not been transmitted within the prescribed time is ineligible until the report or return is transmitted. Where the party no longer exists or the office of leader is vacant, the person who is ineligible under the first paragraph is the last holder of the office of leader of the party. Any person who is not qualified to be elected under subparagraph 1 or 3 of the second paragraph of section 235 of the Election Act ( chapter E-3.3", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "273", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "275", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "276", "mode": "normal", "text": "**65.** Any independent candidate at a previous election who has not paid in full the debts contracted during the term of his authorization in accordance with section 474 is ineligible for four years from his default. Any person who is not qualified to be elected under subparagraph 2 of the second paragraph of section 235 of the Election Act ( chapter E-3.3 Notwithstanding the foregoing, the ineligibility affecting an elected independent candidate shall cease on the day of the transmission of the financial report establishing that the debts have been paid in full where the transmission occurs before the expiry of the four-year period.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "277", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "279", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "280", "mode": "normal", "text": "**66.** Every person disqualified to hold office as a member of the council of a municipality under any of sections 301 to 307 is ineligible for such an office. Every person who, following a judgment that has become res judicata", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "281", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "283", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "284", "mode": "normal", "text": "**67.** A person is ineligible for office as a member of the council of a municipality if he holds office as member of the council of another municipality, or if he is a candidate for such an office or has been declared elected thereto for 30 days or less. Any person who is already holding another office on the council of a municipality is also ineligible for office as a member of the council, except in the event of an election at which the office held by him is open for nominations or ceases to exist. Notwithstanding the first paragraph, any warden of a regional county municipality elected in accordance with section 210.29.2 of the Act respecting municipal territorial organization ( chapter O-9", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "285", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "287", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "288", "mode": "normal", "text": "**68.** The election officers of a municipality include the returning officer, the election clerk and, as the case may be, any assistant, deputy returning officer, poll clerk, member of an identity verification panel, officer in charge of information and order, and every member, secretary and revising officer of a board of revisors and any other person whose services are temporarily required by the returning officer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "289", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "291", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "292", "mode": "normal", "text": "**69.** A person is not qualified to hold office as an election officer of any municipality if he is convicted of an offence that is a corrupt electoral practice within the meaning of section 645, the Act respecting school elections to elect certain members of the boards of directors of English-language school service centres ( chapter E-2.3 The disqualification shall continue for five years from the day on which the judgment convicting the person becomes a res judicata.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "293", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "295", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "296", "mode": "normal", "text": "**70.** The clerk or the clerk-treasurer of the municipality is the returning officer of the municipality ex officio. Where the clerk or the clerk-treasurer is unable or refuses to act or where the office of clerk or clerk-treasurer is vacant, his assistant is the returning officer ex officio. The second paragraph does not apply where an election clerk is in office and he is not unable to act. The Commission may, for cause, dismiss the returning officer after giving him an opportunity to be heard, and designate his substitute.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "297", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "299", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "300", "mode": "normal", "text": "**71.** The returning officer shall ensure that the election is properly conducted and, for that purpose, shall see to the training of the other election officers and direct their work. For that purpose, the returning officer may issue directives that are binding on all the persons to whom they apply.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "301", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "303", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "304", "mode": "normal", "text": "**72.** The returning officer shall appoint an election clerk before issuing the notice of election. Where the returning officer takes office after his predecessor has issued the notice of election, he shall appoint an election clerk as soon as practicable after taking office.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "305", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "307", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "308", "mode": "normal", "text": "**73.** The election clerk shall assist the returning officer in the performance of his duties and, for that purpose, he shall carry out the duties delegated to him by the returning officer. The election clerk shall replace the returning officer if the latter is unable to act or if the office of returning officer is vacant for as long he is so unable or the office remains vacant.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "309", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "311", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "312", "mode": "normal", "text": "**74.** The returning officer may appoint any assistant he considers necessary.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "313", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "315", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "316", "mode": "normal", "text": "**75.** The assistant shall perform the duties delegated to him by the returning officer. The assistant may subdelegate all or part of his duties with the authorization of the returning officer. The person delegating or subdelegating duties may define the territory in which the delegation has effect.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "317", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "319", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "320", "mode": "normal", "text": "**76.** The returning officer shall appoint a deputy returning officer and a poll clerk for each polling station. Where there is only one polling station, the returning officer himself may perform the duties of deputy returning officer and the election clerk may perform the duties of poll clerk.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "321", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "323", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "324", "mode": "normal", "text": "**77.** Where candidates of more than one party authorized under Chapter XIII were elected to the council of a municipality having a population of 100,000 or over at the last general election, the returning officer shall appoint as deputy returning officer and as poll clerk persons recommended by the party with the greatest number of elected candidates and by the party with the second greatest number of elected candidates, respectively. In case of equality between parties for the greatest or second greatest number of elected candidates, their rank for the purposes of the first paragraph is established according to the number of votes obtained by all the candidates of each party. This section does not apply to the deputy returning officer and the poll clerk of the polling station at the office of the returning officer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "325", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "327", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "328", "mode": "normal", "text": "**78.** For the purposes of this section, the meaning of the word “ leader ” is the meaning given to that word in section 364. The recommendation of a party is made by means of a writing signed by the leader of the party or by the person designated by him for that purpose and sent to the returning officer not later than 4:30 p.m. 16 days before polling day. The returning officer may, on reasonable grounds, refuse a recommendation made to him. In such a case, he shall fix a time limit for the sending of a new recommendation by the person who sent the recommendation refused.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "329", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "331", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "332", "mode": "normal", "text": "**79.** If the recommendation is not received within the prescribed time, if the person recommended is not qualified to hold the office, is unable or refuses to act as such, or if the party is no longer authorized, the returning officer shall appoint the person of his choice.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "333", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "335", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "336", "mode": "normal", "text": "**80.** The deputy returning officer shall, in particular,", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "337", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "339", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "340", "mode": "normal", "text": "**81.** The poll clerk shall, in particular, enter in the poll book the particulars relating to the conduct of the polling and assist the deputy returning officer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "341", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "343", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "344", "mode": "normal", "text": "**82.** The returning officer may appoint an officer in charge of information and order for each place where a polling station is situated. He shall do so for every polling place where five or more polling stations are grouped, unless all the polling stations of the municipality are grouped at the same polling place.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "345", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "347", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "348", "mode": "normal", "text": "**83.** The officer in charge of information and order shall, in particular,", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "349", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "351", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "352", "mode": "normal", "text": "**84.** The returning officer may retain, on a temporary basis, the services of any other person he considers necessary for holding the election.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "353", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "355", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "356", "mode": "normal", "text": "**85.** Before taking office, every election officer shall declare under oath that he will perform his duties according to law. The first paragraph does not apply to the returning officer if he is the clerk or the clerk-treasurer or his assistant.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "357", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "359", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "360", "mode": "normal", "text": "**86.** An election officer may not engage in partisan activity on the days on which the officer is to perform his or her duties.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "361", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "363", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "364", "mode": "normal", "text": "**87.** As soon as practicable after making the oath, each election officer shall be registered on a list posted up in the office of the municipality. The name of any election officer who ceases to hold office shall be struck from the list as soon as practicable. Every election officer who has ceased to hold office shall return to the returning officer all the documents and materials pertaining to his functions that he may have in his possession.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "365", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "367", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "368", "mode": "normal", "text": "**88.** Every election officer is entitled to receive remuneration or an expense allowance from the municipality for the duties he performs. The council of the municipality may establish a tariff of remuneration or allowances; it may delegate that power to the executive committee, if any. Any tariff fixing a remuneration or allowance lower than that fixed in the tariff established by the Minister of Municipal Affairs, Regions and Land Occupancy under Title III requires the approval of the Minister. An election officer of a municipality which has not established a tariff or which has not fixed the officer’s remuneration or allowance in the tariff is entitled to the remuneration or allowance fixed in the tariff established by the Minister or, failing that, agreed upon with the returning officer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "369", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "371", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "372", "mode": "normal", "text": "**89.** The chief electoral officer may make recommendations and issue directives to the returning officer regarding the performance of the latter’s duties.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "373", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "375", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "376", "mode": "normal", "text": "**90.** The chief electoral officer may, on request, provide the returning officer with any assistance he may need to perform his duties.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "377", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "379", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "380", "mode": "normal", "text": "**91.** The chief electoral officer may entrust the exercise of any power or any function he indicates that is assigned to him under this Act to such person as he may designate.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "381", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "383", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "384", "mode": "normal", "text": "**92.** A party authorized under Chapter XIII or a ticket recognized under Division III of Chapter VI may designate a person for each polling station where a vote may be cast in favour of one or several of its candidates, and give him a power of attorney to represent the candidate or all the candidates, as the case may be, before the deputy returning officer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "385", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "387", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "388", "mode": "normal", "text": "**93.** An independent candidate may designate a person for each polling station where a vote may be cast in his favour, and give him a power of attorney to represent him before the deputy returning officer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "389", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "391", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "392", "mode": "normal", "text": "**94.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "393", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "395", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "396", "mode": "normal", "text": "**95.** A candidate may be present wherever his representative is authorized to act, assist him in performing his duties or replace him. A candidate who has no representative may act where a representative could act.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "397", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "399", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "400", "mode": "normal", "text": "**96.** An authorized party or a recognized ticket may designate a poll runner for each polling place where there is a polling station at which a vote may be cast in favour of one or several of its candidates, and give him a power of attorney to periodically collect a list of the persons who have already exercised their right to vote. An independent candidate may in the same manner designate a poll runner for each polling place where there is a polling station at which a vote may be cast in his favour. The first two paragraphs do not apply to advance polls.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "401", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "403", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "404", "mode": "normal", "text": "**97.** A person who is convicted of an offence that is a corrupt electoral practice within the meaning of section 645, the Act respecting school elections to elect certain members of the boards of directors of English-language school service centres ( chapter E-2.3 The disqualification shall continue for five years from the day on which the judgment convicting the person becomes a res judicata.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "405", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "407", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "408", "mode": "normal", "text": "**98.** For the purposes of this section, the meaning of the word “ leader ” , in the case of a party, is the meaning given to that word in section 364. The power of attorney shall be signed by the leader of the party or of the ticket, by the independent candidate or by the person designated by the leader or the candidate for that purpose in a writing transmitted to the returning officer. The power of attorney shall be presented to the deputy returning officer. The power of attorney of a representative is valid for the duration of the poll and of the counting of votes taking place at the polling station to which he is assigned. The power of attorney of a poll runner is valid for the whole duration of the poll.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "409", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "411", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "412", "mode": "normal", "text": "**99.** Not later than forty-four days before polling day, the returning officer shall give a public notice setting forth the following particulars: The returning officer shall transmit to the chief electoral officer a certified copy of the notice of election.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "413", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "415", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "416", "mode": "normal", "text": "**100.** The returning officer shall request in writing that the chief electoral officer transmit to him a list of the electors whose names are entered on the permanent list of electors and who are entitled to have their names entered on the municipal list to be used in the election. The request shall be made in the manner determined by the chief electoral officer. It must specify the date on which the qualification to vote of electors must be ascertained, describe the territory concerned by the election and indicate the date on which and form in which the list must be transmitted. The chief electoral officer shall transmit the list requested not later than the date specified in the request. The costs relating to the production of the list, established under section 549 of the Election Act ( chapter E-3.3", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "417", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "419", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "420", "mode": "normal", "text": "**101.** Not later than 30 days before polling day, the returning officer shall draw up the list of electors, adding to the names on the list transmitted by the chief electoral officer the names of the persons entitled to have their names entered on the municipal list by reason of ownership of an immovable or occupancy of a business establishment.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "421", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "423", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "424", "mode": "normal", "text": "**102.** The list shall be prepared according to the situation of the immovables, by thoroughfares, ranges or other sectors, following the numerical order of the immovables, including apartment or room numbers or, failing that, the numerical order of the cadastre.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "425", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "427", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "428", "mode": "normal", "text": "**103.** The list shall contain the name and address of the elector and, so far as it may be obtained, his date of birth. The address of an elector shall be, according to the capacity under which he is entitled to have his name entered on the list, the number of the immovable of his domicile, of the immovable of which he is the owner or of the business establishment of which he is the occupant. The number of the immovable shall include the apartment or room number, if any. If the immovable has no number, the cadastral number shall be used.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "429", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "431", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "432", "mode": "normal", "text": "**104.** The returning officer shall divide the list of electors into polling subdivisions of not more than 500 electors.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "433", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "435", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "436", "mode": "normal", "text": "**105.** After completing the list, the returning officer shall deposit it in the office of the municipality.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "437", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "439", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "440", "mode": "normal", "text": "**106.** Every candidate for the office of mayor is entitled to obtain, on request and free of charge, a maximum of five copies of the list of electors of the municipality. Every candidate for the office of councillor for an electoral district or a ward is entitled to obtain, on request and free of charge, a maximum of five copies of the list of electors of the district or ward. Every candidate for the office of councillor of a municipality whose territory is not divided for election purposes is entitled to obtain, on request and free of charge, not more than two copies of the list of electors of the municipality.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "441", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "443", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "444", "mode": "normal", "text": "**107.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "445", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "447", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "448", "mode": "normal", "text": "**108.** A person who withdraws his nomination after having obtained free copies of the list of electors shall return all copies obtained to the returning officer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "449", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "451", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "452", "mode": "normal", "text": "**109.** Not later than 23 days before polling day, the returning officer shall transmit, free of charge, one copy of the list of electors to each party authorized under Chapter XIII or ticket recognized under Division III of this chapter. Each party or ticket whose authorization or recognition is withdrawn and which obtained free copies of the list of electors must return all copies obtained to the returning officer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "453", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "455", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "456", "mode": "normal", "text": "**110.** Where a poll must be held, the list of electors of the municipality or, as the case may be, of the electoral district or ward shall be revised. Where no poll is to be held, the list may be revised by decision of the returning officer. Where the holding of a poll ceases to be necessary following the end of the period for filing nomination papers, the returning officer shall decide whether the revision is to be continued or interrupted. If he decides to interrupt the revision, he shall give public notice thereof as soon as practicable. If no revision is to be carried out or if the revision is interrupted, the returning officer shall notify the Chief Electoral Officer in writing without delay.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "457", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "459", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "460", "mode": "normal", "text": "**111.** The returning officer shall establish a board of revisors. The returning officer may establish several boards of revisors and apportion and coordinate their work.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "461", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "463", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "464", "mode": "normal", "text": "**112.** Not later than 22 days before polling day, the returning officer shall determine the place where each board of revisors will sit. The place must, insofar as is practicable, be accessible to handicapped persons.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "465", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "467", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "468", "mode": "normal", "text": "**113.** The returning officer shall, not later than 22 days before polling day, inform each party authorized under Chapter XIII or each ticket recognized under Division III of this chapter and each independent candidate concerned of his decision.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "469", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "471", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "472", "mode": "normal", "text": "**114.** Each board of revisors shall be composed of three revisors appointed by the returning officer. The returning officer may be a member of a board.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "473", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "475", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "476", "mode": "normal", "text": "**115.** In the case of a municipality having a population of 100,000 or over, if the council is composed of candidates elected at the last general election from more than one party authorized Chapter XIII, the returning officer shall appoint as revisors a person recommended by the party which elected the greatest number of candidates and another person recommended by the party which elected the second greatest number of candidates. In the case of an equal number of candidates being elected from each party, the rank of the parties for the purposes of the first paragraph is established according to the aggregate of the votes obtained by the candidates of each party.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "477", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "479", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "480", "mode": "normal", "text": "**116.** For the purposes of this section, the word “ leader ” has the meaning assigned by section 364. A party shall make its recommendation by means of a writing signed by the leader of the party or by the person designated by him for that purpose and sent to the returning officer within the time prescribed by the returning officer. The returning officer may, on reasonable grounds, refuse a recommendation made to him. In such a case, he shall fix a time limit for the sending of a new recommendation by the person who sent the recommendation refused.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "481", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "483", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "484", "mode": "normal", "text": "**117.** The returning officer shall appoint a person of his choice if the recommendation has not been received within the prescribed time, if the person recommended is not qualified to hold the office or is unable or refuses to do so, or if the party is no longer authorized.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "485", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "487", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "488", "mode": "normal", "text": "**118.** The returning officer shall appoint the chairman and the vice-chairman of the board of revisors from among its members. The returning officer shall be the chairman of the board of which he is a member. A member recommended by an authorized party may not be appointed chairman of a board of revisors. The member recommended by the authorized party which elected the greatest number of candidates at the last general election shall be appointed vice-chairman of the board.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "489", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "491", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "492", "mode": "normal", "text": "**119.** The returning officer may appoint a secretary to the board of revisors, whose chief duties shall be to draw up notices of hearings and summonses, to assist the board in the performance of its work and to record all decisions of the board.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "493", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "495", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "496", "mode": "normal", "text": "**120.** The returning officer may appoint any revising officer he considers necessary, whose chief duties shall be to notify notices of hearings and summonses and to gather, at the request of the board of revisors, any information relevant to the making of a decision.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "497", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "499", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "500", "mode": "normal", "text": "**121.** Before the beginning of the work of the board of revisors, the returning officer shall provide the revisors with No mention of the date of birth of electors shall be made on the copy deposited for examination.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "501", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "503", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "504", "mode": "normal", "text": "**122.** The board of revisors shall sit on the days and at the times fixed by the returning officer, subject to the second paragraph of section 132, during the period beginning on the day on which the public notice of revision is published and ending on the tenth day before polling day. The returning officer shall, not later than 22 days before polling day, notify each party authorized under Chapter XIII or each ticket recognized under Division III of this chapter and each independent candidate concerned of his decision. The chairman of the board of revisors may, after consulting with the returning officer, extend the board’s sitting hours and add sitting days. The chairman shall inform the returning officer of his decision and the returning officer shall notify the authorized parties, the recognized tickets and the independent candidates concerned.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "505", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "507", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "508", "mode": "normal", "text": "**123.** Two revisors shall constitute a quorum of the board of revisors.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "509", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "511", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "512", "mode": "normal", "text": "**124.** Every question submitted to the board of revisors shall be decided by a majority vote. In the event of a tie-vote, the chairman or, in his absence, the vice-chairman shall have a casting vote.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "513", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "515", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "516", "mode": "normal", "text": "**125.** Not later than 22 days before polling day, the returning officer shall give a public notice setting forth Where the notice is given before the end of the period for filing nomination papers, it may indicate that the list will be revised only if the holding of a poll makes revision mandatory.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "517", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "519", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "520", "mode": "normal", "text": "**126.** Not later than five days before the last day set for making applications for entry, striking off or correction, the returning officer shall send each person whose name is entered on the list of electors to be revised a notice reproducing the particulars concerning that person which appear on the list, including the particulars specified in subparagraphs 3, 3.1 and 4 of the first paragraph of section 125, and send to each address provided by the Chief Electoral Officer under the second paragraph of section 100.1 for which no elector’s name is entered on the list of electors to be revised and which is within the territory of the municipality or within the district or ward whose electoral list is to be revised, a notice including the particulars specified in subparagraphs 3, 3.1 and 4 of the first paragraph of section 125 and indicating that no electors’ names are entered on the list. Notices to be sent to persons at the same address may be combined in one notice. No mention of the date of birth of electors is made in the notice. If two or more boards of revisors are established, the only particulars provided for in subparagraph 3 of the first paragraph of section 125 that are to be included in the notice are those concerning the board responsible for the revision of the part of the list that includes the name of the person to whom the notice is sent or that would include the name of the elector if a name were entered for the address to which the notice is sent.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "521", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "523", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "524", "mode": "normal", "text": "**127.** Where the returning officer has reasonable grounds to believe that a person whose name is not entered on the list of electors would be entitled to have it entered thereon, that a person whose name is entered on the list is not entitled to have it entered thereon or that a particular entered in respect of the person is inaccurate, he may notify the person and indicate the procedure to be followed to have his name entered, struck off or corrected, as the case may be.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "525", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "527", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "528", "mode": "normal", "text": "**128.** Any person whose name is not entered on the list of electors when it could be may apply to the competent board of revisors to have his name entered on the list. An application to have one’s name struck off the list of electors may be submitted by any person In a case referred to in subparagraph 2 of the second paragraph, the striking off may apply only for the purposes of a municipal poll. In a case referred to in subparagraph 3 of the second paragraph, a person’s application to have his name struck off must be accompanied by an application to have his name entered on the list of electors if the person wishes to exercise his right to vote. Where two boards are each competent to hear one of the applications, the board before which a first application is made becomes competent to hear the other application. That board shall notify the returning officer of its decision concerning the part of the list that is not within its competence, and the returning officer shall send the notice to the other board.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "529", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "531", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "532", "mode": "normal", "text": "**129.** If an elector who is entitled to have his name entered on the part of the list of electors for a polling subdivision finds that the name of a person who is not entitled to be entered on that part has been entered thereon, he may apply to the competent board of revisors to have that person’s name struck off the list.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "533", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "535", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "536", "mode": "normal", "text": "**130.** An elector may apply to the competent board of revisors to have an error in the entry of his name, address or date of birth corrected.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "537", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "539", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "540", "mode": "normal", "text": "**131.** An application for entry, striking off or correction, other than an application under section 129, may be made by the spouse or a relative of the person entitled to make the application, or by a person who is cohabiting with the person. For the purposes of the first paragraph, the word “relative” means a father, mother, or one of the parents, grandfather, grandmother, father-in-law or step-father, mother-in-law or step-mother, brother, sister, brother-in-law, sister-in-law, son, daughter, grandson, granddaughter, son-in-law or daughter-in-law.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "541", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "543", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "544", "mode": "normal", "text": "**132.** Every application must be made to the board of revisors The Chief Electoral Officer may determine standards applicable to the choice and use of the means referred to in subparagraph 2 of the first paragraph. The returning officer must provide that the board of revisors must hear the applications made in person on at least two separate days, not later than two days before the last day the board of revisors sits in accordance with the first paragraph of section 122. The sittings must be held between 8:00 a.m. and 10:00 p.m. and last for at least three hours, and one of them must be held between 5:00 p.m. and 8:00 p.m.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "545", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "547", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "548", "mode": "normal", "text": "**133.** Every application to a board of revisors shall be made under oath. The board of revisors may require the person making an application to submit to it any proof necessary for the making of a decision. However, in the case of an application to have the name of a person domiciled in the territory of the municipality entered, the board shall require from the person making the application the former address of the domicile of the person in respect of whom the application is being made as well as two documents, one showing the name and birthdate of the person in respect of whom the application is being made, the other showing the name of that person and the address of the person’s domicile.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "549", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "551", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "552", "mode": "normal", "text": "**134.** The board of revisors shall examine the applications made to it as soon as they are received, and shall decide them immediately in all cases where it is possible to do so. It shall also verify the information provided to its members by the returning officer under section 121.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "553", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "555", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "556", "mode": "normal", "text": "**135.** The board of revisors or any member it authorizes for the purpose may make an inquiry to ascertain whether a person whose name is entered on the list of electors or who is applying to have his name entered thereon is so entitled. The person and any witnesses summoned may be assisted by an advocate.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "557", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "559", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "560", "mode": "normal", "text": "**136.** Where the decision of the board of revisors concerning an application for entry or striking off entails entering or striking off a name for which no application has been made, the board of its own initiative may enter the name or strike it off. The board may also, of its own initiative, enter or strike off a name or make a correction if, after verifying the information provided to its members by the returning officer under section 121, it decides that a change must be made to the list. Where the board decides that such a change is not warranted, it shall specify that its verification confirmed the accuracy of the information or that it was unable to confirm or refute the accuracy of the information. Where a correction is made, a name is entered on or struck off a part of the list that is not within the competence of the board, the board shall give notice of its decision to the returning officer who shall transmit the notice to the competent board.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "561", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "563", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "564", "mode": "normal", "text": "**137.** Before striking off or refusing to enter the name of a person, the board of revisors shall give one clear day’s advance notice to the person. The notice shall be notified at the address entered on the list of electors or at any place where the board or the revising officer has reason to believe that the person may be reached. However, the board is not required to give the notice where", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "565", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "567", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "568", "mode": "normal", "text": "**138.** The board of revisors shall transmit its decisions to the returning officer in accordance with the returning officer’s directives. The returning officer shall incorporate the changes into the list or prepare an abstract of changes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "569", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "571", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "572", "mode": "normal", "text": "**139.** As soon as practicable after receiving the decisions of the board of revisors, the returning officer shall transmit, free of charge, to each party authorized under Chapter XIII or to each ticket recognized under Division III of this chapter, a copy of the revised list or of an abstract of the changes made to the list submitted to be revised. The provisions relating to the free distribution of the list of electors to candidates apply, adapted as required, to the revised list and the abstract of changes. However, the returning officer shall transmit free of charge to candidates who have already obtained free copies of the list submitted to be revised an equal number of copies of the revised list or the abstract of changes made to the list, without those candidates having to request the copies.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "573", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "575", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "576", "mode": "normal", "text": "**140.** The returning officer shall communicate to the chief electoral officer the changes made to the list that concern the persons domiciled in the territory of the municipality, in the manner determined by the chief electoral officer. The returning officer shall also communicate to the chief electoral officer, if the change entails entering the name of a domiciled person, the former address of the domicile of that person and, if the change entails striking off the name of a domiciled person who requests that the striking off apply only for the purposes of a municipal poll, the request made by that person. Furthermore, the returning officer shall communicate the decisions of the board of revisors made after the verification under the second paragraph of section 134 that do not entail changes to the list. That information must be sent to the chief electoral officer not later than the thirtieth day after the revision of the list of electors is completed or interrupted.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "577", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "579", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "580", "mode": "normal", "text": "**141.** The abstract of changes forms part of the list of electors until the changes are incorporated into the list.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "581", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "583", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "584", "mode": "normal", "text": "**142.** (Replaced).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "585", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "587", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "588", "mode": "normal", "text": "**143.** (Replaced).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "589", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "591", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "592", "mode": "normal", "text": "**144.** The list of electors comes into force upon completion or interruption of the revision or, where it is not revised, upon the expiry of the period prescribed in section 153 for filing nomination papers. The returning officer shall indicate at the end of the list of electors the day on which it comes into force.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "593", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "595", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "596", "mode": "normal", "text": "**145.** The list of electors shall remain in force until a new list which replaces it comes into force.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "597", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "599", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "600", "mode": "normal", "text": "**146.** Every eligible person may be nominated as a candidate for one office on the council of a municipality at a time, by filing a nomination paper with the returning officer. Notwithstanding the foregoing, a municipality having a population of 100,000 or over may, by a by-law of its council, allow double candidacies in accordance with this paragraph; in such a case, the clerk shall transmit a certified copy of the by-law, as soon as possible after its coming into force, to the chief electoral officer. If such a by-law is in force 44 days before polling day, the candidate for the office of mayor of a party authorized under Chapter XIII may, jointly with another candidate of the party who is his co-candidate, also be candidate for the office of councillor in an electoral district. Section 6.1 of the Cities and Towns Act ( chapter C-19", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "601", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "603", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "604", "mode": "normal", "text": "**147.** In the case of a municipality to which Chapter XIII applies, candidates may be grouped into authorized parties in accordance with that chapter. In the case of other municipalities, candidates may be grouped into tickets recognized by the returning officer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "605", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "607", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "608", "mode": "normal", "text": "**148.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "609", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "611", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "612", "mode": "normal", "text": "**149.** The leader of the ticket shall transmit to the returning officer a written application for recognition containing the following information: The application must be accompanied by a list including the names, addresses and signatures of at least 10 electors of the municipality who support the application.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "613", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "615", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "616", "mode": "normal", "text": "**150.** The returning officer shall grant the recognition to a ticket making an application therefor in accordance with section 149. The returning officer shall refuse to recognize the ticket if the name of the ticket includes the word “independent” or is likely to mislead the electors as to which ticket they are voting for. The recognition has effect for the purposes of the next general election and every by-election held before the general election following the next one.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "617", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "619", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "620", "mode": "normal", "text": "**151.** A recognized ticket is not authorized to change its name except with the approval of the returning officer. The returning officer shall refuse to approve any change if the proposed new name includes the word “independent” or is likely to mislead the electors as to which ticket they are voting for, or if the application for a change of name is made during the election period within the meaning of section 364. An application for approval is made by means of a writing filed by the leader of the ticket.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "621", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "623", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "624", "mode": "normal", "text": "**152.** The returning officer shall withdraw the recognition of a ticket which has changed its name to include the word “independent” or if the new name is likely to mislead the electors as to which ticket they are voting for or the recognition of a ticket which changes its name during the election period within the meaning of section 364.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "625", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "627", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "628", "mode": "normal", "text": "**153.** The nomination paper shall, under pain of rejection, be filed in the office of the returning officer or in the office of the assistant designated by the returning officer for that purpose during the days and hours the office is open in the period beginning 44 days and ending 30 days before polling day. Thirty days before polling day, the office shall be open from 9:00 a.m. to 4:30 p.m.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "629", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "631", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "632", "mode": "normal", "text": "**154.** The nomination paper shall state the name of the candidate, his date of birth, his address, and the office for which he is a candidate, and shall include a sworn attestation of his eligibility. The nomination paper filed by an independent candidate seeking an authorization must, in addition, include his telephone number and the information specified in subparagraphs 2 to 5 of the first paragraph of section 400.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "633", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "635", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "636", "mode": "normal", "text": "**155.** A person may be a candidate under the name by which he is commonly known provided it is the name he always uses in his political, professional or social life and that he is acting in good faith.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "637", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "639", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "640", "mode": "normal", "text": "**156.** The address of the candidate shall be, according to the capacity under which he is eligible, the street number of the immovable in which he has his domicile or of his residence in the territory of the municipality. The number of the immovable includes the apartment number, if any. If the immovable has no number, the cadastral number shall be used.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "641", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "643", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "644", "mode": "normal", "text": "**157.** The designation of the office of councillor shall specify the electoral district, the ward or the number assigned to the seat.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "645", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "647", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "648", "mode": "normal", "text": "**158.** The nomination paper of the candidate of an authorized party or recognized ticket shall state that he is the candidate for that party or ticket and that he is a co-candidate, where that is the case.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "649", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "651", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "652", "mode": "normal", "text": "**159.** The nomination paper shall be signed by the candidate.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "653", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "655", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "656", "mode": "normal", "text": "**160.** The nomination paper for the office of mayor or borough mayor shall include the supporting signatures of not fewer than the following number of electors of the municipality: The nomination paper for the office of councillor shall include the supporting signatures of not fewer than the following number of electors of the municipality: Each elector shall enter his address opposite his signature as it must be entered on the list of electors.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "657", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "659", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "660", "mode": "normal", "text": "**161.** Only the person who intends to be a candidate and the person he designates for that purpose on the nomination paper are authorized to collect the supporting signatures.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "661", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "663", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "664", "mode": "normal", "text": "**162.** The nomination paper shall be accompanied with a proof of the candidate’s identity and a statement signed by the person who collected the signatures in support of his nomination certifying that he knows the signatories, that they signed the nomination paper in his presence and that to the best of his knowledge they are electors of the municipality. The proof of the identity of the candidate must be a document stating the name and date of birth of the candidate and be issued by the Government of Québec or Canada or any of their departments or agencies, or by a public body or by a public servant who is authorized to issue copies of or extracts from the acts of civil status. After examining the proof of identity, the returning officer shall keep a true copy and return it to the person filing the nomination paper.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "665", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "667", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "668", "mode": "normal", "text": "**163.** For the purposes of this section, the meaning of the word “ leader ” , in the case of a party, is the meaning given to that word in section 364. The nomination paper of the candidate of an authorized party or recognized ticket must be accompanied with a letter signed by the leader of the party or ticket certifying that the person is its official candidate for the office in question and, where that is the case, that he is a co-candidate.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "669", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "671", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "672", "mode": "normal", "text": "**164.** In a municipality to which Chapter XIII applies, the nomination paper of an independent candidate must be accompanied with a writing signed by him in which he designates his official agent for the purposes of this chapter. The candidate may designate himself as his official agent. Except in that case, the writing must include the consent of the official agent and be countersigned by him.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "673", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "675", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "676", "mode": "normal", "text": "**165.** On the filing of a nomination paper, the returning officer shall verify whether it appears to comply with the requirements of this division and whether all the required documents are attached to it. In particular, the returning officer shall verify that Following those verifications, the returning officer shall issue a receipt and a notice of compliance that constitutes proof of the nomination. However, the returning officer shall refuse the filing of the nomination paper of a person whose name appears on the list of ineligible persons drawn up and sent by the Chief Electoral Officer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "677", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "679", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "680", "mode": "normal", "text": "**166.** Every candidate may, on request, obtain, free of charge, a copy of any nomination paper the filing of which has been accepted.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "681", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "683", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "684", "mode": "normal", "text": "**167.** A candidate may withdraw his nomination by transmitting to the returning officer a writing to that effect signed by him.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "685", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "687", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "688", "mode": "normal", "text": "**168.** If, at the end of the period for filing nomination papers, the returning officer has accepted only one nomination paper for an office or if only one candidate for that office remains, he shall declare that candidate elected. In other cases, a poll must be held to determine which candidate will be elected to such office. Notwithstanding the foregoing, where, as a result of a withdrawal after the end of the period contemplated in the first paragraph but before the end of the polling period, there remains only one candidate for an office, the returning officer shall declare that candidate elected. The first and third paragraphs do not apply where election procedures must be recommenced pursuant to subdivision 2 of Division VII.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "689", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "691", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "692", "mode": "normal", "text": "**169.** The declaration of election is made by means of a writing signed by the returning officer who shall indicate the date of declaration, the name and address of the elected candidate and the office to which he is elected. Where applicable, the returning officer shall read the declaration to the persons present at the place where he signs it.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "693", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "695", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "696", "mode": "normal", "text": "**170.** Within three days of the day on which a candidate is declared elected, the returning officer shall transmit a copy of the declaration to the elected candidate.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "697", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "699", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "700", "mode": "normal", "text": "**171.** Not later than 10 days before polling day, the returning officer shall give a public notice setting forth the following particulars: The particulars set forth in subparagraph 7 of the first paragraph need not be mentioned if the returning officer causes a reminder containing them to be distributed pursuant to section 173.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "701", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "703", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "704", "mode": "normal", "text": "**172.** The particulars relating to the office and to the name must correspond to those appearing on the nomination paper. The same applies to the indication of membership in an authorized party or recognized ticket or to the indication “co-candidate” unless, in the meantime, the authorization of the party or the recognition of the ticket has been withdrawn or the co-candidate has ceased to be such, or the name of the party or ticket appearing on the nomination paper is inaccurate.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "705", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "707", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "708", "mode": "normal", "text": "**173.** The returning officer may cause a reminder to be distributed to every person whose name is entered on the list of electors and who is entitled to vote at the poll. The returning officer is required to do so in the case of a municipality having a population of 20,000 or over. The reminder shall contain all the particulars contained in the notice of poll or only those relating to the candidates for whom the addressee is entitled to vote and to the polling station where he may exercise his right.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "709", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "711", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "712", "mode": "normal", "text": "**174.** An advance poll must be held seven days before polling day and, if the returning officer so decides, eight days before polling day. In addition to the advance poll, the returning officer may allow voters to exercise their right to vote at the polling station at his office or at a mobile polling station, which are considered advance polling stations for the purposes of this Act. Voting at the returning officer’s office may, at the discretion of the returning officer, take place on the ninth, sixth, fifth and fourth days before polling day. For municipalities with a population of 20,000 or more, such voting must be held at least nine days before polling day. Voting at a mobile polling station may, at the discretion of the returning officer, take place on the ninth, eighth, sixth, fifth and fourth days before polling day.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "713", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "715", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "716", "mode": "normal", "text": "**175.** Any elector whose name is entered on the list of electors may vote in an advance poll. An elector who has a mobility impairment or is unable to move about for health reasons may vote at a mobile polling station if the following requirements are met: An elector referred to in the second paragraph who is domiciled in any private seniors’ residence within the meaning of the Act respecting the governance of the health and social services system ( chapter G-1.021 An elector who acts as a caregiver for an elector referred to in the second paragraph may vote at the same mobile polling station as that elector if he is registered on the part of the list of electors for the polling subdivision in which the domicile of the person for whom he acts as a caregiver is located.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "717", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "719", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "720", "mode": "normal", "text": "**176.** The provisions of this Act relating to the holding of a poll, except the provision relating to the leave of absence of employees, pupils and students, apply, adapted as required, to the advance poll, so far as they are consistent with this subdivision.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "721", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "723", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "724", "mode": "normal", "text": "**177.** The returning officer may establish as many advance polling stations as he considers necessary. If the returning officer establishes several advance polling stations, he shall determine which polling subdivision is attached to each station. The mobile polling station established for a private seniors’ residence within the meaning of the Act respecting the governance of the health and social services system ( chapter G-1.021 The returning officer shall notify each authorized party or recognized ticket and each independent candidate concerned of his decision as soon as practicable.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "725", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "727", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "728", "mode": "normal", "text": "**178.** Every advance polling station and every office of the returning officer must be accessible to handicapped persons. The operator of any private seniors’ residence within the meaning of the Act respecting the governance of the health and social services system ( chapter G-1.021", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "729", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "731", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "732", "mode": "normal", "text": "**179.** Every advance polling station must be open from 12:00 p.m. to 8:00 p.m. Voting at a mobile polling station shall take place during the hours fixed by the returning officer. Those hours may not, however, coincide with the hours fixed for voting in the advance poll or with those fixed for voting at the office of the returning officer. Voting at the office of the returning officer shall take place during the hours fixed by the returning officer, who must allow at least four consecutive hours, between 9:30 a.m. and 8:00 p.m. For municipalities with a population of 20,000 or over, he must also provide that voting shall take place between 4:00 p.m. and 8:00 p.m. on the ninth day before polling day.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "733", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "735", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "736", "mode": "normal", "text": "**180.** An elector who votes in a mobile polling station and declares that he is unable to mark his ballot paper himself may be assisted by the deputy returning officer and the poll clerk. The elector may also be assisted The person referred to in subparagraph 2 of the second paragraph shall attest under oath to not having assisted another elector who is not that person’s spouse or relative within the meaning of section 131, during the advance poll.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "737", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "739", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "740", "mode": "normal", "text": "**181.** (Replaced).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "741", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "743", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "744", "mode": "normal", "text": "**182.** After the close of the advance polling station on the first day, the poll clerk shall enter the following particulars in the poll book: The deputy returning officer shall place, in separate envelopes, the ballot papers found in the ballot box, the cancelled ballot papers, the unused ballot papers, the forms, and the list of electors, and seal them. He shall then place the poll book and the envelopes, except the envelope containing the list of electors, in the ballot box, and seal it. The deputy returning officer, the poll clerk and the representatives who wish to do so shall affix their initials to the seals of the envelopes and of the ballot box. The deputy returning officer shall then remit the ballot box and the envelope containing the list of electors to the returning officer or the person designated by him.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "745", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "747", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "748", "mode": "normal", "text": "**183.** Immediately before the time fixed for the opening of the polling station on another day, where that is the case, the deputy returning officer, in the presence of the poll clerk and the representatives, shall open the ballot box, resume possession of the poll book and of the envelopes containing the unused ballot papers, the forms and the list of electors, and open the envelopes to resume possession of their contents. The envelopes containing the used and cancelled ballot papers shall remain in the ballot box. After the close of the polling station on that day, the deputy returning officer and the poll clerk shall observe the same formalities as after the close of the polling station on the first day. The ballot papers used or cancelled on that day shall be placed in envelopes separate from those containing the ballot papers used or cancelled on any prior day.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "749", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "751", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "752", "mode": "normal", "text": "**184.** The poll clerk shall prepare the list of the electors who have voted in advance at his polling station and transmit it, as soon as practicable, to the returning officer or to the person designated by the latter. The returning officer shall transmit a copy of the list to each authorized party or recognized ticket and to each independent candidate concerned not later than three days before polling day.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "753", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "755", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "756", "mode": "normal", "text": "**185.** From 8 p.m. on polling day, the deputy returning officer, assisted by the poll clerk, shall proceed with the counting of the votes cast in an advance polling station, in the presence of those representatives who wish to attend. The counting shall be effected at the place determined by the returning officer, in accordance with the rules applicable to the counting of the votes cast on polling day, adapted as required. If the deputy returning officer or poll clerk who acted in the advance polling station is unable to act, the returning officer shall appoint a substitute for the purposes of this section. The substitute need not be recommended by an authorized party, if any.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "757", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "759", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "760", "mode": "normal", "text": "**186.** The returning officer shall establish a polling station for each polling subdivision. The returning officer may, notwithstanding the foregoing, establish several polling stations for the same subdivision and determine which electors of the subdivision are entitled to vote at each polling station. The returning officer shall notify each authorized party or recognized ticket and each independent candidate of his decision as soon as practicable.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "761", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "763", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "764", "mode": "normal", "text": "**187.** Every elector is entitled to vote at the polling station of the polling subdivision which includes him or, where there are several stations for such subdivision, at the polling station determined by the returning officer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "765", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "767", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "768", "mode": "normal", "text": "**188.** The polling station shall be situated in a spacious place of convenient access to the public. It must also be accessible to handicapped persons. The polling stations of the same electoral district or of the same ward must be grouped at the same polling place in the district or ward wherever possible. Notwithstanding the foregoing, the returning officer may establish polling stations of the same district or ward in more than one polling place or establish some of them in a neighbouring district or ward, but all the polling stations for the same polling subdivision must be at the same polling place. In addition, if unable to establish a polling station in a place accessible to handicapped persons, the returning officer shall inform the council of that fact at the first sitting after polling day by filing a document stating the reasons for the decision to establish it elsewhere than in such a place and showing that the returning officer had no other options.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "769", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "771", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "772", "mode": "normal", "text": "**189.** School service centres, school boards, Santé Québec, and institutions governed by the Act respecting the governance of the health and social services system ( chapter G-1.021", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "773", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "775", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "776", "mode": "normal", "text": "**190.** The returning officer shall be responsible for the arrangement and identification of the polling place where a polling station is situated. In particular, the returning officer shall ensure that places where polling stations are located are arranged in such a manner that electors appearing before the identity verification panel do not hinder or delay the polling proceedings.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "777", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "779", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "780", "mode": "normal", "text": "**191.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "781", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "783", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "784", "mode": "normal", "text": "**192.** The returning officer shall cause ballot papers to be printed. The printer shall see that no ballot paper of the model ordered by the returning officer is furnished to any other person.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "785", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "787", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "788", "mode": "normal", "text": "**194.** The paper used to make the ballot papers must be of sufficient weight that writing does not appear through it.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "789", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "791", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "792", "mode": "normal", "text": "**195.** The ballot papers must have a counterfoil and a stub. The back of the stub and of the counterfoil must bear the same number. The ballot papers must be numbered consecutively.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "793", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "795", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "796", "mode": "normal", "text": "**196.** The ballot papers must allow each candidate to be identified. The ballot papers must contain, on the obverse, All circles, as the space between consecutive circles, must be of the same size. Where two or more independent candidates for the same office have the same name, the ballot papers used in the polling for that office must include, under each candidate’s name, an entry allowing a distinction to be made between the candidates. The particulars must appear in alphabetical order of the candidates’ surnames and, as the case may be, of the candidates’ given names. Where two or more candidates for the same office have the same name, the order in which the particulars relating to each of them appear shall be determined by a drawing of lots carried out by the returning officer. Notwithstanding the foregoing, the particulars pertaining to a co-candidate must appear with those pertaining to the candidate with whom he is associated, in the following order: the name of the candidate associated with the co-candidate, the name of the co-candidate and his capacity, and the name of the party. These particulars must appear on the ballot paper in the alphabetical order of the surname of the candidate associated with the co-candidate and opposite a single voting circle; in order to do so, these particulars may be printed in a smaller type. The particulars pertaining to the candidates must correspond to those contained in the nomination papers, unless, in the meantime, the authorization of the party or the recognition of the ticket has been withdrawn or the co-candidate has ceased to be such, or the name of the party or ticket appearing on the nomination paper is inaccurate.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "797", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "799", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "800", "mode": "normal", "text": "**197.** The ballot papers shall contain, on the reverse, The indication of the office concerned shall correspond to that contained in the nomination papers.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "801", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "803", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "804", "mode": "normal", "text": "**198.** Where the withdrawal of a candidate occurs when there is no time to take account of the withdrawal on the ballot papers to be used, the returning officer shall cause the particulars relating to that candidate to be uniformly crossed off the ballot papers by means of a line in ink or any other indelible substance. The deputy returning officer shall inform every elector to whom he gives such a ballot paper of the candidate’s withdrawal. Any vote cast in favour of the candidate, before or after his withdrawal, is absolutely null.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "805", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "807", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "808", "mode": "normal", "text": "**199.** Where the authorization of a party or the recognition of a ticket is withdrawn when there is no time to take account of the withdrawal on the ballot papers to be used, the returning officer shall cause the reference to the party or ticket to be uniformly crossed off the ballot papers by means of a line in ink or any other indelible substance. In the case described in the first paragraph, or where a co-candidate otherwise ceases to be such when there is no time to take account of that fact on the ballot papers to be used for the election at which he is a candidate for the office of councillor, the returning officer shall cause the indication “co-candidate” and the particulars pertaining to the candidate associated with him to be uniformly crossed off the ballot papers by means of a line in ink or any other indelible substance.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "809", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "811", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "812", "mode": "normal", "text": "**200.** The returning officer shall obtain a ballot box for each polling station.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "813", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "815", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "816", "mode": "normal", "text": "**201.** Each ballot box must be made of durable material with a slit or narrow opening on the top so constructed that the ballot papers may be introduced therein through the opening but cannot be withdrawn therefrom unless the box is opened.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "817", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "819", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "820", "mode": "normal", "text": "**202.** The materials required for the poll may not be seized so long as they are required.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "821", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "823", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "824", "mode": "normal", "text": "**203.** The returning officer, on behalf of the municipality, may enter into any contract to procure the materials required for the poll.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "825", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "827", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "828", "mode": "normal", "text": "**204.** Not later than one hour before the time fixed for the opening of the polling station, the returning officer shall deliver to the deputy returning officer, in a sealed ballot box, after affixing his initials or a printed mark bearing his initials to the seals, The returning officer shall also deliver to the deputy returning officer any other materials required for the poll.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "829", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "831", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "832", "mode": "normal", "text": "**205.** The deputy returning officer and the poll clerk shall be present at the polling place in which the polling station to which they are assigned is situated one hour before the opening of the poll, or earlier if so directed by the returning officer. The officer in charge of information and order, if any, and any other election officer assigned to the polling place shall be present one hour before the opening of the polling station, or earlier if so directed by the returning officer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "833", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "835", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "836", "mode": "normal", "text": "**206.** The representatives assigned to a polling station may be present at the polling place in which the polling station is situated one hour before the opening of the polling stations. The representatives may attend any of the activities taking place at the polling place.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "837", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "839", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "840", "mode": "normal", "text": "**207.** During the hour preceding the opening of the polling station, the deputy returning officer, in the presence of the poll clerk, shall open the ballot box and examine the documents found in it and the other materials required for the poll.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "841", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "843", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "844", "mode": "normal", "text": "**208.** The election officers must be identified as such.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "845", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "847", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "848", "mode": "normal", "text": "**209.** Immediately before the time fixed for the opening of the polling station, the deputy returning officer and the poll clerk shall ascertain that the ballot box is empty. The ballot box shall then be sealed and placed on the table of the polling station in full view of the election officers.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "849", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "851", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "852", "mode": "normal", "text": "**210.** The polling period shall begin at the opening of the polling stations, at 10 a.m., and shall end at the closing of the stations, at 8 p.m., subject to any extension of the polling period provided for in section 211.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "853", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "855", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "856", "mode": "normal", "text": "**211.** In the case of a delay or interruption, the returning officer may extend the polling period, to the extent he sees fit, for the polling station affected by the delay or interruption. The extension must not exceed the extent of the delay or interruption.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "857", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "859", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "860", "mode": "normal", "text": "**212.** Any electors on the premises of a polling station at the end of the polling period who have not been able to vote may nevertheless exercise their right to vote. The deputy returning officer shall declare the polling closed after they have voted. For the purposes of the first paragraph, the premises of a polling station extend as far as the end of the waiting line of electors entitled to vote at the polling station, as it stands at the end of the polling period.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "861", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "863", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "864", "mode": "normal", "text": "**213.** During the polling period, every employer shall grant to those of his employees whose names are entered on the list of electors sufficient leave to allow at least four consecutive hours to vote, not counting the time normally allowed for meals. No deduction of wages nor any penalty may be imposed on any employee by reason of this leave. On polling day, every educational institution shall give leave to those of its pupils or students whose names are entered on the list of electors. This section is binding upon the Government and its departments and agencies.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "865", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "867", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "868", "mode": "normal", "text": "**214.** Only one elector may be admitted to the polling station at a time. Notwithstanding the first paragraph, two electors may be admitted at the same time to a polling station that is provided with two polling booths. Only the deputy returning officer, the poll clerk and the representatives assigned to the polling station may be present at the station, together with the returning officer, the election clerk and the assistant returning officer. The officer in charge of information and order may be present at the request of the deputy returning officer for as long as may be required. The poll runner may be present for the time required to perform his duties. Any other person assisting an elector under section 226 may be present for the time required to enable the elector to exercise his right to vote.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "869", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "871", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "872", "mode": "normal", "text": "**215.** The elector shall give his name and address to the deputy returning officer and the poll clerk. He shall also give them his date of birth, if so requested. The address of the elector is the address that must be entered on the list of electors. In addition, the elector shall show his face and identify himself, notwithstanding any incompatible provision, by producing his health insurance card issued by the Régie de l’assurance maladie du Québec, driver’s licence or probationary licence issued in plastic form by the Société de l’assurance automobile du Québec, Canadian passport or any other document that has been issued by the Government or a government department or body or recognized by the Government and is determined by regulation by the Government pursuant to paragraph 4 of section 549 of the Election Act ( chapter E-3.3 Where an elector who has not been directed to the identity verification panel cannot produce identification in accordance with the third paragraph, the deputy returning officer shall invite the elector to submit his case to the members of the panel.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "873", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "875", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "876", "mode": "normal", "text": "**216.** The deputy returning officer shall admit an elector to vote if the elector has not already voted, if he is entered on the list of electors used at the polling station, if his name, address and, where such is the case, date of birth correspond to those appearing on that list and if he has produced identification in accordance with section 213.2 or the third paragraph of section 215. Any elector whose name, address or, where such is the case, date of birth differs slightly from that entered on the list of electors shall nevertheless be admitted to vote, after declaring under oath that the erroneous entry was intended to refer to him. An indication thereof shall be entered in the poll book.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "877", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "879", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "880", "mode": "normal", "text": "**217.** Before admitting a person to vote, the deputy returning officer, the poll clerk or a representative assigned to the polling station may, for reasons he shall specify, require the person to declare under oath that he has the right to vote. The poll clerk shall note in the poll book the name of the person who requires that the voter be sworn together with the reasons therefor and, where that is the case, the fact that the oath was made.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "881", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "883", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "884", "mode": "normal", "text": "**218.** An elector under whose name another person has already voted shall nevertheless be admitted to vote, after declaring under oath that he truly is the elector registered on the list and that he has not already voted. An indication thereof shall be entered in the poll book.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "885", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "887", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "888", "mode": "normal", "text": "**219.** The returning officer may authorize an elector to vote where An elector who has obtained an authorization under this section shall present it to the deputy returning officer and must be admitted to vote after declaring under oath that he is the person who obtained it. An indication thereof shall be entered in the poll book. The returning officer shall send to the chief electoral officer a copy of the authorization given to an elector domiciled in the territory of the municipality unless he is satisfied that the change to the list warranting the authorization was communicated in accordance with section 140.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "889", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "891", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "892", "mode": "normal", "text": "**220.** In no case may the returning officer admit to vote any person who refuses to make the oath that is required of him. An indication thereof shall be entered in the poll book.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "893", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "895", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "896", "mode": "normal", "text": "**221.** The deputy returning officer shall give the elector who is admitted to vote every ballot paper to which he is entitled, after writing his initials in the space reserved for that purpose and detaching the counterfoil. The deputy returning officer shall also give the elector a pencil.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "897", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "899", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "900", "mode": "normal", "text": "**222.** The elector shall enter the polling booth and mark the ballot paper in the circle placed opposite the indications pertaining to the candidate for whom the elector intends to vote, using the pencil given to him by the deputy returning officer. For the purposes of this paragraph, a co-candidate and the candidate with whom the co-candidate is associated shall be counted as one candidate for the office of councillor. The elector shall then fold the ballot paper he has marked.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "901", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "903", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "904", "mode": "normal", "text": "**223.** After marking and folding every ballot paper given to him, the elector shall leave the polling booth. He shall allow the initials of the deputy returning officer to be examined by the latter, by the poll clerk and by any representative assigned to the polling station who wishes to do so. Then, in full view of the persons present, the elector shall detach the stub and hand it to the deputy returning officer, who shall destroy it. Lastly, the elector himself shall place the ballot paper in the ballot box.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "905", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "907", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "908", "mode": "normal", "text": "**224.** The deputy returning officer shall cancel any ballot paper bearing initials that are not his own or not bearing any initials and prevent it from being placed in the ballot box. An indication thereof shall be entered in the poll book. Notwithstanding the foregoing, the deputy returning officer shall not cancel a ballot paper which does not bear any initials where all of the following conditions are met: The deputy returning officer shall then, in full view of the persons present, affix his initials to the reverse of the ballot paper and allow it to be placed in the ballot box. An indication thereof shall be entered in the poll book.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "909", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "911", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "912", "mode": "normal", "text": "**225.** The deputy returning officer shall cancel any ballot paper inadvertently marked or spoiled by an elector and shall give another ballot paper to that elector. The deputy returning officer shall not attempt to learn for whom the elector has voted, where that is the case.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "913", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "915", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "916", "mode": "normal", "text": "**226.** An elector who declares that he is unable to mark his ballot paper himself may be assisted either The person referred to in subparagraph 2 of the first paragraph shall declare under oath that the person has not assisted another elector who is not that person’s spouse or relative within the meaning of section 131, during the poll. A deaf or mute elector may be assisted, for the purposes of communicating with the election officers and representatives, by a person capable of interpreting the sign language of the deaf. An indication that an elector has availed himself of this section shall be entered in the poll book.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "917", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "919", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "920", "mode": "normal", "text": "**227.** The deputy returning officer shall provide a visually handicapped person who so requests a template to enable him to vote without assistance. The deputy returning officer shall adjust the template and the ballot paper, give them to the elector and indicate to him the order in which the candidates appear on the ballot paper and the particulars entered under their names, where such is the case. The deputy returning officer shall, upon request, assist the elector in walking to and back from the polling booth, in folding the marked ballot paper, in detaching the stub and in placing the ballot paper in the ballot box. Where the elector is entitled to more than one ballot paper, the deputy returning officer shall wait until the ballot paper given to the elector is placed in the ballot box before giving him another in accordance with the second paragraph.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "921", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "923", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "924", "mode": "normal", "text": "**228.** As soon as an elector has voted, the poll clerk shall indicate it on the list of electors in the space reserved for that purpose. The first paragraph does not apply where the elector has voted pursuant to an authorization where his name was not entered on the copy of the list of electors used at the polling station.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "925", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "927", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "928", "mode": "normal", "text": "**229.** After the closing of the poll, the deputy returning officer, assisted by the poll clerk, shall proceed to the counting of the votes. The representatives assigned to the polling station may attend. Where several polling stations are situated at the same polling place, the counting of votes shall begin only after the poll is closed at all the polling stations.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "929", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "931", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "932", "mode": "normal", "text": "**230.** Before the ballot box is opened, the poll clerk shall enter the following particulars in the poll book:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "933", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "935", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "936", "mode": "normal", "text": "**231.** The deputy returning officer, the poll clerk and the representatives shall use the compiling sheet provided by the returning officer for the counting of votes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "937", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "939", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "940", "mode": "normal", "text": "**232.** The deputy returning officer shall open the ballot box, count the votes by taking, one by one, the ballot papers placed in the ballot box and allow each person present to examine the ballot papers without touching them.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "941", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "943", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "944", "mode": "normal", "text": "**233.** The deputy returning officer shall reject every ballot paper which", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "945", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "947", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "948", "mode": "normal", "text": "**234.** Every ballot paper that does not bear the initials of the deputy returning officer must be rejected. Notwithstanding the foregoing, no ballot paper contemplated in the first paragraph may be rejected where all of the following conditions are met: The deputy returning officer shall, in full view of the persons present, then affix his initials to the reverse of every ballot paper that does not bear them, and shall enter, on each ballot, following his initials a note indicating that they were affixed as a correction. An indication thereof shall be entered in the poll book.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "949", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "951", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "952", "mode": "normal", "text": "**235.** No ballot paper may be rejected for the sole reason that the stub has not been detached. In that case, the deputy returning officer shall detach the stub and destroy it.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "953", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "955", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "956", "mode": "normal", "text": "**236.** No ballot paper may be rejected for the sole reason that the mark made in one of the circles extends beyond the circumference of the circle or that the circle is not completely filled.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "957", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "959", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "960", "mode": "normal", "text": "**237.** The deputy returning officer shall consider every objection raised by a representative assigned to the polling station in respect of the validity of a ballot paper and make a decision immediately. He may reserve his decision as to an objection based on the absence of his initials until all the ballot papers placed in the ballot box are examined. The objection and the decision of the deputy returning officer shall be entered in the poll book.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "961", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "963", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "964", "mode": "normal", "text": "**238.** After examining all the ballot papers placed in the ballot box, the deputy returning officer shall draw up a statement of votes indicating The statement must be drawn up separately for each office for which a poll was held at the polling station. The deputy returning officer shall draw up a sufficient number of copies of the statement of votes to provide, in addition to his copy, a copy for the returning officer and for each representative assigned to the polling station.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "965", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "967", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "968", "mode": "normal", "text": "**239.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "969", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "971", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "972", "mode": "normal", "text": "**240.** The deputy returning officer shall give a copy of the statement of votes to each representative assigned to the polling station. The deputy returning officer shall keep a copy of the statement for himself and a copy intended for the returning officer under section 244.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "973", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "975", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "976", "mode": "normal", "text": "**241.** After drawing up the statement of votes, the deputy returning officer shall place the ballot papers marked in favour of each candidate, the ballot papers rejected in the counting of votes, the ballot papers cancelled and not placed in the ballot box, the unused ballot papers and the statement of votes in separate envelopes. The first paragraph applies separately in respect of each office for which a poll was held at the polling station.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "977", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "979", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "980", "mode": "normal", "text": "**242.** The deputy returning officer shall then seal the envelopes. The deputy returning officer, the poll clerk and those representatives assigned to the polling station who wish to do so shall affix their initials to the seals.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "981", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "983", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "984", "mode": "normal", "text": "**243.** The deputy returning officer shall place the envelopes, the poll book and the list of electors in the ballot box. He shall then seal the ballot box. The deputy returning officer, the poll clerk and those representatives assigned to the polling station who wish to do so shall affix their initials to the seals.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "985", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "987", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "988", "mode": "normal", "text": "**244.** The deputy returning officer shall deliver the ballot box to the returning officer or to the person designated by the latter to receive it. The deputy returning officer shall at the same time deliver a copy of the statement of votes to the returning officer or designated person.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "989", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "991", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "992", "mode": "normal", "text": "**245.** The addition of the votes shall begin, at the discretion of the returning officer, If the returning officer chooses to begin the addition of the votes after polling day, he shall notify each authorized party, recognized ticket and independent candidate concerned of the date, time and place selected for that purpose.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "993", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "995", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "996", "mode": "normal", "text": "**246.** The addition of the votes shall be conducted at the place determined by the returning officer. Any person may attend.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "997", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "999", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1000", "mode": "normal", "text": "**247.** The returning officer shall proceed to the addition of the votes by using the statements of votes delivered with the ballot boxes and compiling the votes cast in favour of each candidate. The returning officer shall, however, use the statements contained in the ballot boxes if a candidate or an elector concerned produces to him a sworn declaration in writing attesting that there is reason to believe that a statement delivered with a ballot box is erroneous or fraudulent and does not correspond to the statement placed in the ballot box, and that the results may be different if the statement placed in the ballot box is used in conducting the addition of the votes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1001", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1003", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1004", "mode": "normal", "text": "**248.** If a statement of votes to be remitted to him is missing, the returning officer shall adjourn the addition of the votes until he obtains it. If it appears impossible to obtain the statement of votes referred to in the first paragraph, the returning officer shall use the statement of votes of the deputy returning officer or of a representative or the statement contained in the ballot box.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1005", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1007", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1008", "mode": "normal", "text": "**249.** After consulting the statement of votes, the returning officer shall place it in an envelope and seal the envelope. If the statement of votes was taken out of the ballot box, the returning officer shall place the envelope in the ballot box and seal the ballot box.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1009", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1011", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1012", "mode": "normal", "text": "**250.** If it appears impossible to obtain the statement of votes, the returning officer shall cause a summary counting of the votes to be made by the deputy returning officer and the poll clerk on the date, at the time and at the place determined by him. At the summary counting of the votes, the deputy returning officer shall open the ballot box and the envelopes it contains in the presence of the poll clerk. With the poll clerk’s assistance, the deputy returning officer shall count, without questioning whether the ballot papers are valid, rejected or cancelled, the ballot papers cast in favour of each candidate, the ballot papers rejected at the time of the counting of votes, the ballot papers that were cancelled and the unused ballot papers. The formalities applicable after any counting of votes shall then apply. If the deputy returning officer or if the poll clerk is unable or refuses to act, the other shall proceed alone to a summary counting of the votes. If both are unable or refuse to act, the returning officer shall himself proceed thereto. The returning officer shall give advance notice of the summary counting of the votes to each authorized party, recognized ticket and independent candidate concerned. The representatives assigned to the polling station may attend.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1013", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1015", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1016", "mode": "normal", "text": "**251.** Where it appears impossible to obtain the statement of votes and the ballot papers, the returning officer shall inform the Minister of Municipal Affairs, Regions and Land Occupancy in accordance with Division III of Chapter XI.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1017", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1019", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1020", "mode": "normal", "text": "**252.** Immediately upon completion of the addition of the votes, the returning officer shall announce the results to the persons present.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1021", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1023", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1024", "mode": "normal", "text": "**253.** After making the announcement, the returning officer shall communicate the results of the addition of the votes to every person who requests it.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1025", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1027", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1028", "mode": "normal", "text": "**254.** In case of a tie for first place, the returning officer shall apply for a recount of the votes in accordance with Division VII.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1029", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1031", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1032", "mode": "normal", "text": "**255.** If no application for a recount or re-addition of the votes is made within the time prescribed in section 264, or if an application is made and is dismissed, the returning officer shall declare elected the candidate who obtained the greatest number of votes according to his announcement.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1033", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1035", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1036", "mode": "normal", "text": "**256.** Where a recount or re-addition is made, the returning officer shall declare elected the candidate who obtained the greatest number of votes according to the results certified by a judge in accordance with section 273. Where the certified results show a tie for first place, a drawing of lots shall determine which candidate shall be declared elected. For the purposes of this paragraph, a co-candidate and the candidate with whom he is associated shall be counted as one candidate for the office of councillor.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1037", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1039", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1040", "mode": "normal", "text": "**257.** Where a drawing of lots is required, the returning officer shall give one clear day’s advance notice of it to each candidate concerned. At the time and place indicated in the notice, the returning officer shall carry out a public drawing of lots. He shall declare elected the candidate who is favoured by the drawing of lots.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1041", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1043", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1044", "mode": "normal", "text": "**258.** The declaration of election shall be made by means of a writing signed by the returning officer, indicating the date of the declaration, the name and address of the elected candidate and the office to which he is elected. Where such is the case, the returning officer shall read the declaration to the persons present at the place where he signs it.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1045", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1047", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1048", "mode": "normal", "text": "**259.** Within three days after the declaration of election of a candidate, the returning officer shall transmit a copy of the writing to the candidate.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1049", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1051", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1052", "mode": "normal", "text": "**260.** As soon as the returning officer has been informed of the complete results of the election, he shall give public notice thereof, indicating the candidate elected to each office. The returning officer shall transmit a copy of the notice to the chief electoral officer and to the regional county municipality or to the metropolitan community whose territory comprises that of the municipality.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1053", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1055", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1056", "mode": "normal", "text": "**261.** In no case may the person responsible for access to documents held by the municipality deliver any copy of any used ballot paper. He shall allow no one to examine the ballot papers, unless he is required to do so by order of the court or a judge.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1057", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1059", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1060", "mode": "normal", "text": "**262.** Any person who has reasonable grounds to believe that a deputy returning officer, a poll clerk or the returning officer has improperly counted or rejected votes or has drawn up an incorrect statement of the number of votes cast in favour of a candidate may apply for a recount of the votes. The application may be limited to one or certain polling subdivisions but the judge is not bound by that limitation. Any person who has reasonable grounds to believe that the returning officer improperly compiled the votes cast in favour of a candidate may apply for a re-addition of the votes. The first paragraph does not apply where the returning officer applies for a recount of the votes in the case of a tie.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1061", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1063", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1064", "mode": "normal", "text": "**263.** The application for a recount or re-addition is made by way of an application to a judge of the Court of Québec of the judicial district in which all or part of the territory of the municipality is situated, filed in the office of that court. The respondent is the candidate having the greatest number of votes according to the announcement made by the returning officer. Subject to any inconsistent provision of this subdivision, proceedings are conducted in accordance with the rules of contentious proceedings in the Code of Civil Procedure ( chapter C-25.01", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1065", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1067", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1068", "mode": "normal", "text": "**264.** The application must, on pain of dismissal, be served on the returning officer and presented within four days after the end of the addition of the votes. The first paragraph does not apply to an application for a recount of the votes in the case of a tie.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1069", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1071", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1072", "mode": "normal", "text": "**265.** No appeal lies from the decision on the application.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1073", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1075", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1076", "mode": "normal", "text": "**266.** The recount or re-addition shall be made by the judge who granted the application or by any other judge of the Court of Québec designated by the chief judge. It shall begin within four days after the decision granting the application and be carried out as soon as practicable.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1077", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1079", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1080", "mode": "normal", "text": "**267.** The judge shall give one clear day’s advance notice to the candidates concerned of the date, time and place at which he will proceed to the recount or re-addition of the votes. The judge shall summon the returning officer and order him to bring the ballot boxes used in the poll for the office concerned with their contents and the statements of votes used in the addition of the votes, where that is the case. Where the recount is limited to one or certain polling subdivisions, the judge shall order only the ballot boxes and statements he will need.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1081", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1083", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1084", "mode": "normal", "text": "**268.** On the appointed day, the judge, in the presence of the returning officer shall, in the case of a recount, examine the ballot papers and the other documents contained in the ballot boxes and, in the case of a re-addition, the statement of votes. The candidates concerned or their mandataries and the returning officer may, at that time, examine the ballot papers and other documents examined by the judge.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1085", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1087", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1088", "mode": "normal", "text": "**269.** The rules provided in Division V to establish the validity of a ballot paper apply at a recount. The judge may, for that purpose, take any measure he considers appropriate.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1089", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1091", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1092", "mode": "normal", "text": "**270.** If a ballot box or required documents are missing, the judge shall take any appropriate measure to ascertain the results of the vote. For the purposes of this section, the judge is vested with the powers and immunity of a commissioner appointed under the Act respecting public inquiry commissions ( chapter C-37 Every person testifying in an inquiry before the judge has the same privileges and immunity as a witness before the Superior Court. Articles 282 to 285 of the Code of Civil Procedure ( chapter C-25.01", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1093", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1095", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1096", "mode": "normal", "text": "**271.** While the recount or re-addition is in progress, the judge has the custody of the ballot boxes and their contents, and of all the other documents that have been remitted to him.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1097", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1099", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1100", "mode": "normal", "text": "**272.** Immediately upon completion of the recount, the judge shall verify or rectify the statement of votes and make a re-addition of the votes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1101", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1103", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1104", "mode": "normal", "text": "**273.** After completing the re-addition of the votes, the judge shall certify the results of the poll. The judge shall remit the ballot boxes, their contents and all the other documents used for the recount or re-addition to the returning officer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1105", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1107", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1108", "mode": "normal", "text": "**274.** The judge shall award and fix the amount of the costs according to the tariff established by government regulation. Where, according to the results of the poll certified by the judge, the candidate who received the greatest number of votes is the same as according to the announcement made by the returning officer, the costs of that candidate shall be assumed by the appellant. Where the recount is applied for following a tie, there shall be no costs.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1109", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1111", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1112", "mode": "normal", "text": "**275.** Costs are recoverable in the same manner as costs awarded in ordinary cases before the Court of Québec.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1113", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1115", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1116", "mode": "normal", "text": "**276.** The returning officer shall recommence election proceedings to fill an office on the council, subject to section 277, where", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1117", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1119", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1120", "mode": "normal", "text": "**277.** Within 30 days of ascertaining a situation justifying the recommencement, the returning officer shall fix the date of the poll on a Sunday in any of the four following months. Where that is the case, he shall notify the council as soon as practicable of the date fixed for the poll. The persons entitled to have their names entered on the list of electors or to be candidates are the same as in the original election. The list of electors in force shall be used and no new list need be prepared. The list shall be deposited as soon as possible after publication of the notice of election. No revision of the list is required if the revision was completed for the purposes of the original election. It is not necessary to give the public notice prescribed in section 56 if it was given for the purposes of the original election.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1121", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1123", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1124", "mode": "normal", "text": "**278.** Election proceedings may be recommenced only once. Where a situation arises justifying the recommencement of the proceedings a second time, the returning officer shall notify the Minister of Municipal Affairs, Regions and Land Occupancy, who may then appoint an eligible person to the office concerned or order that the proceedings be recommenced according to the rules he determines. The person appointed by the Minister is deemed to have been elected and declared elected on the day of his appointment.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1125", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1127", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1128", "mode": "normal", "text": "**279.** Voting is secret.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1129", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1131", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1132", "mode": "normal", "text": "**280.** No elector may, on the premises of a polling station, indicate publicly, in any manner, in favour of which candidate he proposes to vote or has voted. No candidate, representative or election officer may, on those premises, attempt to learn in favour of which candidate an elector proposes to vote or has voted. The building in which the polling station is located and any neighbouring place where the indications of the elector or the actions of the candidate, representative or election officer may be heard or seen by the electors waiting in line are deemed to be the premises of a polling station.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1133", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1135", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1136", "mode": "normal", "text": "**281.** No candidate or representative, nor any election officer or elector who has given assistance to another elector may disclose for which candidate the elector has voted.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1137", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1139", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1140", "mode": "normal", "text": "**282.** No person may be compelled to disclose for which candidate he has voted.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1141", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1143", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1144", "mode": "normal", "text": "**283.** No person may, on the premises of a polling station, use a sign to indicate his political affiliation or support for or opposition to a party, ticket or candidate or ideas promoted or opposed by the latter, or engage in any other form of partisan publicity. If the party, ticket or candidate promoted by prohibited partisan publicity refuses to stop or remove the publicity after being requested to do so, the returning officer may have it stopped or removed at the expense of the party, ticket or candidate. The building in which the polling station is located and any neighbouring place where the sign or partisan publicity may be seen or heard by the electors are deemed to be the premises of the polling station.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1145", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1147", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1148", "mode": "normal", "text": "**284.** For the sake of maintaining public trust in municipal election proceedings and ensuring respect for the principles of loyalty and political neutrality, an officer or employee of a municipality or of a mandatary body of a municipality referred to in paragraph 1 or 2 of section 307 may engage in partisan activity in connection with an election to an office on the council of the municipality only if the activity is not likely to interfere with the officer’s or employee’s ability to perform his or her duties loyally and impartially. Despite the first paragraph, the following persons may not engage in any such activity:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1149", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1151", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1152", "mode": "normal", "text": "**285.** Attending a political meeting, making a contribution to a party or an authorized independent candidate, being a member of a party or affixing a signature in support of a nomination paper or an application for authorization does not constitute partisan activity. The first paragraph does not apply to the clerk or the clerk-treasurer of the municipality or his assistant, to any other officer or employee of the municipality while he is an election officer, or to the treasurer, within the meaning of section 364, of a municipality, subject to Divisions II to IX of Chapter XIII.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1153", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1155", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1156", "mode": "normal", "text": "**286.** Every person entitled to vote at the election of a member of the council of a municipality may contest the election on the grounds that the person declared elected was ineligible, that he did not obtain the greatest number of the valid votes, that a corrupt electoral practice was used which caused the election to be null, or that the proper formalities were not observed. Every candidate defeated by the person declared elected may also avail himself of the first paragraph.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1157", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1159", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1160", "mode": "normal", "text": "**287.** An election is contested by way of an application to the Superior Court of the judicial district in which all or part of the territory of the municipality is situated. The respondent is the person declared elected. The returning officer must be impleaded.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1161", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1163", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1164", "mode": "normal", "text": "**288.** The application must, on pain of dismissal, be presented within 30 days after the respondent is declared elected, or within 30 days after the corrupt electoral practice was used where the application alleges that such a practice was used after the declaration. Where the alleged corrupt electoral practice consists in incurring election expenses in excess of the maximum fixed in Chapter XIII, the application must, on pain of dismissal, be presented within 90 days from the transmission of the return of election expenses.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1165", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1167", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1168", "mode": "normal", "text": "**289.** The applicant may demand that the election be declared null, or that the election be declared null and the candidate he identifies be declared elected.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1169", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1171", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1172", "mode": "normal", "text": "**290.** Proceedings are conducted in accordance with the rules of contentious proceedings in the Code of Civil Procedure ( chapter C-25.01", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1173", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1175", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1176", "mode": "normal", "text": "**291.** The rules of proof are those applicable in civil matters.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1177", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1179", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1180", "mode": "normal", "text": "**292.** The court shall decide that the member of the council whose election is contested was duly elected, that his election is null or that his election is null and another person designated by the court was duly elected.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1181", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1183", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1184", "mode": "normal", "text": "**293.** The court shall declare the election of the respondent null where the hearing establishes that a corrupt electoral practice within the meaning of section 645 was used by him or, with his knowledge or consent, by another person. The court shall declare the election of the respondent null where the hearing establishes that, without his knowledge and consent, his representative, mandatary or official agent or that of his party used a corrupt electoral practice, unless it is established that the practice could not have had a determining effect on the election of the respondent. For the purposes of this paragraph, a co-candidate and the candidate with whom he is associated shall be deemed to be reciprocal mandataries.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1185", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1187", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1188", "mode": "normal", "text": "**294.** The court shall declare the election of the respondent null where the hearing establishes that he failed to observe the proper formalities and that the inobservance may have had a determining effect on the election of the respondent.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1189", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1191", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1192", "mode": "normal", "text": "**295.** An appeal lies to the Court of Appeal from the judgment rendered on the application. The appeal must, on pain of dismissal, be brought within 30 days from the judgment. No appeal lies from any judgment in the course of a proceeding.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1193", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1195", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1196", "mode": "normal", "text": "**296.** The rules of contentious proceedings in the Code of Civil Procedure ( chapter C-25.01", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1197", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1199", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1200", "mode": "normal", "text": "**297.** The provisional execution of the judgment declaring the election of the respondent null does not result in the termination of his term or, as the case may be, his replacement by the candidate declared elected in his place. Notwithstanding the foregoing, during the provisional execution, the respondent is not entitled to attend, as a member, the sittings of the council of the municipality, of its committees and commissions, or of the council, committees and commissions of the regional county municipality, the metropolitan community or any intermunicipal board of management, or of any other board, committee, commission or public body of which the respondent is a member by reason of the fact that he is a member of the council of the municipality, the regional county municipality, the community or the board. The respondent shall consequently lose the right to receive the remuneration or allowance prescribed for each sitting he is not entitled to attend. Where his remuneration or allowance is not established for each sitting, an amount equal to 1% of the annual amount of the remuneration or allowance is subtracted for each sitting he is not entitled to attend. The sums shall be repaid to the respondent where the judgment having become a res judicata", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1201", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1203", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1204", "mode": "normal", "text": "**298.** The appellant shall notified to the clerk or the clerk-treasurer of the municipality a certified copy of the judgment having become a res judicata Where the judgment granting his application is appealed but is under a provisional order of execution, the appellant shall notify a certified copy of the appealed judgment and, if such is the case, of the order to the clerk or the clerk-treasurer. The clerk or clerk-treasurer shall immediately notify the council, the regional county municipality, the metropolitan community, the intermunicipal board of management or any other body whose sittings the respondent is no longer entitled to attend. He shall also notify them as soon as possible where the respondent recovers the right to attend.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1205", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1207", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1208", "mode": "normal", "text": "**299.** The person declared elected by the court in the place of another person is deemed to have been declared elected on the day the judgment having become a res judicata", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1209", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1211", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1212", "mode": "normal", "text": "**300.** A person holding office as a member of the council is disqualified from holding office as such", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1213", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1215", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1216", "mode": "normal", "text": "**301.** A person who is convicted of an offence under paragraph 1 of section 632 or an offence that is a corrupt electoral practice within the meaning of section 645, the Act respecting school elections to elect certain members of the boards of directors of English-language school service centres ( chapter E-2.3 The disqualification shall continue for five years from the day on which the judgment convicting the person becomes a res judicata.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1217", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1219", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1220", "mode": "normal", "text": "**302.** A person who is convicted, under any Act, of an offence which pursuant to an Act of the Parliament of Québec or of Canada is an offence punishable by imprisonment for a term of two years or more or which, if the prosecutor had proceeded by indictment, would have been punishable by two years of imprisonment or more is disqualified from holding office as a member of the council of a municipality. The disqualification shall last for a period equal to the longer of five years or twice the term of imprisonment, starting from the day on which the judgment convicting the person becomes a res judicata", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1221", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1223", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1224", "mode": "normal", "text": "**303.** Every person who", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1225", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1227", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1228", "mode": "normal", "text": "**304.** A person who knowingly, during his term as member of the council of a municipality or as member of a municipal body, has an interest, directly or indirectly, in a contract with the municipality or body is disqualified from holding office as a member of the council of a municipality. The disqualification shall continue for five years from the day on which the judgment declaring the person disqualified becomes a res judicata.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1229", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1231", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1232", "mode": "normal", "text": "**305.** Section 304 does not apply For the purposes of subparagraph 2.1 of the first paragraph, a solidarity cooperative is a solidarity cooperative whose articles include a clause prohibiting the allotment of rebates and the payment of interest on any category of preferred shares, unless the rebate is allotted or the interest is paid to a municipality, the Union des municipalités du Québec or the Fédération québécoise des municipalités locales et régionales (FQM).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1233", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1235", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1236", "mode": "normal", "text": "**306.** A person who knowingly, during his term as a member of the council of a municipality or member of a municipal body, uses his position to misappropriate moneys or commit a breach of trust or other misconduct is disqualified from holding office as a member of the council of a municipality. The disqualification shall continue for five years from the day on which the judgment declaring the person disqualified becomes a res judicata", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1237", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1239", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1240", "mode": "normal", "text": "**308.** Any elector of a municipality in which a person is a member or former member of the municipal council or is a candidate for that office may bring an action for the declaration of disqualification of that person. The Attorney General, the municipality and the Commission municipale du Québec, in accordance, if applicable, with the first paragraph of section 22 of the Municipal Ethics and Good Conduct Act ( chapter E-15.1.0.1", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1241", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1243", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1244", "mode": "normal", "text": "**309.** The action is brought before the Superior Court of the judicial district which includes all or part of the territory of the municipality. The action must, on pain of dismissal, be brought before the expiry of five years after the end of the term of office of the respondent during which the disqualification is alleged to have existed.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1245", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1247", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1248", "mode": "normal", "text": "**310.** The action is governed by the Code of Civil Procedure ( chapter C-25.01 An appeal lies from the judgment of the Superior Court in accordance with the Code of Civil Procedure.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1249", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1251", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1252", "mode": "normal", "text": "**311.** The provisional execution of the judgment declaring the disqualification of a person who is a member of the council of a municipality has the same effect as the provisional execution, provided for in section 297, of a judgment declaring his election null, with the necessary adjustments. The first paragraph applies also where the judgment grants a demand for ouster from office brought in accordance with the Code of Civil Procedure ( chapter C-25.01", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1253", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1255", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1256", "mode": "normal", "text": "**312.** The applicant must notify to the clerk or the clerk-treasurer of the municipality a certified copy of the judgment having become a res judicata Where the judgment is appealed but is under a provisional order of execution, the appellant must notify a certified copy of the appealed judgment and, where such is the case, of the order of execution to the clerk or the clerk-treasurer. The clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall, as soon as possible, notify the council, the regional county municipality, the metropolitan community, the intermunicipal board of management and every public body whose sittings the respondent is no longer entitled to attend. He shall also notify them as soon as practicable where the respondent recovers the right to attend. The first two paragraphs do not apply where the appellant is the municipality.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1257", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1259", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1260", "mode": "normal", "text": "**313.** Within 30 days after having been declared elected, the person elected shall make the oath provided in Schedule II. His term of office as council member begins when he makes the oath.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1261", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1263", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1264", "mode": "normal", "text": "**314.** The term of the mayor expires when the candidate elected to the office of mayor at the general election makes the oath or, if he fails to do so, at the expiry of the time prescribed therefor. The term of a person holding office as councillor expires when the candidate elected to the office at the general election makes the oath of office or, if he fails to do so, at the expiry of the time prescribed therefor. However, where a person holding office is a candidate for another office at a general election, his term expires at the time the candidate elected to either office makes the oath of office or, if he fails to do so, at the expiry of the time prescribed therefor.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1265", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1267", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1268", "mode": "normal", "text": "**315.** The term of a member of the council ends prematurely upon his death or, in accordance with this chapter, upon his resignation, failure to attend council sittings, disqualification, the annulment of his election or his ouster from office. The term of a councillor elected mayor by co-optation under section 336 ends prematurely when his term as mayor begins.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1269", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1271", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1272", "mode": "normal", "text": "**316.** A member of the council may resign from office by transmitting a writing to that effect signed by him to the clerk or the clerk-treasurer of the municipality. The term of the member ends on the date of transmission of the writing or on any later date specified therein. The clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall table the writing before the council at the first sitting after it is transmitted.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1273", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1275", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1276", "mode": "normal", "text": "**317.** The term of a member of the council who fails to attend council sittings for 90 consecutive days ends at the close of the first sitting after the expiry of the 90 days unless the member attends that sitting. The council may, at the first sitting after the 90 days, grant 30 days of grace to the member if he was in fact unable to attend the sittings. In such case, the term of the member ends 31 days later, unless he attends a sitting of the council during the period of grace. The council may also, not later than at the first sitting following the 90-day period mentioned in the first paragraph, order that a member’s failure to attend sittings of the council for serious reasons beyond his control and causing no prejudice to the citizens of the municipality or of the electoral district or ward, as the case may be, shall not entail the end of his term. The first three paragraphs do not apply where the member is unable to attend the sittings by reason of the provisional execution of a judgment declaring the nullity of his election or his disqualification or ouster from office or by reason of the existence of a judgment declaring him provisionally incapable under section 312.1. Nor do they apply where the member’s failure to attend sittings is due to the member’s pregnancy or the birth or adoption of the member’s child, provided that failure does not exceed a period of 18 consecutive weeks. Where the member fails to attend the first sitting after the expiry of the period specified in the first paragraph by reason of a suspension imposed by the Commission municipale du Québec under section 31 or 31.1 of the Municipal Ethics and Good Conduct Act ( chapter E-15.1.0.1 This section applies only to the member’s attendance in his capacity as member.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1277", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1279", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1280", "mode": "normal", "text": "**318.** The term of a member of the council who is disqualified or was disqualified during his term of office ends on the date on which the judgment declaring the member disqualified becomes a res judicata. Where the disqualification of a member results from the fact that, after his election, he became ineligible pursuant to section 62 or 63, he became a warden of a regional county municipality elected in accordance with section 210.29.2 of the Act respecting municipal territorial organization ( chapter O-9 Where the disqualification of a member results from the fact that he has been convicted of an offence described in section 301, his term ends on the day the judgment convicting him becomes a res judicata. The second and third paragraphs apply subject to sections 321 to 328.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1281", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1283", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1284", "mode": "normal", "text": "**319.** The term of a member of the council ends on the date the judgment declaring the nullity of his election or ousting him from office becomes a res judicata.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1285", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1287", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1288", "mode": "normal", "text": "**320.** The clerk or clerk-treasurer who ascertains that the term of a member of the council has ended by reason of his failure to attend sittings of the council, his disqualification, the nullity of his election or his ouster from office, shall notify in writing the Commission municipale du Québec as soon as possible. The Commission shall, after inquiry, ascertain whether or not the term of office has ended. It shall transmit, at the same time, a copy of its decision to the municipality and to the member concerned. The Commission may, even though it has not been notified as required by the first paragraph, act in accordance with the second paragraph. Where the Commission ascertains that the term has ended pursuant to the second or third paragraph of section 318, it shall attach a notice reproducing sections 321 to 328 to the copy of its decision.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1289", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1291", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1292", "mode": "normal", "text": "**321.** The member of the council may contest the Commission’s decision where the latter ascertains that the term of the member has ended pursuant to the second or third paragraph of section 318. The contestation must, under pain of absolute nullity, be made by means of a writing signed by the member and transmitted to the clerk or the clerk-treasurer and the Commission within 10 days after the transmission of the copy of the Commission’s decision. The Commission shall notify the municipality in writing of the date on which it received the writing in contestation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1293", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1295", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1296", "mode": "normal", "text": "**322.** In case of contestation, the Commission may apply for judicial confirmation of the date of the end of the term of the council member. The municipality, an elector of the municipality or the Attorney General may also make the application.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1297", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1299", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1300", "mode": "normal", "text": "**323.** An application for judicial confirmation of the date on which the member’s term ends is made by an application to a judge of the Superior Court of the judicial district in which all or part of the territory of the municipality is situated, filed in the office of the Court. The respondent is the council member whose end of term is the subject of the application for judicial confirmation. Subject to sections 326 to 328, the procedure shall be according to the rules of contentious proceedings in the Code of Civil Procedure ( chapter C-25.01", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1301", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1303", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1304", "mode": "normal", "text": "**324.** The application must, on pain of dismissal, be made within 30 days after the Commission receives the writing in contestation. An application by the Commission, an elector or the Attorney General shall be served on the municipality before being brought.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1305", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1307", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1308", "mode": "normal", "text": "**325.** If no application is brought within the prescribed time, the term of the council member shall continue. The clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall then notify the member as soon as practicable and the council at its next sitting. The member shall be notified in writing.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1309", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1311", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1312", "mode": "normal", "text": "**326.** The judge to whom the application is validly made may either grant it or dismiss it on the ground that the disqualification of the member of the council is not manifest and that the end of his term must be established, where such is the case, under the first paragraph of section 318 rather than under the second or third paragraph.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1313", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1315", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1316", "mode": "normal", "text": "**327.** No appeal lies from the decision of the judge.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1317", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1319", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1320", "mode": "normal", "text": "**328.** If the application is dismissed, the term of the council member shall continue. The clerk or clerk-treasurer shall then notify the member as soon as practicable and the council at its next sitting. The member shall be notified in writing. The judge’s decision cannot be pleaded as grounds for the inadmissibility of or as a plea of res judicata", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1321", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1323", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1324", "mode": "normal", "text": "**329.** Sections 318 to 328 apply to an elected candidate whose term has not begun and, except sections 325 and 328, prevent it from beginning.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1325", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1327", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1328", "mode": "normal", "text": "**330.** The office of a member of the council of a municipality becomes vacant on the day the person elected to that office is in default to make the oath that he will perform his duties according to law.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1329", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1331", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1332", "mode": "normal", "text": "**331.** The office becomes vacant on the day of the premature end of the term of its holder. The office does not become vacant where the premature end of the term is the result of a judgment which designates another holder. In the case where the premature end of the term occurs in circumstances described in the second or in the third paragraph of section 318, the office becomes vacant upon the expiry of the time prescribed for the transmission of the writing in contestation of the end of the term, if it is not contested, or, on the day on which the judge grants the application to confirm the end of the term, if it is contested.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1333", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1335", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1336", "mode": "normal", "text": "**332.** The office becomes vacant on the day fixed as the end of the term under sections 318 to 328 where the term of the person elected to the office cannot begin. Where the incumbent office holder is still in office on that date, the office becomes vacant on the day his term expires.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1337", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1339", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1340", "mode": "normal", "text": "**333.** The clerk or the clerk-treasurer, on ascertaining that an office has become vacant, shall notify the council at the next sitting or, if the council cannot sit, give public notice of the vacancy. Within 30 days after the date on which the clerk or the clerk-treasurer ascertains that an office has become vacant, he shall also notify the Minister of Municipal Affairs, Regions and Land Occupancy of the vacancy.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1341", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1343", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1344", "mode": "normal", "text": "**334.** This chapter does not apply to a vacancy existing, as a result of the application of the third paragraph of section 314 or of section 314.1, between the expiry of a term occurring after the election of a candidate to that office and the beginning of his term.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1345", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1347", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1348", "mode": "normal", "text": "**335.** Any vacancy occurring more than 12 months before the day fixed for the next general election must be filled by a by-election. Where the vacancy occurs 12 months or less before that day, the council may, within 15 days after notice of the vacancy, order a by-election to fill it.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1349", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1351", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1352", "mode": "normal", "text": "**336.** Where a vacancy occurs in the office of mayor 12 months or less before the day fixed for the next general election and the council has not ordered a by-election to fill it, the councillors shall elect one of their number to the office within 30 days after notice of the vacancy. The election shall be held by secret ballot at a sitting of the council. The clerk or clerk-treasurer shall determine the nomination and voting procedure. He shall declare the person who obtains the greatest number of votes elected. If there is an equality of votes, the person presiding at the sitting shall cast a vote in favour of one of the persons who have received an equal number of votes. The person elected shall, within the following 30 days, make the oath to perform his duties as mayor according to law.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1353", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1355", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1356", "mode": "normal", "text": "**337.** Where a vacancy occurs in the office of a councillor 12 months or less before the day fixed for the next general election and the council has not ordered a by-election to fill it, it shall not be filled until that general election. The first paragraph applies with the reservation that the Minister of Municipal Affairs, Regions and Land Occupancy may order a by-election or make an appointment to fill the vacancy in accordance with Division III.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1357", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1359", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1360", "mode": "normal", "text": "**338.** Chapters V to X, adapted as required and to the extent that they are consistent with this division, apply to a by-election. Notwithstanding the foregoing, the second paragraph of section 146 does not apply to a by-election.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1361", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1363", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1364", "mode": "normal", "text": "**339.** The returning officer, within 30 days after the notice of vacancy or after the council orders a by-election to fill the vacancy, as the case may be, shall fix, as polling day, a Sunday in the four months following the notice or decision. The Minister of Municipal Affairs, Regions and Land Occupancy, at the request of the returning officer, may grant him an extension or allow him to change, even outside the four-month period provided for in the first paragraph, the Sunday fixed as polling day and, consequently, to give a new notice of election. In the second case, the Minister shall prescribe the adaptations to be made to the rules applicable to the by-election. The returning officer shall notify the council as soon as practicable of the day fixed as polling day.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1365", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1367", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1368", "mode": "normal", "text": "**340.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1369", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1371", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1372", "mode": "normal", "text": "**342.** A person who holds another office on the same council is not eligible. Moreover, a member of the council of a municipality is not eligible to run for office as warden of a regional county municipality in an election held in accordance with section 210.29.2 of the Act respecting municipal territorial organization ( chapter O-", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1373", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1375", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1376", "mode": "normal", "text": "**343.** It shall not be necessary to prepare a list of electors of the municipality or, as the case may be, of the electoral district or ward, where the date fixed as polling day occurs 90 days or less after the last revision of the list of electors in force is completed. Where the returning officer does not draw up a new list, he shall deposit the list of electors in force as soon as practicable after publication of the notice of election and it shall not be necessary to give the public notice prescribed in section 56.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1377", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1379", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1380", "mode": "normal", "text": "**344.** Where the returning officer prepares a list of electors of the municipality or, as the case may be, of the electoral district or ward, he shall do so in the period beginning on the day of publication of the notice of election and ending 30 days before polling day.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1381", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1383", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1384", "mode": "normal", "text": "**345.** The clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall notify the Minister of Municipal Affairs, Regions and Land Occupancy in writing if any of the following events occurs and subdivision 2 of Division VII of Chapter VI is not applicable:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1385", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1387", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1388", "mode": "normal", "text": "**346.** Where an event described in section 345 occurs, the Minister may order the holding of a by-election or appoint an eligible person to fill the vacancy. The by-election is governed by Division II, except that the Minister shall designate the returning officer and fix the polling day. The person appointed by the Minister is deemed to have been elected and declared elected on the day of his appointment.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1389", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1391", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1392", "mode": "normal", "text": "**347.** Every employer shall, upon written request, grant leave without pay to his employee who is a candidate at a municipal election. The request may be made at any time after the date of publication of the notice of election, even before the employee becomes a candidate.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1393", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1395", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1396", "mode": "normal", "text": "**348.** Every employer shall, upon written request, grant leave without pay to his employee who is a member of the council of a municipality. The request may be made at any time after the date the employee is declared elected, even before he becomes a member of the council. Notwithstanding the foregoing, no employer may be required pursuant to the first paragraph to grant leave without pay to his employee for a total period of more than eight years or two terms, whichever is longer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1397", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1399", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1400", "mode": "normal", "text": "**349.** Every employer shall, upon written request, grant leave without pay to his employee who is the official agent of an authorized party or of an independent candidate or the deputy of an official agent. The request may be made at any time after the date of publication of the notice of election, even before the employee becomes an official agent or the deputy of an official agent.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1401", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1403", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1404", "mode": "normal", "text": "**350.** The leave begins on the day the employee becomes a candidate, a member of the council, an official agent or the deputy of an official agent, as the case may be, or on the first day for which he requested the leave, whichever is later. The leave of a candidate terminates on the day of the declaration of election to the office concerned, that granted to a member of the council terminates on the expiry of his term and that granted to an official agent or deputy terminates on the expiry of the time prescribed for the transmission of returns of election expenses. An employee may terminate his leave at any time by means of a thirty-day advance notice to the employer in the case of a council member or five days, in other cases.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1405", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1407", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1408", "mode": "normal", "text": "**351.** The leave may be full time or part time, according to the employee’s request. Where an employee requests part time leave, he shall specify the days or hours of his leave.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1409", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1411", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1412", "mode": "normal", "text": "**352.** Notwithstanding any agreement or Act inconsistent herewith, the employee, throughout his leave as a candidate, official agent or deputy, is entitled to all the benefits attached to his employment, except his remuneration.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1413", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1415", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1416", "mode": "normal", "text": "**353.** The employee who makes a written request to that effect at the beginning of his leave may, while on leave, continue to contribute to all the plans in which he participates provided he pays the totality of the premiums, including the employer’s contribution.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1417", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1419", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1420", "mode": "normal", "text": "**354.** At the expiry of the leave, the employer shall reinstate the employee, on the conditions of employment prevailing before the beginning of the leave or conditions more favourable for the employee, in accordance with the provisions of the collective agreement or, failing that, the agreement between the employer and the employee, taking into account the benefits to which he continued to be entitled during his leave.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1421", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1423", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1424", "mode": "normal", "text": "**355.** No employer may, by reason of the leave, dismiss, lay off, suspend, demote or transfer the employee or give him less favourable conditions of employment than he is entitled to or diminish any benefit attached to his employment and to which he is entitled. The employer shall not subtract the leave granted to an employee who is a candidate, an official agent or a deputy from the period of vacation of the employee.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1425", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1427", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1428", "mode": "normal", "text": "**356.** An employee believing himself to be the victim of a contravention of a provision of this division may file a complaint with the Administrative Labour Tribunal. The provisions applicable to a remedy relating to the exercise by an employee of a right under the Labour Code ( chapter C-27 An employee governed by a collective agreement or the association certified to represent him may elect to invoke the grievance settlement and arbitration procedure instead of filing a complaint with the Administrative Labour Tribunal. Sections 17, 100 to 100.10 and 139 to 140.1 of the Labour Code ( chapter C-27 Where a complaint is filed with the Administrative Labour Tribunal at the same time the grievance settlement and arbitration procedure is invoked, the arbitrator must refuse to hear the grievance.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1429", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1431", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1432", "mode": "normal", "text": "**357.** Within 60 days of the declaration of his election, every member of the council of a municipality must file with the council a written statement of his pecuniary interests in immovables located in the territory of the municipality and in the territory of the regional county municipality or of the metropolitan community on whose council the mayor of the municipality sits and in legal persons, partnerships and entreprises likely to make transactions with the municipality or any municipal body of which he is a member. The statement must include a list of the employments and administrative positions held by the member of the council and of the loans he has obtained from a person or body other than a financial institution and the loans he has granted to persons other than his immediate family members, on which the balance in principal and interest is over $2,000. The statement does not indicate the value of the interests listed or the extent of the interests of the council member in legal persons, partnerships or entreprises. No mention shall be made of any sum of money deposited with a financial institution or of any bonds issued by a government, a municipality or any other public body that may be held by the council member. For the purposes of the second paragraph, an immediate family member of the council member is the council member’s spouse within the meaning of the Interpretation Act ( chapter I-16", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1433", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1435", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1436", "mode": "normal", "text": "**358.** Every year, not earlier than at the sitting preceding the last regular sitting of the council and not later than the last regular sitting, each member of the council shall file an updated statement with the council.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1437", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1439", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1440", "mode": "normal", "text": "**359.** A member of the council who fails to file the statement within the prescribed time loses, from the 10th day following the expiry of the prescribed time and until the statement is filed, the right to attend in that capacity the sittings of the council of the municipality or of the committees and commissions thereof, of the councils, committees and commissions of the regional county municipality, the metropolitan community, or any intermunicipal board of management or of any other board, committee, commission or public body of which he is a member by reason of the fact that he is a member of the council of the municipality, regional county municipality, community or board. As soon as practicable after the expiry of the time prescribed for filing the statement, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall notify the member who has not filed the statement of his failure and of the effects thereof. As soon as practicable after the member has lost the right to attend sittings, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall notify in writing the Minister of Municipal Affairs, Regions and Land Occupancy, the council, the regional county municipality, the metropolitan community, the intermunicipal board of management and every other public body the sittings of which he is no longer entitled to attend. He shall also notify them as soon as practicable where the member files the statement and recovers the right to attend sittings.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1441", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1443", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1444", "mode": "normal", "text": "**360.** Every member who has lost the right to attend sittings loses, as a consequence, the right to receive the remuneration or allowance prescribed for each sitting he is not entitled to attend. Where the remuneration or allowance of the member is not established for each sitting, an amount equal to 1% of the annual amount of the remuneration or allowance shall be deducted for each sitting he is not entitled to attend.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1445", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1447", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1448", "mode": "normal", "text": "**361.** Every member of the council of a municipality who is present at a sitting when a matter in which he has a direct or indirect pecuniary interest is taken up for consideration shall disclose the general nature of his interest before discussions on the matter are begun and abstain from participating in the discussions and from voting or attempting to influence the vote on that matter. The first paragraph also applies to a sitting of any board, committee or commission of the municipality or of a municipal body of which the council member is a member. Where a sitting is not public, the member, in addition to complying with the requirements of the first paragraph, shall, after disclosing the general nature of his interest, leave the sitting while the matter is being discussed and voted on. Where the matter is taken up for consideration at a sitting not attended by the member, he shall disclose the general nature of his interest at the first sitting attended by the member after becoming aware of that fact.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1449", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1451", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1452", "mode": "normal", "text": "**362.** Section 361 does not apply where the member’s interest consists of remuneration, allowances, reimbursements of expenses, social benefits or other conditions of employment attached to his duties as a council member with the municipality or the municipal body. Nor does section 361 apply where the interest is so minor that the member could not reasonably be influenced by it.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1453", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1455", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1456", "mode": "normal", "text": "**364.** In this chapter, In this chapter, the expression “independent candidate” includes any person who has indicated the intention to become an independent candidate.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1457", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1459", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1460", "mode": "normal", "text": "**365.** Divisions II to IX apply to every municipality having a population of 5,000 or over. Where Divisions II to IX have begun to apply to a municipality, they continue to apply even if its population falls below 5,000.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1461", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1463", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1464", "mode": "normal", "text": "**366.** The Minister of Municipal Affairs, Regions and Land Occupancy may, upon request, order that Divisions II to IX cease to apply to a municipality having a population of under 5,000, on the terms and conditions he determines and render them again applicable to it in the same manner. Divisions II to IX shall become again applicable to the municipality once its population again reaches 5,000. The Minister shall publish in the Gazette officielle du Québec", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1465", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1467", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1468", "mode": "normal", "text": "**367.** The chief electoral officer shall see to the carrying out of this chapter. He may conduct studies on the financing of municipal political parties and independent candidates and their election expenses.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1469", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1471", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1472", "mode": "normal", "text": "**368.** The chief electoral officer shall, in particular, The Chief Electoral Officer shall have access to all the books, accounts and documents relating to the financial business of the parties and candidates. At the request of the Chief Electoral Officer, parties or candidates must furnish any information required for the purposes of this chapter within 30 days.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1473", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1475", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1476", "mode": "normal", "text": "**369.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1477", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1479", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1480", "mode": "normal", "text": "**370.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1481", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1483", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1484", "mode": "normal", "text": "**371.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1485", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1487", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1488", "mode": "normal", "text": "**372.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1489", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1491", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1492", "mode": "normal", "text": "**373.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1493", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1495", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1496", "mode": "normal", "text": "**374.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1497", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1499", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1500", "mode": "normal", "text": "**375.** Under the authority of the Chief Electoral Officer, the returning officer and, during an election period, the assistant designated by the returning officer to receive nomination papers, may grant an authorization to an independent candidate who files an application for authorization in accordance with sections 400 and 400.1. On granting an authorization, the returning officer or the assistant shall inform the Chief Electoral Officer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1501", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1503", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1504", "mode": "normal", "text": "**376.** For the purposes of the carrying out of this chapter, the treasurer is under the authority of the chief electoral officer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1505", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1507", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1508", "mode": "normal", "text": "**377.** The treasurer is entitled to receive a remuneration or an expense allowance from the municipality for the functions he performs. The council of the municipality may establish a remuneration or allowance tariff; the council may delegate that power to the executive committee, if any. Any tariff fixing a remuneration or allowance that is lower than that fixed by the tariff established by the Minister of Municipal Affairs, Regions and Land Occupancy under Title III shall be submitted for approval to the Minister. The treasurer of a municipality that has not established a tariff is entitled to the remuneration or allowance fixed by the tariff established by the Minister.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1509", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1511", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1512", "mode": "normal", "text": "**378.** Every party seeking or holding an authorization must have a leader. The leader must be an elector of the municipality in whose territory the party intends to carry on its activities.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1513", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1515", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1516", "mode": "normal", "text": "**379.** If the office of leader of an authorized party becomes vacant, the party must, within 30 days, appoint an interim leader and notify the Chief Electoral Officer of the appointment.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1517", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1519", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1520", "mode": "normal", "text": "**380.** Every party or independent candidate seeking or holding an authorization must have an official representative. An authorized party may also have a delegate of its official representative for each electoral district. For the purposes of the designation of the delegate, the municipal by-laws or the decision of the Commission de la représentation establishing the electoral districts may be taken into account upon coming into force.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1521", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1523", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1524", "mode": "normal", "text": "**381.** Every authorized party must have an official agent and it may also have deputy official agents. Every independent candidate must have an official agent.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1525", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1527", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1528", "mode": "normal", "text": "**382.** The official representative and the official agent of a party shall be the same person unless the leader decides otherwise. Where the offices of official representative and official agent are not held by the same person or where the office of official agent is vacant, the holder of the office of official representative is deemed to hold the office of official agent until the vacancy is filled. The official representative and the official agent of an authorized independent candidate shall be the same person.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1529", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1531", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1532", "mode": "normal", "text": "**383.** In no case may an official representative, his delegate, an official agent or his deputy be a person who Disqualification under subparagraph 7 of the first paragraph shall continue for five years from the day on which the judgment convicting the person becomes a res judicata.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1533", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1535", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1536", "mode": "normal", "text": "**384.** The leader of a party shall designate, in writing, the official representative of the party and, where such is the case, his delegate or delegates and the official agent of the party. An independent candidate shall designate his official representative and official agent in his application for an authorization under section 400.1 or in the writing he files with his nomination paper. The writing must include the designated person’s consent and be countersigned by him.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1537", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1539", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1540", "mode": "normal", "text": "**385.** The official agent of an authorized party may, with the approval of the leader of the party, appoint a sufficient number of deputies and authorize each of them to incur or authorize election expenses up to the amount fixed by him in each deed of appointment. The deed of appointment shall include the consent of the deputy and be countersigned by him. The amount fixed in the deed of appointment may, before the filing of the return of election expenses, be changed in writing by the official agent. However, the official agent may not reduce the amount of expenses to less than the amount of election expenses already incurred or authorized according to law by the deputy.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1541", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1543", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1544", "mode": "normal", "text": "**386.** Any person referred to in this subdivision may resign by transmitting a writing to that effect, signed by him, to the person who appointed him. He shall transmit a copy of the writing to the chief electoral officer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1545", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1547", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1548", "mode": "normal", "text": "**387.** Any vacancy in the office of official representative or official agent of an authorized party or of an independent candidate must be filled as soon as practicable. Notwithstanding the foregoing, where the offices of official representative and official agent of the party are held by two persons, a vacancy in the office of official agent need not be filled if the leader of the party decides that both offices will in the future be held by the same person.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1549", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1551", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1552", "mode": "normal", "text": "**388.** The leader of an authorized party shall, not later than 30 days after the day the authorization is granted, appoint an auditor from among the persons duly entitled to practise public auditing in Québec.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1553", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1555", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1556", "mode": "normal", "text": "**389.** The following persons shall not act as auditor: Disqualification under subparagraph 9 of the first paragraph shall continue for five years from the day on which the judgment convicting the person becomes a res judicata. The associates and the employees of the persons contemplated in subparagraphs 1 to 8 of the first paragraph are also disqualified from holding office as auditor.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1557", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1559", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1560", "mode": "normal", "text": "**390.** The auditor may resign by transmitting a writing to that effect signed by him to the party leader. He shall transmit a copy of that writing to the chief electoral officer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1561", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1563", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1564", "mode": "normal", "text": "**391.** Any vacancy in the office of auditor of an authorized party must be filled within 30 days after its occurrence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1565", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1567", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1568", "mode": "normal", "text": "**392.** Every authorized party or party whose application for authorization is pending shall, without delay, notify the chief electoral officer in writing of every appointment made under any of subdivisions 3 to 5, whether as actual holder of the office or as interim, of any vacancy in the office of official agent and of the decision of the leader of the party not to fill the vacancy in the office of official agent. The notice shall be given by the leader of the party, by the official representative or by any other person designated for that purpose by the leader of the party. If the notice cannot be given by one of those persons, it may be given by another officer. The notice of the appointment of the new leader of the party must be accompanied with a copy of the resolution to that effect passed in conformity with the by-laws of the party and certified by two or more officers of the party. The application for authorization constitutes a notice to the chief electoral officer of the appointment of the initial holders of the offices of leader and official representative.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1569", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1571", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1572", "mode": "normal", "text": "**393.** Every independent candidate shall, without delay, notify the chief electoral officer in writing of the appointment of his official representative or official agent whether as first holder of the office or as interim and of any vacancy in that office. The writing accompanying the nomination paper and the application for authorization constitute a notice to the chief electoral officer of the appointment of the initial holders of the offices of official representative and official agent.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1573", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1575", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1576", "mode": "normal", "text": "**394.** At the beginning of the election period, the treasurer shall post a list of the official agents of the parties, including any deputy official agents, and of the official agents of the independent candidates in the office of the municipality. He shall keep the list up-to-date during that period.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1577", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1579", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1580", "mode": "normal", "text": "**395.** Every party or independent candidate wishing to solicit or collect contributions, to incur expenses or to contract loans shall obtain an authorization from the chief electoral officer in accordance with this division.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1581", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1583", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1584", "mode": "normal", "text": "**396.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1585", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1587", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1588", "mode": "normal", "text": "**397.** The leader of the party shall transmit to the chief electoral officer a written application for authorization containing the following information: The application must be accompanied by a list including the names and addresses of party members who are electors of the municipality and who support the application; the minimum number of party members is set out in the third paragraph. The list must include the number and the expiry date of each person’s membership card and contain each person’s signature. The minimum number of party members who must be on the list is", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1589", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1591", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1592", "mode": "normal", "text": "**398.** The chief electoral officer shall grant the authorization to a party which applies therefor in accordance with this subdivision. The chief electoral officer shall refuse his authorization to a party if the name of the party includes the word “independent” or is likely to mislead the electors as to which party they are contributing to. The authorization is valid only in respect of the municipality mentioned in the application.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1593", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1595", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1596", "mode": "normal", "text": "**399.** An authorized party cannot change its name without the approval of the chief electoral officer who shall refuse to approve the proposed new name if it includes the word “independent” or is likely to mislead the electors as to which party they are contributing, or if the application for a change of name is made during the election period´. The application for approval is made by means of a writing by the leader of the party.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1597", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1599", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1600", "mode": "normal", "text": "**400.** The chief electoral officer shall grant an authorization to an independent candidate who applies therefor in writing and furnishes the following information: During the period for filing nomination papers, the application for authorization may be filed at the same time as a nomination paper. The authorization is valid only in respect of the municipality mentioned in the application.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1601", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1603", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1604", "mode": "normal", "text": "**401.** The authorization granted to an independent candidate entitles his official representative to solicit and collect contributions until polling day. After polling day, the authorization granted to the candidate entitles his official representative to solicit and collect contributions only for the purpose of paying the debts contracted during the term of his authorization and to dispose, for the purposes listed in section 498, of the funds or goods he obtained as a candidate and which remain in his possession. Where a candidate withdraws or is declared elected before the end of the polling period, his authorization entitles his official representative, after the withdrawal or declaration of election, to solicit and collect contributions solely for the purpose of paying the debts contracted during the term of his authorization incurred before the withdrawal or declaration of election and to dispose, for the purposes mentioned in the second paragraph, of the funds or goods he obtained as a candidate and which remain in his possession.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1605", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1607", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1608", "mode": "normal", "text": "**402.** The authorization granted to an independent candidate expires on 31 December of the second calendar year following the year of the election unless it is withdrawn before then. The authorization of an independent candidate who was elected and who has not, by that date, discharged all the debts contracted during the term of his authorization expires on the date the financial report establishing that all the debts have been discharged is filed.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1609", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1611", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1612", "mode": "normal", "text": "**403.** The chief electoral officer may, upon the written application of the leader, withdraw the authorization of a party. He may, upon the written application of an independent candidate, withdraw the candidate’s authorization. In the case of a party, the application must be accompanied with Notwithstanding the foregoing, the chief electoral officer shall not withdraw the authorization of an independent candidate who has not paid all the debts contracted during the term of his authorization.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1613", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1615", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1616", "mode": "normal", "text": "**404.** The chief electoral officer may withdraw the authorization of a party or independent candidate which or who fails to make an appointment required under subdivisions 3 to 5 of Division II, to furnish the information required for the purposes of the updating of the register as provided in section 424 or to give the Chief Electoral Officer access to all the books, accounts and documents relating to the party’s or candidate’s financial business, which or who contravenes Division IV or V, or whose official representative contravenes Division VI. In addition, the Chief Electoral Officer must withdraw the authorization of a party which does not comply with section 399.2 and may withdraw the authorization of a party which does not provide the information required under section 399.3. For the purposes of the first paragraph, the failure or contravention of a mandatary is deemed to be a failure or contravention of the party or of the candidate.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1617", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1619", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1620", "mode": "normal", "text": "**405.** The chief electoral officer shall withdraw the authorization of a party which changes its name if the new name includes the word “independent” or is likely to mislead the electors as to which party they are contributing, or the authorization of a party which changes its name during the election period.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1621", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1623", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1624", "mode": "normal", "text": "**406.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1625", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1627", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1628", "mode": "normal", "text": "**407.** The chief electoral officer shall withdraw the authorization of an independent candidate who dies. The chief electoral officer shall also withdraw the authorization of an independent candidate who joins a party. The chief electoral officer shall in addition withdraw the authorization of a person who has undertaken to run as an independent candidate but has not filed nomination papers on the expiry of the time prescribed to do so.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1629", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1631", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1632", "mode": "normal", "text": "**408.** The funds and assets of a party whose authorization has been withdrawn shall be remitted to the chief electoral officer by the persons holding them not later than ten days after they have been notified of the withdrawal. The party shall transmit to the chief electoral officer, within 60 days after the withdrawal of authorization, In addition, the party shall also, at the request of the chief electoral officer, remit to him any book, account or document relating to its financial business.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1633", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1635", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1636", "mode": "normal", "text": "**409.** The chief electoral officer shall liquidate the assets of the party. He shall pay the debts of the party out of the sums remitted to him and the proceeds of the liquidation of its assets. However, if the party’s liabilities exceed the assets, the chief electoral officer shall pay the respective creditors on a pro rata", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1637", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1639", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1640", "mode": "normal", "text": "**410.** After payment of the debts, the balance shall be remitted to the treasurer to be deposited into the general fund of the municipality.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1641", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1643", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1644", "mode": "normal", "text": "**411.** For the purposes of the liquidation of the assets of the party, the chief electoral officer may open accounts in financial institutions having offices in Québec, and designate two or more persons authorized to sign cheques or other orders of payment from among the members of his personnel.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1645", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1647", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1648", "mode": "normal", "text": "**412.** Where the authorization of the party is withdrawn during the election period, the chief electoral officer may prescribe changes to be made to the rules provided in this chapter to ensure the transition from the status of party candidate to that of authorized independent candidate.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1649", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1651", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1652", "mode": "normal", "text": "**413.** Where the authorization of an independent candidate is withdrawn at his request, the sums and assets remaining from those he obtained as a candidate shall be remitted to the chief electoral officer by the persons holding them not later than 10 days after they have been notified of the withdrawal. In such case, the second paragraph of section 408 applies, except subparagraph 3, with the necessary modifications. The chief electoral officer shall liquidate the assets and remit to the treasurer the proceeds of the liquidation and the sums that were remitted to him. The treasurer shall deposit the proceeds and the sums into the general fund of the municipality. Where the authorization of an independent candidate is withdrawn otherwise than at his request, sections 408 to 411 apply, adapted as required. However, in the case referred to in the second paragraph of section 407, the chief electoral officer shall, after payment of the debts, pay the surplus to the party the candidate has joined.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1653", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1655", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1656", "mode": "normal", "text": "**414.** The merger of authorized parties requires the authorization of the chief electoral officer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1657", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1659", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1660", "mode": "normal", "text": "**415.** The application for authorization shall be made by means of a joint application in writing of the leaders of the parties, containing the following information: The application must be accompanied with the balance sheet of each of the applying parties as at the date of the application.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1661", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1663", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1664", "mode": "normal", "text": "**416.** Each applying party shall, at the request of the chief electoral officer, remit to him any book, account or document relating to its financial business and have its balance sheet audited by an auditor.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1665", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1667", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1668", "mode": "normal", "text": "**417.** The chief electoral officer shall grant the authorization to merge to the parties which apply therefor in accordance with this subdivision. The chief electoral officer shall refuse his authorization where the name of the party resulting from the merger includes the word “independent” or is likely to mislead the electors as to which party they are contributing. The authorization is valid only in respect of the municipality mentioned in the application.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1669", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1671", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1672", "mode": "normal", "text": "**418.** Subject to any provision of another Act governing the merger or dissolution of one of the applying parties, the merger takes effect on the day authorization is granted by the chief electoral officer or on any later date indicated in the application. From the merger, the applying parties cease to exist and are replaced by the party resulting from the merger, which then succeeds to their rights and obligations.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1673", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1675", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1676", "mode": "normal", "text": "**419.** Within 60 days after the merger, a financial report for the period running from the date of authorization or, as the case may be, from the end of the period covered by the preceding financial report to the date of the merger shall be transmitted in respect of each applying party to the chief electoral officer. At the request of the chief electoral officer, the financial report shall be accompanied with a report of the auditor of the party.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1677", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1679", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1680", "mode": "normal", "text": "**420.** The official representative of the party resulting from the merger shall, not later than 1 April of the calendar year following that of the merger, file the financial report in accordance with Division VI for that part of the fiscal year that has lapsed since the merger. The financial report of the party shall be accompanied with an opening balance sheet at the date of the merger.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1681", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1683", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1684", "mode": "normal", "text": "**421.** The chief electoral officer may take such measures as he considers expedient to verify the accuracy of the information furnished in support of an application for authorization.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1685", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1687", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1688", "mode": "normal", "text": "**422.** Where the chief electoral officer intends to refuse or withdraw his authorization, he shall give the party or independent candidate, as the case may be, the reasons for his decision and an opportunity to be heard. Every summons is made by registered mail or by any other means considered valid by the chief electoral officer. The first and second paragraphs do not apply where the chief electoral officer is bound to withdraw the authorization, where the withdrawal of authorization is made at the request of the leader of the party and the copy of the resolution of the party is attached to the application, or where the withdrawal of authorization is made at the request of the independent candidate.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1689", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1691", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1692", "mode": "normal", "text": "**423.** As soon as practicable after granting or withdrawing his authorization, the chief electoral officer shall give notice of it on the Chief Electoral Officer’s website. The notice shall indicate the name of the official representative, and of his delegates, if any. The Chief Electoral Officer shall also give notice, on the website, of any replacement of an official representative or delegate or of any change in the name of an authorized party.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1693", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1695", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1696", "mode": "normal", "text": "**424.** The chief electoral officer shall keep, in respect of each municipality, a register of the parties and independent candidates he has authorized, setting out the following information:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1697", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1699", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1700", "mode": "normal", "text": "**425.** Every authorized party or authorized independent candidate shall, within 30 days, furnish in writing to the chief electoral officer, in addition to the information required under sections 392 and 393, all other information required for updating the register. Such information shall, in the case of a party, be furnished by the leader or official representative of the party or by any other person designated for that purpose by the leader and, in the case of an independent candidate, by the candidate or by his official representative. In the case of a party, the information may be furnished by another officer if none of the persons referred to in the second paragraph is able to furnish it.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1701", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1703", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1704", "mode": "normal", "text": "**426.** The chief electoral officer shall inform the treasurer of any change in the information contained in the register kept in respect of the municipality.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1705", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1707", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1708", "mode": "normal", "text": "**427.** The following are contributions: Where goods or services are furnished for political purposes to a party or candidate at a price lower than their value, the difference constitutes a contribution. For the purposes of this section, goods or services furnished by a trader dealing in similar goods or services shall be assessed at the lowest price at which he offers his goods or services to the public at the time they are furnished to the party or candidate; goods or services furnished by a person other than a trader dealing in similar goods or services shall be assessed at the lowest retail price at which they are offered to the public in the ordinary course of business, according to the market conditions prevailing in the area at the time they are furnished to the party or candidate.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1709", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1711", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1712", "mode": "normal", "text": "**428.** The following are not contributions:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1713", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1715", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1716", "mode": "normal", "text": "**429.** Only an elector of the municipality may make a contribution. An elector may make a contribution only in favour of a party or independent candidate holding an authorization that is valid for the municipality. However, an undivided co-owner of an immovable or a co-occupant of a business establishment may only make such a contribution if he is the person designated for that purpose by means of a power of attorney. Sections 55 to 55.2 apply to the power of attorney, with the necessary modifications.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1717", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1719", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1720", "mode": "normal", "text": "**430.** Every contribution must be made by the elector himself and out of his own property. It must be made voluntarily, without compensation and for no consideration, and may not be reimbursed in any way.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1721", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1723", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1724", "mode": "normal", "text": "**431.** The total amount of contributions, other than a contribution described in section 499.7, by the same elector for the same fiscal year may not exceed $100 to each of the authorized parties and independent candidates. During a fiscal year in which a general election is held, an elector may also make contributions the total of which may not exceed $100 to each of the authorized parties and independent candidates. In the case of a by-election, such contributions exceeding the maximum prescribed in the first paragraph may however only be paid as of the date on which notice of the vacancy is given up to the 30th day after polling day. In the case of undivided co-owners of an immovable or co-occupants of a business establishment, the maximum amounts set out in the first and second paragraphs apply as if the co-owners or co-occupants were a single elector. In addition to the contributions described in the first and second paragraphs, a candidate of an authorized party or an authorized independent candidate may, after the nomination papers have been accepted, make contributions for the candidate’s own benefit or that of the party for which the candidate is running, the total of which may not exceed $800.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1725", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1727", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1728", "mode": "normal", "text": "**432.** No contributions may be solicited except under the responsibility of the official representative or through persons designated in writing by the official representative. Every person authorized to solicit contributions shall, on request, produce a certificate of his capacity signed by the official representative.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1729", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1731", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1732", "mode": "normal", "text": "**433.** A contribution shall be made to no one except the official representative of the authorized party or independent candidate for which or for whom it is intended, or the person designated in writing by the official representative.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1733", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1735", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1736", "mode": "normal", "text": "**434.** The person who receives the contribution shall issue a receipt to the contributor. He shall remit any contribution he receives to the official representative along with a duplicate of the receipt in the form prescribed by the Chief Electoral Officer. The receipt must include the contributor’s given name and surname and domiciliary address, the amount of the contribution and a declaration signed by the elector that the contribution is being made out of the elector’s own property, voluntarily, without compensation and for no consideration, and that it has not and will not be reimbursed in any way.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1737", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1739", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1740", "mode": "normal", "text": "**435.** A delegate of the official representative of an authorized party has, for the electoral district for which he is appointed, the powers conferred on the official representative as person responsible for soliciting contributions, for designating persons to do the soliciting and for receiving contributions and duplicates of receipts of contributions. Every delegate shall transmit every contribution and duplicate of the receipt received to the official representative.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1741", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1743", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1744", "mode": "normal", "text": "**436.** Every contribution of money of more than $50 must be made by cheque or other order of payment signed by the elector and drawn on the elector’s account in a financial institution having an office in Québec and be made payable to the order of the authorized party or independent candidate. Such a contribution may also be made, in accordance with the directives of the chief electoral officer, by means of a credit card or by a transfer of funds to an account held by the official representative of the authorized party or independent candidate for which or whom the contribution is intended.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1745", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1747", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1748", "mode": "normal", "text": "**437.** (Replaced).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1749", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1751", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1752", "mode": "normal", "text": "**438.** On being cashed, a contribution is deemed paid by the person who made it and received by the party or the candidate for which or for whom it is intended.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1753", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1755", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1756", "mode": "normal", "text": "**439.** The official representative shall deposit, in a Québec branch of a financial institution, the funds of the party or, as the case may be, those obtained by an independent candidate in such capacity.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1757", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1759", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1760", "mode": "normal", "text": "**440.** If a contribution or part of a contribution was made contrary to this chapter, the party or independent candidate shall, as soon as the fact is known, remit such a contribution to the treasurer. The sums remitted must be paid into the municipality’s general fund. The Chief Electoral Officer may, after notifying the official representative of a party or of an independent candidate of his intention, apply to the competent court for an order to comply with the first paragraph.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1761", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1763", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1764", "mode": "normal", "text": "**441.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1765", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1767", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1768", "mode": "normal", "text": "**442.** Outside an election period, a radio, television or cable broadcaster or the owner of a newspaper, periodical or other publication may, without its constituting a contribution, make air time on the radio or television or space in the newspaper, periodical or other publication available free of charge to authorized political parties, provided he offers such service equitably as to quality and quantity to all the authorized parties in the municipality. The chief electoral officer shall verify the legality of services rendered under this section. Any time or space made available free of charge in accordance with section 464 is not a contribution.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1769", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1771", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1772", "mode": "normal", "text": "**443.** Expenses other than election expenses of an authorized party or independent candidate may be incurred only by the official representative or by a person designated by him in writing for that purpose. Every person authorized to incur such expenses shall, on request, produce a certificate of his capacity signed by the official representative.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1773", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1775", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1776", "mode": "normal", "text": "**444.** A delegate of the official representative of an authorized party has, in the electoral district for which he is appointed, the same powers to incur expenses and to designate persons to incur expenses as the official representative.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1777", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1779", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1780", "mode": "normal", "text": "**445.** The official representative of an authorized party or independent candidate shall pay the accounts and invoices that are transmitted to him within six months of their receipt, unless he contests them.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1781", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1783", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1784", "mode": "normal", "text": "**446.** Only the official representative of an authorized party or independent candidate may contract a loan for the party or candidate.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1785", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1787", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1788", "mode": "normal", "text": "**447.** Every loan shall be evidenced in a writing setting out the name and address of the lender, the date, amount, term and rate of interest of the loan and the terms and conditions of repayment of the principal and payment of the interest, which must take section 448 into account. Where an elector becomes surety for a loan, the contract of suretyship shall set out the name and address of the elector and the amount for which he becomes surety. The deed of loan or contract of suretyship shall also include a declaration by the elector stating that the loan is being granted or the suretyship contracted out of the elector’s own property, voluntarily, without compensation and for no consideration, and that it will not be reimbursed in any other way than as stipulated in the deed or contract.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1789", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1791", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1792", "mode": "normal", "text": "**448.** The official representative must, at least once a year, pay the interest due on the loans he has contracted.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1793", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1795", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1796", "mode": "normal", "text": "**449.** No sums of money other than those collected in accordance with this chapter may be used to repay the principal of or pay the interest on a loan which has been paid into an electoral fund referred to in section 457 or which has been used by the official representative or his delegate to pay election expenses pursuant to section 455.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1797", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1799", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1800", "mode": "normal", "text": "**450.** In addition, for the purposes of sections 452, 459, 460, 461 and 463, the expression “ election expense ” includes expenses referred to in paragraph 9 of section 453 and the expression “ official agent ” includes a private intervenor within the meaning of Division VIII.1 if the private intervenor is an elector, and the representative of such an intervenor if the private intervenor is a group of electors.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1801", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1803", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1804", "mode": "normal", "text": "**451.** The cost of any goods or services used during an election period to", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1805", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1807", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1808", "mode": "normal", "text": "**452.** Where goods or services are used both during and before an election period, the part of their cost that constitutes an election expense shall be established according to a method based on the frequency of use during the election period compared to the frequency of use before and during the election period.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1809", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1811", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1812", "mode": "normal", "text": "**453.** The following are not election expenses:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1813", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1815", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1816", "mode": "normal", "text": "**454.** The reasonable costs incurred by a candidate for attending a convention to select a candidate, for his transportation and other personal expenses are not election expenses provided they are not reimbursed to him and do not include the cost of any form of publicity other than the publicity made by the candidate at the convention.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1817", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1819", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1820", "mode": "normal", "text": "**455.** During the election period, no person other than the official agent of an authorized party or independent candidate or, for any amount up to the amount fixed by the official agent of the party pursuant to section 385, the deputy of the official agent, may incur or authorize election expenses, subject to section 456. All election expenses incurred or authorized by a deputy, up to the fixed amount, are deemed to have been incurred or authorized by the official agent. Within 60 days after polling day, every deputy shall furnish to the official agent a detailed account of the election expenses he has incurred or authorized accompanied with the invoices, receipts and other vouchers. The official representative or his delegate may incur or authorize an election expense contemplated in section 452. Any such expense is deemed to have been incurred or authorized by the official agent.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1821", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1823", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1824", "mode": "normal", "text": "**456.** An official agent may authorize, in writing, an advertising agency to incur or order election expenses up to the amount he fixes in the authorization. The amount may be changed in writing by the official agent before he files his return of election expenses. However, the official agent shall not reduce the amount below the amount of the election expenses already incurred or ordered according to law by the advertising agency. The advertising agency shall furnish to the official agent, within 60 days after polling day, a detailed account of the expenses incurred or ordered, accompanied with the vouchers and advertising proof, including the invoices of subcontractors.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1825", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1827", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1828", "mode": "normal", "text": "**457.** In no case may an official agent or his deputy pay the cost of any election expense otherwise than out of an election fund. Any election expense contemplated in section 452 and paid by the official representative or his delegate is deemed to have been paid out of an election fund.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1829", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1831", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1832", "mode": "normal", "text": "**458.** No sums of money other than those collected in accordance with this chapter by the official representative for an authorized party or independent candidate may be paid by him into the election fund put at the disposal of the official agent or be used by the official representative or his delegate to pay any election expense contemplated in section 452. The official agent shall deposit the sums paid into the election fund put at his disposal in an account opened for that purpose at a Québec branch of a financial institution. In the case of an authorized party, the account shall be separate from that of the official representative. It is not necessary to open such an account if the sums come exclusively from contributions made by an authorized independent candidate.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1833", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1835", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1836", "mode": "normal", "text": "**459.** No goods or services all or part of the cost of which constitutes an election expense contemplated in section 452 may be used during an election period except by the official agent of the authorized independent candidate or of an authorized party or his deputy, or with his authorization.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1837", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1839", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1840", "mode": "normal", "text": "**460.** No person may accept or execute an order for election expenses not given or authorized by the official agent of an authorized party or independent candidate, or in his name by his deputy or the advertising agency authorized by him, where such is the case.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1841", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1843", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1844", "mode": "normal", "text": "**461.** No person may claim or accept, for goods or services all or part of the cost of which constitutes an election expense, a price different from the regular price for similar goods or services outside the election period nor may he refuse to be paid for them. Nothing in the first paragraph prevents any person from performing any work under paragraph 1 of section 428.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1845", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1847", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1848", "mode": "normal", "text": "**462.** The official agent of an authorized party may, so long as no candidate of the party has filed his nomination paper for an office and before the expiry of the period prescribed for the filing of nomination papers, authorize election expenses to be attributed to the eventual candidate of the party for that office. If the party presents no candidate for the office contemplated in the first paragraph, the election expenses are attributed to the candidate of the party for the office of mayor or, failing such a candidate, to each of its candidates for the office of councillor, in equal proportions. Where the party presents no candidates, the election expenses shall be shown as expenses of the party in its financial report.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1849", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1851", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1852", "mode": "normal", "text": "**463.** Any advertising copy, object or material relating to an election shall bear the name of the printer or manufacturer and the name and title of the official agent or deputy who caused it to be printed or manufactured. Any advertisement relating to an election published in a newspaper or other publication must mention the name and title of the official agent or deputy who caused it to be published. In the case of an advertisement relating to an election broadcast on the radio or television or produced using any other medium or information technology, the name and title of the official agent or deputy, as the case may be, must be mentioned at the beginning or at the end of the advertisement. Any advertising copy, object or material, advertisement or publicity that relates to an election and is used jointly by authorized independent candidates must include the information required under the first three paragraphs and the name of each independent candidate in whose behalf the official agent is acting, with the words “independent candidate” next to it. Any goods or services all or part of the cost of which constitutes an election expense shall be deemed to relate to an election.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1853", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1855", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1856", "mode": "normal", "text": "**464.** During an election period, a radio, television or cable broadcaster or the owner of a newspaper, periodical or other publication may, without its constituting an election expense, make air time on the radio or television or space in the newspaper, periodical or other publication available free of charge to the leaders of the authorized parties and to candidates, provided he offers such service equitably as to quality and quantity to all the candidates for the same office or to all the leaders of authorized parties in the municipality. For the purposes of this paragraph, a co-candidate and the candidate with whom he is associated shall be counted as one candidate for the office of councillor. The chief electoral officer shall verify the legality of services rendered under this section.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1857", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1859", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1860", "mode": "normal", "text": "**465.** The amount of election expenses incurred by an authorized party or independent candidate during an election must not exceed, For the purposes of an election to the office of borough mayor, the combined lists of electors of all the electoral districts in the borough concerned is considered to be the list of electors of the municipality. The number of persons entered on the list for the purpose of calculating the amounts shall be the number established on the basis of the unrevised list or the revised list, whichever is higher. The Government may adjust the amounts provided for in the first paragraph according to the formula the Government determines. The Government shall publish the results of the adjustment in the Gazette officielle du Québec", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1861", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1863", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1864", "mode": "normal", "text": "**466.** Every payment of election expenses must be justified by an invoice showing the name and address of the supplier, the date the goods or services were supplied and the amount of the expense. Every payment of election expenses amounting to $100 or more must be justified by an itemized invoice. An itemized invoice must provide, in addition to the information required under the first paragraph, all the particulars required for verifying each item of goods or services and the rate or unit price used for computing the amount.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1865", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1867", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1868", "mode": "normal", "text": "**467.** Every person to whom an amount is due for election expenses shall present his claim to the official agent within 60 days after polling day. Where the offices of official agent and official representative are vacant the claim shall be presented within the same time to the leader of the party or to the independent candidate himself, as the case may be. No claim presented after the expiry of the prescribed time may be paid by the official agent or, as the case may be, by the leader of the party or the independent candidate. The claim shall in that case be presented to the treasurer within 120 days after the expiry of the prescribed time, failing which the claim is prescribed.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1869", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1871", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1872", "mode": "normal", "text": "**468.** Before filing his return of election expenses, the official agent shall pay every claim received within 60 days after polling day, except any claim he contests.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1873", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1875", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1876", "mode": "normal", "text": "**469.** The treasurer shall pay, out of the sums remitted to him with the return of election expenses pursuant to section 494 and according to the rules provided in sections 470 and 471 every claim received within 120 days after the expiry of the time prescribed for presenting claims to the official agent.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1877", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1879", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1880", "mode": "normal", "text": "**470.** The treasurer shall pay in full every claim the amount of which is equal to or less than the amount set aside for the claim by the official agent. Any excess amount shall be remitted by the treasurer to the official representative of the party or independent candidate after the expiry of 180 days after polling day.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1881", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1883", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1884", "mode": "normal", "text": "**471.** Where no amount has been set aside for a claim or where the amount set aside is less than the amount of the claim, the treasurer shall advise the official agent and forward the invoice to him as soon as practicable. The official agent may in that case contest all or part of the claim. Where the official agent does not contest the claim, or contests it in part, the official representative shall, if necessary, forward to the treasurer an additional cheque made to the order of the treasurer or make a transfer of funds to the account held by the treasurer to enable him to pay the claim or the uncontested part thereof. The treasurer shall pay the claim or the uncontested part thereof as soon as practicable after he is advised of the decision of the official agent or, where such is the case, after he receives the additional cheque or the transfer of funds.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1885", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1887", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1888", "mode": "normal", "text": "**472.** Any amount set aside for a claim that is not presented to the treasurer within the prescribed time shall be deposited into the general fund of the municipality.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1889", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1891", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1892", "mode": "normal", "text": "**473.** In no case may an official agent, the leader of a party or an independent candidate pay a contested claim or the contested part of a claim. Only the official representative may pay the claim or part of the claim in execution of a judgment of a competent court obtained by the creditor after a hearing of the case and not upon an acquiescence in the demand or an agreement of settlement. Notwithstanding the foregoing, where no party or independent candidate objects, the treasurer may authorize the official representative to pay a contested claim or the contested part of the claim if the refusal or failure to pay results from an error made in good faith. Where the claim arises from an election expense attributable to one particular candidate, the payment thereof may be contested only by a party having presented a candidate for the same office or by an independent candidate for the same office.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1893", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1895", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1896", "mode": "normal", "text": "**474.** Every independent candidate is required as of 31 December of the second calendar year following that of polling day, to have paid, in accordance with this subdivision, all debts contracted during the term of his authorization.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1897", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1899", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1900", "mode": "normal", "text": "**475.** The treasurer shall reimburse, out of the general fund of the municipality, an amount equal to 70% of the election expenses reported in the return of election expenses and incurred and paid in accordance with this division by a party for its candidate for the office of mayor and for each of its candidates for the office of councillor, if the candidate is elected or obtains at least 15% of the votes cast at the election for the office concerned. When computing the reimbursement, the treasurer shall subtract from the amount of the election expenses reported in the return the amount to which a party is entitled under sections 442.1 to 442.3 for its candidate for the office of mayor or borough mayor and for each of its candidates for the office of councillor.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1901", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1903", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1904", "mode": "normal", "text": "**476.** The treasurer shall reimburse, out of the general fund of the municipality, an amount equal to 70% of the election expenses reported in the return of election expenses and incurred and paid in accordance with this division by an independent candidate who is elected or obtains at least 15% of the votes cast at the election for the office concerned. When computing the reimbursement, the treasurer shall subtract from the amount of the election expenses reported in the return the amount to which an independent candidate is entitled under sections 442.1 to 442.3. However, the amount obtained by adding the amount paid under sections 442.1 to 442.3 and the amount of the reimbursement shall not exceed the total obtained by adding the amount of the debts arising from the election expenses of the candidate and the amount of the personal contribution of the candidate attested by a receipt referred to in the second paragraph of section 484.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1905", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1907", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1908", "mode": "normal", "text": "**477.** No reimbursement shall be made to a party until its return of election expenses has been filed. No reimbursement shall be made to an independent candidate until he has filed his return of election expenses and a financial report provided for in section 484.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1909", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1911", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1912", "mode": "normal", "text": "**478.** The reimbursement of the election expenses of a party shall be made to its official representative. The reimbursement of the election expenses of an independent candidate shall be made jointly to the candidate and to his official representative.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1913", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1915", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1916", "mode": "normal", "text": "**479.** The official representative of every authorized party shall, not later than 1 April each year, file with the treasurer a financial report for the preceding fiscal year in the form prescribed by a directive of the chief electoral officer. The report must contain a balance sheet, an income statement and a cash flow statement prepared in accordance with generally recognized accounting principles. If 1 April falls during an election period, the financial report shall be filed not later than 90 days after polling day.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1917", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1919", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1920", "mode": "normal", "text": "**480.** The income statement must include a general statement of revenues and total expenditures and indicate, in addition,", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1921", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1923", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1924", "mode": "normal", "text": "**481.** The financial report shall also indicate The information described in subparagraph 3 of the first paragraph shall be presented according to the alphabetical order of the names of the electors.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1925", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1927", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1928", "mode": "normal", "text": "**482.** If the auditor of the party must audit the financial report, it shall be deemed filed with the treasurer only if it is accompanied by the report of the auditor of the party.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1929", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1931", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1932", "mode": "normal", "text": "**483.** The official representative of the party shall keep the receipts issued for contributions for seven years after the date the financial report was filed as well as the vouchers necessary to ascertain compliance with sections 430 and 436. The receipts and vouchers shall be remitted to the chief electoral officer every three months. The official representative of the party shall also keep the invoices, evidences of payment and other vouchers relating to the preparation of the financial report for seven years.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1933", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1935", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1936", "mode": "normal", "text": "**484.** The official representative of an authorized independent candidate must, within 90 days after polling day, file a financial report with the treasurer. The report must contain the same information, adapted as required, as that contained in the financial report of a party, except the balance sheet and the cash flow statement, and be accompanied with a copy of every receipt issued for contributions received during the period covered by the report. The financial report must be filed at the same time as the candidate’s return of election expenses and cover the period ending the day before the filing.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1937", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1939", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1940", "mode": "normal", "text": "**485.** If, on the day he files a financial report provided for in section 484, an authorized independent candidate still has debts contracted during the term of his authorization or his official representative is in possession of sums of money or goods obtained by the candidate in his capacity as such, the official representative shall file a financial report with the treasurer not later than 1 April of the year immediately following each fiscal year in which the candidate remained authorized after the filing of the financial report provided for in section 484. Notwithstanding the foregoing, the official representative is not required to file any further financial reports after the filing of a financial report establishing that all the debts contemplated in the first paragraph have been paid. The financial report of an authorized independent candidate must contain the same information, adapted as required, as that contained in the financial report of a party, except the balance sheet and the cash flow statement, and be accompanied with a copy of every receipt issued for contributions received during the period covered by the report. The first report following that provided for in section 484 must cover the period beginning on the day the latter is filed and ending on 31 December next. The report, other than that provided for in section 484, establishing that all debts contracted during the term of his authorization have been paid must cover the period beginning at the end of the period covered by the preceding report and ending on the day all debts are paid.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1941", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1943", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1944", "mode": "normal", "text": "**486.** The chief electoral officer shall transmit to the treasurer a copy of every financial report submitted to him in connection with an application for withdrawal of authorization or with a joint application for authorization to merge.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1945", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1947", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1948", "mode": "normal", "text": "**487.** For the purposes of the first paragraph, “ previous report ” means any financial report already filed as well as any financial report that must be filed. The official representative is required to file the latter report even if he has resigned. Any official representative who ceases to hold office shall, within the ensuing 60 days, transmit to the leader of the party or independent candidate a financial report covering the period during which he was in office that is not covered by a previous report, accompanied with every receipt issued during that period as well as any invoices, evidences of payment and vouchers he has in his possession.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1949", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1951", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1952", "mode": "normal", "text": "**488.** The auditor of an authorized party shall audit the financial report of the party if the revenues exceed $5,000. The auditor shall then deliver to the official representative, not later than five days before the expiry of the time prescribed by section 479 for the filing of the financial report, the audit report prepared in accordance with the directive on preparation issued by the chief electoral officer. Any reimbursement of election expenses or of the expense incurred for the audit of a financial report as well as any supplemental public financing shall be excluded from the revenues referred to in the first paragraph.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1953", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1955", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1956", "mode": "normal", "text": "**489.** The auditor shall have access to all the books, accounts and documents pertaining to the financial business of the party.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1957", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1959", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1960", "mode": "normal", "text": "**490.** The treasurer shall reimburse, out of the general fund of the municipality, the expense incurred by the party for the audit of its financial report, up to the amount of The amounts prescribed in the first paragraph are adjusted on 1 January each year according to the amendment in the average Consumer Price Index for the preceding year, based on the index established for the whole of Québec by Statistics Canada. Those amounts are rounded down to the nearest dollar if they include a fraction that is less than $0.50, or up to the nearest dollar if they include a fraction that is equal to or greater than $0.50. The Minister of Municipal Affairs, Regions and Land Occupancy shall publish the results of the adjustment in the Gazette officielle du Québec", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1961", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1963", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1964", "mode": "normal", "text": "**491.** Where the chief electoral officer requires the audit of a balance sheet submitted with a joint application for authorization to merge or the audit of a financial report submitted after a merger, he shall reimburse the expense incurred for the audit up to the amount prescribed in section 490. Where the chief electoral officer requires the audit of a closing financial report, he shall appoint the auditor and pay the cost of the audit.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1965", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1967", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1968", "mode": "normal", "text": "**492.** The official agent of every authorized party or independent candidate must, within 90 days after polling day, file a return of election expenses with the treasurer in the form prescribed by a directive of the chief electoral officer. The return must include a statement by the official agent attesting the accuracy of the return. The return must be accompanied with the invoices, receipts and other vouchers, or certified copies of those documents, and a list thereof. Where the official agent has appointed a deputy, the return must be accompanied with the deed of appointment and any modification thereto. In the case of an independent candidate, the return must be filed at the same time as his financial report.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1969", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1971", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1972", "mode": "normal", "text": "**493.** In addition to election expenses, the official agent shall indicate in the return the source of the sums paid into the election fund put at his disposal. He shall also mention any claim he is contesting among those he received within 60 days after polling day.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1973", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1975", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1976", "mode": "normal", "text": "**494.** The return of election expenses must be accompanied with an itemized statement setting forth the names and addresses of the creditors who omitted to file their claims within 60 days after polling day, and for each such claim, the amount of the debt, the nature of the goods or services furnished and the date on which they were furnished. The statement must be accompanied with a cheque drawn on the election fund and made to the order of the treasurer for the total amount of the claims contemplated in the first paragraph or with a transfer of funds to the account held by the treasurer. The Chief Electoral Officer may, by directive, determine the terms governing the transfer of funds. The first and second paragraphs do not apply to claims the official agent intends to contest.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1977", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1979", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1980", "mode": "normal", "text": "**495.** The sums remitted to the treasurer to cover the total amount of the unclaimed debts shall be kept by him in the general fund of the municipality.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1981", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1983", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1984", "mode": "normal", "text": "**496.** Any official agent who ceases to hold office before the filing of the return of election expenses under section 492 shall, within the ensuing 10 days, transmit to the leader of the party or independent candidate a return of election expenses covering the period during which he was in office, accompanied with the relevant invoices, receipts and other vouchers and, where such is the case, the deed of appointment of a deputy and any modification thereto. The first paragraph does not dispense the official agent from filing his return of election expenses within the prescribed time even if he has resigned, where such is the case, unless a person has been appointed to replace him.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1985", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1987", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1988", "mode": "normal", "text": "**497.** Every payment of election expenses made after the filing of the return of election expenses in accordance with subdivision 3 of Division V entails an automatic correction of the return of election expenses.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1989", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1991", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1992", "mode": "normal", "text": "**498.** The official agent of an authorized party shall, as soon as practicable after the filing of his return of election expenses, remit to the official representative the sums remaining in his election fund and the goods in his possession all or part of the cost of which constitutes an election expense. After the filing of the return of election expenses, the official representative of an authorized independent candidate shall keep, in that capacity, the sums remaining in the election fund and the goods that are in his possession in his capacity as official agent and all or part of the cost of which constitutes an election expense. He may, in particular, use the sums or the proceeds from the disposition of the goods, provided a fair price was obtained, to pay or cause the treasurer to pay a claim that, pursuant to subdivision 3 of Division V, may be paid after the filing of the return of election expenses. Any balance of the sums referred to in the second paragraph and of the proceeds from the disposition of the goods referred to therein remaining on 31 December of the calendar year following that of polling day, shall be remitted to the treasurer to be deposited into the general fund of the municipality. The goods referred to in the said paragraph that are in the possession on that date of the official representative belong and shall be remitted to the municipality.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1993", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1995", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "1996", "mode": "normal", "text": "**499.** Within 30 days after the expiry of the time prescribed for filing returns of election expenses, the treasurer shall publish a summary of every return received within the prescribed time in a newspaper having general circulation in the municipality. The summary must be accompanied with a notice of the date of receipt of each return and accompanying documents and stating the fact that the public has access to them.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1997", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "1999", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2000", "mode": "normal", "text": "**500.** The treasurer shall, on request, send the Chief Electoral Officer a copy of the reports, returns and documents not already in his possession, except receipts issued for contributions of $50 or less.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2001", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2003", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2004", "mode": "normal", "text": "**501.** The treasurer shall keep the reports, returns, invoices, receipts and other vouchers necessary to ascertain compliance with sections 430 and 436 for seven years after they are received. After the expiry of seven years following the receipt of invoices, receipts and other vouchers, the treasurer may, on request, return them to the party or the independent candidate. Failing such a request, the treasurer may destroy them.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2005", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2007", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2008", "mode": "normal", "text": "**502.** The leader of a party whose financial report or return of election expenses is not filed within the prescribed time loses the right to attend the sittings of the council of the municipality as a member thereof from the tenth day after the expiry of the prescribed time until the report or return is filed, subject to section 505. Where the leader is not a member of the council, the person who was the candidate of the party for the office of mayor at the last election loses the right to attend sittings pursuant to the first paragraph; where that person, also, is not a member of the council, the person who loses the right to attend sittings is the member of the council who, at the last election, was the candidate of the party that obtained the greatest number of votes. Where the party no longer exists, the leader referred to in the first paragraph is the last holder of that position. The first three paragraphs do not apply to a person who resigned from the party if a copy of the person’s letter of resignation was transmitted to the treasurer and the chief electoral officer not less than three months before the expiry of the time fixed for transmission of the report.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2009", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2011", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2012", "mode": "normal", "text": "**503.** An independent candidate who is elected and whose financial report or return of election expenses is not filed within the prescribed time loses the right to attend as a member the sittings of the council of the municipality from the tenth day after the expiry of the prescribed time until the report or return is filed, subject to section 505.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2013", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2015", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2016", "mode": "normal", "text": "**504.** The loss of the right to attend the sittings of the council of the municipality entails the loss of the right to attend, as a member, the sittings of", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2017", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2019", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2020", "mode": "normal", "text": "**505.** A judge may, by order, on an application made before the person loses the right to attend sittings, allow him to continue to do so for an additional period of not more than 30 days.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2021", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2023", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2024", "mode": "normal", "text": "**506.** On proof that the failure to file the report or return is due to the absence, death, illness, misconduct or physical disability of the official representative or official agent, a case of irresistible force or any other reasonable cause, the Chief Electoral Officer may determine an additional period of time for the preparation and delivery of the report or return.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2025", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2027", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2028", "mode": "normal", "text": "**507.** Where an error is found in a report or return that has been filed, the official agent or the official representative may correct it at any time within the period prescribed for filing the report or return. After the period prescribed for filing, the leader of the party or the independent candidate must obtain leave from the chief electoral officer to correct the error on establishing that it was made through inadvertence. Any opposition to the application for correction shall be submitted to the chief electoral officer. If there is no opposition to the application or the chief electoral officer considers that the opposition is not justified, the chief electoral officer shall allow the correction. Otherwise, the leader or candidate shall apply for leave to the judge having jurisdiction.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2029", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2031", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2032", "mode": "normal", "text": "**508.** The judge having jurisdiction to rule on an application under sections 505 and 507 is a judge of the Court of Québec of the judicial district where all or part of the territory of the municipality is situated. No application made under sections 505 to 507 may be heard unless a notice of at least three clear days is given by the applicant to the treasurer, to every candidate for the office concerned at the last election and, where the applicant is the leader of a party, to the leader of every other authorized party.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2033", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2035", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2036", "mode": "normal", "text": "**509.** An independent candidate who is elected and who, on 31 December of the second calendar year following that of polling day, has not paid all debts contracted during the term of his authorization, loses the right to attend, as a member, the sittings of the council of the municipality from that date and until he has paid all such debts and filed a financial report establishing that he has done so. The loss of the right to attend the sittings of the council of the municipality entails the loss of the right to attend, as a member, the sittings of the councils, boards, committees, commissions and bodies referred to in section 504.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2037", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2039", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2040", "mode": "normal", "text": "**510.** If at the expiry of the prescribed time the treasurer has not received the report or return, he shall, as soon as practicable, notify in writing the person who may lose the right to attend sittings of such failure and of the effects thereof. If on 31 December of the second calendar year following that of polling day, the treasurer has not received a financial report from an elected independent candidate establishing that all debts contracted during the term of his authorization have been paid, he shall, as soon as practicable, notify in writing that council member of such failure and of the effects thereof.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2041", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2043", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2044", "mode": "normal", "text": "**511.** As soon as practicable after a person has lost the right to attend the sittings of the council of the municipality, the treasurer shall notify the council, the regional county municipality, the metropolitan community, the intermunicipal board of management and any other body whose sittings he is no longer entitled to attend. The treasurer shall also notify them as soon as practicable where the person recovers the right to attend sittings.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2045", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2047", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2048", "mode": "normal", "text": "**512.** A person who loses the right to attend sittings consequently loses the right to receive the remuneration or allowance provided for each sitting he is not authorized to attend. Where the remuneration or allowance is not established for each sitting, 1% shall be deducted from the annual amount for each sitting the person is not authorized to attend.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2049", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2051", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2052", "mode": "normal", "text": "**513.** The treasurer shall, if applicable, not later than 1 April of each year, table before the council of the municipality a report of his operations under this chapter for the preceding fiscal year. He shall also transmit the report to the chief electoral officer.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2053", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2055", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2056", "mode": "normal", "text": "**514.** For the purposes of this Title,", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2057", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2059", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2060", "mode": "normal", "text": "**515.** This Title applies to all local municipalities except the Northern, Cree or Naskapi villages.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2061", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2063", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2064", "mode": "normal", "text": "**516.** This Title governs the consultative referendums contemplated in Chapter II and all referendums held pursuant to a general law or special Act which consist in submitting a municipal by-law, resolution or ordinance to the qualified voters of the municipality or of another municipality for approval where that approval is a prerequisite to the passage or putting into force of the by-law, resolution or ordinance. This Title also governs every consultation of qualified voters which, under the Act providing therefor, must be conducted in accordance with this Title.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2065", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2067", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2068", "mode": "normal", "text": "**517.** The council of a municipality may for consultation purposes submit any question within its competence to its qualified voters or to those of that part of its territory concerned by the question. The question shall be formulated in such a manner as to require “yes” or “no” as an answer; it shall be defined by a resolution which, for the purposes of this Title, is deemed to be the subject of the referendum. The council may order that a referendum poll be held without it being subject to the provisions of Chapter IV.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2069", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2071", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2072", "mode": "normal", "text": "**518.** A person is a qualified voter of the municipality or, as the case may be, of the sector concerned, if, on the date of reference, the person is not disqualified from voting under section 524 and meets one of the following two requirements: A natural person must also be, on the date of reference, of full age and a Canadian citizen, and must not be disqualified from voting as a result of a judgment rendered under article 288 of the Civil Code.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2073", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2075", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2076", "mode": "normal", "text": "**519.** The domicile of a person is as provided in the Civil Code for all civil purposes. Notwithstanding the foregoing, a person who has left his principal establishment in Québec for more than one year is deemed to have changed his domicile except where he carries on duties outside Québec on behalf of the Government of Québec or of Canada.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2077", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2079", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2080", "mode": "normal", "text": "**520.** A detained person retains his domicile notwithstanding his detention.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2081", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2083", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2084", "mode": "normal", "text": "**521.** A person who leaves his domicile temporarily to work or study in the territory of another municipality may be considered as being domiciled either in the territory where his actual domicile is situated or in the territory where he resides for the purposes of his work or studies. A person living in a facility maintained by an institution which operates a hospital centre, a residential and long-term care centre or a rehabilitation centre within the meaning of the Act respecting the governance of the health and social services system ( chapter G-1.021 A person is deemed to choose to be considered domiciled at the place where he resides rather than at his actual domicile where he makes an application to that effect during the revision of the list of electors or referendum list. The person’s choice remains valid until it is revoked and as long as the person resides at the same place.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2085", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2087", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2088", "mode": "normal", "text": "**522.** The rules provided in the Civil Code concerning the setting up, against third persons, of acts transferring immovable real rights apply in determining whether a person is the owner of an immovable.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2089", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2091", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2092", "mode": "normal", "text": "**523.** To exercise a right conferred by a provision of this Title, a qualified voter must, on the date of exercising the right, meet the requirements that would, if that date were the date of reference, qualify the person as a voter entitled to have his name entered on the referendum list of the municipality or, as the case may be, of the sector concerned. In the case of the right to vote, the person’s name must also, at the time of voting, be entered on the referendum list of the municipality or, as the case may be, of the sector concerned. A qualified voter who obtained an authorization to vote under the first paragraph of section 219 and section 567 is, after being admitted to vote under the second paragraph of section 219 and section 567, deemed to have his name entered on the list at the place where it should have been entered.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2093", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2095", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2096", "mode": "normal", "text": "**524.** Any person who is convicted of an offence that is a corrupt electoral practice within the meaning of section 645, the Act respecting school elections to elect certain members of the boards of directors of English-language school service centres ( chapter E-2.3 The disqualification shall continue for five years from the day the judgment convicting the person becomes a res judicata.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2097", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2099", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2100", "mode": "normal", "text": "**525.** Every qualified voter of the municipality or, as the case may be, of the sector concerned, is entitled to have his name entered on the referendum list. However, in the case of undivided co-owners of an immovable and of co-occupants of a business establishment, only the co-owner or the co-occupant designated for that purpose pursuant to section 526 is entitled to have his name entered on the referendum list as the owner of the immovable or as the occupant of the business establishment.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2101", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2103", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2104", "mode": "normal", "text": "**526.** Co-owners or co-occupants who are qualified voters of the municipality or, as the case may be, of the sector concerned shall designate, from among themselves, if necessary, by means of a power of attorney signed by a majority of them, a person who is not entitled, under section 531, to have his name entered on the referendum list in a higher ranking capacity.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2105", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2107", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2108", "mode": "normal", "text": "**527.** Not later than 40 days before the day fixed for the referendum poll, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall give a public notice stating that sole owners or occupants and designated co-owners and co-occupants are entitled to have their names entered on the referendum list and mentioning how they may obtain information on the rules governing the entry of their names on the referendum list. The notice shall invite sole owners and occupants who wish to make a first application for entry or to withdraw the existing entry to transmit to the clerk or the clerk-treasurer, within the prescribed time, the application, a signed writing or a resolution requesting the withdrawal. The notice shall also invite co-owners and co-occupants who wish to make a first designation or replace the existing designation to transmit to the clerk or the clerk-treasurer, within the prescribed time, the power of attorney.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2109", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2111", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2112", "mode": "normal", "text": "**528.** Every legal person qualified to vote shall exercise its rights under this Title through one of its members, directors or employees designated by it for that purpose by resolution. The person designated must, on the date of reference and upon exercising any of those rights, be of full age and a Canadian citizen, and must be neither disqualified from voting under section 524 nor disqualified from voting as a result of a judgment rendered under article 288 of the Civil Code. The name of the designated person shall be placed next to that of the legal person on the referendum list. The resolution takes effect upon receipt by the municipality and remains valid until it is replaced. A resolution adopted for the purposes of the referendum list to be used in a poll must be transmitted to the clerk or the clerk-treasurer not later than 30 days before the day fixed for the referendum poll. A resolution transmitted after the time prescribed in the fifth paragraph but before the end of the work of the board of revisors on the last day fixed for applications to be made under sections 132 and 561 shall be deemed to be an application to amend the referendum list, unless the clerk or the clerk-treasurer has taken it into account before the deposit of the list. The clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall transmit any such resolution to the competent board of revisors.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2113", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2115", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2116", "mode": "normal", "text": "**529.** Not later than 40 days before the day fixed for the referendum poll, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall give a public notice stating that legal persons are entitled to designate a representative, mentioning how they may obtain information on the rules governing the designation of a representative, and inviting the legal persons wishing to make a first designation or replace the existing designation to send him the resolution within the prescribed time.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2117", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2119", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2120", "mode": "normal", "text": "**530.** In no case may the name of a person appear more than once on the referendum list of the municipality or, as the case may be, of the sector concerned. The first paragraph does not apply to a qualified voter who is designated to represent a legal person or to a person designated to represent several legal persons.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2121", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2123", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2124", "mode": "normal", "text": "**531.** In addition to having his name entered on the list following a designation to represent a legal person, where such is the case, a person who is, in several capacities, a qualified voter of the municipality or, as the case may be, of the sector concerned, shall have his name entered on the list in only one capacity according to the following order of preference: Where several immovables are contemplated in subparagraph 2 or 4 of the first paragraph, the immovable with the highest property value shall be the immovable considered. Where several business establishments are contemplated in subparagraph 3 or 5 of the said paragraph, the business establishment with the highest rental value shall be the business establishment considered.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2125", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2127", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2128", "mode": "normal", "text": "**532.** The registration procedure applies to determine whether a referendum poll must be held. Notwithstanding the first paragraph, the procedure does not apply In the case contemplated in subparagraph 3 of the second paragraph, the by-law, resolution or ordinance being the subject of the referendum is deemed to be approved by the qualified voters. The clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall inform the council thereof at the next sitting. If a list of electors whose names are on the permanent list of electors has been transmitted by the Chief Electoral Officer under section 546, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall also inform the Chief Electoral Officer, in writing, of the referendum poll waiver and of the date of the sitting at which the council was informed of it.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2129", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2131", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2132", "mode": "normal", "text": "**533.** Any qualified voter entitled to have his name entered on the referendum list of the municipality or, as the case may be, of the sector concerned may demand that a referendum poll be held by entering his name, address and capacity in a register open for that purpose and affixing his signature opposite those entries. The address of a qualified voter shall be, according to the capacity entitling him to have his name entered on the referendum list of the municipality or, as the case may be, of the sector concerned, the address of the immovable where he is domiciled, of the immovable of which he is the owner or of the business establishment of which he is the occupant. The address of the immovable shall include the apartment or room number, if any. If the immovable has no number, the cadastral number shall be used.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2133", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2135", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2136", "mode": "normal", "text": "**534.** A qualified voter may make only one application for a referendum poll.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2137", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2139", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2140", "mode": "normal", "text": "**535.** The clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall fix the days and places where the register will be open for registration to qualified voters. The places must be accessible to handicapped persons. He shall fix as many consecutive days, up to a maximum of five, as there are multiples of 500 in the number of applications needed under section 553 to require that a referendum poll be held. Where the number is less than 500, he shall fix only one day. Every day fixed must be comprised in the 45-day period following the date of reference.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2141", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2143", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2144", "mode": "normal", "text": "**536.** The register shall be open, from 9 a.m. to 7 p.m. without interruption, on every day fixed by the clerk or the clerk-treasurer, subject to any extension under section 537. Notwithstanding the first paragraph, where several days have been fixed and where the number of applications needed to require that a referendum poll be held is reached before the last day, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall close the register at 7 p.m. on the day the number is reached if the council of the municipality passed a by-law to that effect before the first day the register is open for registration.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2145", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2147", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2148", "mode": "normal", "text": "**537.** In the case of a delay or interruption, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer may extend the period during which the register is open for registration, for as long as he determines, in respect of the place affected by the delay or interruption. The extension shall not exceed the length of the delay or interruption.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2149", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2151", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2152", "mode": "normal", "text": "**538.** The qualified voters who are present on the premises where the register is open for registration at the time the register is scheduled to be closed and who have not been able to make the entries concerning them may nevertheless exercise their right to do so. The person in charge of the register within the meaning of section 541 shall declare the period of registration closed after such persons have exercised their right. For the purposes of the first paragraph, the premises where the register is open for registration extend as far as the end of the waiting line of qualified voters as it stands at the time the register is scheduled to close.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2153", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2155", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2156", "mode": "normal", "text": "**539.** Not later than five days before the day the register opens for registration, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall give a public notice to the qualified voters entitled to have their names entered on the referendum list of the municipality or, as the case may be, of the sector concerned. The heading of the notice shall clearly identify the group of persons for whom the notice is intended. If the notice is intended for the qualified voters entitled to have their names entered on the referendum list of a sector, the heading shall include a summary description of the sector. The notice shall set out Where the by-law, resolution or ordinance that is the subject of the referendum is a loan by-law, resolution or ordinance, the notice shall also indicate the amount and intended use of the proposed loan. Where the notice is intended for the qualified voters entitled to have their names entered on the referendum list of the sector concerned, it shall illustrate the perimeter of the sector by means of a sketch. In addition to or in lieu of the sketch, the notice may describe the perimeter of the sector by using the names of thoroughfares wherever possible.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2157", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2159", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2160", "mode": "normal", "text": "**540.** Where it is necessary to hold a simultaneous registration procedure in respect of several by-laws, resolutions or ordinances, each shall be the subject of a separate notice and have separate registers. Notwithstanding the foregoing, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer may publish a single notice respecting all the by-laws, resolutions and ordinances which concern the same qualified voters.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2161", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2163", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2164", "mode": "normal", "text": "**541.** The clerk or clerk-treasurer shall be the person in charge of the register unless another person is specially designated by him for that purpose. Before taking office, the person shall swear that he will perform his duties according to law. The clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall make designations as provided in the first paragraph if he establishes several places where the register is open for registration.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2165", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2167", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2168", "mode": "normal", "text": "**542.** While the register is open for registration, the person in charge of it shall keep it under his supervision at all times. The clerk or the clerk-treasurer may, however, specially designate an assistant to the person in charge of the register to replace him when he is absent and assist him in performing his duties. Before taking office, the assistant shall swear that he will perform his duties according to law.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2169", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2171", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2172", "mode": "normal", "text": "**543.** The text of the by-law, resolution or ordinance and of the notice shall accompany the register and be posted up at the place where the register is open for registration.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2173", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2175", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2176", "mode": "normal", "text": "**544.** Qualified voters entitled to have their names entered on the referendum list shall make and sign their entries in the register, in the order they present themselves to do so.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2177", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2179", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2180", "mode": "normal", "text": "**545.** On presenting himself to make his entries in the register, a person shall state his name, address and capacity to the person in charge of the register. The person must also produce identification in accordance with the third paragraph of section 215 or, failing that, establish his identity in accordance with section 213.2, which applies with the necessary modifications. After ascertaining that the person has established his identity, is a qualified voter, is entitled to have his name entered on the referendum list, meets the requirements set out in the first paragraph of section 523 and has not already made any entry in the register, the person in charge of the register shall give him access to the register, subject to section 547. No person may write down or otherwise record information contained in a document produced pursuant to the second paragraph.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2181", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2183", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2184", "mode": "normal", "text": "**546.** The clerk or the clerk-treasurer may draw up a list of the qualified voters entitled to have their names entered on the referendum list from any referendum list, list of electors, property assessment roll, roll of rental values, collection roll or other document he considers appropriate. For this purpose, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer may request, in writing, that the chief electoral officer transmit to him a list of the electors whose names are entered on the permanent list of electors for the territory of the municipality or for the sector concerned. The request must be made in the manner determined by the chief electoral officer. It must specify the date of reference, describe the territory concerned and state the date on which and form in which the list must be transmitted. The chief electoral officer shall transmit the list requested not later than the date indicated in the request. The costs relating to the production of the list, established under section 549 of the Election Act ( chapter E-3.3 A person whose name is not entered on any of the documents contemplated in the first or second paragraph may be allowed to make his entries in the register if he proves to the person in charge of the register that he is a qualified voter entitled to have his name entered on the referendum list of the municipality or, as the case may be, of the sector concerned and meets the requirements set out in the first paragraph of section 523.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2185", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2187", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2188", "mode": "normal", "text": "**547.** To be admitted to make his entries in the register, a person shall, at the request of the person in charge of the register, declare under oath that he is a qualified voter entitled to have his name entered on the referendum list of the municipality or, as the case may be, of the sector concerned and meets the requirements set out in the first paragraph of section 523. A person under whose name another person has already made entries in the register shall nevertheless be admitted to do so, after declaring under oath that he is really the qualified voter entitled to be entered on the referendum list under that name, that he meets the requirements set out in the first paragraph of section 523 and that he has not made his entries in the register. No person may be admitted to make entries in the register by the person in charge thereof if he refuses to make the oath required of him.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2189", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2191", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2192", "mode": "normal", "text": "**548.** Each person admitted to make his entries shall do so without undue delay, failing which the person in charge of the register may compel him to leave whether or not he has completed his entries.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2193", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2195", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2196", "mode": "normal", "text": "**549.** The clerk or the clerk-treasurer has, during each day of registration, the powers of a returning officer in matters of maintaining order.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2197", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2199", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2200", "mode": "normal", "text": "**550.** No person shall, on the premises where the register is open for registration, use any sign to indicate that he supports or opposes the holding of a referendum poll or that he favours an affirmative or a negative answer to a question that would be submitted to such a poll or engage in any other form of publicity to the same effect. The person in charge of the register may have any prohibited publicity stopped or removed. The building in which those premises are situated and any neighbouring place where the sign or publicity may be seen by the qualified voters are deemed to be the premises where the register is open for consultation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2201", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2203", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2204", "mode": "normal", "text": "**551.** Every person who performs duties under this chapter is entitled to receive a remuneration or an expense allowance from the municipality in respect of such duties. The council of the municipality may establish a tariff of remuneration or allowances; it may also delegate that power to the executive committee, if any. The tariff requires the approval of the Minister of Municipal Affairs, Regions and Land Occupancy if it fixes a lower remuneration or allowance than that established by the Minister pursuant to Title III. Every person contemplated in the first paragraph is entitled to the remuneration or allowance fixed in the tariff established by the Minister if the municipality has failed to establish its own or has failed to fix the remuneration or allowance of that person.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2205", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2207", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2208", "mode": "normal", "text": "**552.** One application for the holding of a referendum poll shall be counted for each qualified voter having made his entries according to law and who is entitled to have his name entered on the referendum list of the municipality or, as the case may be, of the sector concerned.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2209", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2211", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2212", "mode": "normal", "text": "**553.** Unless the by-law, resolution or ordinance is withdrawn, a referendum poll shall be held where, at the end of the period of registration, the number of applications reaches Where the result of the computation under the first paragraph is a number including a fraction, the fraction is counted as a unit. For the purposes of the first paragraph, qualified voters are persons entitled to have their names entered on the referendum list of the municipality or, as the case may be, of the sector concerned.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2213", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2215", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2216", "mode": "normal", "text": "**554.** The by-law, resolution or ordinance being the subject of the referendum is deemed to be approved by the qualified voters where, at the end of the period of registration, the number of applications is lower than the number needed to require that a referendum poll be held.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2217", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2219", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2220", "mode": "normal", "text": "**555.** As soon as practicable after the end of the period of registration, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall draw up a certificate showing", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2221", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2223", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2224", "mode": "normal", "text": "**556.** As soon as practicable after the certificate is drawn up, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall read it publicly to the persons present at the place where the sittings of the council of the municipality are held or at any other place determined by him.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2225", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2227", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2228", "mode": "normal", "text": "**557.** The clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall table the certificate before the council at its next sitting. If a list of electors whose names are on the permanent list of electors has been transmitted by the Chief Electoral Officer under section 546, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall send the Chief Electoral Officer a copy of the certificate showing the date on which the certificate was tabled before the council.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2229", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2231", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2232", "mode": "normal", "text": "**558.** Where a referendum poll must be held, the council shall fix, not later than at the sitting following that at which the certificate is tabled, the date of the poll, in accordance with Chapter VI. The clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall inform the Chief Electoral Officer in writing of the date of the poll.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2233", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2235", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2236", "mode": "normal", "text": "**559.** So long as the notice of the referendum poll has not been published, the council may, by resolution, withdraw the by-law, resolution or ordinance. Within 15 days of the withdrawal, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall inform the persons concerned by a public notice. The clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall send the Chief Electoral Officer a copy of the notice showing the date on which the notice was published.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2237", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2239", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2240", "mode": "normal", "text": "**560.** The clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall prepare the referendum list of the municipality or, as the case may be, of the sector concerned after the day on which the date of the referendum poll is determined and not later than 25 days before that date. Notwithstanding the foregoing, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer is not required to prepare a new list if a referendum list drawn up in relation to a date of reference that precedes the date of reference applicable to the referendum concerned by less than 90 days is already in force in the municipality or, as the case may be, in the sector concerned or in a territory comprising the sector concerned. The clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall deposit the referendum list already in force or the relevant part thereof in the office of the municipality not later than 25 days before the day of the referendum poll; in such a case, the public notices provided for in sections 527 and 529 need not be given.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2241", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2243", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2244", "mode": "normal", "text": "**561.** Division II of Chapter VI of Title I applies, adapted as required, and so far as it is consistent with this Title, to the preparation, revision and coming into force of the referendum list of the municipality or, as the case may be, of the sector concerned. However, the clerk or clerk-treasurer is not required to make a request under section 100 if he has made a request under section 546, for the same date of reference, in respect of the territory concerned by the referendum or a territory that includes it.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2245", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2247", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2248", "mode": "normal", "text": "**562.** The clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall appoint as revisor any person he may choose, without recommendation from the authorized parties, if any.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2249", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2251", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2252", "mode": "normal", "text": "**563.** Before taking office, every member, secretary and revising officer of a board of revisors shall swear that he will perform his duties according to law.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2253", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2255", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2256", "mode": "normal", "text": "**564.** The representative of the qualified voters who favour an affirmative answer to the referendum question and the representative of the qualified voters who favour a negative answer to the question are entitled to receive, on request and free of charge, a maximum of five copies of the referendum list and of the abstract of changes. The clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall, on a written application, designate the representative contemplated in the first paragraph for each of the two groups. Authorized parties, recognized tickets and candidates are not entitled to free copies of the list or abstract.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2257", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2259", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2260", "mode": "normal", "text": "**565.** The clerk or the clerk-treasurer and every member, secretary and revising officer of a board of revisors are entitled to receive remuneration or an expense allowance from the municipality in respect of the duties they perform under this chapter. The council of the municipality may establish a tariff of remuneration or allowances; it may also delegate that power to the executive committee, if any. The tariff requires the approval of the Minister of Municipal Affairs, Regions and Land Occupancy if it fixes a remuneration or allowance lower than that fixed in the tariff established by the Minister pursuant to Title III. Every person contemplated in the first paragraph is entitled to the remuneration or allowance fixed in the tariff established by the Minister if the municipality has failed to establish its own or if it has failed to fix the remuneration or allowance of that person.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2261", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2263", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2264", "mode": "normal", "text": "**566.** This chapter applies to a referendum poll required as a result of a registration procedure carried out in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV, and to a referendum poll required pursuant to the Act providing for the referendum or as a result of a decision taken in accordance with the third paragraph of section 517.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2265", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2267", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2268", "mode": "normal", "text": "**567.** To the extent that they are consistent with this chapter, the following provisions of Title I, adapted as required, apply to a referendum: Notwithstanding subparagraph 2 of the first paragraph, subdivision 2 of Division IV of Chapter VI of Title I respecting advance polling does not apply if the referendum is intended for part only of the qualified voters of the municipality, unless the council of the municipality orders that the said subdivision applies to the referendum.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2269", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2271", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2272", "mode": "normal", "text": "**568.** The referendum poll shall be held on the date fixed by the council of the municipality; the date must be a Sunday comprised in the 120 days following the date of reference. The Minister of Municipal Affairs, Regions and Land Occupancy may, on request, allow the council to fix the date of the poll at a later date within the limit he specifies.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2273", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2275", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2276", "mode": "normal", "text": "**569.** The clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall appoint as deputy returning officer, as poll clerk and as a member of an identity verification panel any person he may choose, without recommendation from the authorized parties, if any.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2277", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2279", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2280", "mode": "normal", "text": "**570.** On a written application, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall appoint, for each polling station, a representative of the qualified voters who favour an affirmative answer to the referendum question and a representative of the qualified voters who favour a negative answer. For the purposes of provisions applicable to the referendum by reference, the representatives shall have a status equivalent to that of the representatives of candidates assigned to a polling station. On a written application, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall appoint, for each place where there is a polling station and for each group of qualified voters described in the first paragraph, a poll runner authorized to periodically collect a list of the persons who have already exercised their right to vote. The appointment of the representative and of the poll runner shall be made by means of a writing signed by the clerk or the clerk-treasurer and presented to the deputy returning officer. The appointment of the representative is valid for the duration of the poll and of the counting of the votes taking place at the polling station; that of the poll runner is valid for the duration of the poll. The representatives appointed under section 564 are entitled to receive the notices and documents that must be given to candidates under the provisions applicable by reference to the referendum.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2281", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2283", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2284", "mode": "normal", "text": "**571.** The list used shall be the referendum list in force in the municipality or, as the case may be, in the sector concerned.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2285", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2287", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2288", "mode": "normal", "text": "**572.** Not later than 10 days before the day of the referendum poll, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall give public notice of the poll to the persons whose names are entered on the referendum list. The heading of the notice shall identify the group of persons for whom it is intended. If the notice is intended for the persons whose names are entered on the referendum list of the sector concerned, the heading shall give a summary description of the sector. The notice shall set out The particulars referred to in subparagraph 6 of the third paragraph are not needed if the clerk or the clerk-treasurer causes reminders containing those particulars to be distributed. Where the by-law, resolution or ordinance that is the subject of the referendum is a loan by-law, resolution or ordinance, the notice shall indicate the amount and intended use of the proposed loan. Where the notice is intended for the persons whose names are entered on the referendum list of the sector concerned, the notice shall illustrate the perimeter of the sector by means of a sketch. In addition to or in lieu of the sketch, the notice may describe the perimeter of the sector by using the names of thoroughfares wherever possible.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2289", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2291", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2292", "mode": "normal", "text": "**573.** The clerk or the clerk-treasurer may cause a reminder to be distributed to every person whose name is entered on the referendum list of the municipality or, as the case may be, of the sector concerned. He shall do so in a municipality having a population of 20,000 or over. The reminder shall contain all the particulars that must be set out in the notice of referendum poll; however, the particulars relating to polling stations may concern only the polling station where the addressee is entitled to vote.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2293", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2295", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2296", "mode": "normal", "text": "**574.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2297", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2299", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2300", "mode": "normal", "text": "**575.** The ballot paper shall include, on the obverse,", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2301", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2303", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2304", "mode": "normal", "text": "**576.** The by-law, resolution or ordinance that is the subject of the referendum is deemed to be approved by the qualified voters where the results of the poll show a greater number of affirmative votes than negative votes, unless the provisions governing the referendum establish a different rule. In the latter case, the clerk or the clerk-treasurer is not required to request a recount of the votes in case of a tie.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2305", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2307", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2308", "mode": "normal", "text": "**577.** Where the results of the poll certified by the judge following a recount or re-addition of the votes show a tie-vote, the mayor or, as the case may be, the warden may give a voice vote at the next council sitting after the judge’s decision. The vote shall be counted as if it had been cast by a person whose name is entered on the referendum list. The first two paragraphs do not apply where, according to the provisions governing the referendum, an affirmative vote by the mayor or the warden is not sufficient to cause the by-law, resolution or ordinance to be deemed to be approved by the qualified voters.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2309", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2311", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2312", "mode": "normal", "text": "**578.** The clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall draw up a statement of the final results of the poll and table it before the council at the next sitting. The clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall inform the chief electoral officer, in writing, of the date of the tabling of the statement.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2313", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2315", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2316", "mode": "normal", "text": "**579.** In no case may the person in charge of access to documents held by the municipality deliver any copy of any used ballot papers. He shall allow no one to examine the ballot papers, unless he is required to do so by order of the court or a judge.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2317", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2319", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2320", "mode": "normal", "text": "**580.** The Minister of Municipal Affairs, Regions and Land Occupancy shall establish, by regulation, a tariff of the remuneration or expense allowances which the following persons are entitled to receive in respect of duties performed under this Act: Notwithstanding the foregoing, the Minister is not required to establish the remuneration and allowance of election or referendum officers whose services are temporarily required in accordance with section 84.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2321", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2323", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2324", "mode": "normal", "text": "**582.** The Minister may prescribe, by regulation, the form or minimum content of or a model for any document prescribed by this Act except a document prescribed by Chapter XIII of Title I, or the information that any such document must contain. The chief electoral officer may prescribe, by regulation, the form or minimum content of or a model for any document prescribed by Chapter XIII of Title I, or the information that any such document must contain.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2325", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2327", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2328", "mode": "normal", "text": "**583.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2329", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2331", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2332", "mode": "normal", "text": "**584.** The Government may establish, by regulation, a tariff of costs for the recount or re-addition of votes by a judge.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2333", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2335", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2336", "mode": "normal", "text": "**585.** Categories of municipalities or cases, and appropriate rules for each category or combination of categories may be established by regulation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2337", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2339", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2340", "mode": "normal", "text": "**586.** The following persons are guilty of an offence:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2341", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2343", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2344", "mode": "normal", "text": "**587.** Every deputy returning officer who admits a person to vote with the knowledge that he has already voted and has no other voting right to exercise is guilty of an offence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2345", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2347", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2348", "mode": "normal", "text": "**588.** The following persons are guilty of an offence:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2349", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2351", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2352", "mode": "normal", "text": "**589.** Every person who knowingly violates or attempts to violate the secrecy of voting, inhibits or attempts to inhibit the freedom to vote, prevents or attempts to prevent any procedure relating to the vote, or alters or attempts to alter the results of the election or referendum, is guilty of an offence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2353", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2355", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2356", "mode": "normal", "text": "**590.** Every person is guilty of an offence who,", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2357", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2359", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2360", "mode": "normal", "text": "**591.** Every person is guilty of an offence who, Every gift made or promised during an election period within the meaning of Chapter XIII of Title I by a candidate or a person who subsequently becomes a candidate, or in his name or in his behalf, is deemed, to have been made in order to influence the vote of an elector. The first paragraph does not apply", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2361", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2363", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2364", "mode": "normal", "text": "**592.** Every person is guilty of an offence who, Every gift made or promised, from the date of reference within the meaning of Title II to the end of the registration procedure provided for in Chapter IV of the said Title, by a person or in his name or in his behalf is deemed to have been made in order to influence the opinion of a person as to the holding of a referendum poll. The first paragraph does not apply to a person who,", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2365", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2367", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2368", "mode": "normal", "text": "**593.** Every person is guilty of an offence who, Every gift made or promised, from the day on which the date of the referendum poll is fixed to the time scheduled for the close of the polling stations on polling day, by a person, or in his name or in his behalf is deemed to have been made in order to influence the vote of a qualified voter. The first paragraph does not apply to a person who,", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2369", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2371", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2372", "mode": "normal", "text": "**594.** The following persons are guilty of an offence:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2373", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2375", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2376", "mode": "normal", "text": "**595.** Every official agent or deputy of an official agent is guilty of an offence who Every elector referred to in section 512.2 or in the last paragraph of section 512.3 is guilty of an offence who makes a false declaration, files a false report or produces a false or falsified invoice, receipt or other voucher.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2377", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2379", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2380", "mode": "normal", "text": "**596.** The following persons are guilty of an offence:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2381", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2383", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2384", "mode": "normal", "text": "**597.** Every official representative or delegate of an official representative who files a report, return, statement, invoice, receipt or other voucher that is incomplete or contains a false indication or false information is guilty of an offence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2385", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2387", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2388", "mode": "normal", "text": "**598.** Every auditor of an authorized party who produces a report with the knowledge that it is incomplete or contains a false indication or false information is guilty of an offence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2389", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2391", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2392", "mode": "normal", "text": "**599.** The following are guilty of an offence:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2393", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2395", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2396", "mode": "normal", "text": "**600.** Every person who accepts an appointment as official representative, delegate of an official representative, official agent, deputy of an official agent or auditor with the knowledge that he is disqualified from holding that position is guilty of an offence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2397", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2399", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2400", "mode": "normal", "text": "**601.** Every person is guilty of an offence who", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2401", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2403", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2404", "mode": "normal", "text": "**602.** Every person responsible for collecting signatures in support of an application for authorization of a party who allows a signature he knows to be that of a person who is not an elector of the municipality mentioned in the application, or of a person other than the person affixing it, to be affixed to the writing accompanying the application, is guilty of an offence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2405", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2407", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2408", "mode": "normal", "text": "**603.** Every person who makes a contribution to a person with the knowledge that he is not the official representative of an authorized party or independent candidate, or a person designated by the latter in writing to solicit and collect contributions, is guilty of an offence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2409", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2411", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2412", "mode": "normal", "text": "**604.** Every official agent who fails to pay, before filing his return of election expenses, every claim received in respect of such expenses within 60 days after polling day, except any claim he contests, is guilty of an offence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2413", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2415", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2416", "mode": "normal", "text": "**605.** Every treasurer is guilty of an offence who", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2417", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2419", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2420", "mode": "normal", "text": "**606.** Every official representative of an authorized party who fails to keep, for seven years after the filing of a financial report, the receipts issued for contributions collected as well as the invoices, evidences of payment and vouchers for the period covered by the report or who fails to remit the receipts and vouchers to the chief electoral officer is guilty of an offence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2421", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2423", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2424", "mode": "normal", "text": "**607.** Every official representative of an authorized independent candidate is guilty of an offence who, after polling day, after the candidate withdraws or after the candidate is declared elected before the end of the polling period, as the case may be,", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2425", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2427", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2428", "mode": "normal", "text": "**608.** Every person holding sums of money or assets of a party or of an independent candidate who fails to remit the money or the assets to the chief electoral officer within 10 days after he is notified of the withdrawal of authorization of the party or candidate is guilty of an offence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2429", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2431", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2432", "mode": "normal", "text": "**609.** The following are guilty of an offence :", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2433", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2435", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2436", "mode": "normal", "text": "**610.** The following persons are guilty of an offence:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2437", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2439", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2440", "mode": "normal", "text": "**611.** Every person who solicits or collects contributions or incurs expenses other than election expenses for an authorized party or independent candidate without being its or his official representative, his delegate or a person designated in writing for that purpose by either, is guilty of an offence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2441", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2443", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2444", "mode": "normal", "text": "**612.** Every official representative, delegate of an official representative or person designated by either to solicit and collect contributions is guilty of an offence who", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2445", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2447", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2448", "mode": "normal", "text": "**613.** The following persons are guilty of an offence:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2449", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2451", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2452", "mode": "normal", "text": "**614.** Every person holding a contribution made contrary to Chapter XIII of Title I who fails to remit the amount of the contribution or the amount at which the contribution is evaluated to the treasurer immediately on becoming aware of the fact is guilty of an offence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2453", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2455", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2456", "mode": "normal", "text": "**615.** Every radio, television or cable broadcaster or owner of a newspaper, periodical or other publication who makes air time on the radio or television or space in the newspaper, periodical or other publication available free of charge to an authorized party outside an election period or to the leader of an authorized party or to a candidate during an election period without offering such service equitably as to quality and quantity to the other authorized parties in the municipality, their leaders or the other candidates for the same office, as the case may be, is guilty of an offence. For the purposes of the first paragraph, a co-candidate and the candidate with whom he is associated shall be counted as one candidate for the office of councillor.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2457", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2459", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2460", "mode": "normal", "text": "**616.** Every official representative of an authorized party or independent candidate who fails to pay the accounts and invoices transmitted to him, within six months of receipt, is guilty of an offence, unless he contests them.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2461", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2463", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2464", "mode": "normal", "text": "**617.** Every person who contracts a loan for an authorized party or independent candidate without being its or his official representative or grants a loan for an authorized party or independent candidate to a person with the knowledge that he is not its or his official representative is guilty of an offence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2465", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2467", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2468", "mode": "normal", "text": "**618.** Every official representative is guilty of an offence who Every elector is guilty of an offence who grants a loan in a manner that is not in accordance with section 446.1 or grants a loan or makes a contract of suretyship knowing that by so doing, the maximum amount specified in section 447.1 will be exceeded.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2469", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2471", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2472", "mode": "normal", "text": "**619.** The following persons are guilty of an offence:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2473", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2475", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2476", "mode": "normal", "text": "**620.** Every official agent or deputy of an official agent who pays any election expenses otherwise than out of the election fund put at the disposal of the official agent is guilty of an offence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2477", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2479", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2480", "mode": "normal", "text": "**621.** The following persons are guilty of an offence:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2481", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2483", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2484", "mode": "normal", "text": "**622.** For the purposes of subparagraph 2 of the first paragraph, the expression “ election expense ” includes expenses referred to in paragraph 9 of section 453 and the expression “ official agent ” includes a private intervenor within the meaning of Division VIII.1 of Chapter XIII of Title I, if the private intervenor is an elector, and the representative of such an intervenor if the private intervenor is a group of electors. Every person is guilty of an offence who", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2485", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2487", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2488", "mode": "normal", "text": "**623.** For the purposes of this section, the expression “ election expenses ” includes expenses referred to in paragraph 9 of section 453 and the expression “ official agent ” includes a private intervenor within the meaning of Division VIII.1 of Chapter XIII of Title I, if the private intervenor is an elector, and the representative of such an intervenor if the private intervenor is a group of electors. Every person is guilty of an offence who", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2489", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2491", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2492", "mode": "normal", "text": "**624.** The following persons are guilty of an offence:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2493", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2495", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2496", "mode": "normal", "text": "**625.** Every person authorized to incur election expenses who pays such an expense without the payment being justified by an invoice containing the particulars contemplated in section 466 is guilty of an offence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2497", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2499", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2500", "mode": "normal", "text": "**626.** Every official representative, official agent or financial representative of a leadership candidate, including one who has ceased prematurely to exercise such functions, who fails to file a report or return required under section 420, 479, 483.1, 484, 485, 487, 492, 496, 499.16, 499.17 or 499.19 or the documents required to be filed with such a report or return within the time prescribed in those sections, or who fails to file the receipts required under section 499.9 within the time prescribed in that section, is guilty of an offence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2501", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2503", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2504", "mode": "normal", "text": "**627.** Every auditor who fails to transmit the report provided for in section 488 within the prescribed time is guilty of an offence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2505", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2507", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2508", "mode": "normal", "text": "**628.** Every deputy of an official agent, official representative of a party or financial representative of a party leadership candidate who fails to transmit a detailed account of the election expenses or party leadership campaign expenses he has incurred or authorized and the documents that must accompany it, within the time prescribed in section 455, is guilty of an offence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2509", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2511", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2512", "mode": "normal", "text": "**629.** Every advertising agency who fails to transmit a detailed account of the election expenses it has incurred or ordered and the documents that must accompany it, within the time prescribed by section 456, is guilty of an offence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2513", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2515", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2516", "mode": "normal", "text": "**630.** Every person who attends a sitting of a council, board, committee, commission or body as a member thereof, with the knowledge that he has lost the right to do so under this Act is guilty of an offence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2517", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2519", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2520", "mode": "normal", "text": "**631.** The following persons are guilty of an offence:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2521", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2523", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2524", "mode": "normal", "text": "**632.** Every person is guilty of an offence who", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2525", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2527", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2528", "mode": "normal", "text": "**633.** Every person is guilty of an offence who", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2529", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2531", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2532", "mode": "normal", "text": "**634.** The following persons are guilty of an offence:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2533", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2535", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2536", "mode": "normal", "text": "**635.** The following persons are guilty of an offence:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2537", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2539", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2540", "mode": "normal", "text": "**636.** Every person who uses intimidation, threats or sanctions to incite an officer or employee to commit the offence contemplated in section 594 or to punish the officer or employee for refusing to commit it is guilty of an offence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2541", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2543", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2544", "mode": "normal", "text": "**637.** Every person who, by his act or omission, aids another person to commit an offence is guilty of the offence as if he had committed it himself if he knew or should have known that his act or omission would probably result in aiding to commit the offence. Every person who incites or leads another person to commit an offence is guilty of the offence, and of any other offence the other person commits as a result of his encouragement, advice or order, as if he had committed it himself, if he knew or should have known that his encouragement, advice or order would probably result in the commission of the offences. The fact that no means or plan for committing the offence was proposed or that it was committed otherwise than as proposed does not constitute a defence.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2545", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2547", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2548", "mode": "normal", "text": "**638.** If the leader of a political party, another of its officers, its official representative, a delegate of its official representative, its official agent or a deputy of its official agent commits, allows or tolerates an offence under this Act, the political party is presumed to have committed the same offence. The first paragraph applies, with the necessary modifications, to a ticket.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2549", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2551", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2552", "mode": "normal", "text": "**639.** Every person who is guilty of an offence described in any of sections 586 to 588, 631 to 634 and 636.1 is liable,", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2553", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2555", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2556", "mode": "normal", "text": "**640.** Every person who is guilty of an offence described in section 594, paragraph 1 of section 596 or section 598 is liable to a fine of not less than $1,000 nor more than $10,000 in the case of a natural person or, in the case of a legal person, to a fine of not less than $3,000 nor more than $25,000.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2557", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2559", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2560", "mode": "normal", "text": "**641.** Every person who commits an offence under section 599, to the extent that it pertains to an expense or a loan, or any of sections 603, 607 to 609, 611 to 613, 615 to 618 and 623 to 625 and paragraph 1 of section 625.1 is liable to a fine of not less than $500 nor more than $10,000.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2561", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2563", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2564", "mode": "normal", "text": "**642.** Every person who is guilty of an offence described in any of sections 626 to 629 is liable to a fine of not more than $50 for each day of delay.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2565", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2567", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2568", "mode": "normal", "text": "**643.** Every person who is guilty of an offence described in section 630 is liable to a fine of not less than $50 nor more than $500 for each sitting which he attends without right.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2569", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2571", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2572", "mode": "normal", "text": "**644.** Every person who is guilty of an offence described in section 636 is liable to a fine of not less than $50 nor more than $5,000.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2573", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2575", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2576", "mode": "normal", "text": "**645.** An offence under any of sections 586 to 588, 589 to 593, paragraphs 1 and 2 of section 594, sections 595 to 598, paragraphs 2, 3 , 4 and 5 of section 610, paragraph 2 of section 610.1, and section 636.3 to the extent that it is an offence described in any of paragraphs 2, 3, 4 and 5 of section 610, is a corrupt electoral practice. Notwithstanding the foregoing, in the case of an offence described in subparagraph 1 of the first paragraph of section 595, the judge may rule that the alleged offence is not a corrupt electoral practice if", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2577", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2579", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2580", "mode": "normal", "text": "**646.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2581", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2583", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2584", "mode": "normal", "text": "**647.** The chief electoral officer may institute proceedings for any offence described in this Title. However, proceedings may not be instituted for an offence described in section 630 unless the loss of the right to attend a sitting mentioned in that section results from the application of Chapter XIII of Title I. Section 18 of the Act respecting the Director of Criminal and Penal Prosecutions ( chapter D 9.1.1", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2585", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2587", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2588", "mode": "normal", "text": "**648.** Penal proceedings for an offence referred to in section 647 are prescribed seven years after the date the offence was committed. However, proceedings relating to an offence under any of sections 586 to 588 and 589 to 594 are prescribed 10 years after the date the offence was committed.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2589", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2591", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2592", "mode": "normal", "text": "**649.** The clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall, not later than 30 days after an election, transmit to the Minister of Municipal Affairs, Regions and Land Occupancy and to the Chief Electoral Officer a statement naming the persons who form the council of the municipality. The clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall also, at the request of the Minister or the Chief Electoral Officer and for the purpose of drawing up a statistical portrait of the election, transmit, as soon as possible, any data relating to the nominations, to the participation of electors in the election or to the results of the election. The clerk or the clerk-treasurer shall notify, within 30 days, the same persons of any change occurring in the composition of the council after the election of the mayor by the councillors or after the decision of the council not to fill a vacancy in the office of a councillor.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2593", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2595", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2596", "mode": "normal", "text": "**650.** No warrant of arrest may be executed against an election or referendum officer on polling day.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2597", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2599", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2600", "mode": "normal", "text": "**651.** Disqualification from office or from voting resulting from a judgment of guilty or from such a judgment and a sentence of imprisonment is lifted where the person contemplated in the judgment obtains a pardon.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2601", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2603", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2604", "mode": "normal", "text": "**652.** No act performed by a council, committee, commission or body during a sitting attended by a member while he is disqualified from holding office or not entitled to attend the sitting is invalidated by reason only that the member attends the sitting.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2605", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2607", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2608", "mode": "normal", "text": "**653.** An oath required by this Act may be made before the mayor or the clerk or the clerk-treasurer of the municipality, an election or referendum officer, a person responsible for the register contemplated in Chapter IV of Title II or any other person authorized by law to administer oaths. A person referred to in the preceding paragraph shall, upon request and free of charge, administer the oath and issue a certificate attesting that the oath was made.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2609", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2611", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2612", "mode": "normal", "text": "**654.** (Repealed).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2613", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2615", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2616", "mode": "normal", "text": "**655.** Every person who is required to sign his name on a document and who is unable to do so shall affix his mark in the presence of a witness who shall affix his signature.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2617", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2619", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2620", "mode": "normal", "text": "**656.** The inobservance of a formality prescribed in this Act does not invalidate an act, unless the inobservance causes a serious prejudice or unless the effect of the inobservance is provided by law, and particularly, if it is prescribed that the formality must be complied with under penalty of absolute nullity or rejection of the act.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2621", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2623", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2624", "mode": "normal", "text": "**657.** Except on a question of jurisdiction, no application for judicial review under the Code of Civil Procedure ( chapter C-25.01 A judge of the Court of Appeal may, on an application, summarily annul any decision, order or injunction made or granted contrary to the first paragraph.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2625", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2627", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2628", "mode": "normal", "text": "**658.** No person who is required or authorized under this Act to perform an act is liable for any damage caused by his act or omission in accordance with this Act or resulting from an error made in good faith and due to reasonable cause.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2629", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2631", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2632", "mode": "normal", "text": "**659.** Personal information required on a document prescribed in this Act is public information within the meaning of the Act respecting Access to documents held by public bodies and the Protection of personal information ( chapter A-2.1 Notwithstanding the first paragraph, the list of the members of an authorized party and any personal information appearing on a list of electors or referendum list, a list of the qualified voters entitled to have their names entered on a referendum list, on an application made before a board of revisors, or on receipts for contributions of $50 or less to an authorized party, an authorized independent candidate or a leadership candidate of an authorized party and not required to appear in a financial report, return of leadership campaign income and expenses or complementary return, as applicable, is not public information. Nor is a candidate’s or elected candidate’s address appearing on his nomination paper or declaration of election, as the case may be, except the name of the municipality. The information contemplated in the second paragraph shall be transmitted in accordance with this Act, and sections 59 and 66 to 68 of the Act respecting Access to documents held by public bodies and the Protection of personal information shall not apply to any such transmission. The municipality and the chief electoral officer are not required to file the information in the personal information file provided for in the said Act. Division II of Chapter II of the said Act does not apply to a document prescribed in this Act.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2633", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2635", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2636", "mode": "normal", "text": "**660.** (Amendment integrated into c. A-2.1, Schedule A).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2637", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2639", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2640", "mode": "normal", "text": "**661.** (Amendment integrated into c. A-15, s. 2).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2641", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2643", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2644", "mode": "normal", "text": "**662.** (Inoperative, 1987, c. 102, s. 6).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2645", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2647", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2648", "mode": "normal", "text": "**663.** (Amendment integrated into c. A-19.1, s. 51).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2649", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2651", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2652", "mode": "normal", "text": "**664.** (Amendment integrated into c. A-19.1, s. 53).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2653", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2655", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2656", "mode": "normal", "text": "**665.** (Amendment integrated into c. A-19.1, s. 57).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2657", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2659", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "2660", "mode": "normal", "text": "**666.** (Amendment integrated into c. A-19.1, s. 79).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "2661", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "