**373.** In order to liquidate the insurance fund, a liquidator must be appointed by the board of directors or the Superior Court, depending on whether the liquidation arises from a decision of the board or of the Court. On being appointed, the liquidator has the seisin of the insurance fund, and the decision-making committee ceases to exist.

