**416.** The guarantee fund of a federation is to be used to provide financial support to its member companies in order to protect the rights of their insureds and of the holders of insurance contracts that they underwrite. The fund consists of capital made up of the contributions of the member companies and, if applicable, the remaining property from the liquidation of a member company.

**417.** The federation determines the amount of capital that must be maintained in the guarantee fund. It informs the Authority of the amount as well as the reasons that led to that amount being determined and, if applicable, the circumstances justifying its modification.

**418.** The creditors of the federation have no right to the assets of the guarantee fund.

**419.** The federation must require its member companies to pay a contribution whenever this is necessary to maintain the capital of the guarantee fund.

