"8418", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8419", "mode": "normal", "text": ", ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8420", "type": "codeInline", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8421", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8422", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8423", "mode": "normal", "text": "forEach", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr"}, {"id": "8424", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8425", "mode": "normal", "text": ", or ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8426", "type": "codeInline", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8427", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8428", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8429", "mode": "normal", "text": ".map()", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr"}, {"id": "8430", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8431", "mode": "normal", "text": ". Loading a list of 50 users and then running a separate query for each one to fetch their related data produces 51 database round trips. In development with 5 items this is imperceptible. In production with 500 items per page it produces 501 round trips, each with network latency, and the page load time scales linearly with data volume. The fix is a single query with a ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8432", "type": "codeInline", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8433", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8434", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8435", "mode": "normal", "text": "JOIN", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr"}, {"id": "8436", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8437", "mode": "normal", "text": " or an ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8438", "type": "codeInline", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8439", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8440", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8441", "mode": "normal", "text": "IN (...)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr"}, {"id": "8442", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8443", "mode": "normal", "text": " clause.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "8444", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8445", "mode": "normal", "text": "Deadlocks from inconsistent lock acquisition order.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "8446", "mode": "normal", "text": " If two concurrent transactions each lock the same two rows or tables but in opposite order — Transaction A locks Row 1 then waits for Row 2; Transaction B locks Row 2 then waits for Row 1 — they wait for each other forever. PostgreSQL will eventually detect this and kill one of them with an error, but the error surfaces as a random, intermittent failure to users. Look for code where multiple rows are locked within a transaction and the order in which they are locked varies depending on runtime conditions (e.g., user input determines which rows are touched first).", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "8447", "type": "horizontalrule", "version": 1}, {"id": "8448", "tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8449", "mode": "normal", "text": "Category 3 — Silent Failures (The User Gets Wrong Data, Not an Error)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr"}, {"id": "8450", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8451", "mode": "normal", "text": "These are often worse than crashes because no alert fires, no error is logged, and the developer never knows anything went wrong. The user silently receives incorrect, incomplete, or stale data.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "8452", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8453", "mode": "normal", "text": "Empty ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "8454", "type": "codeInline", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8455", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8456", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8457", "mode": "normal", "text": ".catch(() => {})", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr"}, {"id": "8458", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8459", "mode": "normal", "text": " blocks.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "8460", "mode": "normal", "text": " An async operation fails, the error is swallowed, and execution continues as if the operation succeeded. The user sees a blank section, missing data, or a partial result with no explanation. Every no-op catch block is a silent data hole.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "8461", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9374", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8462", "type": "codeInline", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8463", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8464", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8465", "mode": "normal", "text": "try/catch", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr"}, {"id": "8466", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8467", "mode": "normal", "text": " that catches an error but continues rendering or responding as if success.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "8468", "mode": "normal", "text": " The catch logs the error but returns an empty object, ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8469", "type": "codeInline", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8470", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "