": [{"id": "9379", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8602", "type": "codeInline", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8603", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8604", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8605", "mode": "normal", "text": "new Date()", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr"}, {"id": "8606", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8607", "mode": "normal", "text": " stored without UTC normalization.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "8608", "mode": "normal", "text": " If the server''s system timezone is not UTC (common in many hosting environments), ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8609", "type": "codeInline", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8610", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8611", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8612", "mode": "normal", "text": "new Date()", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr"}, {"id": "8613", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8614", "mode": "normal", "text": " returns the local server time. Dates stored this way will be off by hours for users in other timezones and will sort incorrectly across DST boundaries.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "8615", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8616", "mode": "normal", "text": "\"Last N days\" calculated with millisecond arithmetic.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "8617", "mode": "normal", "text": " ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8618", "type": "codeInline", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8619", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8620", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8621", "mode": "normal", "text": "Date.now() - (30 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr"}, {"id": "8622", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8623", "mode": "normal", "text": " is not always 30 days. During the two DST transitions per year, a day is either 23 or 25 hours long. This calculation will silently include or exclude an extra day twice per year, affecting date-range filters and report generation for all users simultaneously. Use date manipulation with timezone awareness rather than raw milliseconds for human-calendar calculations.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "8624", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9380", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8625", "type": "codeInline", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8626", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8627", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8628", "mode": "normal", "text": "TIMESTAMP WITHOUT TIME ZONE", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr"}, {"id": "8629", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8630", "mode": "normal", "text": " columns in PostgreSQL for user-facing dates.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "8631", "mode": "normal", "text": " PostgreSQL stores the value exactly as given with no timezone information. If the application server and the database server are in different timezones — or if the app is ever deployed to a different timezone — all stored timestamps will be systematically wrong by the offset. For any date that a user will see, ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8632", "type": "codeInline", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8633", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8634", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8635", "mode": "normal", "text": "TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr"}, {"id": "8636", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8637", "mode": "normal", "text": " (", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8638", "type": "codeInline", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8639", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8640", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8641", "mode": "normal", "text": "TIMESTAMPTZ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr"}, {"id": "8642", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8643", "mode": "normal", "text": ") is the correct type.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "8644", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8645", "mode": "normal", "text": "Dates compared as strings.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "8646", "mode": "normal", "text": " ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8647", "type": "codeInline", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8648", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8649", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8650", "mode": "normal", "text": "\"2024-10-01\" > \"2024-09-30\"", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr"}, {"id": "8651", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8652", "mode": "normal", "text": " happens to work with ISO format. But if the format ever deviates — different locale formatting, a ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8653", "type": "codeInline", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8654", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8655", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8656", "mode": "normal", "text": "Date.toString()", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr"}, {"id": "8657", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8658", "mode": "normal", "text": " instead of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8659", "type": "codeInline", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8660", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8661", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8662", "mode": "normal", "text": "toISOString()", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr"}, {"id": "8663", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8664", "mode": "normal", "text": ", a database returning a different format — the comparison produces silently wrong sort order.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "8665", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8666", "mode": "normal", "text": "Expiry logic using ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "8667", "type": "codeInline", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8668", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8669", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8670", "mode": "normal", "text": ">", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr"}, {"id": "8671", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8672", "mode": "normal", "text": " instead of ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "8673", "type": "codeInline", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8674", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8675", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8676", "mode": "normal", "text": ">=", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr"}, {"id": "8677", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8678", "mode": "normal", "text": " or vice versa on exact timestamp boundaries.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "8679", "mode": "normal", "text": " A token that expires at exactly ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8680", "type": "codeInline", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8681", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8682", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8683", "mode": "normal", "text": "2024-10-01T00:00:00Z", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr"}, {"id": "8684", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8685", "mode": "normal", "text": " — is it valid at that exact millisecond? Off-by-one errors on boundaries cause tokens that should be valid to be rejected, or tokens that should be expired to be accepted, for users who happen to act at exactly the boundary moment.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "8686", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8687", "mode": "normal", "text": "No handling of month-end edge cases.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"id": "8688", "mode": "normal", "text": " Adding one month to January 31 produces February 31, which doesn''t exist. Different environments handle this differently — some roll over to March 2 or 3, some throw. Any code that does date arithmetic involving months without accounting for variable month lengths will fail for users who act on month-boundary dates.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"id": "8689", "type": "horizontalrule", "version": 1}, {"id": "8690", "tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8691", "mode": "normal", "text": "Category 5 — Edge Case Input Failures", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr"}, {"id": "8692", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8693", "mode": "normal", "text": "These bugs exist because the code was written for the happy path — reasonable input from a cooperative user. They surface when users do anything outside that narrow band of expectation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"id": "8694", "type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "9381", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8695", "type": "codeInline", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"id": "8696", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cursor", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"id": "8697", "mode": "normal", "text": "﻿", "type": "cur